{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness","id":864699,"title":"Ask a Simple Question, Get a Simple Answer: General Chronicles/World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-12T21:25:09-07:00","id":864699,"title":"Ask a Simple Question, Get a Simple Answer: General Chronicles/World of Darkness","content":"I realized just now that we didn't have one of these so... I figure why not start one. Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage all have one. Maybe a few other lines. Either way, this is here now.<br /> <br /> <br /> My first question... How exactly does Armor Piercing work against objects's Durability? I always assumed it was a subtract AP from Durability deal, but apparently it's not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 04-13-2016, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T22:03:04-07:00","id":864709,"title":"","content":"I would personally run it that way anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T22:08:28-07:00","id":864710,"title":"","content":"I would also assume it subtracts from Durability. <br /> <br /> How do you guys handle guns being fought over or used in a Grapple? Are we meant to simply use them in a Damage Move with successes determined by the Grappling roll like any other weapon? That's the impression I get, since the thing determining your capacity to shoot the person is your ability to control the weapon and use it on them in close quarters.<br /> <br /> As a related question, how do you handle the damage for throwing somebody against a wall? While Vigor in Vampire comes to mind, I'm thinking about this generally as well. Do any books discuss this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-12T23:38:52-07:00","id":864742,"title":"","content":"What material is the wall made of? Use that material's durability score as bashing dice added to the throwers strength to determine damage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T00:12:32-07:00","id":864754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=864742#post864742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What material is the wall made of? Use that material's durability score as bashing dice added to the throwers strength to determine damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was considering using Durability as a Weapon Modifier with the damage generated by successes on the throw as Bashing Damage, but that's also a decent idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T00:39:57-07:00","id":864764,"title":"","content":"Falling 3 meters only does 1 bashing damage. It would take quite a throw to equal the force of a fall like that, so I probably wouldn't have throwing someone against a wall deal any damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T06:36:19-07:00","id":865471,"title":"","content":"Hi guys! i'm missing certain rules on CofD.<br /> <br /> Like jump distance, rules about drowning. how do you handle these questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7761-glauber","name":"Glauber","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7761_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T07:39:01-07:00","id":865491,"title":"","content":"Drowning is a tilt now. You take 1 bashing damage per turn until you can breathe again. Holding your breath is stamina + composure, but I'd probably just not bother rolling unless they were in a fight or something. Jumping is still strength + athletics, 1 foot vertical per success. It doesn't give mechanics for a horizontal jump, but you could either multiply successes like in first edition, or just give a bonus for a run up and/or a penalty based on the distance you need to cover and just say one success does it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T07:51:38-07:00","id":865499,"title":"","content":"Is the distance you can wall run using 3rd of Parkour a typo, or are you really supposed to be able to pretty much double the world's record in wallrunning the instant when you buy it? I've got a player who bought Parkour and started calculating it, and she is kinda like, &quot;huh&quot;.<br /> <br /> In Weapon Rating description, it says that you add weapon rating &quot;as successe&quot; on a successful attack. Is this an artifact, or should I really apply it as successes, making EX!Successes in combat much more frequent? I never did that before, applying them simply as a &quot;base&quot; damage, and always felt that was the intent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T08:10:26-07:00","id":865506,"title":"","content":"Why is jumping measured in &quot;feet&quot; while every other measurement I could find in meters? Is this a hold over?<br /> <br /> While granted, it's easy to do the simple math of 3 feet equals a meter, this inconsistency does admittedly bother me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T08:12:18-07:00","id":865507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865499#post865499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the distance you can wall run using 3rd of Parkour a typo, or are you really supposed to be able to pretty much double the world's record in wallrunning the instant when you buy it? I've got a player who bought Parkour and started calculating it, and she is kinda like, &amp;quot;huh&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>As with many things in CofD, the distance Wall Run allows you to climb before having to roll is an abstraction. If it doesn't make sense to narrate it all as wall running, don't. Maybe only the first few feet is wall running and the rest is just free climbing, riding the momentum of the starting wall run. Once you get to the height where you have to start making rolls, that's the point where you can't keep up the flow and have to climb more methodically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865499#post865499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Weapon Rating description, it says that you add weapon rating &amp;quot;as successe&amp;quot; on a successful attack. Is this an artifact, or should I really apply it as successes, making EX!Successes in combat much more frequent? I never did that before, applying them simply as a &amp;quot;base&amp;quot; damage, and always felt that was the intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exceptional successes in combat don't do anything special, so the difference is pretty academic anyway. The only functional difference that comes to my mind immediately is staking vampires, which requires five successes in a targeted attack to the heart. And weapon damage (such as from Vigor) <i>does</i> count as successes for the purposes of staking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T08:14:19-07:00","id":865509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865506#post865506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is jumping measured in &quot;feet&quot; while every other measurement I could find in meters? Is this a hold over?<br /> <br /> While granted, it's easy to do the simple math of 3 feet equals a meter, this inconsistency does admittedly bother me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's given in both, but I guess &quot;1 foot per success&quot; is a little less clunky-sounding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T08:18:32-07:00","id":865510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865506#post865506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is jumping measured in &amp;quot;feet&amp;quot; while every other measurement I could find in meters? Is this a hold over?<br /> <br /> While granted, it's easy to do the simple math of 3 feet equals a meter, this inconsistency does admittedly bother me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point. Well, success on a jumping action does read &quot;Your character leaps a number of feet equal to the successes rolled, or a number of meters equal to the successes rolled divided by three.&quot; So I would just ignore the first option if it bothers you. As for Parkour, I would just fudge Wall Run to give you 3 meters + 1.5 meters per dot of Athletics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T08:28:03-07:00","id":865514,"title":"","content":"Is there a specific rule or place in the book saying that combat breaks the general rule of EX!Successes allowing you to create a Condition?<br /> As for Wall Running...even with narrative tricks, it feels weird, because it pretty much never makes sense - minimal distance you can Wall Run is 10 feet + 5*2 (as you need 2 in Athletics to even get there), so 20 feet before even having to roll. Which can escalate to 25, 30 and 35 feet. That's 10 meters vertically covered in an instant (well, instant action), with option for rolling if you want to go even higher and climb, which feels...surreal. This made me suspect that somebody either didn't check the numbers, or it was supposed to be something like 10 feet + Athletics dots travelled. <br /> While I don't care about this in the current Chronicle (as it's a asian fantasy game, so a skilled scout wall running a fortified wall without even a roll is certainly ninja-like enough for the genre), I'm kinda worried about it in more standard and less superhuman chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T08:48:45-07:00","id":865520,"title":"","content":"The issue with counting the bonus successes (and that is what they are - they count as such for everything else) for the exceptional success bonus is that some weapons would get an exceptional success with every single successful hit. If you're ok with that, then go for it. &quot;Covered in blood&quot; is a fine condition to apply to someone who just used a chainsaw in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T08:51:48-07:00","id":865522,"title":"","content":"We never added Weapon Rating to successes - we assumed that the goal of the roll is to apply damage = damage rating, and each success increased it by 1. Which is why I was very confused when rereading the weapon rating section. I think I will continue doing that, though now I know it's a home rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T08:53:45-07:00","id":865525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865514#post865514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a specific rule or place in the book saying that combat breaks the general rule of EX!Successes allowing you to create a Condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not specifically, but GMC defined Tilts as a special kind of Condition that applies specifically to combat. Most hits that are exceptional successes would also apply a Tilt, and it seems excessive to apply a Tilt <i>and</i> a normal Condition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865514#post865514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Wall Running...even with narrative tricks, it feels weird, because it pretty much never makes sense - minimal distance you can Wall Run is 10 feet + 5*2 (as you need 2 in Athletics to even get there), so 20 feet before even having to roll. Which can escalate to 25, 30 and 35 feet. That's 10 meters vertically covered in an instant (well, instant action), with option for rolling if you want to go even higher and climb, which feels...surreal. This made me suspect that somebody either didn't check the numbers, or it was supposed to be something like 10 feet + Athletics dots travelled. <br /> While I don't care about this in the current Chronicle (as it's a asian fantasy game, so a skilled scout wall running a fortified wall without even a roll is certainly ninja-like enough for the genre), I'm kinda worried about it in more standard and less superhuman chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div>The amount of time it takes to complete an instant action is also an abstraction. Essentially, Wall Run grants the character a certain distance they can climb without having to make a roll. How exactly the character gets herself up there and how long it takes her to do so is ultimately just a matter of narration and heavily context dependent. How ever you need to describe it to make it feel versimilar for you, describe it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T09:12:17-07:00","id":865536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865522#post865522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We never added Weapon Rating to successes - we assumed that the goal of the roll is to apply damage = damage rating, and each success increased it by 1. Which is why I was very confused when rereading the weapon rating section. I think I will continue doing that, though now I know it's a home rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...you're saying that if you successfully hit somebody, you'd deal [Weapon Rating] damage, and then apply successes on the attack roll as additional damage?<br /> <br /> Because that's how it works in 2E by RAW, though it's worded differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T10:19:51-07:00","id":865568,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's how it works in practice. The difference between &quot;it's base damage&quot; and &quot;it's extra successes&quot; was important for me, because we allow to conjure beneficial Condition on a Ex!Success during combat*, and I planned to introduce a few things that triggered off Ex!Successes in combat - like tilts that downgrade your success rate by one step (Ex!Success into Success, Success into Failure, Failure into Ex!Failure); under the &quot;successes&quot; reading, they would be not near as strong as I want them to be.<br /> I just like to have my homerules neatly organized and tagged as such, to minimize rules discussions during actual play (like that Parkour thing, where my player went o_o after understanding how much she can traverse in a single action; and because it was combat, handwaving it as a really long climb didn't work either).<br /> <br /> *People usually go for Inspired, so they can go &quot;into the Zone&quot; and regain Willpower, and I can usually be talked into a once per Scene Steadfast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T10:41:08-07:00","id":865589,"title":"","content":"You could be nitpicky and say that it is successes, but it only applies after the success level of the roll has already been calculated so it has been locked in already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T11:13:33-07:00","id":865606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865568#post865568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(like that Parkour thing, where my player went o_o after understanding how much she can traverse in a single action; and because it was combat, handwaving it as a really long climb didn't work either).</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's in combat you should still be limited in how far you can go in one turn by your speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T11:19:17-07:00","id":865610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865606#post865606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it's in combat you should still be limited in how far you can go in one turn by your speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>*in any direction except straight down, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T11:26:04-07:00","id":865619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865610#post865610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*in any direction except straight down, obviously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, depends on the medium. We talking straight down through air? Water? Concrete? Jell-O? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T11:27:24-07:00","id":865621,"title":"","content":"That was my gut instinct, but then I figured out that she is basically using Instant Action to move again in a way modified by the Merit, which brought her total movable distance to 28 meters. So enough to get to the wall, wall run in it, and then jump off; not enough Speed to make it a safe jump, so she rolled for falling damage, and due to Parkour being awesome and her Athletics being big, she made it like a cat. Needless to say, her opponents were pretty confused. :P<br /> <br /> ...actually, Wall Run merit references &quot;[ability to climb normally] 10 feet as a Instant Action&quot;. Is it a reference to some Climbing rules? Because it sounds like it's the default state, and merit modifies that default state...but I can't see anything like that in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T11:59:55-07:00","id":865638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865621#post865621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was my gut instinct, but then I figured out that she is basically using Instant Action to move again in a way modified by the Merit, which brought her total movable distance to 28 meters. So enough to get to the wall, wall run in it, and then jump off; not enough Speed to make it a safe jump, so she rolled for falling damage, and due to Parkour being awesome and her Athletics being big, she made it like a cat. Needless to say, her opponents were pretty confused. :P<br /> <br /> ...actually, Wall Run merit references &amp;quot;[ability to climb normally] 10 feet as a Instant Action&amp;quot;. Is it a reference to some Climbing rules? Because it sounds like it's the default state, and merit modifies that default state...but I can't see anything like that in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a legacy reference to the 1e Climbing rules, which are not reproduced in Chronicles:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dice Pool: Strength + Athletics + equipment<br /> Action: Instant or extended (one success is required per 10 feet of height; in an extended task each roll repre- sents one minute of climbing)<br /> Climbing an object requires a number of successes in an instant or extended action. Your character can climb 10 feet with each success rolled. Objects that are 10 feet or less in height can be climbed as an instant action. Rolls may be modified based on the availability of hand- and footholds, sheerness or slipperiness of the slope, and wind conditions, all at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion. By the same token, if the character chooses to take his time and pick his way carefully up the incline, each minute added to the roll provides a +1 modifier, to a maximum of +3. Thus, if a character takes his time and each roll represents three minutes of effort instead of one, a +2 modifier is added to each roll. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-14T21:43:03-07:00","id":865803,"title":"","content":"As strange and anime induced as wall running seems to be, I once saw a documentary (I think it was on the Learning Channel) produced by the Chinese government to promote Chinese culture and history that had a section on the Shaolin monks (apparently there is a troop of them who do demonstrations around the world) and it showed a monk literally run up a wall. Now this wall was maybe ten or twelve feet high but he literally ran up it without using his hands. Now he didn't run straight up it but at an angle like stairs and he wasn't standing perpendicular but parallel to the wall. To put it simply he was using a combination of momentum and whatever traction his feet could gain on the wall to 'climb' it like stairs. Twenty or thirty feet is probably too much to believe but the principle is real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T02:53:16-07:00","id":865861,"title":"","content":"Wall Running definitely is real, it's just that the current world's record is something you beat with the merit automatically - it's 13 feet, and the bare minimum you can wall run with the merit is 20. If it was 10 + Athletics, instead of 10 + 2x Athletics, you would actually start below it, then catch up to it, and finally barely get above it at 4 and 5 dots. That's why I asked if it was a typo. <br /> <br /> Thanks for reminding me of legacy Climbing rules, now I know I'm not crazy! I'm kinda sad that some of these are gone; I wouldn't mind a big blue book focused solely on skills, conditions and tilts, expanding on various things you could possibly do with them, starting with classic combinations (press strength + athletics to jump!) and getting more and more interesting (press athletics + intelligence to plan out a fantastic training routine for your boyfriend!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T03:05:46-07:00","id":865865,"title":"","content":"Maybe the God Machine has an occult matrix that requires everyone proficient at parkour to be unusually good at scaling walls for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T03:23:47-07:00","id":865870,"title":"","content":"Now I can see a complicated sensor-clock-furnace-meter thing, that tracks every wall run meter, and every 42,42 meters it resets, spawning a bunch of biomechanical wall crawling shapeshifting spiders with a side effect of imprinting parkourers personality upon them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T21:11:38-07:00","id":866245,"title":"","content":"Are spears and throwing javelins &quot;Aerodynamic&quot; for the purposes of throwing attacks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T21:49:42-07:00","id":866254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865861#post865861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wall Running definitely is real, it's just that the current world's record is something you beat with the merit automatically - it's 13 feet, and the bare minimum you can wall run with the merit is 20. If it was 10 + Athletics, instead of 10 + 2x Athletics, you would actually start below it, then catch up to it, and finally barely get above it at 4 and 5 dots. That's why I asked if it was a typo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, by the 1e climbing rules, anyone can climb 10 feet as an instant action, as long as they succeed on the roll. Wall Run effectively just gives you that first success automatically (which can be narrated as actual climbing), and adds 2-10 extra feet from the actual wall running part. Still below the world record.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=865861#post865861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for reminding me of legacy Climbing rules, now I know I'm not crazy! I'm kinda sad that some of these are gone; I wouldn't mind a big blue book focused solely on skills, conditions and tilts, expanding on various things you could possibly do with them, starting with classic combinations (press strength + athletics to jump!) and getting more and more interesting (press athletics + intelligence to plan out a fantastic training routine for your boyfriend!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's definitely too bad some of the stuff that had to be left out of CofD from the old core book to make room for new material. Like, we lost some details on things like climbing and example drugs and whatnot, but we gained chases, investigations, and horrors.<br /> <br /> If the word count from God Machine Chronicle appendix could have been traded out for more of the material from the 1e core that didn't make the cut, I would have gladly made that trade. But, I kind of doubt that was ever an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T00:59:16-07:00","id":866305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=866245#post866245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are spears and throwing javelins &quot;Aerodynamic&quot; for the purposes of throwing attacks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. That's what they're for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T05:49:03-07:00","id":866771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=866305#post866305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course. That's what they're for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well javelins are. Spears are a bit too heavy for efficient aerodynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T06:21:25-07:00","id":868363,"title":"","content":"1. Is my deciphering of Feint correct:<br /> You attack. You hit. You can decide to deal no damage in order to enhance your next attack, which ignores Defense equal to Damage the Feint would deal before any kind of reduction, and deals extra Damage equal to Successes rolled on the Feint?<br /> <br /> 1.a When do you declare it? Before you attack, or after your hit is confirmed?<br /> 1.b Would you allow two and more feints of the same person attacking the same target to stack? John Feints Bob in Round 1, then Feints again in Round 2, for a Super Strike in Round 3.<br /> 1.c How much time can expire between Feint and Follow Up Attack? Do they have be in linked turns? Or does it have to &quot;just&quot; be next attack character performs in the Scene?<br /> 1.d Do you have any actual play experience using Feints? Did any of your players purchase the Style and used it? What is your opinion on it and it's usefulness?<br /> <br /> I'm asking because until today I considered it a pretty crappy, but it has found a pretty cool use - character facing heavily armored opponent who was easy to hit but was soaking pretty much any damage. Instead of escaping or switching weapons, the hero decided to start Feinting, and it proved really useful - it allowed to apply damage in one big burst which was reduced by armor only once, instead of negating it every turn, and successfully applied fight tilting tilt.<br /> So now I have someone really excited about whole new world of Feinting, and picturing scenarios like Fist of the North Star with sudden explosions of damage. Or using it as a leverage, which ties directly to question c, as there was a question of &quot;Could I Feint someone into situation where they are going to be hurt really badly if I as much as tap them, and Intimidate them with that prospect so they will stop fighting?&quot;, which I find actually interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-19T07:27:44-07:00","id":868409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=868363#post868363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could I Feint someone into situation where they are going to be hurt really badly if I as much as tap them, and Intimidate them with that prospect so they will stop fighting?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. That's not how feinting works in real life at all, so it shouldn't be how it works here. Feinting is a method of misdirecting your opponent to effectively launch a surprise attack in the middle of a fight. If you stop to point it out then that should ruin the effort you went to to get them off-balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T08:14:34-07:00","id":872379,"title":"","content":"Exactly, a feint is when I twitch my right shoulder to make you think I'm about to throw a jab with my right hand and then I sucker-punch you with my left.<br /> <br /> Edit: A better example is with a sword. A feint is when I fake lunge at your left foot and then slice open your right arm as you try to parry my fake lunge at your left foot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T08:30:36-07:00","id":872386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=868363#post868363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.a When do you declare it? Before you attack, or after your hit is confirmed?<br /> 1.b Would you allow two and more feints of the same person attacking the same target to stack? John Feints Bob in Round 1, then Feints again in Round 2, for a Super Strike in Round 3.<br /> 1.c How much time can expire between Feint and Follow Up Attack? Do they have be in linked turns? Or does it have to &quot;just&quot; be next attack character performs in the Scene?<br /> 1.d Do you have any actual play experience using Feints? Did any of your players purchase the Style and used it? What is your opinion on it and it's usefulness?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I'd rule it:<br /> <br /> 1a. You declare something is a feint before you make the attack roll. A feint is a deliberate action that you have to plan out first.<br /> 1b. Only if the character is able to make multiple attacks or attack rolls per turn. The entire point of a feint is to create a time window where the opponent is distracted. You can't create a distraction and then just prolong it for turn after turn after turn. If you can cram in a lot of attacks in a single round, you can create a greater distraction, so I'd allow them to stack.<br /> 1c. As per the previous point, they need to be in linked turns. Not sure if 2e is maintaining the 1e duration of a turn, but this would mean you need to make your follow-up attack within 3 seconds of the feint.<br /> 1d. One of my players expressed interest in it and we discussed how it'd work in play. He ended up not having enough leftover XP to pick it up, but I assume he'll be picking it up at some point. I myself am considering that style on some of my character concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T08:33:07-07:00","id":872388,"title":"","content":"I'm less interested in being an actual Feint, as I can refluff the manuever to make it make more sense. Also, come on, a Intimidate Feint would be something like that movie thing where you end up with a sword blade touching their throat <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I'm more interested in the rest of the questions, especially practical gameplay experiences, because for some reason until now we only saw half of the Light Weapons in action - 1st dot is sometimes used to dick with initiative (A classic manuever of &quot;I have initative advantage on him? I delay it to be one point behind him, let him attack me, then Thrust for my full Defense pool, and then I use 1st dot to get a point or two of extra initiative, ending up point ahead of him in next turn and going for full Thrust for the kill!&quot;), and 2nd dot is used all the time as a just plain out better All Out Attack. 3rd dot almost never came into play until now, and due to 5th dot being kinda meh, I've seen more &quot;Improvised Weapons 2 + Light Weapons 2&quot; than Light Weapons 3 and more. I wouldn't mind giving that 3rd dot little more bite to make it cool and not a deadweight.<br /> [If someone wonders, no, my games are not combat fests :P I just put a lot of work into combat sections to make them satisfactory when they pop up, and combat subsystem relies a lot on these little things to make it work smooth and fun.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T08:41:24-07:00","id":872398,"title":"","content":"Intimidation would not be a feint. A feint is <i>deception</i>. If you wanted to make a merit that allows you to bluff your opponents by slashing at them with a fake knife (which would have garbage stats, weapon-wise, but looks real enough to make them flinch so that you can suckerpunch them with Brawl), it'd be a Subterfuge roll, not Intimidation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T18:43:14-07:00","id":872790,"title":"","content":"Are there rules anywhere for shoving people?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking just something like fighting at a cliff-side and shoving someone off of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T20:47:59-07:00","id":872851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=872790#post872790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there rules anywhere for shoving people?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking just something like fighting at a cliff-side and shoving someone off of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make it an overpower maneuver over a grapple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T14:18:18-07:00","id":873277,"title":"","content":"Is the total modifier limited to a max of +/-5 or is that the maximum bonus from a single source?<br /> <br /> I ask because I had been taught it was a max of +/-5 to the dice pool period and after reading the section in the book about dice pools I am not certain what I was taught is true by the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:02:24-07:00","id":874632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=872790#post872790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there rules anywhere for shoving people?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking just something like fighting at a cliff-side and shoving someone off of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're surprising them out-of-combat, I'd make it a Down &amp; Dirty Combat roll, with your attack roll against their...I dunno, Strength+Stamina? Strength+Athletics?<br /> <br /> In-combat, yeah, establish a grapple and use the Overpower maneuver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:21:08-07:00","id":874647,"title":"","content":"Those are both awesome answers, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:21:14-07:00","id":874648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=873277#post873277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the total modifier limited to a max of +/-5 or is that the maximum bonus from a single source?<br /> <br /> I ask because I had been taught it was a max of +/-5 to the dice pool period and after reading the section in the book about dice pools I am not certain what I was taught is true by the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the maximum from a single source, but you can stack bonuses to get more than +/-5 on a roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:29:38-07:00","id":875556,"title":"","content":"Huh. I thought that each type of bonus (circumstancial, equipment, etc) maxed out at 5, not 5 per source (so 2 sources of equipment bonus to +6), to avoid equipment arms race.<br /> <br /> Is Investigative Prodigy doing literally nothing if you bought only 1 dot? It seems silly; I think it should allow you to gain Clues equal to 1+merit dots instead of merit dots, or, even simplier, up to one extra Clue per merit dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:21:14-07:00","id":875607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=875556#post875556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh. I thought that each type of bonus (circumstancial, equipment, etc) maxed out at 5, not 5 per source (so 2 sources of equipment bonus to +6), to avoid equipment arms race.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're right. It's not terribly clear in the core rules. Here are a few relevant quotes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 69</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many rolls have modifiers, either from equipment, circumstance, or someone working against your character. Most modifiers are within the range of +3 to -3, though they can range as low as -5 or as high as +5. Apply the modifiers to your dice pool before you roll. Add all the bonuses first, then apply penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div> Later on the same page there's a similar quote about circumstantial modifiers:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 69</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of the time, the modifier from circumstances will be between +3 and \u20133, though in very rare cases \u2014 picking a lock while the room is on fire \u2014 it can range from +5 to \u20135.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between these two quotes, I got the impression that each individual source of bonuses and caps at +/-5, but nothing to suggest stacking bonuses and penalties from different sources couldn't exceed that cap. Later, however, there are some potentially contradictory quotes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 78</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clues can go above the normal +5 limit on dice bonuses; they\u2019re limited only by the character\u2019s Investigation Skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>This quort mentions &quot;the normal +5 limit on dice bonuses&quot; as if that's a thing that's been established, but I couldn't find anything earlier in the rules that actually says such a limit exists. However, in the equipment section (later in the book) it says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>page 100</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most equipment offers a bonus to dice rolls pertaining to its use. Multiple items can influence a given roll, but a roll should not receive more than a +5 bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>From context, it seems to me like this is specifically talking about equipment bonuses. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=875556#post875556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Investigative Prodigy doing literally nothing if you bought only 1 dot? It seems silly; I think it should allow you to gain Clues equal to 1+merit dots instead of merit dots, or, even simplier, up to one extra Clue per merit dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does seem odd. +1 Merit dots does make more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T15:00:11-07:00","id":876019,"title":"","content":"I personally follow a guideline from Building the equipment that suggests to assign non-dice bonuses when you go beyond +5. You know, like small perks; you might have a perfect dress, incredible make up and fantastic dossier on your target, but while first two combine to +5 together and dossier has a value of +3 (so adding it would go beyond 5), I will translate it into stepping up impression level.<br /> Keeps going beyond 5 interesting, and doesn't escalate the arms race into DND levels of &quot;but thou must have level appropiate sword to reliably hit this!&quot;. I like idea of bound accuracy.<br /> <br /> How Dark Eras and other pre-modern settings utilize ballistic armor value? Is there anything interesting written about it, for example a suggestion to use it for something else (like, downgrading weapons attacks to bashing)? I like split of General / Downgrading armor, and I would like to keep it even in games where firearms are not a thing. I feel it adds some granularity without going too deep into armor charts and tables.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T20:23:48-07:00","id":876216,"title":"","content":"You could have ballistic armor apply vs. Archery attacks instead of Firearms attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T17:38:00-07:00","id":877157,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I guess that's one way to do it. I'm still considering doing something like applying it to all attacks, but reducing General armor; this way characters are more likely to end up with their wound track filled with Bashing instead of Lethal, putting them into unconcious and lessening chance of accidentally dying on me. I aim for &quot;fights can be lost, and it will have consequences, but death is unfun&quot;. Unless characters possess some kind of anti-bashing powers (like, regeneration or healing or ignoring them), and Chronicle i plan to use it for won't, it also shouldn't make combat last longer. In fact, it will probably make it last shorter, due to...Pierced Armor being a thing much more often? Huh.<br /> <br /> Another question: how is Killer Instinct from Beast supposed to work? Can you pick one thing multiple times, or are you picking different thing for each merit point?<br /> <br /> And question #2: Bring the Pain penalty checks how much damage you did before any Armor substractions, or after?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-28-2016, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T23:51:58-07:00","id":881559,"title":"","content":"Hey quick question. Lets say someone losses 10-again on a roll for some reason, but they have 9 or 8-again on that same roll. Do they keep the 9 or 8-again quality?<br /> <br /> Also is it allowed to use your Next Instant action to use the dodge action? My player think so, but I'm not so sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T04:08:16-07:00","id":881645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=881559#post881559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey quick question. Lets say someone losses 10-again on a roll for some reason, but they have 9 or 8-again on that same roll. Do they keep the 9 or 8-again quality?<br /> <br /> Also is it allowed to use your Next Instant action to use the dodge action? My player think so, but I'm not so sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I replace it. If you have 9 again but lose 10 again, you keep rolling 10 again and disregard 9 again.<br /> <br /> Hope that wasn't too convoluted an explanation.<br /> <br /> Can you give us an example on the Dodge? Did the character already used his instant action? If so? Nope. No banking actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 05-04-2016, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T05:33:03-07:00","id":881682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=881559#post881559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey quick question. Lets say someone losses 10-again on a roll for some reason, but they have 9 or 8-again on that same roll. Do they keep the 9 or 8-again quality?</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules aren't really clear on this, but personally I would allow them to re-roll 8s or 9s but not 10s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=881559#post881559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also is it allowed to use your Next Instant action to use the dodge action? My player think so, but I'm not so sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your player is correct. The wording in the dodge action is:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At any point before a character\u2019s action, she can choose to Dodge. Doing so takes up her normal action. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T11:31:08-07:00","id":882031,"title":"","content":"I personally consider 10 again, 9 again, 8 again 3 &quot;stages&quot; of the same quality; losing 10 again while you posses 8 again would degrade you to 9 again, and so on. This is however not something stated in the books, just a &quot;logical&quot; homerule.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T12:27:28-07:00","id":882086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=882031#post882031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally consider 10 again, 9 again, 8 again 3 &quot;stages&quot; of the same quality; losing 10 again while you posses 8 again would degrade you to 9 again, and so on. This is however not something stated in the books, just a &quot;logical&quot; homerule.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works fine, and is statistically the same as re-rolling 8s and 9s but not 10s, just changing which numbers you re-roll.<br /> <br /> I also wouldn't object if the ST of a game I was in ruled that the dice tricks build on one another, so that if you lose 10-again you also lose 9 and 8-again. I don't think there's an official rule on this, so what ever works for your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T16:26:48-07:00","id":882337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=881645#post881645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I replace it. If you have 9 again but lose 10 again, you keep rolling 10 again and disregard 9 again.<br /> <br /> Hope that wasn't too convoluted an explanation.<br /> <br /> Can you give us an example on the Dodge? Did the character already used his instant action? If so? Nope. No banking actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>your explanation is just fine its something I've been planing to do in the first place, I just wanted to see if their was an official answer I missed and/or get feed back on it. And you guys have been very helpful on that thank you.<br /> <br /> Also to clarify an example of what he has done is use his instant action to cast a spell, and then when attacked us the dodge action in the same turn. It seemed fair enough sense we had it where he lost his next instant action. But as before I just wanted to an official answer and/or feedback. So thanks for that as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T10:29:59-07:00","id":882987,"title":"","content":"If you get bonus dice or dice tricks (8-again) to Wits, Dexterity, or Athletics, does this bonus also work on a Dodge roll? Or is the Dodge roll a separate derived trait that doesn't get affected?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T17:23:52-07:00","id":883330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=882987#post882987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you get bonus dice or dice tricks (8-again) to Wits, Dexterity, or Athletics, does this bonus also work on a Dodge roll? Or is the Dodge roll a separate derived trait that doesn't get affected?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow them (But not for Wits. You aren't rolling Wits to dodge).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T05:51:43-07:00","id":883673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=883330#post883330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd allow them (But not for Wits. You aren't rolling Wits to dodge).</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Defense the lower of Wits or Dexterity plus Athletics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T06:36:37-07:00","id":883696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=883673#post883673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't Defense the lower of Wits or Dexterity plus Athletics?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It is, so it depends on your character build really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T08:59:58-07:00","id":883828,"title":"","content":"So if you get a dice bonus to Athletics, say from a Tilt or something, does that also affect your Dodge dicepool?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:00:32-07:00","id":883829,"title":"","content":"Also am I interpreting correctly that you get a Beat for resolving any Condition, even positive ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:44:28-07:00","id":883855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=882987#post882987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you get bonus dice or dice tricks (8-again) to Wits, Dexterity, or Athletics, does this bonus also work on a Dodge roll? Or is the Dodge roll a separate derived trait that doesn't get affected?</div> </div> </div> </div> This is how I run it: Defense is a derived trait; rolling Defense is not the same thing as an Athletics, a Wits or a Dexterity roll. Something that gives you bonus dice or X-again/rote to an Athletics roll won't affect your Defense or Dodge rolls. A magic that increases your Wits/Dex or Athletics dots seems to increase your Defense trait, and thus Dodge roll, unless otherwise stated. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=883829#post883829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also am I interpreting correctly that you get a Beat for resolving any Condition, even positive ones?</div> </div> </div> </div> Absolutely. There are ways to hand out Inspired like candy, and then have people resolve it for beats pretty much at whim. Auspex and the Mind Arcana can give it out, as can a merit or two. I'll have to check WtF and CtL as well. The Informed Condition is another popular one I've seen show up a lot.<br /> <br /> Of course, its well within an ST's rights to put a stop to such shinanigans, but its more than possible to do this strictly by the base rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:14:22-07:00","id":883910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ophidimancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=883673#post883673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't Defense the lower of Wits or Dexterity plus Athletics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but to dodge you're rolling Dexterity + Athletics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:17:39-07:00","id":883914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=883855#post883855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll have to check WtF and CtL as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Song in Your Heart merit: Give your whole pack the Inspired (Persistent) condition akin to the Inspiring merit, with it's pre-requisites being only Glory at 2, (bypassing Inspiring's Pre-requisites), apply the Siskur Dah condition and everyone's getting potentially 3 beats every time they score 3 successes or more on a Hunt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T11:52:25-07:00","id":883944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=883910#post883910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but to dodge you're rolling Dexterity + Athletics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm .. that's not what I'm reading. The way it looks to me it takes your Defense and doubles it, then rolls it. It would take your Defense whether it was derived from your Wits or your Dexterity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/avatar/20th%20Anniversary/2013~Mage%20The%20Ascension/img.php?h=120&amp;w=120&amp;img=1~M20.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1018-ophidimancer","name":"Ophidimancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1018_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"596"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T18:00:22-07:00","id":885046,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you are not rolling Dex+Athletics. You are rolling for Dodge. It's its own thing.that has value derived from Defense, which has it's value derived from multiple possible sources which could be Wits, Dexterity, Athletics, Weaponry, Brawl and other defense modifiers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T04:32:13-07:00","id":887073,"title":"","content":"There's a few abilities out there that reduce to the cost of other things. These &quot;cost 1 experience point less, to a minimum of 1 experience point.&quot; Now, what happens when you are buying a Style merit? One dot to five dots, each dot costing one experience point. Does the discount do nothing? Do you get the two dots for the price of one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T04:43:11-07:00","id":887075,"title":"","content":"1) Which abilities are you referring to?<br /> <br /> 2) Make a bulk purchase, then subtract 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T09:51:15-07:00","id":887254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=887073#post887073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a few abilities out there that reduce to the cost of other things. These &amp;quot;cost 1 experience point less, to a minimum of 1 experience point.&amp;quot; Now, what happens when you are buying a Style merit? One dot to five dots, each dot costing one experience point. Does the discount do nothing? Do you get the two dots for the price of one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are these abilities from 1st edition? I assume so, because of the verbiage &quot;experience point&quot; rather than &quot;experience.&quot;<br /> <br /> Note that in the 1st edition version of Professional Training, the third dot reduced the experience point cost of Asset Skills by 1. The 2nd edition version instead gives you a Beat every time you purchase a dot in an Asset Skill. This makes sense, since a 2e experience has five times the purchasing power of a 1e experience point.<br /> <br /> In conclusion, don't reduce the experience costs. Grant Beats for making experience purchases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T13:42:25-07:00","id":887463,"title":"","content":"No, its from 2e. I just paraphrased without quoting directly. It does say experience here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:38:51-07:00","id":887558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=887463#post887463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, its from 2e. I just paraphrased without quoting directly. It does say experience here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, ok. What was the ability?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T16:23:57-07:00","id":887600,"title":"","content":"They're in the Hurt Locker notes and the ones for Secrets of the Covenant. To my knowledge, I think that David A. Hill was experimenting with the concept of it there, but I don't know if those merits made it into the final draft. He might be able to offer some insight here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T19:26:14-07:00","id":887758,"title":"","content":"Where are the rules / Are there rules for running? By a post I saw on the forum it seems like you sacrifice your action. Does this give you 2x speed? <br /> A page number would be also greatly helpful. I've had a player suggest using dnd's version of running ( I think it was 4x) because we could not find the rule in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:11:48-07:00","id":887778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=887758#post887758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A page number would be also greatly helpful. I've had a player suggest using dnd's version of running ( I think it was 4x) because we could not find the rule in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me. Anyone can answer this? <br /> <br /> Running rules. Where do they work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 05-10-2016, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T20:41:23-07:00","id":887802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=887758#post887758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are the rules / Are there rules for running? By a post I saw on the forum it seems like you sacrifice your action. Does this give you 2x speed?<br /> A page number would be also greatly helpful. I've had a player suggest using dnd's version of running ( I think it was 4x) because we could not find the rule in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 92 of the CoD corebook<br /> <br /> Movement<br /> A character can move his Speed in a single turn and still<br /> take an instant action. He can give up his action to move at<br /> double his normal Speed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T21:00:46-07:00","id":887823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=887802#post887802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Page 92 of the CoD corebook<br /> <br /> Movement<br /> A character can move his Speed in a single turn and still<br /> take an instant action. He can give up his action to move at<br /> double his normal Speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much appreciated thank you. Hu, it works like Dnd 5ths dash not 3.5's run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:03:17-07:00","id":888096,"title":"","content":"I do not understand the change from nWoD to chronicle of darkness, I know there are changes but what do these changes entail? is it a shift like frol old to new WoD or is it just an update of the rules? Furthermore how have these changes affected the sourcebooks? There is some big kickstarter project with additions to different playsets like hunter the vigil, but as far as I can see it is basicly a few historical points and then a bunch of covenants, is this the new changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11379-mrimperator","name":"MrImperator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:13:28-07:00","id":888101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrImperator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=888096#post888096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not understand the change from nWoD to chronicle of darkness, I know there are changes but what do these changes entail? is it a shift like frol old to new WoD or is it just an update of the rules? Furthermore how have these changes affected the sourcebooks? There is some big kickstarter project with additions to different playsets like hunter the vigil, but as far as I can see it is basicly a few historical points and then a bunch of covenants, is this the new changes?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's an edition change: Chronicles of Darkness is nWoD second editon. Dark Eras (the big kickstarter project) is a giant historical-play sourcebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:35:20-07:00","id":888119,"title":"","content":"Chronicles of Darkness is the second edition, so there are a lot of changes to the game. You still have the same nine attributes and twenty-one skills, and you still have merits, the same derived traits, and so on. However... the details on how certain merits work is different, the combat subsystem has a number of changes to it, we have new rules for Investigation, Crafting, Social Maneuvering and Chases. Psychic merits, ala Second Sight, are now part of the core book. <br /> <br /> All the books are basically updated - lots of material from older books has been rendered null, or at least redundant. Lots of things clarified. I personally would not suggest using any source book (except for a few suggested in the beginning of the new core books). These books have nothing to do with the Kickstarter project, which is basically like some sourcebooks for the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T15:40:00-07:00","id":906758,"title":"","content":"Where is the maximum penalties or bonuses's sidebar? <br /> <br /> Also, what kinds of penalties or bonuses are exempt from it? I'm thinking Defense might be one of those penalties that are exempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T16:05:00-07:00","id":906770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=906758#post906758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is the maximum penalties or bonuses's sidebar?<br /> <br /> Also, what kinds of penalties or bonuses are exempt from it? I'm thinking Defense might be one of those penalties that are exempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stuff that's based off stats and supernaturally imposed penalties as a rule of thumb. You'll have to find the table on your own because I'm lazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:27:43-07:00","id":906869,"title":"","content":"So with spirits is there anything comparable to a city father spirit from cwod? I get the concept of a powerful spirit of the city's river and a street but is there one lord to rule them all or do all the little bits make up the choir as a whole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T19:21:50-07:00","id":906899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=906869#post906869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with spirits is there anything comparable to a city father spirit from cwod? I get the concept of a powerful spirit of the city's river and a street but is there one lord to rule them all or do all the little bits make up the choir as a whole?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much any concept can and probably does have a spiritual reflection in the Shadow, and that would include cities. It's not really its own special thing though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T20:03:52-07:00","id":906912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=906869#post906869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with spirits is there anything comparable to a city father spirit from cwod? I get the concept of a powerful spirit of the city's river and a street but is there one lord to rule them all or do all the little bits make up the choir as a whole?</div> </div> </div> </div>On non-iconic cities, the most influential spirit is usually given the tittle. On iconic cities with centuries under their belt, the spirit can be easily said to be literally the spirit of the city because it's had the opportunity to consume a large number of things that reflect the city. Think main landmarks eating their way to our collective conscience, and they may take multiple forms. Or be so gigantic that make several avatars, such as NYC's boroughs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T20:56:46-07:00","id":906928,"title":"","content":"While I do not recall any specific City spirits... there is apparently a Spirit for the whole of the USA, so that might count in a weird way...<br /> <br /> <br /> Surprisingly, it's only Rank 4, but that might have to do with the fact it's very unstable due to a mess of collective and contradictory ideologies from centuries of existing and being....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T21:29:44-07:00","id":906949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=906928#post906928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I do not recall any specific City spirits... there is apparently a Spirit for the whole of the USA, so that might count in a weird way...<br /> <br /> <br /> Surprisingly, it's only Rank 4, but that might have to do with the fact it's very unstable due to a mess of collective and contradictory ideologies from centuries of existing and being....</div> </div> </div> </div>Irinam is <i>a </i>spirit of certain aspects of America, not <i>the </i>spirit of America, which would likely be Rank 6 or higher. Similar to Lunes not being Luna.<br /> <br /> The same book that has Irinam also has Lonesome Forest, the spirit of a town that has claimed the entire town, from people to pets to parks. It says if the spirit hadn't spent so much energy absorbing all the other spirits in the town and claiming everything it would likely be Rank 6, which is telling because it's not a huge metropolis. Based on that you could infer that 'town father' spirits are equivalent to Rank 6 providing the town is relevant, while 'city father' spirits may be higher. There tends to be a hierarchy and odds are in a balanced city the leaders of the various choirs are offering up tithes of Essence to the supreme city spirit. The Man Under London, who you might call a suburban spirit, is believed to be the spirit of London's Tube trains, and functions as a minor god at Rank 5. I believe in Dave Brookshaw's Actual Plays the city of Washington DC is heavily divided, giving it effectively two 'patron spirits,' one for each section.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/EdQElQh.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-04-2016, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:25:40-07:00","id":910323,"title":"","content":"This may sound silly, but on here I've seen people talk about 2nd eds I didn't know have come out yet, especially since I kickstarted a couple. Can anyone tell me which 2nd eds have come out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:26:29-07:00","id":910325,"title":"","content":"Demon the Descent and Beast the Primordial, which are technically in their first edition but using Chronicles of Darkness second edition rules. 'Core' Chronicles of Darkness, Vampire the Requiem, Werewolf the Forsaken and Mage the Awakening.<br /> <br /> Promethean and Changeling and Hunter have been announced for second edition and are being worked on. Systems have been leaked by the Changeling developer to give you enough to start playing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-08-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:38:47-07:00","id":910332,"title":"","content":"Adding on to that, Promethean appears to be in the later stages of production, and will likely be the next full splat to be released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:57:16-07:00","id":910338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=910325#post910325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon the Descent and Beast the Primordial, which are technically in their first edition but using Chronicles of Darkness second edition rules. 'Core' Chronicles of Darkness, Vampire the Requiem, Werewolf the Forsaken and Mage the Awakening.<br /> <br /> Promethean and Changeling and Hunter have been announced for second edition and are being worked on. Systems have been leaked by the Changeling developer to give you enough to start playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say it was leaked, so much as previewed. To me, &quot;leak&quot; suggests that something slipped out that wasn't supposed to, and has implications of dubious legality. Changeling drafts were released officially with the hopes that people will playtest them and provide feedback via the survey that was linked to along with them.<br /> <br /> I would also add that while Hunter hasn't gotten a full Second Edition treatment, Mortal Remains included advice for running Hunter using the 2e rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:59:05-07:00","id":910339,"title":"","content":"Thank You for the speedy reply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T17:16:03-07:00","id":910412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=910338#post910338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't say it was leaked, so much as previewed. To me, &quot;leak&quot; suggests that something slipped out that wasn't supposed to, and has implications of dubious legality. Changeling drafts were released officially with the hopes that people will playtest them and provide feedback via the survey that was linked to along with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I couldn't think of a good word for it, preview seems more like a glimpse or sneak peek, which I guess is appropriate. Fully authorized preview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T17:38:02-07:00","id":910427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=910412#post910412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah I couldn't think of a good word for it, preview seems more like a glimpse or sneak peek, which I guess is appropriate. Fully authorized preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoiler might be another good word for it. Anyway, sorry to be nitpicky about word choice, normally I wouldn't have corrected you, but I didn't want 3Comrades to get the wrong idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T19:27:12-07:00","id":924729,"title":"","content":"Are there any spirits or goetia or ghosts or hobgoblins that exist on multiple otherworlds simultaneously, or can call more than one &quot;home&quot; with equal sincerity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T19:50:07-07:00","id":924738,"title":"","content":"Wound-spirits seem to be at home in the Shadow while the Inferno is their 'true' home. Presumably demonic ghosts have a similar relationship with the Underworld. I thought there were spirits of death and such in the Underworld but it doesn't look like it. Pangaeans seemed at home in multiple worlds, arguably idigam too.<br /> <br /> Werewolves, of course, find both to be a home away from home. I'd guess Sin-Eaters were like that in the Underworld. But you probably aren't counting earth as an otherworld.<br /> <br /> Angels are made by the God Machine for a specific purpose, so it's possible one was made to be at home in multiple worlds. But most creature 'lines' seem to stick to one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-01-2016, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T03:46:26-07:00","id":929644,"title":"","content":"Is 'rote action' a step after '8-Again' or I can combine them? Are they exclusive?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T05:41:27-07:00","id":929672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=929644#post929644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is 'rote action' a step after '8-Again' or I can combine them? Are they exclusive?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not exclusive or related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T06:10:53-07:00","id":929677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=929672#post929672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are not exclusive or related.</div> </div> </div> </div>It basically doubles your pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T13:07:46-07:00","id":929922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=929677#post929677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It basically doubles your pool.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. The mechanics still aren't exclusive from each other, or mechanically related to each other (as 8-again is to 9-again and 10-again).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T23:16:32-07:00","id":930195,"title":"","content":"The rerolls from &quot;rote&quot; happen AFTER you've done the initial roll, but BEFORE you roll explodes. Failures on explodes don't get rerolled, everything that wasn't a reroll though gets rerolled.<br /> <br /> As he said, it basically doubles your dice pool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/873174-dragon-rekindled-the-orobori-chronicles-embers-reboot#post873174\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Dragon Rekindled: The Oroboroi Chronicles.</b></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#696969\">The official reboot of <b>Dragon: The Embers</b>.</span></span></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10120-rockstarraccoon","name":"RockstarRaccoon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10120_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T19:03:56-07:00","id":931135,"title":"","content":"Any particular reason why Ghosts outside of the Underworld may not progress beyond Rank 2? I assume that it's something Geist related; if I don't own Geist, don't play on owning and incorporating it into my games, is there anything that will stop working if this limitation is lifted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-13-2016, 10:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T19:50:03-07:00","id":931148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=931135#post931135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any particular reason why Ghosts outside of the Underworld may not progress beyond Rank 2? I assume that it's something Geist related; if I don't own Geist, don't play on owning and incorporating it into my games, is there anything that will stop working if this limitation is lifted?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anything breaks if you change it, but I think it has to do with ghosts generally remaining 'static' until the Underworld begins to change them. So a ghost gets created at rank 1 or rank 2 usually, then if it loses all its anchors or is sent to the Underworld via some other means, the ambient energies and weirdness of the Underworld begin to twist them into something other, mechanically akin to gaining Rank.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are static by default, and when you introduce Change into them, it tends to warp them into something Other, that kinda thing, y'know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T20:09:21-07:00","id":931157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=931135#post931135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any particular reason why Ghosts outside of the Underworld may not progress beyond Rank 2? I assume that it's something Geist related; if I don't own Geist, don't play on owning and incorporating it into my games, is there anything that will stop working if this limitation is lifted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts are effectively Underworld natives distracted from their &quot;natural&quot; roles by business in the land of the living.<br /> <br /> A lot of Ghost and Underworld Stuff is implicitly in an unclear level of flux where it hasn't just plain not been covered, but assuming that elements which fit with larger trends in setting metaphysics will carry over into 2e, more powerful ghosts are more likely to have lost interest in or lost influence over the mortal realm, in addition to often having gotten too weird to be recognizably the people they resemble.<br /> <br /> That last part arguably has the biggest impact on removing the hobble; when things that run on memory get weirder without having to spend time in weirder parts of the cosmology, something has to be done to account for the state of ghostly Twilight. The Underworld is where Ghost Stuff gets really otherworldly in the existing setup and if you let ghosts reach that point without extended leave of absence you need an explanation for how and why it happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T21:08:41-07:00","id":931173,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. We don't own any Underworld-mapping product (it would be Geist and Book of the Dead, right?), so we might shift the Ghost Focus from Underworld to material world, simply due to the lack of materials (and the fact that we don't play in games that do a lot of world-jumping).<br /> So I guess that Ghosts that would evolve past Rank 2 would become more and more removed from their original form, and would have to find more and more twisted ways to feed, being less and less sustainable by being remembered as their living counterpart? I kinda like where it might go. What kind of feeding methods would you suggest for these grotesque twisted ghosts?<br /> I mean, we could just leave them capped at Rank 2, but that feels like a waste of potential due to the fact that Underworld probably won't be a thing.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> Hm. Ghosts require 1 Essence per day to function, and regain 1 Essence by being near their Anchors. So they get just enough to exist if they never spend anything. <br /> They can regain it by either being remembered and recognized, or by eating other Ghosts. First one isn't really what we are aiming at, and second one is hard, unless you are anchored to a place with a lot of other Ghosts; then you eat their Essence, let them hibernate for two days, and eat them again. Unless you beat up their Corpus, they won't become permanently destroyed.<br /> Huh. So pretty much, your best option without adding another feeding method is to lure mortals into your lair, traumatize them to death in order to make them spawn a Ghost, then proceed to create your own farm of Ghosts using the above method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-14-2016, 12:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:01:20-07:00","id":934354,"title":"","content":"Can I spend Willpower and apply dice tricks from Conditions to a Clash of Wills? I tried but cannot find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 07-20-2016, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T14:22:20-07:00","id":934702,"title":"","content":"Guys. Help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T14:55:14-07:00","id":934720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=934354#post934354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I spend Willpower and apply dice tricks from Conditions to a Clash of Wills? I tried but cannot find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. As long as it makes sense for the Clash of Wills to benefit from the Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T20:32:16-07:00","id":934878,"title":"","content":"Note that the &quot;usual suspects&quot; Conditions that tend to tilt the balance of supernatural powers, Steadfast and Informed, don't actually do much for Clash of Wills - they turn your 0 successes into 1 success. In contested roll, this will help you literally only when your opponent also rolled 0 successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T01:46:57-07:00","id":934963,"title":"","content":"Thats right, but if you can spend WP and Conditions on it that means that certain mages are actually immune to CoW if prepared. With Prime I'd say that you can craft condition that adds spell potency to a cartain number of CoW rolls. And make it 8-Again. Mind can make WP point to add 5 or 6 dices instead of 3.<br /> Thats cool but I wanted to be sure. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T07:28:46-07:00","id":935049,"title":"","content":"There no such spells currently as written. If you are afraid that it would make Arcana unbalanced by making Prime too strong, then give every Arcanum ability to boost CoWing things under their subject (so Death spell could help you to win CoWs involving your Death Magic, and Prime would let you help any kind of magic); personally, I wouldn't allow these spells to directly add to CoW roll, but would make them turn target spell into virtually more Duration-y. This way, there is always a maximum ceiling for CoW bonuses, even if you are a super duper wizard.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T09:42:45-07:00","id":935101,"title":"","content":"There's no such spells as written but 2ed is all about creative thaumaturgy. Although I dont think that it makes Prime too strong I like the idea of &quot;virtual duration&quot;. Thats cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T21:49:14-07:00","id":936921,"title":"","content":"This is a Changeling simple question, but I don't see a simple questions thread on the Changeling board, so hopefully someone here can help! Where is there material published on Huntsmen-- who they are, what they do and why? I've looked at all the open development stuff I can find and I'm coming up empty. Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T23:21:32-07:00","id":936956,"title":"","content":"A write up on the Huntsman was posted here. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/805704-meet-the-huntsmen\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...t-the-huntsmen</a><br /> <br /> The doc itself. <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoXzJKNkVaSzlvMFU/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K...VaSzlvMFU/view</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T19:54:25-07:00","id":938527,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Simple question, hoping for a simple answer. Has anyone developed a fighting style, or some sort of system, for counter-attacks?<br /> <br /> Note, still playing 1E and only have had access to original Armory book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T19:57:57-07:00","id":938529,"title":"","content":"2nd E core fighting styles have a lot of counter like mechanics - for example, light/heavy/kung fu styles all have one manuever dedicated to punishing enemies that end their round next to you, which could be easily flavored as countering attacks. <br /> There are also defensive styles, that enhance dodging; one of them literally makes you roll a Brawl+Strength pool instead of Dodge pool to check if you countered your opponent. These styles are your best bet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T12:37:39-07:00","id":939043,"title":"","content":"Once two Characters are Grappling they both roll Strength + Brawl vs Strength + Brawl as a Contested Action.<br /> <br /> My Question is Say Character A rolled 4 Successes and Character B Rolled 5 Success....<br /> <br /> Did Character B win the Grapple Contest for the Round with 1 Success or with 5 Successes?<br /> <br /> If Character B decides to use a Damage Maneuver will Character B inflict 1 Bashing, or 5 Bashing and have the opportunity to apply a second Maneuver?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T12:54:01-07:00","id":939054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=939043#post939043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once two Characters are Grappling they both roll Strength + Brawl vs Strength + Brawl as a Contested Action.<br /> <br /> My Question is Say Character A rolled 4 Successes and Character B Rolled 5 Success....<br /> <br /> Did Character B win the Grapple Contest for the Round with 1 Success or with 5 Successes?<br /> <br /> If Character B decides to use a Damage Maneuver will Character B inflict 1 Bashing, or 5 Bashing and have the opportunity to apply a second Maneuver?</div> </div> </div> </div>There has been some discussion about this on the Requiem forum lately. The answer, by the book, is that character B got 5 successes and won the Contested action, so they can choose two Maneuvers. If they choose the Damage Maneuver as one of the two Maneuvers, character A will take 5 bashing damage (or 5 lethal + Weapon damage if character B also chooses the Control Weapon Maneuver).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:11:45-07:00","id":971591,"title":"","content":"What's the functional difference between a story and a chronicle, exactly? I get that several Scenes make up a Chapter (which is a game session), but is a Story a major plot arc or the full campaign/Chronicle?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:47:58-07:00","id":971607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=971591#post971591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the functional difference between a story and a chronicle, exactly? I get that several Scenes make up a Chapter (which is a game session), but is a Story a major plot arc or the full campaign/Chronicle?</div> </div> </div> </div>What D&amp;D calls an adventure, CofD calls a story. What D&amp;D calls a campaign (or sometimes an adventure path), CofD calls a chronicle.<br /> <br /> To borrow The Angry GM's definition, <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u201cAn adventure is the smallest segment of a role-playing game that can be considered a complete and satisfying story.\u201d and, &quot;[A campaign is] </span></span><span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">A series of adventures connected together by common characters, a common setting, and a common narrative or plot.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:30:58-07:00","id":971750,"title":"","content":"A major plot arc is a decent example for a story. A story should have a beginning, a middle, and an end. A chronicle is the whole thing so it ends when you're done with the characters. It begins and ends with the chronicle being everything between. To use a movie example, The Lord of the Rings trilogy is a story that is part of a chronicle including the Hobbit movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:04:21-07:00","id":971763,"title":"","content":"Can a Ghost/Spirit/Angel inflict damage using an Influence, or is that strictly reserved for the Blast Numina?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7951-taroh","name":"Taroh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:05:57-07:00","id":971765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=971750#post971750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A major plot arc is a decent example for a story.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be, but plot arcs can also span multiple stories. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=971750#post971750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A story should have a beginning, a middle, and an end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good advice for writing, but for RPGs specifically, I find it more useful to say that a story/adventure should have a motivation, a structure, and a resolution. The beginning, middle, and end are what happen when player characters interact with the afformentioned elements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=971750#post971750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A chronicle is the whole thing so it ends when you're done with the characters. It begins and ends with the chronicle being everything between. To use a movie example, The Lord of the Rings trilogy is a story that is part of a chronicle including the Hobbit movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. You can run multiple chronicles/campaigns in the same setting and/or involving the same characters, as long as they have different overarching narratives. To use another beloved film series as an example, look at Star Wars. Each Star Wars film is a compete story, including a beginning, a middle, and an end, and each stands on its own as a narrative experience. They had to, with three years between each film - if New Hope hadn't been satisfying outside the context of the trilogy, no one would have come back for Empire, especially not after such a long wait. The trilogy overall is a complete chronicle. It tells a series of stories about the same set of characters in the same setting, connected by a common narrative - the Rebels' struggle against the Empire.<br /> <br /> The prequel trilogy is another Chronicle in the same setting, involving many of the same characters, but with a different narrative - Anakin's fall to the Dark Side. The individual films were complete stories, as well. Less well-written stories than their predecessors, but complete stories nonetheless. The new trilogy is yet another chronicle set in the same universe, which brings back many of the characters from the previous two chronicles, but features another new narrative. And then there are the side films that are coming out. Standalone stories in the same setting, but starring different characters and featuring different narratives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-18-2016, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:07:11-07:00","id":971766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taroh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=971763#post971763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Ghost/Spirit/Angel inflict damage using an Influence, or is that strictly reserved for the Blast Numina?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can, they might just have to get creative about it. For example, Influence 4 (Fire) can make fire. Fire does damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:14:33-07:00","id":971820,"title":"","content":"Question: What can the numbing touch merit do? It says it messes with its victim's sensory perception, and manual dexterity. So If someone swings a punch will they suffer penalties? What about defense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:43:05-07:00","id":971836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=971820#post971820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: What can the numbing touch merit do? It says it messes with its victim's sensory perception, and manual dexterity. So If someone swings a punch will they suffer penalties? What about defense?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Having your manual dexterity screwed with inhibit throwing a punch I'd think, same with the natural ducks, dodges and general steppings out of the way that defence represents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T03:14:45-07:00","id":971853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=971766#post971766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can, they might just have to get creative about it. For example, Influence 4 (Fire) can make fire. Fire does damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Influence: Puppies is just as brutal.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.smbc-comics.com/?id=499\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.smbc-comics.com/comics/20060608.gif\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.smbc-comics.com/?id=499\" target=\"_blank\"> Saturday Morning Breakfast Cereal - 2006-06-08 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.smbc-comics.com/?id=499\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.smbc-comics.com/?id=499 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Saturday Morning Breakfast Cereal - 2006-06-08 </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:27:18-07:00","id":972164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=971765#post971765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can be, but plot arcs can also span multiple stories.<br /> <br /> <br /> Good advice for writing, but for RPGs specifically, I find it more useful to say that a story/adventure should have a motivation, a structure, and a resolution. The beginning, middle, and end are what happen when player characters interact with the afformentioned elements.<br /> <br /> <br /> I disagree. You can run multiple chronicles/campaigns in the same setting and/or involving the same characters, as long as they have different overarching narratives. To use another beloved film series as an example, look at Star Wars. Each Star Wars film is a compete story, including a beginning, a middle, and an end, and each stands on its own as a narrative experience. They had to, with three years between each film - if New Hope hadn't been satisfying outside the context of the trilogy, no one would have come back for Empire, especially not after such a long wait. The trilogy overall is a complete chronicle. It tells a series of stories about the same set of characters in the same setting, connected by a common narrative - the Rebels' struggle against the Empire.<br /> <br /> The prequel trilogy is another Chronicle in the same setting, involving many of the same characters, but with a different narrative - Anakin's fall to the Dark Side. The individual films were complete stories, as well. Less well-written stories than their predecessors, but complete stories nonetheless. The new trilogy is yet another chronicle set in the same universe, which brings back many of the characters from the previous two chronicles, but features another new narrative. And then there are the side films that are coming out. Standalone stories in the same setting, but starring different characters and featuring different narratives.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is no disagreement. Each Star Wars movie could be considered a story, technically not a chronicle because they keep making more. Each trilogy could be considered a story or a chronicle. All three trilogies together could be considered a chronicle as well. Story is specific but somewhat arbitrary. Chronicle is vague and arbitrary. When you call it over that is the chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChroniclesOfDarkness2e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Story \u2014 A story tells an entire tale, following the dramatic arc of a related series of events. It might be comprised of several chapters or be completed in just one. It has an introduction, rising tension, a number of twists, and a climax that brings things to a conclusion. <br /> \u2022 Chronicle \u2014 The big picture; a chronicle is the collection of interlinked stories that involve your characters. They might be linked by a common theme or overarching plotline, or they may only share characters and locations. As your story progresses, the players and Storyteller work together to create an ongoing chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>A rigid definition won't fit all possibilities. Technically, the Tolkien stuff is one chronicle and all the Star Wars movies are one chronicle and the MCU is one chronicle. They are so massive they likely would never be completed as a gaming experience so that is a logical problem with the example. As a game, a trilogy is probably as big as a chronicle could reasonably get. People would want to move on, that is when the chronicle ends. Basically, it ends when you want it to end. Not possible to define a subjective experience in objective terms. You give an example, I give an example. I don't know if that creates less confusion or more, but the point should still be clear that a Chronicle is what a group makes of it. No rule requires a Chronicle to have more than one story or less than a 1000 stories. Your D&amp;D example was fine but I don't know who is familiar. Beyond that, imprecision is a certainty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:01:12-07:00","id":972184,"title":"","content":"Ask a simple question, get an answer that spans two pages. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T16:49:12-07:00","id":972206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=972164#post972164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no disagreement. Each Star Wars movie could be considered a story, technically not a chronicle because they keep making more. Each trilogy could be considered a story or a chronicle. All three trilogies together could be considered a chronicle as well. Story is specific but somewhat arbitrary. Chronicle is vague and arbitrary. When you call it over that is the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there is disagreement. I would not describe any Star Wars trilogy as a story. They are chronicles, made up of multiple complete stories. A story is the smallest unit of the game that can be considered a complete and satisfying narrative experience on its own. If your narrative spans multiple units of complete satisfying sub-narratives, it's not a story, it's a chronicle made up of multiple stories.<br /> <br /> I would also not describe the trillogies together a single chronicle (or story) because although they share common characters and common settings, they do not share common narratives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=972164#post972164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A rigid definition won't fit all possibilities. Technically, the Tolkien stuff is one chronicle and all the Star Wars movies are one chronicle and the MCU is one chronicle. They are so massive they likely would never be completed as a gaming experience so that is a logical problem with the example. As a game, a trilogy is probably as big as a chronicle could reasonably get. People would want to move on, that is when the chronicle ends. Basically, it ends when you want it to end. Not possible to define a subjective experience in objective terms. You give an example, I give an example. I don't know if that creates less confusion or more, but the point should still be clear that a Chronicle is what a group makes of it. No rule requires a Chronicle to have more than one story or less than a 1000 stories. Your D&amp;D example was fine but I don't know who is familiar. Beyond that, imprecision is a certainty.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I would argue that a definition that tries to fit all possibilities isn't a useful definition. If &quot;story&quot; and &quot;chronicle&quot; don't mean specific, different things, then they don't help us describe the divisions between different levels of narrative structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T23:11:26-07:00","id":972955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=972206#post972206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, there is disagreement. I would not describe any Star Wars trilogy as a story. They are chronicles, made up of multiple complete stories. A story is the smallest unit of the game that can be considered a complete and satisfying narrative experience on its own. If your narrative spans multiple units of complete satisfying sub-narratives, it's not a story, it's a chronicle made up of multiple stories.<br /> <br /> I would also not describe the trillogies together a single chronicle (or story) because although they share common characters and common settings, they do not share common narratives.<br /> <br /> <br /> See, I would argue that a definition that tries to fit all possibilities isn't a useful definition. If &quot;story&quot; and &quot;chronicle&quot; don't mean specific, different things, then they don't help us describe the divisions between different levels of narrative structure.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Difference of opinion. A completely subjective statement, also known as an opinion, can't be judged as wrong even if it is considered not right unless you are saying the opinion is invalid. When you disagree with an opinion, you would actually be telling a person they have no right to express that opinion.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I strictly interpret the definitions given so I will not add that a story must be the smallest unit that fits the definition into the definition of a story. The definition of a chronicle includes only sharing characters and locations, but there is a shared theme in all Star Wars movies. The theme is finding balance in the Force. Prequel trilogy has the Force shift to Dark Side dominant. Original trilogy shifts back to Light. Latest trilogy is a work in progress but so far is consistent with the Star Wars theme. You could take the Force out of Star Wars to tell the same stories but it wouldn't be Star Wars anymore. The stories might be just as good, just not Star Wars. We may differ though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sorry but developers are not the only people that think words have meanings that should be respected. Disagreement and difference of opinion are not interchangeable. I seldom get offended by someone expressing an opinion different from my own, but if I say &quot;I like the color blue&quot; and someone says &quot;no because blue is not a likable color&quot; then I will want to slap someone.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 09-20-2016, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T00:03:34-07:00","id":972973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=972955#post972955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Difference of opinion. A completely subjective statement, also known as an opinion, can't be judged as wrong even if it is considered not right unless you are saying the opinion is invalid. When you disagree with an opinion, you would actually be telling a person they have no right to express that opinion.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Umm... Difference of opinion is <i>literally</i> one of the dictionary definitions of the word disagree. You have the right to express what ever opinion you want, that doesn't mean I have to agree with your opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=972955#post972955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">I strictly interpret the definitions given so I will not add that a story must be the smallest unit that fits the definition into the definition of a story. The definition of a chronicle includes only sharing characters and locations, but there is a shared theme in all Star Wars movies. The theme is finding balance in the Force. Prequel trilogy has the Force shift to Dark Side dominant. Original trilogy shifts back to Light. Latest trilogy is a work in progress but so far is consistent with the Star Wars theme. You could take the Force out of Star Wars to tell the same stories but it wouldn't be Star Wars anymore. The stories might be just as good, just not Star Wars. We may differ though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><br /> *Shrug* sorry, I don't think your definition is useful. Use it if you like, but I'm not going to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=972955#post972955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry but developers are not the only people that think words have meanings that should be respected. Disagreement and difference of opinion are not interchangeable. I seldom get offended by someone expressing an opinion different from my own, but if I say &quot;I like the color blue&quot; and someone says &quot;no because blue is not a likable color&quot; then I will want to slap someone.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> Words having meanings that should be respected is the reason I use the strict definitions I do. And, as established above, &quot;to have a difference of opinion&quot; is absolutely one of the dictionary definitions of &quot;disagree&quot;. So, I can't help but feel like I'm not the one who isn't respecting word meanings in this conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T02:38:47-07:00","id":973006,"title":"","content":"Is there a Willpower cap in the 2E RAW? <br /> <br /> I know Ephemerals cap out at 10 WP, but I'm playing a character with a temporary value of 10 in resolve and 12 in Composure. Not sure if that caps out at 10, or goes straight to 22.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]}