:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:03:31-07:00","id":979579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=979564#post979564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Piggybacking, what should the availability of non-basic housing be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that represented with merits?<br /> I'm probably mistaken.<br /> Thinking about it now, the resources merit might be a good way to extrapolate the availability of either of these.<br /> Now I gotta go car shopping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","user":"Yelesom","date":". 10-01-2016, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T05:16:36-07:00","id":979601,"title":"","content":"Does anywhere cover what happens when you tie a contested roll? Clash of Wills in some books says you roll again until there's a winner; is this always the case for contested rolls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:23:13-07:00","id":979643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=979601#post979601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anywhere cover what happens when you tie a contested roll? Clash of Wills in some books says you roll again until there's a winner; is this always the case for contested rolls?</div> </div> </div> </div>Contested rolls default to the defender, iirc. Trying to find the source now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T07:39:37-07:00","id":979650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=979564#post979564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Piggybacking, what should the availability of non-basic housing be?</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by non-basic housing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T09:34:46-07:00","id":979722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=979643#post979643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contested rolls default to the defender, iirc. Trying to find the source now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they cover it explicitly in 2e. Though, despite common thought otherwise, the default in 1e was you rerolled ties unless an action says otherwise (Many supernatural powers explicitly put ties in the failure category, for instance). So, by RAW, it's 'ST decides' unless they add it to the FAQ, I believe. I could be wrong and just missed it, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T12:07:24-07:00","id":979789,"title":"","content":"World of Darkness core, first edition, p130, 'If it\u2019s a tie or neither side gets any successes, the effort fails altogether or successive at tempts (see p. 132) may be made in subsequent turns, if appropriate. The Storyteller decides if the effort can be attempted over and over until one competitor wins. If both try to grab a fish that swims downstream, they both probably have only one chance before the fish is gone. If one tries to hack into another\u2019s computer, the effort might persist as long as the intruder likes or until fail-safes shut him out. If either side of a contested roll gets a dramatic failure, he either fails utterly or his opponent automatically achieves the equivalent of an exceptional success.'<br /> <br /> For vehicle Availability, since Availability is basically cost,you can just use cost. First edition had them splashed across the books, I'm not sure if they're going to come up in second, where it's assumed everyone has a vehicle or access to one. <a href=\"http://wodcodex.com/wiki/Vehicles_(1st_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Here's the first edition costs for vehicles</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T23:13:28-07:00","id":980123,"title":"","content":"Opinion question: What Skill would you use to win a skill-based strategy game like chess or Go? Maybe Politics? I like the idea that knowing group dynamics would be helpful. Or like, Intelligence plus a Social Skill to manipulate your opponent. In a Dark Eras games I might use Enigmas or Warfare.<br /> <br /> Maybe it would be best to run it as a sort of Mental Chase.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T23:20:39-07:00","id":980125,"title":"","content":"Empathy, to read the motivations of your opponent, or Subterfuge to hide your own, perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T23:33:13-07:00","id":980130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=980123#post980123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opinion question: What Skill would you use to win a skill-based strategy game like chess or Go? Maybe Politics? I like the idea that knowing group dynamics would be helpful. Or like, Intelligence plus a Social Skill to manipulate your opponent. In a Dark Eras games I might use Enigmas or Warfare.<br /> <br /> Maybe it would be best to run it as a sort of Mental Chase.</div> </div> </div> </div>A strictly strategy game would probably be Intelligence or Wits + Academics or Investigation, depending on the exact game and the methodology. Things like social rolls or the like probably would be additional rolls you could make to provide bonuses or penalties; Wits + Empathy might give you a +2 to your roll because you can guess what they'll do, and Manipulation + Subterfuge might let you give off a false impression of your plans (or cheat). It'd probably be an extended, contested sort of roll otherwise, with specific ways of accruing bonuses or penalties and deciding target numbers again depending on the game.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I do agree in a Dark Eras game Enigmas or Warfare would be very appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T03:25:38-07:00","id":980184,"title":"","content":"Changeling 1e puts playing games as an Attribute task using Intelligence + Composure, if you want to use that.<br /> <br /> Winter Masques page 97. It leans towards gambling games, but one of the examples is Chess.<br /> <br /> Attribute tasks are pretty explicitly for rolls that don't have an associated skill, though a lot of people don't like using them. It's understandable, given some games really are pretty skill-based, but there you have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T09:59:39-07:00","id":980314,"title":"","content":"It depends very much on the game. Bluffing games like poker I would say Composure + Subterfuge to bluff or Wits + Empathy to call a bluff. Strategy games like chess or go would probably be Intelligence + Composure, but if the character has studied the game and its strategy extensively I'd definitely allow Intelligence + Academics. Reflex games like War, I'd go with Dexterity + Composure. Cooperative games like Arkham, maybe Wits + Socialize. It's all very context-dependent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T08:47:28-07:00","id":984898,"title":"","content":"OK, question about Princesses:the Hopeful. There is a Princess who are high-school Lovable Alpha Bitch. She found out that some of her classmates get severely bulled by a clique of just Alpha Bitches (bulling is bad enough for suicide is not excluded). The Princess defeat the clique with gossip, provocations, manipulations and blackmail. Who this Princess could be and which is her Court (I think, Air, may be)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T03:39:50-07:00","id":990884,"title":"","content":"Maybe not a simple question, but in that case you can resend me in right direction.<br /> How you understate shooting penalty?<br /> Even when your cover is 3/4 (Head-sholders figure) enemy receive only -3 (yes, if he wont hit head itself he need add -3 for head). It's understandable - simplification is our all.<br /> But when it come for long range i lose the logic. When you need to hit fullheight target on fourth distant your mighty dicepool of 6 (from 8) reduced to zero. Even if you are sniper (my starter one can accumulate in aiming up to +7 dices).<br /> Do i understand correctly, that distants penalty sacrificed for sake of hitting target (and hitting specific part of target)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T07:48:37-07:00","id":990954,"title":"","content":"I'm having trouble understanding your question. Do you want to know why firearms attacks suffer penalties at greater distances?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T08:41:31-07:00","id":990978,"title":"","content":"I wont to know why at medium and long distances penalty so small, it is considered that they are not, and at greater distances become almost impossible regardless of the circumstances?<br /> I have home rule, where I use &quot;realistic&quot; model with a quadratic dispersion. But it seems to use home rule without understanding, why the authors (which has more than 20 years digest this system) left in this form, are misdeal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T08:58:42-07:00","id":990984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=990978#post990978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wont to know why at medium and long distances penalty so small, it is considered that they are not, and at greater distances become almost impossible regardless of the circumstances?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to keep it simple and easy to manage. At close range you take no penalty, at medium you take -1, and at long you take -2; it's easy to remember, easy to use, and gets the idea across that shots at a greater distance are harder to make accurately. Beyond a weapon's long range, it's a chance die, because a gun can only shoot a bullet as far as it can shoot it. Beyond that range, you'd be lucky to hit anything you were aiming for.<br /> <br /> The ranges themselves aren't the most realistic, nor is the difficulty curve, but it works well enough to use without slowing down play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=990978#post990978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have home rule, where I use &quot;realistic&quot; model with a quadratic dispersion. But it seems to use home rule without understanding, why the authors (which has more than 20 years digest this system) left in this form, are misdeal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quadratic dispersion sounds like way more math than I want to have to do every time a character makes an attack with a firearm. Even if you put it in a table for reference, I'd still have to look it up, which slows down play. Conventional wisdom in RPG design says ease of use is more important than realism.<br /> <br /> That all said, I do prefer the way Range Bands work in the Hurt Locker preview more than the default. Instead of different weapons having different close/medium/long ranges, range bands are the same for any weapon. The penalty for hitting a target at 100 yards is the same no matter what gun you're using unless it has a scope. The only thing the weapon itself affects is its maximum range - the point after which you always use a chance die, because the gun can't fire a bullet further than it can fire a bullet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-21-2016, 12:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T09:41:18-07:00","id":990993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=990984#post990984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to keep it simple and easy to manage.<br /> -//-<br /> Conventional wisdom in RPG design says ease of use is more important than realism.</div> </div> </div> </div> As I thought.<br /> It just looks as if a character hit for sure - roll decides only the amount of damage.<br /> But thank you anyway.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=990984#post990984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quadratic dispersion sounds like way more math than I want to have</div> </div> </div> </div> Not so scary as named. just twice as penalty for each same length segment. For example, light revolver -1/-2/-4/-8/-16 for 20+/40+/60+/80+/100+.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:20:24-07:00","id":991220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=990993#post990993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just looks as if a character hit for sure - roll decides only the amount of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hitting is more common than missing, biasing action scenes towards having dangerous shit happen rather than not, but (especially in the second edition rules, where weapon ratings don't add bonus dice) target number 8 on 10-sided dice means it's still not unheard of to get a flat failure, even with a pretty solid dice pool. So a one or two die penalty can still have a significant impact on a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:36:28-07:00","id":998754,"title":"","content":"With targeted melee attacks is it still minus defence then minus target modifyer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11719-mutedmirth","name":"MutedMirth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T07:37:44-07:00","id":998757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MutedMirth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=998754#post998754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With targeted melee attacks is it still minus defence then minus target modifyer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T03:24:37-08:00","id":999140,"title":"","content":"In Psychokinesis merit written that you need spend Will to <i>activate </i>ability. I dont really understand: per scene or per use?<br /> And if per use, how to describe &quot;Paper master&quot; (Read or die), where characters create sharp weapon from paper. As far as I understand, you cand spend the success of the roll in order for paper to harden (and become weapon). However, it is not clear how long such weapons can exist? Success on round? Scene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T04:35:37-08:00","id":999156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=999140#post999140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Psychokinesis merit written that you need spend Will to <i>activate </i>ability. I dont really understand: per scene or per use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per use. The word 'activate' is a bit confusing but the rest of the merit pretty clearly indicates it's a one use ability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if per use, how to describe &quot;Paper master&quot; (Read or die), where characters create sharp weapon from paper. As far as I understand, you cand spend the success of the roll in order for paper to harden (and become weapon). However, it is not clear how long such weapons can exist? Success on round? Scene? </div> </div> </div>I'd modify the merit. Papermasters don't seem to get tired from using their abilities.<br /> <br /> I'd probably just let the player craft an item from it. It's not totally clear how those items are supposed to work, so I'd just have them function as normal items. So if you make a paper sword it functions as a sword. I assume the item remains until it's destroyed or the character lets the effect go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T05:09:21-08:00","id":999170,"title":"","content":"Was &quot;Charge&quot; or &quot;Charging&quot;, the special maneuver that allowed you to make a melee attack after moving at twice your speed by sacrificing your defence, removed or just forgotten from the new set of rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12173-basilistik","name":"Basilistik","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T10:11:43-08:00","id":999794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basilistik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=999170#post999170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was &quot;Charge&quot; or &quot;Charging&quot;, the special maneuver that allowed you to make a melee attack after moving at twice your speed by sacrificing your defence, removed or just forgotten from the new set of rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's on pg. 91 under possible modifiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T22:34:59-08:00","id":1009643,"title":"","content":"Couple quick questions.<br /> <br /> Is the -1 penalty to pursuers from Fleet of Foot cumulative with each dot, or 1 flat penalty regardless of your dots? <br /> <br /> If you break a grapple as the person lower in the initiative queue, does the other grappler lose his turn? Is this not the case if you're ahead in the queue?<br /> <br /> If you grapple using an ability that allows you to attack and initiate a grapple (as wolf forms in werewolf, or vampire in frenzy, or a fighting style) do you still get the potential extra damage maneuver for an exceptional grapple initiation?<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T05:09:09-08:00","id":1009728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1009643#post1009643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you break a grapple as the person lower in the initiative queue, does the other grappler lose his turn? Is this not the case if you're ahead in the queue?<br /> <br /> If you grapple using an ability that allows you to attack and initiate a grapple (as wolf forms in werewolf, or vampire in frenzy, or a fighting style) do you still get the potential extra damage maneuver for an exceptional grapple initiation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the opponent loses their turn, it's spent grappling.<br /> <br /> Yes, at my table I'd allow the extra maneuver, even though it's technically not an attempt to initiate a grapple, but rather the grapple is a side effect of an attack. I could understand different STs ruling this differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T05:54:28-08:00","id":1016079,"title":"","content":"What happens when you hit 0 dots in an attribute? Would a character who was reduced to 0 intelligence (temporarily or not) simply just drop to the ground in a mindless puddle for instance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T06:13:29-08:00","id":1016083,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking attributes can't be reduced to 0. The spell Degrading the Form (Life \u2022\u2022\u2022) can only reduce attributes down to a minimum of 1.<br /> However, there are a few effects that can reduce attributes to 0 (such as one of the Cr\u00faac Styles in the recently released Secrets of the Covenants for Vampire). In that case I have no idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T11:18:40-08:00","id":1016164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1009643#post1009643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the -1 penalty to pursuers from Fleet of Foot cumulative with each dot, or 1 flat penalty regardless of your dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cumulative. 'He gains +1 Speed per dot, and anyone pursuing him suffers a -1 per dot to any foot chase rolls.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you break a grapple as the person lower in the initiative queue, does the other grappler lose his turn? Is this not the case if you're ahead in the queue? </div> </div> </div>The grapple contest is done at the spot of the highest person in the queue, and takes up both players rolls for that turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you grapple using an ability that allows you to attack and initiate a grapple (as wolf forms in werewolf, or vampire in frenzy, or a fighting style) do you still get the potential extra damage maneuver for an exceptional grapple initiation? </div> </div> </div>Yes, you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-12-2016, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T14:09:39-08:00","id":1017790,"title":"","content":"Is there an official ruling on the durability of guns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12771-revanreborn","name":"RevanReborn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T14:27:43-08:00","id":1017800,"title":"","content":"Think it would just be the usual durability for metal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T14:37:53-08:00","id":1017805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1017800#post1017800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think it would just be the usual durability for metal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Thanks. That's what I was leaning towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12771-revanreborn","name":"RevanReborn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12771_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T17:08:45-08:00","id":1021076,"title":"","content":"How does the Madness Condition affect characters who don't use Integrity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T17:29:15-08:00","id":1021083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1021076#post1021076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Madness Condition affect characters who don't use Integrity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably just substitute what ever Integrity stat they do use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:01:26-08:00","id":1021145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1021083#post1021083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably just substitute what ever Integrity stat they do use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even Beasts and Werewolves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:16:38-08:00","id":1021147,"title":"","content":"It would be weird for it to work with Satiety, but a lot about Beast was weird.<br /> <br /> With Werewolf you could just consider them as having 7 Integrity, or rather than using 10 - Current Integrity, the difference between 5 Harmony and whatever their current Harmony is, which seems more appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:32:38-08:00","id":1021155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1021145#post1021145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Beasts and Werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. A Werewolf with Balanced Harmony is not exactly &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;sane&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; by human standards, so it makes sense that one with Madness would have a harder time at 5 than at 10.<br /> <br /> Not sure about Beasts, but I guess you could say that being hungrier drives them to more monstrous, less &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;sane&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; behavior? I dunno, I'd have to actually read the book before I could answer with any confidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:43:23-08:00","id":1021160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1021155#post1021155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. A Werewolf with Balanced Harmony is not exactly &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;sane&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; by human standards, so it makes sense that one with Madness would have a harder time at 5 than at 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the Condition doesn't state that it's based on human standards of sanity. Nor does the ability that inflicts it, Madness and Terror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T22:49:33-08:00","id":1021162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1021160#post1021160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the Condition doesn't state that it's based on human standards of sanity. Nor does the ability that inflicts it, Madness and Terror.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is totally a fair observation. I would say the fact that it was designed for human characters and refers to Integrity kind of imply that it is based on a human standard, but I wouldn't fault anyone for ruling otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T23:26:48-08:00","id":1021172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1021155#post1021155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure about Beasts, but I guess you could say that being hungrier drives them to more monstrous, less &amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;q uot;sane&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&amp;quot; &amp;quot;&amp;quot; behavior? I dunno, I'd have to actually read the book before I could answer with any confidence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd say it works; the less satiety that a Beast has, the more they're pushed towards feeding and in less predicated ways. The more satiety they have, the more they need to work to satisfy their inner Horror, plan the terrifying event off and such. However, that also puts the Beast more in mind for a single target, rather than the more scattered approach that a low Satiety Beast would have. I guess that technially makes a high-satiety Beast more &quot;sane&quot; than a low satiety Beast?<br /> <br /> Another way to go about it, the more Satiety a Beast has, the more sated their Horror is, and thus the less likely it is to be pushing at the Beast's psyche. A low satiety Beast thus would become more susceptible with the Madness condition, potentially with the Horror using that to potentially gain Satiety. Could work too, potentially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T13:57:43-08:00","id":1025151,"title":"","content":"I heard that you can't have 9 or 8 Again and Rote Quality on the same roll. Can anyone find the page which says this? I looked at pages 72-73 and didn't find that rule among the Permutations.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T14:53:34-08:00","id":1025173,"title":"","content":"That would be the first time I've heard about that rule. There's the possibility that I've also missed it, but I doubt it. What purpose would such a rule even serve?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T15:50:26-08:00","id":1025183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1025151#post1025151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard that you can't have 9 or 8 Again and Rote Quality on the same roll. Can anyone find the page which says this? I looked at pages 72-73 and didn't find that rule among the Permutations.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard that too, but I don't think it's written anywhere in the rules. Certainly not the second edition rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T15:54:29-08:00","id":1025186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1025173#post1025173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be the first time I've heard about that rule. There's the possibility that I've also missed it, but I doubt it. What purpose would such a rule even serve?</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, having both Rote and 8-again on the same roll would basically just double your dice pool. Which doesn't seem like an unreasonable thing to disallow. But if it's on the books then I missed it too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T05:48:39-08:00","id":1025385,"title":"","content":"Question: When your dice pool turns out negative, can you choose to apply further penalties, since the roll is reduced to a chance die anyway?<br /> <br /> I think there was something about this in the nWoD rulebook, but I can't seem to find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6119-morningstar","name":"morningstar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T05:58:13-08:00","id":1025392,"title":"","content":"You can. I think that the limit is -5 after penalties and bonuses. -6 is an impossible action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T06:29:31-08:00","id":1025400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1025392#post1025392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can. I think that the limit is -5 after penalties and bonuses. -6 is an impossible action.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you. Do you have / remember a source on that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6119-morningstar","name":"morningstar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T06:37:01-08:00","id":1025405,"title":"","content":"It's from 2E Mage and I'm not sure that it is in CofD core but I find it quite logical. That said you need to remember that when something is impossibleto do you just don't roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T09:55:08-08:00","id":1025996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1025151#post1025151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard that you can't have 9 or 8 Again and Rote Quality on the same roll. Can anyone find the page which says this? I looked at pages 72-73 and didn't find that rule among the Permutations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly in reference to/transposed from stacking effects from Mage (MtA p.118) ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3557-grey_goose","name":"grey_goose","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T23:55:02-08:00","id":1026369,"title":"","content":"Can someone give me a rundown of Toxicity rules and how they (should) work in play?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Context: Matter Mage who wants to play with Toxicity mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 01-04-2017, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T01:29:21-08:00","id":1026397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1026369#post1026369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone give me a rundown of Toxicity rules and how they (should) work in play?<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Context: Matter Mage who wants to play with Toxicity mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, every poison, toxin, or drug has a Toxicity rating, a duration, and an interval. At each interval until the duration expires, the victim must roll Stamina + Resolve - Toxicity, and suffer lethal damage equal to Toxicity - successes. Drugs only behave this way if the user overdoses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T07:51:25-08:00","id":1026517,"title":"","content":"How in the name of the Archmasters and Great Luna herself has the Ashwood Abbey not devolved into a Slasher Conspiracy yet? I mean, yeah it could make a cool story hook to see the process of it happening in your game, but their goals and methods seem far closer to Slashers than even the rottenest of the other Compacts and Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Not sure if this is appropriate to the purpose of this thread, but I couldn't find one of these for Hunter. And I wasn't sure it was worth starting a new thread for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 01-04-2017, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T08:00:00-08:00","id":1026521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1026517#post1026517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How in the name of the Archmasters and Great Luna herself has the Ashwood Abbey not devolved into a Slasher Conspiracy yet? I mean, yeah it could make a cool story hook to see the process of it happening in your game, but their goals and methods seem far closer to Slashers than even the rottenest of the other Compacts and Conspiracies.</div> </div> </div> </div>They hunt monsters, just like every other compact. They're not a conspiracy. Slasher conspiracies were theorized well after the creation of the Ashwood Abbey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-04-2017, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T11:24:20-08:00","id":1026624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1026397#post1026397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, every poison, toxin, or drug has a Toxicity rating, a duration, and an interval. At each interval until the duration expires, the victim must roll Stamina + Resolve - Toxicity, and suffer lethal damage equal to Toxicity - successes. Drugs only behave this way if the user overdoses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I thought it was more complicated than that. Cool! Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:16:56-08:00","id":1026716,"title":"","content":"The list of example Vices and Virtues in the book is really short, unless I'm missing something. Anyone got a link to a longer list or some homebrew ones? (Couldn't find it in my initial search by title in the search bar)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:55:25-08:00","id":1026740,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine rules update has a longer list. It must've been cut for word count.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T16:43:54-08:00","id":1026759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1026716#post1026716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The list of example Vices and Virtues in the book is really short, unless I'm missing something. Anyone got a link to a longer list or some homebrew ones? (Couldn't find it in my initial search by title in the search bar)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/114078.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\"> World of Darkness: God-Machine Rules Update - Onyx Path Publishing | World of Darkness (new) | Demon: The Descent | Chronicles of Darkness | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> World of Darkness: God-Machine Rules Update - What Has Risen May Fall What is the God-Machine? That question doesn't have a single, easy answer, but that doesn't stop </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T17:52:25-08:00","id":1026787,"title":"","content":"Do note that CofD explicitly encourages you to make up your own to fit your character. Those are only examples. Examples are nice to have, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T19:52:55-08:00","id":1026828,"title":"","content":"Aha! Thanks. I thought I was going crazy when I saw how small the list was. I get that they encourage people to make their own, but they shouldn't have cut such an important part of creation just to save a page. People often look for examples for baselines or inspiration, and only having 4(?) examples is far too little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T21:20:38-08:00","id":1026846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Captain Shoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1026828#post1026828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aha! Thanks. I thought I was going crazy when I saw how small the list was. I get that they encourage people to make their own, but they shouldn't have cut such an important part of creation just to save a page. People often look for examples for baselines or inspiration, and only having 4(?) examples is far too little.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wordcount is a precious, precious resource. This was likely not a matter of &quot;cut examples to save a page&quot;, but a matter of &quot;do we include all of the examples that are already published in a product that is available to anyone for free, or do we cut a few of them so we can afford to publish this 100% new equipment crafting system?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T20:25:18-08:00","id":1028003,"title":"","content":"Question: &quot;Add the chain\u2019s weapon bonus to your dice pool when grappling.&quot; does this apply when entering/establishing a grapple, when using a melee manuever or at both situations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6119-morningstar","name":"morningstar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-06T20:53:51-08:00","id":1028015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>morningstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1028003#post1028003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: &quot;Add the chain\u2019s weapon bonus to your dice pool when grappling.&quot; does this apply when entering/establishing a grapple, when using a melee manuever or at both situations?</div> </div> </div> </div>It applies to the Contested Strength + Brawl vs. Strength + Brawl roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T04:10:03-08:00","id":1028102,"title":"","content":"Didn't see this asked in a question, and didn't see this in the core, is there any source that gives a good idea on the correlation between attribute dots and how strong that would be in a story? I know it comes down to the storyteller's discretion at the end, but was curious if there's a general idea of 'If you have 3 dots in strength, you're considered to be as strong as (a/an) X'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11491-thehallow1","name":"thehallow1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11491_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T04:19:25-08:00","id":1028109,"title":"","content":"2 is an average human. 5 is an average gauru-form werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T05:31:44-08:00","id":1028124,"title":"","content":"2 in attributes is the average for humans. 3 is definitely better than average but not really amazing. 4 is really, really good. 5 is peak performance. World class athletes probably has 5 in their relevant attributes. Other professional athletes probably has 4 in theirs.<br /> <br /> At least that's my interpretation. I think it's close to what's intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T07:51:58-08:00","id":1028148,"title":"","content":"It's brought up very briefly on page 30.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All characters start with one dot in each Attribute, which is below average for that Attribute. Two dots represents average ability, three dots is above average, and four dots is someone who is truly exceptional. A character with five dots in an Attribute has reached the peak of human potential within that ability. </div> </div> </div>So, using Strength as an example, a 1 is someone with a small build who doesn't exersize. A 2 is someone with an average strength, who makes some effort to stay fit. A 3 is someone who works out seriously. A 4 is a body builder who could probably compete in strongman competitions. A 5 is one of the strongest humans in the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T09:50:18-08:00","id":1028193,"title":"","content":"You could probably justify 3 dots as someone who is just naturally strong. any higher than that definitely requires effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T10:06:59-08:00","id":1028198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1028193#post1028193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could probably justify 3 dots as someone who is just naturally strong. any higher than that definitely requires effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could, definitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T10:21:25-08:00","id":1028203,"title":"","content":"I have a question about band movement. In Speed and Movement chart from HurtLocker described number of action needed for one distance to another. And there question appear. If movement divide from round to round there will be no difference in speed up to 31. Because it's always move from close to short... if we don't divide movement action then we assume character spend in move all rounds until he reach next band... And question there what kind of space-time is it?<br /> I know, we do not apply euclidean geometry for this, we should feel distance, not to know. But here there was a situation, when the characters are not in an equilibrium distance from each other. For example, player decided leave PC-sniper on <i>nest </i>to protect themselves in case of trouble. Under the <i>nest </i>they leave car on which they arrived. From point of interest to <i>nest </i>extreme distance.<br /> And I, as &quot;good&quot; ST, provided trouble for PC.<br /> And when trouble arrive they start run. Where they just run in one direction all was simple: each PC on the run have it's personal distance counter (how mach round needed for reaching next band). But when one of them stop (he got needle in calf) and other decided to help him there appear trouble for me. How much distance between them? If fast runner additionally had &quot;fleet of foot&quot;.<br /> From band mechanics and framing scene mechanics i got main idea that's each framed scene have some distance in them (from close of kitchen to extreme of wheat field). And i intuitively understand that's from each point of interest to another lye some distance expressed by bands. But where character exist when they are no longer here, but still not there? And, I'm afraid to even talk about it, character can stop on run willingly! We can assume that the character always &quot;carries&quot; framed scene of close range what surrounds him.<br /> the problem is further complicated by the fact that i have a feeling that's when character move from close to short for one observer he does not automatically move from extreme to long for another observer (whats logical). Should we just assume in that case that's extreme distance contain ten close distances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-07-2017, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T11:57:59-08:00","id":1028221,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I wouldn't bother with the chart. In my experience, abstract distances and &quot;theater of the mind&quot; work best by presenting it in terms of choices and consequences. &quot;You can get from point A to point B in one turn if you use your action to run, or in two turns if you move at your normal speed.&quot; &quot;you can get to your ally in your regular move, but the orc gets an opportunity attack unless you use your action to disengage.&quot; (I know CofD doesn't have orcs, opportunity attacks, or a disengage action, just using D&amp;D language to illustrate the point). &quot;You can get to your friend and help him up, but it'll take you two more turns to get all the way to the nest, or one more if you use your action to run.&quot; &quot;With your leg injury, it'll take you four more turns to get to the nest, and you can't use your action to run. If your ally helps support your weight you can both get there in two more turns, but he has to use his action on each of his turns to help you.&quot; That kind of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T12:31:54-08:00","id":1028231,"title":"","content":"It has Ogres. That's not far off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T12:45:52-08:00","id":1028238,"title":"","content":"Then rely on common sense? How bothersome. And ... what a relief. The absence of rigid logic simplifies the situation. However, in this case, the system looks raw, IMHO. By the way, where to complain on typing errors in the publication?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T14:15:31-08:00","id":1028265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1028238#post1028238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Then rely on common sense? How bothersome. And ... what a relief. The absence of rigid logic simplifies the situation. However, in this case, the system looks raw, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's supposed to be an abstract system as an easy-to-use alternative to the more precise but more complex standard system of measuring distances in yards. If you want a system with more rigid logic, the standard rules should serve you fine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1028238#post1028238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, where to complain on typing errors in the publication?</div> </div> </div> </div>The final published version hasn't been released yet, what you have is a pre-errata advance copy. There was a thread for submitting errata, but the submission period is over now and the thread has been closed. Chances are most of the errors you find have already been submitted in the errata thread and will be revised in the final release.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T18:19:16-08:00","id":1029395,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this is already answered. Can the Supernatural Merit Templates in Hurt Locker have &quot;regular&quot; supernatural merits? It is clear that they cannot take them from another template, but not if they can have, say, Unseen Sense or Medium. I did notice that one of the sample characters do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T18:28:02-08:00","id":1029397,"title":"","content":"With no explicit rule saying no coupled with an example of it being possible I'd say it's definitely possible. Major templates generally can't have Supernatural Merits, but that's because they're not human enough to have them. Some or most minor templates such as those in Hurt Locker but also Ghouls from VtR should be able to take Supernatural Merits since they still are fundamentally human on all relevant metaphysical levels.<br /> <br /> Edit: Not ghouls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-09-2017, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T18:49:25-08:00","id":1029403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1029397#post1029397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With no explicit rule saying no coupled with an example of it being possible I'd say it's definitely possible. Major templates generally can't have Supernatural Merits, but that's because they're not human enough to have them. Some or most minor templates such as those in Hurt Locker but also Ghouls from VtR should be able to take Supernatural Merits since they still are fundamentally human on all relevant metaphysical levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls are actually explicitly Forbidden from them per CofD core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T18:51:08-08:00","id":1029406,"title":"","content":"Oh? Would you mind giving page number?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T18:52:25-08:00","id":1029407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1029406#post1029406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh? Would you mind giving page number?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Page 56, first paragraph under Supernatural Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\">Community Content Creator</a><a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Sean%20Creef\" target=\"_blank\"> - OPP Freelancer</a> - Storyguide / Storyteller<br /> Currently Running: Trinity Continuum Core, Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3331-tragedyjones","name":"tragedyjones","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T18:59:02-08:00","id":1029412,"title":"","content":"You're right. I guess it kinda makes sense since they are less human than the templates from Hurt Locker. They gain both a fuel stat as well as a major template's powers.<br /> Trying to stack Supernatural Templates on ghouls might be a fun focus of a Zirnitra Dragon's Scale research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T11:01:29-08:00","id":1030137,"title":"","content":"If you have one point of lethal damage, a day passes, and you gain another point, does your natural healing counter 'reset'? Or do you still heal one of those points after another day passes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T11:25:57-08:00","id":1030152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1030137#post1030137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have one point of lethal damage, a day passes, and you gain another point, does your natural healing counter 'reset'? Or do you still heal one of those points after another day passes?</div> </div> </div> </div>You should still heal at your normal rate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T03:20:50-08:00","id":1031515,"title":"","content":"Any suggestion on Servant (from Fate series) mechanic? Where i should start to look? If Masters are Mages as is then what Servant is it? Changeling? Scions (if nothing is confusing and there is just about legendary heroes)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-14-2017, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T18:45:38-08:00","id":1031912,"title":"","content":"Fate isn't easily mapped to CofD, and Mage in general is bad for adapting anything specific, because it's extremely broad. Servants are so unique that you probably should create them on case by case basis using Horror rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:22:01-08:00","id":1032702,"title":"","content":"What kind and level of Influences would work best to nudge someone into committing deadly industrial sabotage while thinking it was their own idea in the first place? For context, his union has been on strike for months with negotiations going nowhere and it's looking like the company's just about to just replace them all with new people, having already announced that the strikers were all fired.<br /> <br /> And what power would be able to convince a vicious, but loyal dog to kill its owner because the owner suddenly registers as prey to its mind?<br /> <br /> Also, what entities beside ghosts, spirits, and other ephemeral entities have access to Influence powers? Do Sin-eaters get them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:02:56-08:00","id":1032740,"title":"","content":"Generally people wouldn't notice an Influence as an outside source. If the desire to do it is already there, all you might need is level 1, Strengthen. If someone is suitably amoral, Influence 2 would be enough to Manipulate it, as that level would make them do something natural to them, within the bounds of reason. Rank 3 would make anyone do it.<br /> <br /> As for the dog, and still going with Influence, Rank 3 would be more than enough. Rank 1 and 2, perhaps, depending on the 'loyalty' of the dog. If you're including powers beyond Influence, there's a lot.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters don't seem to get Influences, but they are bound with a Rank 3 ghost, so if they did, it would be because of that. Werewolves can use Influences, Mages can get power over them through controlling others and Fetishes. Claimed, too, and idigam when Coalesced. Pangaeans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-16-2017, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:22:17-08:00","id":1032786,"title":"","content":"Cool. so, would Influence (Prey), or Influence (Predation) work better for the second situation?<br /> <br /> <br /> and how does this power manifest? In the book that inspired these questions, the villainous entity insinuated itself as a sounding board in the character's head, nudging him towards the idea while he just thought he was mulling over the issue while never acknowledging or realizing that those thoughts were not entirely his own. Is that a pretty good example of how Influence can work? or is it more manipulating probability?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:37:03-08:00","id":1032795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1032786#post1032786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool. so, would Influence (Prey), or Influence (Predation) work better for the second situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Predation. With Prey you'd use it on the target, making them seem like the best, easiest and most tempting prey possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and how does this power manifest? In the book that inspired these questions, the villainous entity insinuated itself as a sounding board in the character's head, nudging him towards the idea while he just thought he was mulling over the issue while never acknowledging or realizing that those thoughts were not entirely his own. Is that a pretty good example of how Influence can work? or is it more manipulating probability? </div> </div> </div>That's a better description than manipulating probability. Though obviously Fate or Chance Influences would be more like manipulating probability.<br /> <br /> The target would think more 'predatory.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:35:26-08:00","id":1032841,"title":"","content":"Everything (except humans and things that were once human) has a spirit, and most humans aren't even aware that they exist. Infleunces aren't very overt by RAW until you get into really powerful and rare ephemera.<br /> <br /> You might also consider looking at the Horror rules. Since you asked if anything but Ephemera gets Influence; Horrors can have Influences. They also have a few other power options that might fit your goal more directly, depending on your goals. The Numen (available to both Ephemera and Horrors) &quot;Implant Mission&quot; might be worth looking at, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:08:26-08:00","id":1032969,"title":"","content":"Hello. I was planning on picking up Chronicles of Darkness soon, and had some questions about what will work with it and what won't. I know that the nWoD had some cool supplemental books likes Armory, Slashers, Reliquary and Mysterious Places, as well as location-based supplements like Shadows of Mexico; are any of these compatible with CoD? If not, are there new versions of them, or will there be? I can't seem to find any on Drive Thru RPG if there are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:44:00-08:00","id":1032993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1032969#post1032969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. I was planning on picking up Chronicles of Darkness soon, and had some questions about what will work with it and what won't. I know that the nWoD had some cool supplemental books likes Armory, Slashers, Reliquary and Mysterious Places, as well as location-based supplements like Shadows of Mexico; are any of these compatible with CoD? If not, are there new versions of them, or will there be? I can't seem to find any on Drive Thru RPG if there are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hurt locker is the only second edition supplement out so far. Even so mirrors will still have some useful stuff. The core CofD has so much you can do. Clues, Dread Horrors, Equipment, Social Manuvering. Lots my group hasn't even touched on yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T16:49:47-08:00","id":1032996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1032993#post1032993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hurt locker is the only second edition supplement out so far. Even so mirrors will still have some useful stuff. The core CofD has so much you can do. Clues, Dread Horrors, Equipment, Social Manuvering. Lots my group hasn't even touched on yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome. So most nWoD supplements besides Mirrors probably aren't much use then? I really hope we get an updated Slashers or Shadows of Mexico. Also, Chronicles has God-Machine Chronicles built in, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:00:50-08:00","id":1033005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1032969#post1032969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello. I was planning on picking up Chronicles of Darkness soon, and had some questions about what will work with it and what won't. I know that the nWoD had some cool supplemental books likes Armory, Slashers, Reliquary and Mysterious Places, as well as location-based supplements like Shadows of Mexico; are any of these compatible with CoD? If not, are there new versions of them, or will there be? I can't seem to find any on Drive Thru RPG if there are.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Editions are similar enough that most 1e material is usable. Pretty much any setting material is still valid, and most mechanics can be ported over without too much work. There is a spiritual sequel to Armory, it's called Hurt Locker. It covers different stuff than the original Armory and Armory Reloaded though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:17:49-08:00","id":1033019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1033005#post1033005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Editions are similar enough that most 1e material is usable. Pretty much any setting material is still valid, and most mechanics can be ported over without too much work. There is a spiritual sequel to Armory, it's called Hurt Locker. It covers different stuff than the original Armory and Armory Reloaded though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that's reassuring. I was looking at Hurt Locker, but I want the print version of it. Do you happen to know how much that will cost, and/or what the discount will be on it if I get the PDF version first?<br /> <br /> Edit: And when it will be available?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12885,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","user":"E11even-E11even","date":". 01-16-2017, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:27:52-08:00","id":1033033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1033019#post1033019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that's reassuring. I was looking at Hurt Locker, but I want the print version of it. Do you happen to know how much that will cost, and/or what the discount will be on it if I get the PDF version first?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know for sure, but comparing to V20DA Tome of Secrets, which is the same price for the PDF, that one is $24.99 for standard POD and $34.99 for premium POD. The discount you get for buying the advance PDF is equal to the difference between the price of the PDF and the price of the PDF + POD combo, so assuming it's the same price as Tome of Secrets, you'd end up paying $26.99 for the standard ecombo or $36.99 for the premium combo, in total.<br /> <br /> Personally I find the premium prints to be worth the extra 10 bucks, but YMMV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:32:09-08:00","id":1033036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1033033#post1033033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know for sure, but comparing to V20DA Tome of Secrets, which is the same price for the PDF, that one is $24.99 for standard POD and $34.99 for premium POD. The discount you get for buying the advance PDF is equal to the difference between the price of the PDF and the price of the PDF + POD combo, so assuming it's the same price as Tome of Secrets, you'd end up paying $26.99 for the standard ecombo or $36.99 for the premium combo, in total.<br /> <br /> Personally I find the premium prints to be worth the extra 10 bucks, but YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Excellent. Thank you very much for the info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T05:29:47-08:00","id":1033280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1032996#post1032996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome. So most nWoD supplements besides Mirrors probably aren't much use then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Many of them are still useful, although certain mechanics require a little translation to the new system, especially any that contain ephemeral beings, or abilities that allow multiple attacks on one target.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Chronicles has God-Machine Chronicles built in, right? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think I must have been a page or two back without realizing it...all of this has been answered already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T09:13:59-08:00","id":1033396,"title":"","content":"Certain sections of god machine chronicles are not included, i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:42:20-08:00","id":1033455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1033396#post1033396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certain sections of god machine chronicles are not included, i think.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rules update chapter wasn't, but the rest of the book was. Most of what was in the rules update chapter made it in, but a few things did not, like some of the example virtues and vices. But the rules update chapter is still available for free from drivethruRPG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:18:13-08:00","id":1034129,"title":"","content":"Putting this here because Ghosts are technically Core (could also go in the Geist sub-forum).<br /> <br /> How much do Ghosts &quot;retain&quot; from their mortal sources? Skills may or may not be kept, depending on ST needs. But do Ghost get the same Merits as the person who died* to create them? Specifically asking for odd cases, like a Ghost with Medium (can they create their own Anchor/Open/Controlled Conditions via it?), or Skinthief (Ghost that can skin and take the form of other Ghosts), etc.?<br /> <br /> *Death may not be necessary in all Ghost creation. Or at least not lasting death.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Medium being a Supernatural Merit, and Supernatural Merits being limited to Mortals, which a Ghost no longer is, probably answers that one, but Skinthief isn't listed as a Supernatural Merit (though it probably should be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 01-18-2017, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:19:40-08:00","id":1034162,"title":"","content":"I don't think ghosts typically have Merits at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T12:36:53-08:00","id":1036223,"title":"","content":"Is there a maximum limit of attributes for things that let you 'exceed' the human max? I know in 1e 10 was a hard limit (I think), but I haven't seen anything to that effect in 2e. Could supernatural powers theoretically give you attributes of like 20 dots?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T12:40:43-08:00","id":1036227,"title":"","content":"my god, that sounds like &quot;6.0 earthquake if I stomp angrily&quot; levels","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T12:45:18-08:00","id":1036230,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure you can go over 10, though not by buying it as much as through abilities. Usually the abilities will say something like, 'This can take you over the normal limits for Attributes.' Humans are generally stuck at 5, though I believe they have some abilities like this too.<br /> <br /> Werewolf forms allow you to exceed your natural limitations, a werewolf with 10 Strength would get 13 when turning Gauru, potentially more with the Favored Form Merit.<br /> <br /> And there's Crimson Spasm. 'Each success allows the Rahu to add two dots to Strength or Stamina, to add a point of general armor, or to increase the lethal damage done by his natural weapons by +1. These benefits stack on top of those granted by other Facets and forms. The Spasm lasts as long as the Rahu fuels it by paying 1 Essence each turn. If the Rahu uses this Facet while in Hishu or Urhan, he will cause Lunacy in that form as if he were in Dalu.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-22-2017, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:20:58-08:00","id":1036240,"title":"","content":"Vampires' Vigor and Resilience can push their Strength and Stamina respectively to a theoretical maximum of 15.<br /> Then there's Life and Mind spells in Mage to temporarily increase any attribute or skill. It requires a Reach (meaning it's more difficult to do safely) to get above the normal maximum, but with that Reach the spells has no hard caps. Only a practical maximum since more extra dots is more difficult to pull off. It's definitely possible to get above 20 dots for a sufficiently skilled Mage, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:14:12-08:00","id":1036324,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's a cap, and if it was the case in 1e they broke that rule at least once in a Night Horrors book. Granted, it was to represent a True Fae at full power, and explicitly an exception to normal rules. <br /> <br /> In second edition I know Changelings can get to 21 strength or dexterity, maybe more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T23:04:39-08:00","id":1036454,"title":"","content":"What are the rules for lifting heavy things also how much is the base damage for a punching someone. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T23:15:22-08:00","id":1036458,"title":"","content":"Punching is: Unarmed Combat: Strength + Brawl - opponent\u2019s Defense. Fists are 0B weapons.<br /> <br /> Lifting heavy things, for some unknowable reason, has not been included in 2e rules. It's in the 1e rulebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T23:20:22-08:00","id":1036459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036454#post1036454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the rules for lifting heavy things</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/961462-where-are-the-rules-for-lifting-stuff\">You asked this before.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also how much is the base damage for a punching someone. </div> </div> </div>0. It's entirely based on your dice roll. And it's not a weapon so outside of special circumstances it does Bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T23:20:45-08:00","id":1036460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036454#post1036454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the rules for lifting heavy things</div> </div> </div> </div>They got left out, presumably by mistake. We can pretty much assume they're the same as the 1e rules for lifting heavy things though, and those are on page 47 of the 1e core rule book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036454#post1036454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also how much is the base damage for a punching someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Zero. Unless you have a Merit that enhances your Brawl damage, unarmed attacks deal bashing damage equal to successes on the attack roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-23-2017, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:46:51-08:00","id":1036586,"title":"","content":"Am I the only one who finds it weird that the rules for Dodging work uniquely (your successes canceling out that of your opponent)? It could have been a contested action. Is there a reason why it works that way? And if it were to become a contested action, would it break anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:14:51-08:00","id":1036599,"title":"","content":"The majority of rolls in CoD are pass/fail, and successes beyond the first (or fifth, for exceptional) don't alter the outcome. Since attack rolls already break with this pattern it makes sense that the counter strategy would be modified to account for that.<br /> <br /> Honestly combat as a whole runs on a different set of rules and expectations from the rest of the game. Not hugely different, but different enough to create dissonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T07:17:14-08:00","id":1036600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036599#post1036599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The majority of rolls in CoD are pass/fail, and successes beyond the first (or fifth, for exceptional) don't alter the outcome. Since attack rolls already break with this pattern it makes sense that the counter strategy would be modified to account for that.<br /> <br /> Honestly combat as a whole runs on a different set of rules and expectations from the rest of the game. Not hugely different, but different enough to create dissonance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Combat is a whole sub-system, right there with Social Maneuvering and the like, so a little deviation is to be expected. I just found this particular bit the most dissonant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:38:51-08:00","id":1036654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036586#post1036586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who finds it weird that the rules for Dodging work uniquely (your successes canceling out that of your opponent)? It could have been a contested action. Is there a reason why it works that way? And if it were to become a contested action, would it break anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>So if the attacker rolls one more success than the defender, the defender takes damage equal to the attacker's successes + weapon modifier? That wouldn't break anything exactly, but it would make Dodging an inferior option to using regular defense. It makes Dodging an all-or-nothing prospect, where you either take full damage or take no damage, in addition to making it more variable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:42:27-08:00","id":1036656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036586#post1036586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who finds it weird that the rules for Dodging work uniquely (your successes canceling out that of your opponent)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Containing Paradox (Mage) also works this way, likely for the same reason: neither of these are things you want to be all-or-nothing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:03:17-08:00","id":1036919,"title":"","content":"I want to start storytelling again, but it's been a hot minute since I've run anything. Can I get some recommendations on supplements to pick up, and/or resources on storytelling? Anything that could help me plan, come up with hooks, get ready for the inevitable plot derailing, or that just stands out as a good example of a nicely planned out, well-run story would be helpful. I'd most likely run Changeling or mortals in CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:17:20-08:00","id":1036924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036919#post1036919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to start storytelling again, but it's been a hot minute since I've run anything. Can I get some recommendations on supplements to pick up, and/or resources on storytelling? Anything that could help me plan, come up with hooks, get ready for the inevitable plot derailing, or that just stands out as a good example of a nicely planned out, well-run story would be helpful. I'd most likely run Changeling or mortals in CoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>SAS adventures are a good starting point, and in general the SAS style of adventure design is a really great way to plan out your own stories when you feel ready. Planning scenes and organizing them in a flowchart is just plain good design, and running SAS games can be great practice for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:28:22-08:00","id":1036965,"title":"","content":"AngryDM (or GM? I don't remember) has a lot of good advice about structured approach towards writing your games. While he writes from a perspective of DND gamer, his advice is usually system agnostic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:46:06-08:00","id":1036977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036965#post1036965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AngryDM (or GM? I don't remember) has a lot of good advice about structured approach towards writing your games. While he writes from a perspective of DND gamer, his advice is usually system agnostic.</div> </div> </div> </div>GM. And I'll second that, his articles are some of the best GMing advice I've ever read. Apparently he's writing a book now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:50:07-08:00","id":1036982,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys, I appreciate the advice. I'm going to look up some 2e CoD SAS modules.<br /> <br /> Edit: And check out AngryGM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:14:53-08:00","id":1036993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>E11even-E11even</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036982#post1036982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you guys, I appreciate the advice. I'm going to look up some 2e CoD SAS modules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... the only SAS module that's specifically for 2e at the moment is Reap the Whirlwind, which is a direct port of the 1e module Into the Void. It's cool though, the 1e modules aren't too hard to convert to 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:23:08-08:00","id":1036998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036993#post1036993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Err... the only SAS module that's specifically for 2e at the moment is Reap the Whirlwind, which is a direct port of the 1e module Into the Void. It's cool though, the 1e modules aren't too hard to convert to 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, gotcha. And, I think what I'll mostly need is the layout and structure of it all anyways, so that should be fine. I see a few for regular WoD, so I'll see what looks interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12885-e11even-e11even","name":"E11even-E11even","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12885_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T01:53:30-08:00","id":1037088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036654#post1036654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if the attacker rolls one more success than the defender, the defender takes damage equal to the attacker's successes + weapon modifier? That wouldn't break anything exactly, but it would make Dodging an inferior option to using regular defense. It makes Dodging an all-or-nothing prospect, where you either take full damage or take no damage, in addition to making it more variable.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1036656#post1036656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Containing Paradox (Mage) also works this way, likely for the same reason: neither of these are things you want to be all-or-nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that makes sense now. All-or-nothing defense would be dangerous, in a system already tilted in favor of offense than defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T07:56:03-08:00","id":1038414,"title":"","content":"What does it mean when an attack or weapon does 0L/+0L or 0A/+0A? I understand that L is Lethal and A is Aggravated, but beyond that I'm stumped","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T07:58:23-08:00","id":1038416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1038414#post1038414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does it mean when an attack or weapon does 0L/+0L or 0A/+0A? I understand that L is Lethal and A is Aggravated, but beyond that I'm stumped</div> </div> </div> </div>0L or 0A means it doesn't add any extra damage. It just converts the damage from your rolled successes from bashing to lethal or aggravated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T08:34:34-08:00","id":1038433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1038416#post1038416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 0L or 0A means it doesn't add any extra damage. It just converts the damage from your rolled successes from bashing to lethal or aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's a way more powerful effect than I thought it was 0_0. Damn. So +2L means all your successes do lethal and then add two more successes? Or is it just two extra Lethal Damage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T08:41:52-08:00","id":1038437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1038433#post1038433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a way more powerful effect than I thought it was 0_0. Damn. So +2L means all your successes do lethal and then add two more successes? Or is it just two extra Lethal Damage</div> </div> </div> </div>All of your successes do lethal and you add two more lethal damage (the extra two damage isn't considered &quot;successes&quot;, which seems like a distinction without difference, but can matter for the purposes of determining exceptional successes, for example.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T09:16:04-08:00","id":1038443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1038437#post1038437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of your successes do lethal and you add two more lethal damage (the extra two damage isn't considered &quot;successes&quot;, which seems like a distinction without difference, but can matter for the purposes of determining exceptional successes, for example.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, if you roll 3 successes on the attack, and you're using a 2L weapon, is that considered an exceptional success?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T09:19:58-08:00","id":1038445,"title":"","content":"No, that's what she just said. They're not extra successes, so don't cause exceptional successes, but on paper it can look like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T09:21:46-08:00","id":1038447,"title":"","content":"Ah, gotcha. I was reading and responding too fast it seems. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T22:44:31-08:00","id":1046190,"title":"","content":"Is it possible for a ghost to have a whole city as their Anchor? For example: a Hunter who belongs to the Barrett Commission dies while upholding the Vigil. He was the mayor of the city, and genuinely cared about its citizens. Though the city's politics have been overtaken by vampires or what have you, his desire to protect others was so strong that he left behind a Rank 2 ghost upon dying in shady circumstances. Since the mayor was emotionaly attached to the city as a whole, could he Manifest anywhere within it? The same could happen to a vigilante who watches over their city like Batman watches over Gotham.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T00:34:34-08:00","id":1046203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1046190#post1046190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible for a ghost to have a whole city as their Anchor? For example: a Hunter who belongs to the Barrett Commission dies while upholding the Vigil. He was the mayor of the city, and genuinely cared about its citizens. Though the city's politics have been overtaken by vampires or what have you, his desire to protect others was so strong that he left behind a Rank 2 ghost upon dying in shady circumstances. Since the mayor was emotionaly attached to the city as a whole, could he Manifest anywhere within it? The same could happen to a vigilante who watches over their city like Batman watches over Gotham.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possible AFAIK, in the sense I don't remember huge Anchors like that explicitly forbidden, but even though it feels like stretching the rules too much. I'd have the Anchor be something personal like the mayor's office or the vigilante's favored weapon, while give it Influence over concepts like the City or Protection.<br /> <br /> (Ghostly Anchors and Influences being separate is the rules, right?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T03:33:39-08:00","id":1046233,"title":"","content":"Ghosts have only Influence: Anchors. When Geist 2E comes out we will probably see Rank 3+ ghosts (Geists) with different Influences, but those are changed by stuff in the Underworld.<br /> There's no explicit limitations to what can be an Anchor, but I would personally rule that an Anchor has to be intimate. A whole city would not be intimate enough, but places he often frequented would work. But in your game you might rule differently. As I said there are no explicit limitations to what can constitute an Anchor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T04:47:54-08:00","id":1046247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1046233#post1046233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts have only Influence: Anchors. When Geist 2E comes out we will probably see Rank 3+ ghosts (Geists) with different Influences, but those are changed by stuff in the Underworld.<br /> There's no explicit limitations to what can be an Anchor, but I would personally rule that an Anchor has to be intimate. A whole city would not be intimate enough, but places he often frequented would work. But in your game you might rule differently. As I said there are no explicit limitations to what can constitute an Anchor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying that ghosts have Influence: Anchors is much like saying that spirits have Influence: Resonance and angels have Influence: Infrastructure. Past discussion over the subject <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/71851-unpacking-manifestation-conditions\">here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T05:29:27-08:00","id":1046253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1046233#post1046233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no explicit limitations to what can be an Anchor, but I would personally rule that an Anchor has to be intimate. A whole city would not be intimate enough, but places he often frequented would work. But in your game you might rule differently. As I said there are no explicit limitations to what can constitute an Anchor.</div> </div> </div> </div>In one 1e book there was a ghost who had the entire United States as their anchor if I remember right. I can easily see a whole city being the anchor for a particularly dedicated ghost (like a founder of the city or one of the more dedicated politicians / political activists there), it'd just be a lot rarerthan say, a ring or a person or a building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T05:39:36-08:00","id":1046259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1046247#post1046247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saying that ghosts have Influence: Anchors is much like saying that spirits have Influence: Resonance and angels have Influence: Infrastructure. Past discussion over the subject <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/71851-unpacking-manifestation-conditions\">here</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 130 about Influences: &quot;Ghosts have power over their own anchors&quot;<br /> This suggests either that the ghost has a singular Influence over all their Anchors, or Influence dots spread over individual Anchors. I assumed the former interpretation because otherwise they would never be able to new temporary Anchors as per the fourth Influence dot. However, I now realise that the ghost would have to be Rank 4+ to even get an Influence that high and by then they could have more exotic Influences due to metaphysical changes gained in the Underworld.<br /> And yes, spirits kinda do have Influence: Resonance (except often spread over several types of Resonances) since the concepts that is Resonant to a particular spirit also governs the spirit's Influences. It's just impractical to write since you want to know what that concept is, and because spirits can have several (related but distinct) concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T08:30:35-08:00","id":1046326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1046253#post1046253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one 1e book there was a ghost who had the entire United States as their anchor if I remember right. I can easily see a whole city being the anchor for a particularly dedicated ghost (like a founder of the city or one of the more dedicated politicians / political activists there), it'd just be a lot rarerthan say, a ring or a person or a building.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't look to a legendary specter from a Night Horrors book who was written with the (pre-Geist) 1e ghost mechanics in mind for useful precedent in how to handle a ghost with city-level unconstrained geographical range. A frequent cooldown period or a mystical support structure (e.g. rituals, relics, frequent use of Avernian Gates, etc) does more to engage with how weird that kind of mobility is for a Rank 2 ghost than &quot;the mayor is personally anchored to the whole town.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1046259#post1046259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This suggests either that the ghost has a singular Influence over all their Anchors, or Influence dots spread over individual Anchors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or that their original Influences can collectively apply to the context of all of their original Anchors. That's a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I assumed the former interpretation because otherwise they would never be able to new temporary Anchors as per the fourth Influence dot. </div> </div> </div>An angel capable of Creating instances of its Influence can always generate the Infrastructure Condition, applicable to all angels, regardless of what that Influence ordinarily governs. Creating Anchors through Influence works the same way for individual ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, spirits kinda do have Influence: Resonance (except often spread over several types of Resonances) since the concepts that is Resonant to a particular spirit also governs the spirit's Influences. It's just impractical to write since you want to know what that concept is, and because spirits can have several (related but distinct) concepts. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Whether something has the Resonant Condition for a particular is determined by whether it matches the description of one of its Influences&quot; and &quot;Spirits have Influence: Resonance&quot; combine into a tautological statement that means nothing. That's more than just &quot;impractical.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T09:21:52-08:00","id":1046350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1046253#post1046253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one 1e book there was a ghost who had the entire United States as their anchor if I remember right. I can easily see a whole city being the anchor for a particularly dedicated ghost (like a founder of the city or one of the more dedicated politicians / political activists there), it'd just be a lot rarerthan say, a ring or a person or a building.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1046326#post1046326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't look to a legendary specter from a Night Horrors book who was written with the (pre-Geist) 1e ghost mechanics in mind for useful precedent in how to handle a ghost with city-level unconstrained geographical range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which ghost is this?<br /> <br /> Sure you're not thinking of Irinam? One of its Influences is American Symbols.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T09:36:55-08:00","id":1046356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1046350#post1046350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure you're not thinking of Irinam? One of its Influences is American Symbols.</div> </div> </div> </div>Baykosh, from Wicked Dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T09:51:27-08:00","id":1046360,"title":"","content":"I was wondering how I missed that but his section is pretty small.<br /> <br /> He is considered a unique ghost the section calling out his anchor as an example. Holding him up as an example of how ghosts work, especially since it's, as Satchel pointed out, before more proper ghost rules even in first edition.<br /> <br /> Still if someone was invested with a city or area it does seem reasonable to have it as an anchor. Someone like George Washington, a prestigious mayor or family whose life was entangled with their city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T08:35:34-08:00","id":1047230,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: City Wide Anchor</b><br /> <br /> I had to give this some thought. Rules As Written, there is really nothing that would keep a Ghost of any rank from having a large territory as a Anchor. However, this could easily lead to relatively weak Ghost having a absurdly large mobility ( like trying to define &quot;Texas&quot; or &quot;China&quot; as an Anchor). I personally rule that the sort of connection needed to form an anchor has to be <i>intimate</i>. No matter how much someone cares about their City or State or what have you, no one can know that much territory well enough or deeply enough to claim the sort of connection that an Anchor is supposed to represent. Instead, the Ghost would likely have key locations within the City (possibly Several) that serve Anchors (City Hall, a particular Park,maybe even a Bar popular with local politicians). To use Batman as the ever popular example,despite his obsession with keeping Gotham safe,his theoretical ghost would be tied to specific locations that have specific significance. His ghost would haunt Wayne Manor and the caves beneath it, Crime Ally where his parents were slain, or the rooftop of the Police Precinct that hosts the bat signal. He would then use Fetter/Unfetter to manage Essence Bleed and roam more freely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T14:10:55-08:00","id":1047385,"title":"","content":"What would one suggest the roll be to search an environment for hazards or valuables?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8064-mp122984","name":"mp122984","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T14:25:11-08:00","id":1047392,"title":"","content":"Wits+Investigation is the fairly standard roll for actively searching (Wits+Composure is known as a Perception roll and used for more passive noticing by contrast).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T15:48:33-08:00","id":1047429,"title":"","content":"And depending on the environment, Wits + Survival could do the trick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T00:29:00-08:00","id":1047592,"title":"","content":"How aware are the different types of ephemeral entities about their banes and bans?<br /> I'm guessing they all have at least subconscious understanding of their ban since it governs their behaviour. Banes, I don't know.<br /> Also, can they recognise their bane when confronted by it? Would a ghost be able to distinguish between a regular willow stick and a stick from the willow that grows above their unmarked grave?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T01:23:36-08:00","id":1047602,"title":"","content":"Yes, because banes are solid to ephemeral entities: to the ghost, its bane-willow-stick would look real, rather than the ghostly fog-shapes everything not in ghost-Twilight looks like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T01:49:22-08:00","id":1047610,"title":"","content":"Thanks. That seems really obvious in hindsight. But would the ghost know that it's a bane/dangerous object instead of a really weird object unless it had been subjected to it before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T02:59:47-08:00","id":1047627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1047592#post1047592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How aware are the different types of ephemeral entities about their banes and bans?<br /> I'm guessing they all have at least subconscious understanding of their ban since it governs their behaviour. Banes, I don't know.<br /> Also, can they recognise their bane when confronted by it? Would a ghost be able to distinguish between a regular willow stick and a stick from the willow that grows above their unmarked grave?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess they're mostly aware of them, if only to prevent odd situations like &quot;Wait, I can't do that?&quot; or &quot;Huh, looks I can't help but doing that,&quot; and &quot;Woah, why does that even hurt me?!&quot;<br /> <br /> Newly minted ghosts probably don't understand why they have this newfound compulsions and allergic reactions, but spirits are likely to have an instictual awareness of what bans and banes are. Same for angels and Goetia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T04:30:19-08:00","id":1048173,"title":"","content":"I know this particular post is kind of dated, but I think it's important...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=875607#post875607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're right. It's not terribly clear in the core rules. </div> </div> </div> </div>If you go back to the 1e core rulebook, it becomes clear that you can have modifiers above -5/+5, but not by a single source. <br /> So you were correct! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1e Core Rulebook, Page 124:<br /> As a rule, a single modifier never exceeds five, whether as a bonus or penalty. That means all tools and situational effects are each rated one to five. [...] That is, they\u2019re all cumulative. </div> </div> </div>The total max of -5/+5 is an optional rule:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1e Core Rulebook, Page 124:<br /> Or your Storyteller may simply consider all the factors at work in terms of a one-to-five range and come up with one total that applies for an effort. He might allow players to calculate some bonuses, but he summarily decrees that weather and character disabilities make an effort \u201ca trying task,\u201d and three dice are removed from a player\u2019s pool. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Waiting for new Chronicles of Darkness Dice! \ud83e\udd17 \ud83c\udfb2","edited":{"userid":1825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","user":"Elythia","date":". 02-13-2017, 07:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1825-elythia","name":"Elythia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1825_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T20:50:25-08:00","id":1048568,"title":"","content":"Which Government Agency in the US. Would be sent to investigate a whole city of people and supernaturals going missing in a single night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T20:58:28-08:00","id":1048570,"title":"","content":"An entire city's population disappearing?<br /> <br /> Pretty much everyone. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Emergency_Management_Agency\" target=\"_blank\">FEMA</a> would be the big one. The National guard would probably be called out to help, at the least keeping people from entering the city until someone like the CDC determined if there was risk of whatever happened spreading or infecting anyone who came inside. FBI would probably show up as an intelligence agency, since it might be some sort of terrorism.<br /> <br /> News crews everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T22:37:04-08:00","id":1048591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1048568#post1048568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Government Agency in the US. Would be sent to investigate a whole city of people and supernaturals going missing in a single night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much everybody, just like nofather said. <i>Unless</i> something like quiescence kicked in on a large scale and kept people from noticing. Apparently Manhatten rearranges itself daily or something and nobody notices, so I could see this being something mundanes don't notice if that's how the ST wants it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T23:09:46-08:00","id":1049710,"title":"","content":"Is their a supernatural in world of darkness that dies and get reincarnated ?<br /> <br /> I'm looking for a template to work off of for this NPC I made <br /> <br /> each time they die and get reincarnated into a new body they don't remember their past life till around 18 or till a traumatic event reminds them. Flashes of their past lives keep coming back to them. Advantage of this they would have access to all the skills of their past life. Messed up part is they remember how they died. I thought it was fun for the vampire game were the person remembers what a player character did to them roughly 200 years ago. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T23:30:42-08:00","id":1049718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1049710#post1049710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is their a supernatural in world of darkness that dies and get reincarnated ?<br /> <br /> I'm looking for a template to work off of for this NPC I made<br /> <br /> each time they die and get reincarnated into a new body they don't remember their past life till around 18 or till a traumatic event reminds them. Flashes of their past lives keep coming back to them. Advantage of this they would have access to all the skills of their past life. Messed up part is they remember how they died. I thought it was fun for the vampire game were the person remembers what a player character did to them roughly 200 years ago.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Check the Reborn in Chapter 4 of Immortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T03:24:38-08:00","id":1049776,"title":"","content":"Are there any resources for location based supernatural phenomena? I mean things like cold spots, areas interfering with electronics, places where flashlights break and flames get snuffed out, areas that react to or instill different emotions, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T04:07:35-08:00","id":1049781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1049776#post1049776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any resources for location based supernatural phenomena? I mean things like cold spots, areas interfering with electronics, places where flashlights break and flames get snuffed out, areas that react to or instill different emotions, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds a lot like an ephemeral messing around. Or a Beast having way too much fun with his Lair Traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T08:36:48-08:00","id":1049872,"title":"","content":"Horrors can be used for locations, too. One of the examples is a house, if I remember right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T13:21:23-08:00","id":1050019,"title":"","content":"Hello guys a couple of question regarding the blue book.<br /> <br /> Question about how Investigation works regarding clues. <br /> <br /> So each &quot;Clue&quot; is compose by elements. Elements are bonus dies that can be used to anything pertaining the investigation, be that getting more clues or chasing the suspect but they are a one time use.<br /> <br /> So say i got a Clue with 2 elements. I can use 1 element to give my character a +1 when searching his apartment for more clues. And another element to give my character a +1 to fight/chase down the suspect and then the Clue would spent right?<br /> <br /> So getting 5 clues (which the book says is the standard) is rolling and succeeding the &quot;Uncover the clue&quot; roll 5 times regardless on how many elements the rules have right? <br /> <br /> The number of Clues i can use its elements for a roll is limited to 1 or my character Investigation rating. But that limit doesnt apply to elements in a single roll? If i have no investigation i can use the elements of a clue in single roll even if the clue has 3 elements (so a +3). Can i use the elements of a clue in different rolls? In the example above +2 in a roll and +1 in another?<br /> <br /> Another question about grapple.<br /> When 2 characters are in a grapple each turn they roll on the highest initiative turn between the 2 characters to see if the grapple continues but what happens with the turn of the lowest character? He loses his turn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:13:13-08:00","id":1050053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1048568#post1048568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which Government Agency in the US. Would be sent to investigate a whole city of people and supernaturals going missing in a single night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homeland Security, FBI, the Army. But the media would get a hold of it first. The people would just up and vanish out of thin air?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T18:14:13-08:00","id":1050203,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised nobody has suggested VALKYRIE. Why wouldn't the government's supernatural task force be sent in to investigate such an obviously supernatural happening? Unless I'm missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T18:19:02-08:00","id":1050207,"title":"","content":"Valkyrie's more of a Task Force. They deal with an issue. Until anyone knows what's up, what can they do? Shoot at empty buildings? There's not even supernaturals in the area.<br /> <br /> Plus a city going missing is going to be big news, not the time to put out the super secret and super illegal hit squad. Let someone find out what happened first, then send Valkyrie in to deal with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-16-2017, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T07:31:22-08:00","id":1050482,"title":"","content":"I know the rules on what happens to Beasts, Mages, and Vampires in the Hedge and the rumor about Werewolves becoming Briarwolves, but do any of the books say anything about Mummies going into or sleeping in the Hedge or a Hollow?<br /> <br /> Also, while I'm on this topic, how about Sin-Eaters? Anything weird happen to them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T12:11:49-08:00","id":1051082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1050207#post1050207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Valkyrie's more of a Task Force. They deal with an issue. Until anyone knows what's up, what can they do? Shoot at empty buildings? There's not even supernaturals in the area.<br /> <br /> Plus a city going missing is going to be big news, not the time to put out the super secret and super illegal hit squad. Let someone find out what happened first, then send Valkyrie in to deal with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. More VASCU's cup of tea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:15:07-08:00","id":1054935,"title":"","content":"Question about falling Integrity:<br /> <br /> Can Integrity drop to 0? Does anything in particular happen when this occurs?<br /> How is Integrity regained?<br /> <br /> (if you can point me to page numbers, that'd be fine)<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:40:02-08:00","id":1054945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1054935#post1054935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Integrity drop to 0?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there is no mention of Integrity 0 (can't give a page reference as none exists), no entry on the Breaking Point chart (page 75) for what penalty Integrity 0 would impose, and the Soulless Condition (bottom of page 290 to top of page 291) stops inflicting Breaking Points at Integrity 1. So I would assume there is no Integrity 0.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1054935#post1054935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anything in particular happen when this occurs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that's mentioned in the core book (no page reference)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1054935#post1054935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is Integrity regained?</div> </div> </div> </div>By paying 2 Experiences (page 77). As with all exp purchases, the purchase must be justified by the narrative (maybe the character seeks therapy, spiritual enlightenment, or otherwise learns to cope with the trauma that caused them to lose their Integrity in the first place.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T14:45:17-08:00","id":1054947,"title":"","content":"I was hoping there was a write-up of the narrative justifications / process for regaining Integrity... but it seems clear enough. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:44:37-08:00","id":1056884,"title":"","content":"Asked here since it's relevant to both Mage and Beast (and possibly Vampire if Auspex 5 functions similarly to Mage's Psychic Projection): Are derived traits affected by the changed attributes in the Dream Form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:10:26-08:00","id":1056903,"title":"","content":"No.<br /> <br /> (Otherwise you'd halve your Willpower)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:18:35-08:00","id":1056912,"title":"","content":"That makes sense. I thought it would be so, but wanted to make sure I didn't assume anything. Thanks for the swift answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T06:46:14-08:00","id":1057068,"title":"","content":"If a spirit uses it's influences to directly create more of its Resonance (as in Influence 5 (frogs) being used to create frogs, for examples), can it get Essence from the increased Resonance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T07:32:08-08:00","id":1057081,"title":"","content":"Sure, though it would be best to do it in a way that would allow for more Essence created than consumed. A wind spirit might not be able to get much, if its wind dies after the duration. A fire spirits fire might spread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:34:28-08:00","id":1058497,"title":"","content":"More of a forum question, but what's the time limit before posting in a thread becomes thread necromancy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T11:37:41-08:00","id":1058500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1057081#post1057081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, though it would be best to do it in a way that would allow for more Essence created than consumed. A wind spirit might not be able to get much, if its wind dies after the duration. A fire spirits fire might spread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> actually, that leads to another question. is there anything in the rules saying that animals created temporarily using Influences are infertile? Cause I'm imagining an Influence-guided breeding program","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:11:57-08:00","id":1059000,"title":"","content":"I think they'd need to be male, because you can't keep a temporary creation going long enough to finish a pregnancy, but as long as the zygote had a few cells when it ended it should remain viable, since most of the proteins would only have been <i>templated</i> by dna that no longer exists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:22:52-08:00","id":1059030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1058500#post1058500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">actually, that leads to another question. is there anything in the rules saying that animals created temporarily using Influences are infertile?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. You might go by what Elfive said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:45:21-08:00","id":1059071,"title":"","content":"huh, so it's fertile, but the offspring will be monoploid mutants with half the mother's genes, and half of their children will be monoploid. That could fuel a few interesting plot hooks. Like Les Mysteres tries to save an endangered species and it goes horribly wrong","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T11:23:57-08:00","id":1059084,"title":"","content":"Well, I was actually thinking that only the <i>original</i> cell or two would lose half it's genes, because the way cells divide is just making more dna from protein that matches up with the existing strands.<br /> <br /> But hey, it's magic. Maybe some other weird shit could happen instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T14:01:13-08:00","id":1059187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1059084#post1059084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I was actually thinking that only the <i>original</i> cell or two would lose half it's genes, because the way cells divide is just making more dna from protein that matches up with the existing strands.<br /> <br /> But hey, it's magic. Maybe some other weird shit could happen instead.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> that also makes sense. but I feel like that DNA would be sympathetically connected to the original. could go either way","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T06:40:50-08:00","id":1060496,"title":"","content":"Do Mummies have blood?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T07:19:58-08:00","id":1060505,"title":"","content":"No. Just Sekhem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"ht