t a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T08:18:53-08:00","id":1060524,"title":"","content":"triple post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T08:24:43-08:00","id":1060527,"title":"","content":"I... think so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T10:40:15-08:00","id":1060569,"title":"","content":"The Unnatural Affinity Merit doesn't necessarily mean that the vampire is drinking the fuel stat from other supers. Rather, they probably drink directly from the victim's health (as long as the victim doesn't already contain Vitae). I think one point of Vitae for every Lethal dealt to or inflicted on the victim sounds reasonable for most supernaturals, but since it's not described in the Merit it's up to the ST to decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T10:50:16-08:00","id":1060574,"title":"","content":"Mummies are first edition, and Unnatural Affinity is a second edition one. If you were playing a first edition vampire, then they wouldn't need any special Merit to drink from mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T12:57:13-08:00","id":1060619,"title":"","content":"I'm really not familiar with MtC, but if mummies are brought back to life (or otherwise inhabit a living body) instead of being just reanimated bodies it'd be perfectly possible for vampires to drink their blood without Unnatural Affinity in 2E. But then they'd only get regular blood that needs to be converted to Vitae instead of blood that already counts as Vitae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T13:16:42-08:00","id":1060626,"title":"","content":"I'm confused. Can I do it or not? For the sake of sanity, let's say everyone in this situation is using the most recent rules applicable","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T13:21:04-08:00","id":1060631,"title":"","content":"I am 99% sure a vampire cannot drink Sekhem (or any other fuel stat) with Unnatural Affinity.However, a vampire with Unnatural Affinity for mummies can still drink from them and gain Vitae. But the Vitae does not come from their Sekhem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T13:32:50-08:00","id":1060639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1060626#post1060626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused. Can I do it or not? For the sake of sanity, let's say everyone in this situation is using the most recent rules applicable</div> </div> </div> </div>You can drink from 'living' mummies. This does not drink their Sekhem, it drinks their Health.<br /> <br /> You would need some sort of special ability to drain the power supply of other, non-Vampire supernatural beings, Unnatural Affinity doesn't do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T13:37:21-08:00","id":1060644,"title":"","content":"all i wanted was to see if a vamp could get sustenance from drinking a Mummy, so I guess I'm good here. Thanks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T18:21:56-07:00","id":1063066,"title":"","content":"I see that the Soul Loss rules from the God-Machine rules update is absent from Chronicles of Darkness. Only the first Condition is listed in the Appendix. How come? Were Enervated and Thrall deemed to harsh?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T18:51:36-07:00","id":1063076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1063066#post1063066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that the Soul Loss rules from the God-Machine rules update is absent from Chronicles of Darkness. Only the first Condition is listed in the Appendix. How come? Were Enervated and Thrall deemed to harsh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wordcount. Enervated and Thrall both still appear in Mage, but soul loss isn't super common outside of Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-15T18:58:32-07:00","id":1063077,"title":"","content":"It's a bit weird since GMC didn't have any rules for causing soul loss (that I've found) while CofD at least has one Dread Power that can cause it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T00:22:56-07:00","id":1065611,"title":"","content":"This is more for other gamelines, and is probably not too simple, but can the Empath and Support Network merits from Hurt Locker be used for the breaking points of supernatural beings? Vampires I could see it working for, Changelings too, but a Demon's cover break not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T06:16:43-07:00","id":1065709,"title":"","content":"Probably a case by case basis, but I would expect it to need modifications or work at a penalty.<br /> <br /> Alternatively there's a Monster AA style Tactic in the newest Mortal Remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T04:44:27-07:00","id":1066774,"title":"","content":"How should I read Services under Equipment section? Lets say my character has Athletics 3 and I use it to find Personal Trainer. Where does the +3 apply to? Athletics tests? After what time?<br /> Other one. Brawl. Self-defense classes seems to apply +1 to Brawl tests. What about Bodyguard? Is this also a +3 to Brawl tests when his with me?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:13:57-07:00","id":1067246,"title":"","content":"So, the DEC vaguely touched upon something I've (and my group, as it turned out when I voiced my opinion) found lacking in CofD material: Supernatural Rites that can be used by mortals. However, that was part of the Mummy era so it did not really touch upon Rites that can be used outside Mummy centric games.<br /> <br /> Outside of the ones listed as Open Rites in DCE (which included Binding, Exorcism, Summoning, and Warding from the core book), are there any other Rites (although probably not referred to as such in the books) that can be used by regular people without any supernatural abilities or help from any supernatural sponsors?<br /> I know of two, at least. Opening Graveyard Gate from Book of the Dead, and the Lure/Incantation stuff from Inferno to make deals with demons.<br /> <br /> Edit: If it's possible that a bunch of kids finds some obscure ritual in a weird book at the local library and decides to try it out and it actually works, then it's what I'm looking for. Of course, some rituals might include components that regular kids hopefully will be hesitant to acquire/perform.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Abjuration is actually not a Rite. 03-23-2017, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:26:46-07:00","id":1067252,"title":"","content":"Hunter probably has a few. We've been asking for something to boost the mortal Occult skill for a while. There's a few scattered across the books. Immortals, Skinchangers, Second Sight has more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T19:00:14-07:00","id":1067885,"title":"","content":"I went through some books during tonight's session and found that Witch Finders has some gutter magic rituals that can be performed by regular people. Unfortunately most mechanics seemed to be tied to the Gnosis Merit as I skimmed through it.<br /> Second Sight also had a section about rituals that seemed like they could be performed about anyone, but I didn't read much yet so I don't know if they're what I'm looking for or also tied to a minor template.<br /> How's Immortals and Skinchangers? I though the latter was about a (collection of) minor template(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-24-2017, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T19:59:15-07:00","id":1067894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1067885#post1067885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How's Immortals and Skinchangers? I though the latter was about a (collection of) minor template(s).</div> </div> </div> </div>Both have sections devoted to 'already created' templates, but Immortals has a fairly open customizable systems. The Blood Bather section in Immortals, for instance, revolves around people who slaughter others in order to remain youthful, but the system also allows for permanent Attribute increases, regeneration and resurrection. Without having a template. Body Thieves do have a template but you're still effectively human providing you end up in a human body.<br /> <br /> The Skin Thief is a template, and the book does have minor templates throughout, but it's easy to toss that aside and just have it as a ritual or magic object.<br /> <br /> The whole 'minor template' structure is needlessly limiting to begin with and I'm glad second edition has moved away from it in parts. Though at least because of it we don't have to deal with people posting mash-ups of however many mortal templates and insisting the entire game is broken because of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:13:30-07:00","id":1067901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1067246#post1067246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the DEC vaguely touched upon something I've (and my group, as it turned out when I voiced my opinion) found lacking in CofD material: Supernatural Rites that can be used by mortals. However, that was part of the Mummy era so it did not really touch upon Rites that can be used outside Mummy centric games.<br /> <br /> Outside of the ones listed as Open Rites in DCE (which included Binding, Exorcism, Summoning, and Warding from the core book), are there any other Rites (although probably not referred to as such in the books) that can be used by regular people without any supernatural abilities or help from any supernatural sponsors?<br /> I know of two, at least. Opening Graveyard Gate from Book of the Dead, and the Lure/Incantation stuff from Inferno to make deals with demons.<br /> <br /> Edit: If it's possible that a bunch of kids finds some obscure ritual in a weird book at the local library and decides to try it out and it actually works, then it's what I'm looking for. Of course, some rituals might include components that regular kids hopefully will be hesitant to acquire/perform.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, the Violent Skills section of <b>Chronicles of Darkness: Hurt Locker </b>mentions in the Occult section that anyone with the knowhow can make a basic charm that can do any number of things. The section explicitly calls out that you don't need Supernatural Merits to use the system. It mentions, as suggestions, boosting Stealth rolls against a supernatural creature, directly adding to the Damage Rating of a given weapon, and reducing the amount of Vitae a vampire could draw from the target's blood. It suggests basically allocating successes on a roll to various effects. As a general consideration, these charms last only for a day, but this can be extended with successes.<br /> <br /> If it were me, I'd probably tie it to the Equipment Building subsystem instead; trade dice penalties for effects instead of successes, sort of like Mage spell casting. Heck, if you were the kind of ST willing to push it a little further, you could even make it a kind of mortal thaumaturgy tied to ritual and esoteric paraphernalia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T20:54:42-07:00","id":1067912,"title":"","content":"If you want normal people enacting rituals, have ephemeral entities have bans related to certain actions that they may take (usually in a slasher flick logic) That's how I run it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T21:55:21-07:00","id":1067918,"title":"","content":"Ooh, Ritualistic Bans are indeed a lot of fun. I think there was a great section about them in the First Edition <b>Book of Spirits</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T04:05:13-07:00","id":1067956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1067894#post1067894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both have sections devoted to 'already created' templates, but Immortals has a fairly open customizable systems. The Blood Bather section in Immortals, for instance, revolves around people who slaughter others in order to remain youthful, but the system also allows for permanent Attribute increases, regeneration and resurrection. Without having a template.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they got a 2E update in DEC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1067912#post1067912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want normal people enacting rituals, have ephemeral entities have bans related to certain actions that they may take (usually in a slasher flick logic) That's how I run it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't quite understand. Could you explain further?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T11:22:13-07:00","id":1068055,"title":"","content":"I think they mean have the ritual be a specific series of actions that causes a spirit or ghost to have to do something. Presumably supernatural in nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T11:33:49-07:00","id":1068057,"title":"","content":"For instance, if you bury a human alive in the center of your corn fields, the spirit has to use its power to make sure they grow strong. Or if you throw a coin in the well, the spirit must bless you with luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T11:39:15-07:00","id":1068058,"title":"","content":"So basically finding out what a spirit's ban might be and just fulfil the conditions that trigger it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T11:48:42-07:00","id":1068062,"title":"","content":"Yes, providing the ban offers a beneficial option. Not all spirits have things like that, some might have something like, 'Can't kill someone wearing the color red,' or 'Cannot stop attacking someone wearing the color red.' Though obviously as a storyteller you can create how you want. When it does, though, it could probably end up creating a cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T13:26:40-07:00","id":1068079,"title":"","content":"&quot;The spirit of Mount Iliamna, a volcano in Alaska, will use its Numina to kill a victim named by anyone who makes it an offering of platinum that was mined from its foothills.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T13:59:02-07:00","id":1068087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1068079#post1068079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The spirit of Mount Iliamna, a volcano in Alaska, will use its Numina to kill a victim named by anyone who makes it an offering of platinum that was mined from its foothills.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that works. And by kill, it'd likely have the person be swallowed by the very earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T20:56:36-07:00","id":1068536,"title":"","content":"How much damage would you use to represent someone getting a hand or foot chopped off? How about for an arm or leg? Would you add more if it ripped or twisted off by pulling or getting by a fast-moving object? Also, would you need a new Persistent Condition to model having lost a limb, or do you think making Arm/Leg Wreck Persistent work well enough.<br /> <br /> Also what would the roll to chop off a limb with a long cutting instrument in combat look like? Does Cod have called shots? And would you add extra bashing damage per turns for the blood loss from the stump, considering the important arteries in those places?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T03:56:51-07:00","id":1068601,"title":"","content":"Persistent arm/leg wrack definitely covers missing limbs. That's one of the examples given for it. <br /> <br /> And yes, CoD does have called shots. They give a list of dice penalties for targeting specific body parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T05:27:23-07:00","id":1068621,"title":"","content":"Would you target the arm or the hand to cut off a hand? And unrelated, do you think a broken finger that's unusable is bashing damage or lethal damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T05:40:42-07:00","id":1068623,"title":"","content":"Target the arm to cut the arm off somewhere between the wrist and the elbow. If you target the hand you might cut off part of it along with most or all fingers. Directly aiming at the joint between the arm and the hand requires more finesse than can be expected during a combat situation. (Outside combat situations you wouldn't use Specified Targets and other combat rules.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T05:57:40-07:00","id":1068627,"title":"","content":"A broken finger would probably be Bashing damage, since it's not Lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T06:03:47-07:00","id":1068631,"title":"","content":"But even if the Bashing heals in an hour I'd have the finger be broken longer for regular humans. Vampires and werwolves would probably heal the bone as quick as the Bashing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T07:02:50-07:00","id":1068650,"title":"","content":"Isn't there an option in <b>Hurt Locker</b> where you can trade out damage for Trauma Conditions, and use the Condition to turn lasting Tilts into Beat engines, or was that just an ability of the micro-template The Plain? Describing damage is... odd... in the CofD since the level of damage doesn't necessarily equate to the amount of trauma. Take Vampires, for example, since they downgrade damage that would seriously injure a human. What is Lethal damage for a vampire would probably present as Aggravated on a human, so a vampire suffering Lethal damage has tissue flapping with the wind, missing chunks of flesh, etc, and if they have Resilience this gets <i>worse </i>since Active Resilience lets them ignore incoming damage even though it still hits, so you could have a vampire reduced to mostly a skeleton from sheer trauma and they would probably be mostly fine.<br /> <br /> It's also tonally relevant based on the game you're playing. For mortals, injuries should feel consequential, especially for Hunters. Fight smarter, not harder, avoid getting yourself laid out, because if your buddies need you on a hunt and you aren't 100% then they're screwed as much as you are. For a Vampire, even traumatic injury should feel trivial. If you're in combat and your opponent has blood, it doesn't matter how badly they've hurt you, if you can close the distance you can fix that <i>real </i>quick. For a Werewolf, injury should <i>piss you off</i>. Sure, even your average Werwolf, on death's door, would have pulled themselves together if they're beaten within an inch of their lives and left for dead within two hours, but that doesn't mean the trauma doesn't still <i>hurt</i>. It's easily fixed, especially if you have Essence to burn or the Gauru form in your back pocket (or even just a bigger form to take a bit of the edge off) but it's still an affront. A predator who gets injured by their prey is sloppy, or just plain bad at hunting.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And if it was Bashing Damage that inflicted a Tilt, I'd probably have it be something like a sprain or a really nasty hold as opposed to a break. At my martial arts club, we do a whole lot of practical training, and am I sore after getting thrown around on the floor? Yup. Does my arm basically become useless after a while? Definitely. Does this mean that I need a splint or a cast? Nope. I need a nap and some hot chocolate, but I'll be alright eventually. The main thing they teach you in martial arts, if you're planning on using it for self-defence, is that it doesn't matter how badly you hurt the person if they don't feel pain. Breaking something is <i>bad </i>unless you plan on destroying a limb, because adrenaline and anger means an opponent will ignore something as silly as pain or trauma.<br /> <br /> As my master says &quot;pain makes believers&quot;. You don't need to break a person's arm to get them to stop using it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 03-27-2017, 10:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T12:23:45-07:00","id":1070231,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I'm getting that tone is relevant here. still how much damage in one hit would you say would be enough to justify saying a human's arm got ripped off, possibly with different amounts for humans vs. supernaturals that don't pass out like Vampires.?<br /> <br /> Also, unrelated, but do LSD and Shrooms have Toxicity Ratings, or just penalties?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T14:07:43-07:00","id":1070286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1070231#post1070231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so I'm getting that tone is relevant here. still how much damage in one hit would you say would be enough to justify saying a human's arm got ripped off, possibly with different amounts for humans vs. supernaturals that don't pass out like Vampires.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aggravated damage in excess of stamina. Im still inviting everyone to contribute <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1062245-describing-wounds-and-pain\">here.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-29-2017, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T14:21:47-07:00","id":1070297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1070286#post1070286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aggravated damage in excess of stamina. Im still inviting everyone to contibute <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1062245-describing-wounds-and-pain\">here.</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> huh. Human body is pretty strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T14:47:30-07:00","id":1070313,"title":"","content":"Fun thing about fiction is that it exaggerates human ability to survive a lot of things, but at the same time, it also severely undersells it in many other aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T15:40:13-07:00","id":1070350,"title":"","content":"So the thing about broken bones is that there's a fair amount of variance in how bad a break is, and I would save major breaks for agg damage and gloss over minor ones. The difference between a cracked rib and one that's merely badly bruised isn't necessarily obvious, but the former takes forever to heal. Same with a jammed finger. I didn't realize I had actually broken mine until three weeks had passed it still ached, because the fracture was minor and didn't prevent me from using it. I thought it was just a jammed knuckle. That ambiguity can be your friend, an injury that might be a broken rib but is really a bad bruise can be lethal damage from a blunt weapon, or even bashing from a fall. Let the characters worry that injuries are more severe than the sheet indicates. Should help keep the tension while allowing you to dole out less crippling types of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T15:14:16-07:00","id":1070879,"title":"","content":"Something to consider is that, narratively, the wound may not be completely healed in the sense that it may cause discomfort or pain to utilize the anatomy, but mechanically you can. John McClain may have walked over glass in the beginning of the movie, but by it's end he clearly isn't crippled by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T09:28:08-07:00","id":1072047,"title":"","content":"So, I'm reading through <b>Hurt Locker </b>again, thinking of fiddling with some of the stuff I've been doing to update Mummy-style Cults into 2E using Violence Groups as a base and the Violent Skills section mentions that a given Violence Group has a number of Doors for Social Maneuvering &quot;equal to the sum of their Mental and Social Traits&quot;. How would you guys define that? The chapter says to treat average members as if they had two dots in every Attribute, which would mean every Violence Group would have the same number of Doors, but could it maybe mean taking the dice pools for average members that you have decided represent Mental and Social rolls and adding them together? Would you add dots in Organization Size to the total?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T14:05:29-07:00","id":1072171,"title":"","content":"Been searching for &quot;Chronicles of Darkness Agony Tilt&quot; around online, and &quot;Agony&quot; throughout the PDFs I have, nothing seems to detail the tilt. Thinking of taking the biting fighting style (as a Gangrel Vampire) but there's nothing describing this tilt anywhere (likewise for one of the Grapple Maneuvers)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T14:14:22-07:00","id":1072175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1072171#post1072171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been searching for &amp;quot;Chronicles of Darkness Agony Tilt&amp;quot; around online, and &amp;quot;Agony&amp;quot; throughout the PDFs I have, nothing seems to detail the tilt. Thinking of taking the biting fighting style (as a Gangrel Vampire) but there's nothing describing this tilt anywhere (likewise for one of the Grapple Maneuvers)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Agony Tilt was meant to be in Hurt Locker, but got left out accidentally for one reason or another. References to the Tilt got removed in the Errata phase, so if your PDF still contains them, you don't have the most up-to-date version, check DrivethruRPG for the final download. That said, David Hill, the book's developer, did post the Tilt on the forums <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1013866-hurt-locker?p=1036467#post1036467\">here</a> if you want to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T15:15:17-07:00","id":1072209,"title":"","content":"Are the published books updated, or is it just &quot;one run&quot; printed repeatedly? Thinking of getting a book or two but I'd have to print off FAQs and Erratas alongside them it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T15:19:56-07:00","id":1072211,"title":"","content":"The model is that they release one PDF, corrects some of the errors, then they release a final version of the PDF. The book is also the updated version and is released alongside the final PDF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T15:25:49-07:00","id":1072213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1072209#post1072209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the published books updated, or is it just &amp;quot;one run&amp;quot; printed repeatedly? Thinking of getting a book or two but I'd have to print off FAQs and Erratas alongside them it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books are initially released as &quot;advance PDFs&quot; before the full official publication. People who buy the advance PDFs can submit any errors they find to be revised during the errata phase, which usually lasts a few weeks. Once the errata submission period ends, they make any necessary changes and update DrivethruRPG's PDF file, and that is the version that can be ordered Print On Demand, and anyone who bought the advance PDF gets a discount on the Print On Demand copy to bring the total cost down to the same price as the PDF/POD combo bundle.<br /> <br /> Any errors that get missed during the errata submission period are unfortunately there in the POD for good. But, if your PDF has references to the Agony Tilt, you've got the advance PDF. Check your DrivethruRPG library, it should have been updated to the official, post-errata version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T09:52:44-07:00","id":1072583,"title":"","content":"Is that list of upcoming projects on the Onyx Path site still accurate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T10:00:42-07:00","id":1072591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1072583#post1072583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that list of upcoming projects on the Onyx Path site still accurate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you're talking about the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/schedule/\" target=\"_blank\">Current Projects page</a>? In terms of what projects are upcoming, yes. In terms of the dates listed, they have never been accurate in the first place. Note the disclaimer that the dates are statements of intent, and are subject to change. They change a lot. I would recommend not putting any stock in those dates whatsoever. Personally, I stopped even checking that page after watching Forsaken 2e get pushed back and pushed back until well over a year after the originally posted date, and the same happen with Mage 2e You get far more reliable (and far less disheartening) information from the Monday Meeting Notes, which is really the best source available for the most up-to-date information about OPPs projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-03-2017, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T10:15:46-07:00","id":1072603,"title":"","content":"Changeling 1e game it is<br /> <br /> So, then what is the current intended date for The Huntsman Chronicle if not this April?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T10:22:35-07:00","id":1072609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1072603#post1072603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling 1e game it is<br /> <br /> So, then what is the current intended date for The Huntsman Chronicle if not this April?</div> </div> </div> </div>When it's finished. Unfortunately that's the best we can tell. That's the best we can ever tell about upcoming OPP books, until they announce in a Monday Meeting Notes that it'll be out on Wednesday (new releases are always on Wednesdays and they usually let us know the Monday something is about to come out.<br /> <br /> For a very, very rough idea how far along a project is, check the Monday Meeting Notes development status section at the end of the blog post. We don't know how long any given step in the project might take, but we do know how many steps there are. Changeling 2e is currently in the Development step, which means it still needs to go through Editing and Art Direction before it's ready to release. We don't know how long any of those will take, but no point in getting hyped for it beckre it's in the last step.<br /> <br /> That said, if you want to play Changeling, note that there is a ton of 2e material available for open playtest - easily enough to run a game with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-03-2017, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T10:36:08-07:00","id":1072613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1072609#post1072609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When it's finished. Unfortunately that's the best we can tell. That's the best we can ever tell about upcoming OPP books, until they announce in a Monday Meeting Notes that it'll be out on Wednesday (new releases are always on Wednesdays and they usually let us know the Monday something is about to come out.<br /> <br /> For a very, very rough idea how far along a project is, check the Monday Meeting Notes development status section at the end of the blog post. We don't know how long any given step in the project might take, but we do know how many steps there are. Changeling 2e is currently in the Development step, which means it still needs to go through Editing and Art Direction before it's ready to release. We don't know how long any of those will take, but no point in getting hyped for it beckre it's in the last step.<br /> <br /> That said, if you want to play Changeling, note that there is a ton of 2e material available for open playtest - easily enough to run a game with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A lot of it references Page &quot;XX&quot; though, which i assume to mean unrevealed stuff. It is pretty full, but I'm new to Game Mastering and that missing stuff makes me nervous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T10:49:51-07:00","id":1072618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1072613#post1072613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of it references Page &amp;quot;XX&amp;quot; though, which i assume to mean unrevealed stuff. It is pretty full, but I'm new to Game Mastering and that missing stuff makes me nervous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page XX is just the stand in they use for page numbers prior to layout. So, let's say in talking about Clarity, there is mention of Seeming blessings, since those give you a way to increase Clarity. They might want to give a page number to refer back to Seeming blessings. Even though Seemings and their blessings have already been previewed, they don't know what page it's going to be on because the pages haven't been laid out yet, so they reference Page XX instead. Once the book has been laid out and the pages finalized, they can go back through and replace all references to Page XX with the proper page number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T04:24:02-07:00","id":1073664,"title":"","content":"In the supernatural equipment section of the GMC book, there's an Energy Meter. It talks about how it's different from EMF in that it only detects supernatural locations charged with energy, but then the mechanics at the end say to choose an unseen sense associated with a creature? Which is it supposed to be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T07:37:12-07:00","id":1073714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1073664#post1073664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the supernatural equipment section of the GMC book, there's an Energy Meter. It talks about how it's different from EMF in that it only detects supernatural locations charged with energy, but then the mechanics at the end say to choose an unseen sense associated with a creature? Which is it supposed to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>An EMF detector pinpoints the specific location of a ghost, but is not 100% reliable (hence the dice roll). An Energy Meter detects the presence of a particular kind of entity in a general area and works automatically with no chance of failure, but can't determine precisely where the entity is. The latter is exactly how the Unseen Sense Merit works. So the two statements don't contradict each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T08:18:42-07:00","id":1073730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1073714#post1073714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An EMF detector pinpoints the specific location of a ghost, but is not 100% reliable (hence the dice roll). An Energy Meter detects the presence of a particular kind of entity in a general area and works automatically with no chance of failure, but can't determine precisely where the entity is. The latter is exactly how the Unseen Sense Merit works. So the two statements don't contradict each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they do. The energy meter talks about a location up until the unseen sense comment. Nothing about creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T08:31:09-07:00","id":1073733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1073730#post1073730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes they do. The energy meter talks about a location up until the unseen sense comment. Nothing about creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and when you know there is a ghost in a house but not where in the house the ghost is, what you have detected is not a ghost but a haunted house. Like the Unseen Sense Merit, Energy Meters tell you when the type of creature they are attuned to is in a general area, thereby detecting a location which contains that creature, not the creature itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-05-2017, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T08:46:57-07:00","id":1073740,"title":"","content":"I believe Charlaquin is correct in that it's the intended description, but the rules text is not very clear about it. The fluffy part of the text talks about locations as if it would detect locations specifically while the crunchy part of the text explains that it detects creatures and entities in a way that can be completely unrelated to the location.<br /> <br /> Edit: It's like saying the EMF Detector detects a location where a Numen is used when it actually just detects that a Numen is used. If one of them can be said to detect locations then the other also does that, but the Energy Meter text says that it detects locations <i>unlike</i> the EMF Detector. No wonder there's confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-05-2017, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:28:37-07:00","id":1073762,"title":"","content":"If you want something that more reflects the fluff I'd have it ping whenever in a location that houses a Manifestation Condition (Anchor/Infrastructure, Open, Controlled) relating to a specific type of ephemeral entity, or otherwise is mystically connected to that type of entity (for example Avernian Gates for ghosts, or a place that has seen repeated sacrifices to angels).<br /> I left out Resonant since my understanding is that basically everything is Resonant to some kind of spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-05-2017, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T18:59:35-07:00","id":1073975,"title":"","content":"That's fair. I just think it's rather inconsistent and was wondering what the actual -intent- was. That said, it's not too hard to say both types of energy meters could be a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T19:52:48-07:00","id":1073992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1073975#post1073975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fair. I just think it's rather inconsistent and was wondering what the actual -intent- was. That said, it's not too hard to say both types of energy meters could be a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I definitely see what you mean. I think the intent is supposed to be that Energy Meters tell you without fail when a general area has a supernatural presence in it, but only a particular sort of supernatural presence. One might detect if a building is haunted but not by how many ghosts or where they are, and not if it's home to a spirit or an angel. Another might tell you if a patch of forest is home to werewolves but not if a particular person there is a werewolf and not if there's a Cryptid there. And strictly speaking that is not identical to the way Unseen Sense functions, but it's certainly similar in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T10:11:02-07:00","id":1074726,"title":"","content":"Reading through the CoD Core and want to clarify something. Merits are flat cost, correct? You pay one experience per dot?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T10:36:26-07:00","id":1074740,"title":"","content":"Yes.<br /> <br /> ......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T10:41:31-07:00","id":1074743,"title":"","content":"how about for skills post character creation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T10:49:24-07:00","id":1074749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1074743#post1074743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how about for skills post character creation?</div> </div> </div> </div>2 Experiences per dot. Everything in 2e is flat cost, nothing is ever &quot;x New Dot&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T11:07:52-07:00","id":1074753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1074749#post1074749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2 Experiences per dot. Everything in 2e is flat cost, nothing is ever &quot;x New Dot&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is much better. So, same goes for all the splats' supernatural powers?<br /> <br /> Also, not fully sure i understand, so here's an example of what's confusing me. If I have Computer 2 and want to raise it to Computer 3 during the game, do I need 2 xp or 6 xp (and then 8 xp for the next one)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T11:33:41-07:00","id":1074764,"title":"","content":"It would cost 2 XP. That's what flat cost means. And yes, it also applies to any supernatural powers in 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T13:02:18-07:00","id":1074833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1074753#post1074753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is much better. So, same goes for all the splats' supernatural powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>Same for literally everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1074753#post1074753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, not fully sure i understand, so here's an example of what's confusing me. If I have Computer 2 and want to raise it to Computer 3 during the game, do I need 2 xp or 6 xp (and then 8 xp for the next one)?</div> </div> </div> </div>2 xp. And 2 xp for the next one and 2 xp for the one after that. Xp costs are never multiplied by the number of dots in second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T02:40:52-07:00","id":1075051,"title":"","content":"So, General Supernatural Merits. it says that they are generally for humans (considering most Major Templates have similar stuff) but I've been wondering. Can Mages/Essentially Human Supernaturals get them? I mean, the rulebook says that it depends on the ST and Chronicle but generally speaking can i make a Psychokinetic Mage without dipping into Force at chargen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T03:20:04-07:00","id":1075059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1075051#post1075051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, General Supernatural Merits. it says that they are generally for humans (considering most Major Templates have similar stuff) but I've been wondering. Can Mages/Essentially Human Supernaturals get them? I mean, the rulebook says that it depends on the ST and Chronicle but generally speaking can i make a Psychokinetic Mage without dipping into Force at chargen?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's intended, but the game doesn't stop if you do. It would also really depend what exactly psychic powers are in your setting. A mage having access to some God-machine infrastructure that allows psychic powers unrelated to their magic could be fun. Just giving a mage a merit to do something they could probably do otherwise anyway is kinda pointless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T13:19:20-07:00","id":1075227,"title":"","content":"So, Medium's fluff at the start talks about the words and moans of the dead, but it then talks about ephemeral beings in general and lets you mess with all three of the base conditions for the different ephemera types (in the core). Can they hear all ephemera, or just ghosts, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T18:04:25-07:00","id":1075315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1075227#post1075227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Medium's fluff at the start talks about the words and moans of the dead, but it then talks about ephemeral beings in general and lets you mess with all three of the base conditions for the different ephemera types (in the core). Can they hear all ephemera, or just ghosts, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd recommend picking a variety and adding a dot to the cost for each extra type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T09:28:36-07:00","id":1075500,"title":"","content":"I think they can hear all ephemera. It's just that a mortal Medium isn't going to know the difference between ghosts, spirits, and other ephemera. They'd probably just think they're all the same thing with different levels of crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T23:07:23-07:00","id":1079691,"title":"","content":"So, uh, another question. For the number of attribute dots that ephemera get, does it count a free dot in each category?<br /> <br /> I figured I'd check by looking at examples, but my god onyx path clearly didn't even GLANCE at the rank chart when making their own NPCs in the core. There's a rank 2 and rank 3 angel <i>right next to each other</i> that both have 14 total dots, for instance, and they can't both be right since there's no blending between the rank and attribute correspondence. There's also a Rank 1 angel with 4/4/3, and then a rank 2 with 4/3/2. Clearly nobody double checked that section.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately the ghost in the same book and the example spirits in the wolf book are all firmly in the center of the ranges and could be either. So, uh, which is right? Do you count the first dot or no?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 04-17-2017, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-17T02:59:26-07:00","id":1079732,"title":"","content":"No, they should not get free dots. Otherwise a maxed Rank 5 ephemeral would have 3 Attribute dots more than they would be able to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T06:45:02-07:00","id":1080296,"title":"","content":"Some questions about Merits. <br /> <br /> Does Fighting Finesse apply to grapples, and under what circumstances does it?<br /> <br /> Does Interdisciplinary Specialty and Area of Expertise stack?<br /> <br /> And how focused must a Specialty be? Can I have a Shadows specialty or does it have to be In the Dark instead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T07:19:37-07:00","id":1080304,"title":"","content":"1. If you have Fighting Finesse tagged to a Specialty on Grappling on the Brawl skill you may use the effects of Fighting Finesse on all Brawl rolls where the Grappling Specialty applies.<br /> 2. Yes.<br /> 3. It depends on what your group finds reasonable. There's no hard rules on how focused a Specialty can be. However, I recommend looking at the examples (starting at page 31 in Chronicles of Darkness) to get a sense of what the devs intended.<br /> Edit: I'd personally allow either example (and apply both on the same situations), but only one of them because of the overlap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-18-2017, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T07:55:36-07:00","id":1080315,"title":"","content":"Does carpenting fall under Crafts or Expression?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T08:18:13-07:00","id":1080329,"title":"","content":"Crafts. Unless you're, I suppose, trying to make some wooden piece of art that expresses something or attempts to instill something in others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T08:21:30-07:00","id":1080333,"title":"","content":"Do Gauntlets fall under Brawl or Weaponry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T08:25:49-07:00","id":1080335,"title":"","content":"Brass Knuckles use Brawl so I'd imagine Gauntlets do as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T09:23:56-07:00","id":1080374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DArchon5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1080315#post1080315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does carpenting fall under Crafts or Expression?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's a useful quote for this in the core CofD book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In general,<br /> Crafts should be used when you are trying to make some-<br /> thing that is accurate (a scale model, an eye-witness sketch,<br /> or a reconstruction of a damaged manuscript) or useful for<br /> a specific task, as opposed to something that is being created<br /> to be beautiful or convey emotion. </div> </div> </div>And:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is some overlap between this Skill and the Crafts<br /> Skill. Expression is generally used when trying to create a piece<br /> of artwork specifically for aesthetic or emotional reasons, as op-<br /> posed to making an accurate copy or model, which uses Crafts. </div> </div> </div>Under the write-ups for Craft and Expression respectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T21:16:45-07:00","id":1080732,"title":"","content":"Are Range Bands from Hurt Locker supposed to be a &quot;new standard&quot; to which future rules will default to, or is it a purely one shot optional hack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-18T21:55:36-07:00","id":1080742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1080732#post1080732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Range Bands from Hurt Locker supposed to be a &quot;new standard&quot; to which future rules will default to, or is it a purely one shot optional hack?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it's just a one shot optional hack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T00:32:33-07:00","id":1080770,"title":"","content":"They might be a standard in CofD 2.0 just like many of the Armory Reloaded hacks landed in CofD. But we have at least 5 years before that happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T09:39:31-07:00","id":1080945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1080770#post1080770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They might be a standard in CofD 2.0 just like many of the Armory Reloaded hacks landed in CofD. But we have at least 5 years before that happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume by CofD 2.0 you mean a hypothetical 3rd edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-19T10:30:21-07:00","id":1080966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1080945#post1080945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I assume by CofD 2.0 you mean a hypothetical 3rd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. A very, very distant new edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T08:23:34-07:00","id":1082624,"title":"","content":"how much damage does sulfuric Acid do ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T08:41:33-07:00","id":1082631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1082624#post1082624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how much damage does sulfuric Acid do ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the core book includes rules for acid damage. I'd probably repurpose the rules for fire damage. Assign a size and an acidity (instead of heat), add together the damage from each, and deal this much damage per turn until the acid is washed off. Maybe have the Size reduce by a point per turn automatically instead of requiring the character to use an action to stop drop and roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T09:03:04-07:00","id":1082641,"title":"","content":"There is the chemical fire type of fire, which makes absolutely no sense since all fires are chemical processes. That might actually refer to corrosive materials that give chemical burns. But I'd recommend Charlaquin's suggestion anytime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T10:59:46-07:00","id":1082711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1082631#post1082631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think the core book includes rules for acid damage. I'd probably repurpose the rules for fire damage. Assign a size and an acidity (instead of heat), add together the damage from each, and deal this much damage per turn until the acid is washed off. Maybe have the Size reduce by a point per turn automatically instead of requiring the character to use an action to stop drop and roll.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wanted to know because I wanted a character to keep someone on him in a ampoule that says holy water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T04:57:00-07:00","id":1083918,"title":"","content":"I have a question about movement during combat:<br /> The books say a character can move their speed and still do an instant action. Is there an order to how these need to be performed? Can a character move a bit, take an action, then move some more? Can they do an action and then move?<br /> <br /> I was also wondering about movement when it comes to ranged weapons in close combat. Since using a large firearm (like a rifle) in close combat is penalized and there doesn't seem to be an equivalent of an &quot;attack of opportunity&quot; when moving away from close combat, is there anything in RAW that prevents a character from just walking away from a melee attacker on their turn and then shooting? So the defense bonus the target would get is nullified if the shooter just walks away?<br /> <br /> Of course since there is no such thing as &quot;turn based combat&quot; IRL, I would rule that a melee combatant moves with it's target, but still I feel like there might be some issues with this if a player wants to exploit this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13318,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","user":"Cainite","date":". 04-26-2017, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T07:31:34-07:00","id":1083963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1083918#post1083918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books say a character can move their speed and still do an instant action. Is there an order to how these need to be performed? Can a character move a bit, take an action, then move some more? Can they do an action and then move?</div> </div> </div> </div>In going with the lack of 'turn based combat' I think it would be seen more as moving while shooting. Yes you can do so. I thought there was a Merit that allowed this, but a brief check says no so I believe it's something anyone can do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was also wondering about movement when it comes to ranged weapons in close combat. Since using a large firearm (like a rifle) in close combat is penalized and there doesn't seem to be an equivalent of an &quot;attack of opportunity&quot; when moving away from close combat, is there anything in RAW that prevents a character from just walking away from a melee attacker on their turn and then shooting? So the defense bonus the target would get is nullified if the shooter just walks away? </div> </div> </div>Nothing but the obvious, like Grapple or Delayed Actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:15:32-07:00","id":1084720,"title":"","content":"Can the Miracle Dread power replicate the Resurrection Numina?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:32:09-07:00","id":1084732,"title":"","content":"Well, it's a little more powerful than the example uses of Miracle, but Dread Powers are just examples and guidelines. You could use Miracle to resurrect someone or just come up with a whole new Resurrection Dread Power. And if you want to adhere to published rules there's the Numen Dread Power that can replicate any Numina, including Resurrection.<br /> Either way I'd personally include a steeper drawback regardless of how I do it. Letting the resurrected subject come back wrong, or requiring a soul (your own or someone else's) in order to activate the Dread Power. But you might not be quite as sadistic as me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T13:39:17-07:00","id":1085567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1084732#post1084732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it's a little more powerful than the example uses of Miracle, but Dread Powers are just examples and guidelines. You could use Miracle to resurrect someone or just come up with a whole new Resurrection Dread Power. And if you want to adhere to published rules there's the Numen Dread Power that can replicate any Numina, including Resurrection.<br /> Either way I'd personally include a steeper drawback regardless of how I do it. Letting the resurrected subject come back wrong, or requiring a soul (your own or someone else's) in order to activate the Dread Power. But you might not be quite as sadistic as me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a horror game. You are exactly the right amount of sadistic. I was thinking more Pet Sematary than Easter story anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T14:12:56-07:00","id":1085580,"title":"","content":"Do endowments that give you powers, like the Knights of Saint George and the Lucifuge, make you a Sleepwalker?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T19:36:20-07:00","id":1085657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage: the Awakening Second Edition Sleepwalker Merit, p. 306</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character is immune to the Curse, causes no Dissonance, and follows the other guidelines for Sleepwalkers in this section. <b>This Merit is not necessary for a character with any other Supernatural Merit involving an internal power, or any supernatural template.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Castigations are an internal power, drawn out from your infernal bloodline. Definitely count. I'd count applied occult knowledge too, which would cover the Goetic Gospels and the Benedictions.<br /> <br /> In general, I would suggest the only published Endowments that wouldn't qualify would be Advanced Armory, Relic, and the compact Endowments in Compacts &amp; Conspiracies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T12:18:51-07:00","id":1085846,"title":"","content":"Assume you want to stat up a Competent FBI Agent PC using normal mortal chargen and no Experience. What kind of Attributes, Merits, skill buys and Persistent Conditions would fit the build?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T12:42:01-07:00","id":1085851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1085846#post1085846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assume you want to stat up a Competent FBI Agent PC using normal mortal chargen and no Experience. What kind of Attributes, Merits, skill buys and Persistent Conditions would fit the build?</div> </div> </div> </div>Attributes: Rounded. Dexterity and Wits 3 are important since so many Merits have those as prerequisites, but otherwise I'd just say don't leave any Attribute with a single dot.<br /> <br /> Skills: At least one dot in Academics, Computer, Medicine, Athletics, Brawl, Drive, Stealth, Intimidation and Persuasion. If you have points over you could add some more into these. They are probably common Skills, but not something every agent needs to focus on.<br /> Skills that all agents should have more than one dot in are Investigation, Firearms and Empathy.<br /> <br /> Merits: Quick Draw (handguns) and Professional Training (Investigaiton, Firearms and Empathy as Asset Skills). Maybe Language (Spanish) depending on what state the agent's in the most.<br /> A few dots spread over a few fighting styles such as Firefight, Grappling, Marksmanship, Martial Arts and Police Tactics depending on the agent's training and focus. There might be other fitting styles in Hurt Locker.<br /> Allies, Contacts, and Resources are Merits that should be granted by the job so it's up for the ST to say if you need to buy them or if you character gets them from backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T12:50:59-07:00","id":1085854,"title":"","content":"It's going to depend on what kind of agent they are. A hostage rescue agent is going to have a vastly different set of skills than an intelligence analyst, and both from a forensic examiner.<br /> <br /> The FBI hires a lot of people with a wide range of skillsets, which is the point.<br /> <br /> At the least a special agent would have no 1s in Physical or Mental Attributes, a decent amount of Academics, at least 1 in Drive, Firearms, Weaponry.<br /> <br /> Tales from the 13th Precinct has 'minimum criteria' for things like cadets at police academy and detectives. If you're going for more of the media-driven idea of an FBI agent you might go with their detective minimums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T11:22:50-07:00","id":1087243,"title":"","content":"What should the roll be for hotwiring a car? My first thought is either Dex + Streetwise or Crafts. And should it be extended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T11:27:22-07:00","id":1087246,"title":"","content":"Dexterity + Larceny.<br /> <br /> As for extended actions, I'd let it be an instant action if the character has a moment to do it, but an extended action if the situation calls for combat time. E.g. if people are firing at your group and you need to hotwire it in order to escape. One roll per turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 05-03-2017, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T12:10:01-07:00","id":1087275,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Larceny is kind of the go-to Skill for doing illegal things.<br /> <br /> As for Instant vs. Extended, my opinion is that Extended actions should be used when there is a visible cost associated with each roll. For example, if there is some kind of ticking clock - the cops are on their way and will arrive in five turns so you have to finish hotwiring the car so you can make your getaway before then - then time is the cost. Alternatively, if each attempt costs a limited resource. Otherwise, use an Instant action.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T13:54:27-07:00","id":1087329,"title":"","content":"*facepalm* how could i forget larceny? Dexterity + Larceny then? or Intelligence + Larceny?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-03T14:12:27-07:00","id":1087334,"title":"","content":"Larceny is an easy Skill to forget. It's more of a collection of separate skills more than anything else.<br /> I'd say Dex. The knowledge of how to do so is part of the Skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T05:27:44-07:00","id":1087632,"title":"","content":"Wait is Defense in 2E calculated as the higher of (Wits) and (Dexterity + Athletics), or the higher of (Wits +Athletics) and (Dexterity +Athletics)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12398-darchon5","name":"DArchon5","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T05:46:21-07:00","id":1087637,"title":"","content":"The <b>Lower</b> of (Wits + Athletics) and (Dexterity + Athletics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T05:56:00-07:00","id":1087641,"title":"","content":"You're not wrong, but technically it's the (lower of Wits and Dexterity) plus Athletics (or Weaponry or Brawl if you have the correct Merit and choose to use the other Skill). Doesn't matter, though, since it's the same result.<br /> <br /> However, animals and ephemeral entities of Rank 1 use the higher because of their animalistic instincts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-04T08:33:10-07:00","id":1087715,"title":"","content":"And also werewolves with a particular merit in their canine forms, but we're getting into edge cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T06:14:44-07:00","id":1091924,"title":"","content":"So Armory would lead me to believe if you lose 10-agains, you lose 9 or 8-agains as well.<br /> Is this still true? a la Covert Operative from Hurt Locker. Everybody has Trained Observer, I think it's been houseruled that you only lose 1 <i>level</i> of it. So if something would deny you 10-against you go from 8-agains to 9-agains.<br /> <br /> What's the correct (2E) way of handling this? I would think if you can't even get 10-agains on the roll, anything else should be forfeit since the effect is essentially &quot;don't reroll, what you get is what you get.&quot; with the &quot;natural language&quot; bs people creatively interpret to fit their whim :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T06:24:50-07:00","id":1091927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1091924#post1091924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Armory would lead me to believe if you lose 10-agains, you lose 9 or 8-agains as well.<br /> Is this still true? a la Covert Operative from Hurt Locker. Everybody has Trained Observer, I think it's been houseruled that you only lose 1 <i>level</i> of it. So if something would deny you 10-against you go from 8-agains to 9-agains.<br /> <br /> What's the correct (2E) way of handling this? I would think if you can't even get 10-agains on the roll, anything else should be forfeit since the effect is essentially &amp;quot;don't reroll, what you get is what you get.&amp;quot; with the &amp;quot;natural language&amp;quot; bs people creatively interpret to fit their whim :/</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ironic, because your interpretation is a natural one, not a technical one. Under a technical reading, if you have 9-again and lose 10-again, you would still reroll 9s, since 10-again only says you get to reroll 10s. Technically speaking, losing that ability wouldn't cause you to lose the ability to reroll 9s. Your &quot;what you get is what you get&quot; interpretation is creative, but not supported by a strict technical reading of the rules.<br /> <br /> That said, your interpretation is the correct one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T10:17:49-07:00","id":1093691,"title":"","content":"With Influence: Disease 4 . Could a spirit infect a human with a disese for a few minutes. If another person gets infected from patien 0, would they still have the disese and spread it further?<br /> Im guessing this is the case right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T11:21:28-07:00","id":1093712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1093691#post1093691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Influence: Disease 4 . Could a spirit infect a human with a disese for a few minutes. If another person gets infected from patien 0, would they still have the disese and spread it further?<br /> Im guessing this is the case right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue no. The disease was created temporarily. When the Duration expires, the disease created in this way should cease to exist. If the patient zero spreads the disease to another patient, it is still the same disease, they just both have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:36:31-07:00","id":1093745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1093712#post1093712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue no. The disease was created temporarily. When the Duration expires, the disease created in this way should cease to exist. If the patient zero spreads the disease to another patient, it is still the same disease, they just both have it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see that i wrote something else from what i meant. In the example, would the other patients have the disease after the duration.<br /> <br /> Like this: Influence 4 creates a disease in patient Zero, its duration is just a few minutes. But its a very virulent disease and Patient zero spreads it to Patient 1, 2 and 3.<br /> After a few minutes, patient Zero is now free from the disease, though i would argue Patient 1,2 and 3 are still infected.<br /> <br /> I'd argue that it's the same if you switch out Influence Disease to Influence Fire. If you create a flame out of thin air with it, that flame would seize to exist after the duration, but not the torches lit from it, they would burn on, on their own.<br /> <br /> And if im wrong, what good is influence at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:42:55-07:00","id":1093750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1093745#post1093745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue that it's the same if you switch out Influence Disease to Influence Fire. If you create a flame out of thin air with it, that flame would seize to exist after the duration, but not the torches lit from it, they would burn on, on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The difference there is that objects burn on their own when heated, but people won't have the disease on their own. The effects of the disease <b>would</b> last after the duration, if some one coughed so hard it tore their lungs, they would still have the damage after the disease is gone, if it gave them pocks they may be scarred, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1093745#post1093745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if im wrong, what good is influence at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't use Influence to Create a disease for a short time, use it to Strengthen a disease for a long time. Make the flu more deadly, or make a hard to spread disease easier to spread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:48:09-07:00","id":1093755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1093750#post1093750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The difference there is that objects burn on their own when heated, but people won't have the disease on their own. The effects of the disease <b>would</b> last after the duration, if some one coughed so hard it tore their lungs, they would still have the damage after the disease is gone, if it gave them pocks they may be scarred, etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Don't use Influence to Create a disease for a short time, use it to Strengthen a disease for a long time. Make the flu more deadly, or make a hard to spread disease easier to spread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So it really comes down to semantics, if the influence would've been &quot;influence : Viruses&quot; it would be fine, cus of virus reproduction inside of living host cells. Wheras influence Disease would just be the symptoms then from that standing.<br /> <br /> The other ideas are pretty good though and i've must say I looked way past them. Leprosy for example with some strenghen on it so it can spread is pretty mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:57:12-07:00","id":1093759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1093755#post1093755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> So it really comes down to semantics, if the influence would've been &quot;influence : Viruses&quot; it would be fine, cus of virus reproduction inside of living host cells. Wheras influence Disease would just be the symptoms then from that standing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually just contemplating the semantics myself. In a different way though. &quot;Disease&quot; isn't a very good word in this case since it doesn't actually refer to a &quot;thing&quot; as much as a categorization of phenomena. <br /> <br /> I don't recall if Created things can reproduce and if so if the offspring last longer than Duration. If it works for a Created rabbit then it works for a virus; if not then not.<br /> <br /> Same would apply to bacteria and fungus and such as well.<br /> <br /> It would also depend on the being with Influence and what their mind space is like. Do they really work on the level of Virus vs Bacteria? Or are they just a Spirit of Disease? I think that's the most important thing to consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T14:12:00-07:00","id":1093803,"title":"","content":"There are viral spirits. And they're as weird as they should be, just like real viruses.<br /> <br /> I think it'd spread.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, you could just have a Numen to inflict the disease, and the spirit use its Influence to control where it goes, or weaken victims or strengthen the disease to make it spread faster. If the spirit were able to interact with the targets in person, you wouldn't even necessarily need that, the nature of the spirit itself might be enough to infect a person on being hit. Though thinking about it you should probably represent that, mechanically, with a Numen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-17-2017, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T20:58:49-07:00","id":1093974,"title":"","content":"Does the Aggressive Meme Numen spread only through in person verbal communication, or does it also work through phones, writing and such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T21:01:15-07:00","id":1093975,"title":"","content":"I'm not convinced a disease created with Create Disease would actually come with the attendant virus or bacteria. In the same way that fire created with Create Fire doesn't come with the attendant fuel source.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T06:18:38-07:00","id":1094102,"title":"","content":"I have a question about Open Rites and Open Rite Mastery:<br /> <br /> Do you buy Open Rite Mastery for <i>each </i>open rite or once bought it applies to every open rite you can perform? I have tried in several Mummy forums, but people dont seem to lurk in those often.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T07:55:59-07:00","id":1094127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1093975#post1093975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not convinced a disease created with Create Disease would actually come with the attendant virus or bacteria. In the same way that fire created with Create Fire doesn't come with the attendant fuel source.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that was my thought as well. A Spirit of Viruses with Influence: Viruses would Create actual viruses and not just the results, but Create Disease I agree would just manifest the disease without cause.<br /> <br /> Which still has its uses, the doctors examining the patients would see all the symptoms they expect but culture tests would come back negative, the cause of death would be unknown, things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T17:15:06-07:00","id":1103331,"title":"","content":"Here's a question. Is it really necessary to use the Armoury Prototype rules to upgrade firearms? I was hoping to make a Firearms or Crafts roll to either manufacture higher precision tolerance gun parts or otherwise augment existing weapons for better attributes. My character is a master marksman (4 firearms, both Firefight style and Marksman maxed) and on top of that a vampire with a couple favours owed in the current game.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of taking an Assault Rifle and giving it either one more damage, a die bonus, or even just a better range - also modding a rifle for a tad more damage and/or a die bonus similar to sighting in. He has a reloading/firearms bench in his Haven and 2 Crafts.<br /> <br /> Rules as written I could make a couple simplistic augmentations with 2 Crafts (professional level) by taking the difference as a penalty.<br /> For precision fabrication if required, I have 4 resources and an Arms Dealer contact familiar with Carthians which might be easier.<br /> <br /> The damage mod can be most easily explained by changing the chamber and barrel out for a higher cal. Ideally the initiative penalty goes down too (either lightweight composite materials or otherwise making it easier to handle or collapsible/folding perhaps)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 06-13-2017, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T18:30:42-07:00","id":1103349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1103331#post1103331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question. Is it really necessary to use the Armoury Prototype rules to upgrade firearms? I was hoping to make a Firearms or Crafts roll to either manufacture higher precision tolerance gun parts or otherwise augment existing weapons for better attributes. My character is a master marksman (4 firearms, both Firefight style and Marksman maxed) and on top of that a vampire with a couple favours owed in the current game.<br /> <br /> I was thinking of taking an Assault Rifle and giving it either one more damage, a die bonus, or even just a better range - also modding a rifle for a tad more damage and/or a die bonus similar to sighting in. He has a reloading/firearms bench in his Haven and 2 Crafts.<br /> <br /> Rules as written I could make a couple simplistic augmentations with 2 Crafts (professional level) by taking the difference as a penalty.<br /> For precision fabrication if required, I have 4 resources and an Arms Dealer contact familiar with Carthians which might be easier.<br /> <br /> The damage mod can be most easily explained by changing the chamber and barrel out for a higher cal. Ideally the initiative penalty goes down too (either lightweight composite materials or otherwise making it easier to handle or collapsible/folding perhaps)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you kind of answered your own question here, but you could use the crafting rules from the CofD core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T13:38:17-07:00","id":1103599,"title":"","content":"It's more, how in depth do I need to explain every little detail? Could I give a gun 8-agains (-2 to the roll for 9 agains then 8 agains) is it limited to just raising the damage / lowering the initiative modifier? In the context of firearms and weapons at what point is it expected (as in the norm, not some hardcore or super lax game) that you tediously explain every step of the process in order to justify the roll? What limitations are there to modding/crafting/upgrading?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T08:39:35-07:00","id":1103819,"title":"","content":"Does meditative mind apply to one or more resolve composure rolls in a day? The merit says any but with the standard rules of meditation I'm not certain if that instance of any is singular or plural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T19:40:54-07:00","id":1104120,"title":"","content":"To add to the question above, does Meditation grant any benefits for supernatural creatures, who don't suffer the typical integrity breaks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T09:17:31-07:00","id":1104322,"title":"","content":"I dunno the official stance but Ive always ruled that it does, since it's still a breaking point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T12:55:51-07:00","id":1104831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1104322#post1104322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno the official stance but Ive always ruled that it does, since it's still a breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a few places where it specifically says you can substitute Humanity or Wisdom, etc. for Integrity - particularly for Hard Leverage iirc. and other things (like meditation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T14:24:30-07:00","id":1104860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1104831#post1104831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a few places where it specifically says you can substitute Humanity or Wisdom, etc. for Integrity - particularly for Hard Leverage iirc. and other things (like meditation).</div> </div> </div> </div>Its more how it adds to a resolve composure roll rather than a breaking point but I do see your point for the supernatural morality stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-17T15:26:20-07:00","id":1104879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1104860#post1104860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its more how it adds to a resolve composure roll rather than a breaking point but I do see your point for the supernatural morality stats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I rule that it applys to Breaking Points against variant Integrity stats only if the dice pool is Resolve + Composure. So, it works for Harmony Breaking Points and Acts of Hubris, but not for Humanity Breaking Points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T07:12:39-07:00","id":1105066,"title":"","content":"Is there a trick to creating social characters?<br /> My group is a bit (read: a lot) gamey so we invariably end up creating quite focused characters, but whenever I try to create a character who is charismatic and/or diplomatic (rather than a mystic, fighter, techie, etc.) I only end up with someone who's barely more than average despite really trying to focus on the social aspects since I want to use at least four, preferably six, Social Skills while almost every other character concept can get by with two high Skills and then Merits (and/or powers depending on gameline) to add extra functionality. I just don't see how to do that with social characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T08:20:34-07:00","id":1105085,"title":"","content":"I find it helps to choose either presence or manipulation to build around, and then pick skills and merits that supplement/build off of having lots of dots in that trait. You can lead by force of personality or you can subtly pull people's strings, but it takes a lot of investment to be good at both styles.<br /> <br /> Is this purely a mortals question or are you looking for advice on social supernats too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T08:33:24-07:00","id":1105088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1105085#post1105085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it helps to choose either presence or manipulation to build around, and then pick skills and merits that supplement/build off of having lots of dots in that trait. You can lead by force of personality or you can subtly pull people's strings, but it takes a lot of investment to be good at both styles.<br /> <br /> Is this purely a mortals question or are you looking for advice on social supernats too?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a generic question since my problem is having to focus on too many skills, and I've found the problem in CofD, VtR and WtF to varying degrees. (I haven't tried such a character in Mage and Changeling, and I haven't played any of the other gamelines yet.)<br /> <br /> Right now I'm trying out different character concepts for a future VtR campaign. A Mekhet cult leader in the shadow cult Followers of Set. I know they are a more subtle bunch by the book, but it's a historical campaign and if I choose that character concept I'd probably work out a more force of personality-style cult for my character. Which means I want both Presence and Manipulation since Cr\u00faac uses Manipulation for whatever reason (I personally think Presence makes more sense). At least the ritual Mantle of Amorous Fire from Secrets of the Covenants can boost Presence with your Cr\u00faac dots (only a bit pricey since it costs a Willpower point in addition to the Vitae), so i guess Manipulation still is best when it comes to choosing Attributes.<br /> <br /> Edit: I would be grateful for more specific advice as well, but I don't think this thread is the right venue for VtR talk. Drop me a PM if you'd like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 06-18-2017, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T01:13:48-07:00","id":1107570,"title":"","content":"Very unlikely to happen, but one I thought I'd ask;<br /> <br /> Say a player is doing an extended action requiring around 10 successes. They roll 3 for the first roll, and then get an exceptional success with 6 successes (totaling to 9). They opt to take the option that allows them to reduce the number of successes required by the number they rolled, meaning they have succeeded the action. Does the additional successes (in this case, the 5 over) mean they end up with the action concluding with another exceptional success? Or does it just count for the one roll?<br /> <br /> It's 1 am as I write this, so apologies if I'm complicating matters, or it's stated very obviously in the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T09:34:41-07:00","id":1107661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1105066#post1105066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a trick to creating social characters?<br /> My group is a bit (read: a lot) gamey so we invariably end up creating quite focused characters, but whenever I try to create a character who is charismatic and/or diplomatic (rather than a mystic, fighter, techie, etc.) I only end up with someone who's barely more than average despite really trying to focus on the social aspects since I want to use at least four, preferably six, Social Skills while almost every other character concept can get by with two high Skills and then Merits (and/or powers depending on gameline) to add extra functionality. I just don't see how to do that with social characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly focused one of my characters on social ability in a changeling game as sort of a challenge a few years back. I've found that, while Attributes and Skills are helpful, having Merits and 'magic abilities' that revolve around or demand social interaction are a big plus, they encourage you to start being the mouth because you need to be able to talk to people to get things going. It continued in my last werewolf character, who was an Elodoth. One of the auspice gifts allows him to detect deceit in people, but only if he's been talking to or watching them for a bit. Once activated it lasts for a while but if you're talking with them you can figure out the questions you want to ask to determine what's true or not. The Half-Moon Gifts continue in that vein. There's also neat things like 'knowledge based' powers that don't absolutely require social interaction but really thrive with it. One of the first Changeling abilities I had was one that let my character know the fear of the target, which technically could be used if plotting an ambush but I found was more useful in asserting subtle or not-so-subtle threats. The werewolf had a nice power that informed him of a targets social Merits, including Status, Allies and Contacts, which led to other routes of investigation and potential lies and ways in when socializing with a character.<br /> <br /> Without dealing with powers, I've found that listening is probably more important than just being the face. One doesn't necessarily need to talk to everyone, but listen to when NPCs and PCs are speaking so you know when to talk and that when you do it will matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-25T10:38:54-07:00","id":1107680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1107570#post1107570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very unlikely to happen, but one I thought I'd ask;<br /> <br /> Say a player is doing an extended action requiring around 10 successes. They roll 3 for the first roll, and then get an exceptional success with 6 successes (totaling to 9). They opt to take the option that allows them to reduce the number of successes required by the number they rolled, meaning they have succeeded the action. Does the additional successes (in this case, the 5 over) mean they end up with the action concluding with another exceptional success? Or does it just count for the one roll?<br /> <br /> It's 1 am as I write this, so apologies if I'm complicating matters, or it's stated very obviously in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Chronicles of Darkness those additional successes mean nothing. The only normal way to get the exceptional success result is rolling an exceptional success in one of the individual rolls and choosing to apply the exceptional success result to the whole extended action, instead of, for example, reducing the target number of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T08:07:37-07:00","id":1108030,"title":"","content":"If a Character gets an exceptional success during a grapple and is then able to perform two grapple maneuvers, can the same Maneuver be used twice?<br /> <br /> Say Rowdy Rowdy Piper wins a Grapple with 7 Success, could he choose the Damage Maneuver twice to inflict 14 Bashing Damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T09:28:11-07:00","id":1108045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1108030#post1108030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Character gets an exceptional success during a grapple and is then able to perform two grapple maneuvers, can the same Maneuver be used twice?<br /> <br /> Say Rowdy Rowdy Piper wins a Grapple with 7 Success, could he choose the Damage Maneuver twice to inflict 14 Bashing Damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most people rule that you can't choose the damage maneuver twice, but I don't think there's actually anything in RAW preventing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T11:56:28-07:00","id":1108090,"title":"","content":"The damage maneuver is the only maneuver that makes any sense at all to choose twice. Therefore, it seems to me that choosing the same maneuver twice is probably beyond the intent of the rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T13:08:35-07:00","id":1108121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1108090#post1108090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The damage maneuver is the only maneuver that makes any sense at all to choose twice.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ignore merits, yes.<br /> If you don't, that's no longer the case.<br /> <br /> 1) Choke benefits, allowing you the potential to hit the target number of successes early.<br /> 2) \u200bJoint lock benefits a little as well, though mostly as a kind of delayed damage maneuver, so that contributes little to the argument.<br /> 3) Small Joint Manipulation benefits largely (crippling both hands)<br /> 4) Tap or Snap benefits immensely (inflicting multiple tilts if the opponent doesn't surrender)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-26-2017, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T14:14:09-07:00","id":1108140,"title":"","content":"So, I was looking at the equipment rules and saw that mystical equipment could be built, but I couldn't find any sample examples in my book. Do I keep skipping over the page in the book, or is it something I'll have to make up on my own?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-26T14:48:33-07:00","id":1108155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1108140#post1108140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was looking at the equipment rules and saw that mystical equipment could be built, but I couldn't find any sample examples in my book. Do I keep skipping over the page in the book, or is it something I'll have to make up on my own?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some examples in GMC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T20:17:32-07:00","id":1110741,"title":"","content":"Does BOdy as Weapon provide +1 lethal damage for 'unarmed' strikes that are upgraded to lethal damage otherwise, such as a changeling with an appropriate lethal mien?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T07:14:56-07:00","id":1110835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1110741#post1110741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does BOdy as Weapon provide +1 lethal damage for 'unarmed' strikes that are upgraded to lethal damage otherwise, such as a changeling with an appropriate lethal mien?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean martial arts 4 &quot;hand as weapon&quot; merit? Then no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T10:09:35-07:00","id":1110905,"title":"","content":"No, I mean the general merit in hurt locker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T13:05:09-07:00","id":1110959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1110905#post1110905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I mean the general merit in hurt locker.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd run it that way for simplicity's sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T15:48:32-07:00","id":1111043,"title":"","content":"Dumb question: is the +3 bonus from spending a point of willpower in addition to the maximum +5 to a dice pool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T16:04:41-07:00","id":1111051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1111043#post1111043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dumb question: is the +3 bonus from spending a point of willpower in addition to the maximum +5 to a dice pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Most equipment offers a bonus to dice rolls pertaining to <br /> its use. Multiple items can influence a given roll, but a roll <br /> should not receive more than a +5 bonus.&quot;<br /> <br /> Except for that part (which I read that the total modifier from equipment is limited since it's written in the equipment rules) only individual modifiers are limited to -5 and +5. The +3 from Willpower is a new modifier.<br /> <br /> Edit: My group limits modifiers by source. Max +5 from equipment, max +5 from environment, max +5 from Specialties (it has actually been relevant), and so on. Certain things, like Physical Intensity in VtR, does not have that limit, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 07-03-2017, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T03:01:33-07:00","id":1111199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1111043#post1111043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dumb question: is the +3 bonus from spending a point of willpower in addition to the maximum +5 to a dice pool?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spending WP is a single bonus. Multiple bonuses stack normally. The rule you're referencing concerns individual mundane bonuses not being able to go above a +/-5, because that's what differentiates a bonus or penalty as mundane or supernatural. So, no, if you have a nice set of clothes that affords you say, a +3 to seduce someone and you spend WP on top of it, do feel free to let the player roll at +6.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T05:59:11-07:00","id":1111221,"title":"","content":"I don't really think of the extra dice from willpower as a &quot;bonus&quot; per se. More as a way of momentarily boosting your natural dice pool. Physical intensity is the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T06:15:21-07:00","id":1111229,"title":"","content":"Holy cow, this got me thinking. <br /> Is the penalty from you opponent caped at -5 dice?<br /> <br /> say you have 10 dice to attack, your opponent has Defense 7, do you roll 5 or 3 dice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T06:20:57-07:00","id":1111232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1111229#post1111229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy cow, this got me thinking. <br /> Is the penalty from you opponent caped at -5 dice?<br /> <br /> say you have 10 dice to attack, your opponent has Defense 7, do you roll 5 or 3 dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Defense is not a penalty to the dice pool. Defense is explicitly part of the dice pool as a resistance. &quot;Strength + Brawl or Weaponry - Defense&quot;<br /> Just like you're not capping someone's resistance attribute in 5 when using resisted supernatural powers and they happen to have more than five in that attribute (possible even for mortals to up their resistances with +2 by spending WP).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T19:40:41-07:00","id":1111508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1111221#post1111221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really think of the extra dice from willpower as a &quot;bonus&quot; per se. More as a way of momentarily boosting your natural dice pool. Physical intensity is the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it adds dice to the roll? Yes? I'll refer to that broad category of things as bonus or penalty then. Making up more terms is just juggling semantics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1111229#post1111229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy cow, this got me thinking.<br /> Is the penalty from you opponent caped at -5 dice?<br /> <br /> say you have 10 dice to attack, your opponent has Defense 7, do you roll 5 or 3 dice?</div> </div> </div> </div>1 if they boost Defense by spending WP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T02:11:04-07:00","id":1111588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1111232#post1111232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Defense is not a penalty to the dice pool. Defense is explicitly part of the dice pool as a resistance. &quot;Strength + Brawl or Weaponry - Defense&quot;<br /> Just like you're not capping someone's resistance attribute in 5 when using resisted supernatural powers and they happen to have more than five in that attribute (possible even for mortals to up their resistances with +2 by spending WP).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks this was what I've always read it as and done. But the latest posts got me doubting a bit. Thanks for clearing it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:35:18-07:00","id":1111843,"title":"","content":"Does burning an inspired condition in a contested roll allow you beat someone with equal or greater successes than you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13619-hellomynameis","name":"HelloMyNameIs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T15:38:11-07:00","id":1111847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelloMyNameIs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1111843#post1111843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does burning an inspired condition in a contested roll allow you beat someone with equal or greater successes than you?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Inspired doesn't grant any successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T15:08:30-07:00","id":1112365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1111847#post1111847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Inspired doesn't grant any successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to this, since I think I know where this questions is coming from:<br /> <br /> An exceptional success in a contested action only gives you the effects of an exceptional success if you score more raw successes than the opponent. Additionally, your opponent's roll has no other impact on your degree of success - if they get five successes and you get six, you get an exceptional success and they get a failure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T06:39:24-07:00","id":1115923,"title":"","content":"I have three unrelated questions<br /> <br /> 1) This might have been explained in the book, but the language still confuses me: If you take Lethal Damage before you fill up your Bashing track, do you have to roll to resist unconsciousness just like if you filled up your Bashing track?<br /> <br /> Edit: yes, I know that if it pushed the bashing to the edge you would, but what happens when it doesn't?<br /> <br /> 2) Can a Spirit gain Essence from performing resonant actions using the body of someone it has Claimed or Possessed? Like, say, a Spirit of Gluttony making its claimed victim gorge themselves?<br /> <br /> 3) Are there non-Infernal Spirits of the various sins, are all Sin-Spirits Infernal?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 07-14-2017, 09:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T07:00:44-07:00","id":1115929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1115923#post1115923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might have been explained in the book, but the language still confuses me: If you take Lethal Damage before you fill up your Bashing track, do you have to roll to resist unconsciousness just like if you filled up your Bashing track?<br /> <br /> Edit: yes, I know that if it pushed the bashing to the edge you would, but what happens when it doesn't?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm pretty sure you roll to stay up when your last health box is filled with bashing or lethal. If you suddenly take a full track of lethal from a bullet or something, yes. If you're at perfect health and take 1 lethal damage from touching a stovetop, then no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>she/her","edited":{"userid":13652,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","user":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","date":". 07-14-2017, 10:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","name":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13652_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T08:39:42-07:00","id":1115955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1115923#post1115923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Can a Spirit gain Essence from performing resonant actions using the body of someone it has Claimed or Possessed? Like, say, a Spirit of Gluttony making its claimed victim gorge themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's the big reason spirits cross the Gauntlet or just Influence people through it. The first adventure in Chronicles involved a hive-claimed of fire spirits that were claiming people and starting arson sprees.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Are there non-Infernal Spirits of the various sins, are all Sin-Spirits Infernal? </div> </div> </div>The former. Infernal spirits are considered 'wounded' spirits, and it's a form of corruption. Normal spirits of Greed, Violence, Deceit, Wrath, Envy, Pride, Gluttony and Lust and Sloth are all there. Of course, they're probably more likely to become corrupted, since the wound-born things that corrupt spirits already have an 'in' in terms of Resonance and access or knowledge about the sin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T11:33:50-07:00","id":1116034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1115929#post1115929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure you roll to stay up when your last health box is filled with bashing or lethal. If you suddenly take a full track of lethal from a bullet or something, yes. If you're at perfect health and take 1 lethal damage from touching a stovetop, then no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool. That makes the drawbacks of a lot of powers and magical items make more sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T11:51:54-07:00","id":1116043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1115923#post1115923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have three unrelated questions<br /> <br /> 1) This might have been explained in the book, but the language still confuses me: If you take Lethal Damage before you fill up your Bashing track, do you have to roll to resist unconsciousness just like if you filled up your Bashing track?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is only one health track.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">If a character\u2019s Health track is filled with <u><b>any</b></u> damage, his<br /> player must make a reflexive Stamina roll each turn for him to<br /> remain conscious.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>So yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T12:19:22-07:00","id":1116052,"title":"","content":"Since we are on the topic of injuries:<br /> A character needs to make a Stamina roll each turn. If a character fails they falls down unconscious.<br /> <br /> So, do they keep making these rolls at the start of each of their turns until they are either healed enough to not be full of damage, or until they die? Also, if a character has previously failed and fallen to the ground unconscious and then the next round they succeed, they can do their turn as usual for that round at least? After a successful roll they basically wake up with the knocked down tilt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-14T12:38:32-07:00","id":1116062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1116052#post1116052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since we are on the topic of injuries:<br /> A character needs to make a Stamina roll each turn. If a character fails they falls down unconscious.<br /> <br /> So, do they keep making these rolls at the start of each of their turns until they are either healed enough to not be full of damage, or until they die?</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep making these rolls until you're healed or you fail one, falling unconscious. You can be healed of that one Bashing by resting, like in your unconscious state, for 15 minutes or some external help. Death only potentially occurs if you're full of Lethal, or if someone crushes your head with a rock while you're unconscious. If you're Lethal, you need medical assistance, which can be done with the Medicine skill or calling for an ambulance or other things. Death is instant if you're full of Aggravated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if a character has previously failed and fallen to the ground unconscious and then the next round they succeed, they can do their turn as usual for that round at least? After a successful roll they basically wake up with the knocked down tilt? </div> </div> </div>Once you've failed a roll to stay conscious you stop making the rolls to resist falling unconscious, because you're unconscious. At that point you're out, barring something else bringing you back in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-14-2017, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T06:45:56-07:00","id":1117176,"title":"","content":"Also, remember Wound Penalties apply normally to that Stamina roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T07:39:52-07:00","id":1117187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1117176#post1117176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, remember Wound Penalties apply normally to that Stamina roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you cite that? Because I've heard the opposite. And if it's correct, what happens if you dramatically fail to stay conscious?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>she/her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","name":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13652_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T07:45:42-07:00","id":1117190,"title":"","content":"You heard right.<br /> <br /> &quot;When one of her three rightmost Health boxes has damage marked, she suffers a penalty accordingly. Subtract this penalty from every action she performs, including rolling for Initiative, <b>but not including Stamina rolls to stay conscious.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> That's on page 95 if you want to check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T08:45:16-07:00","id":1117217,"title":"","content":"Huh, that's what I get from posting while AFB. Pretty sure that's new to 2E, in my defense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:36:33-07:00","id":1117317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1117217#post1117217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, that's what I get from posting while AFB. Pretty sure that's new to 2E, in my defense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah was the same in 1st edition too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T11:39:07-07:00","id":1117318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1117217#post1117217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, that's what I get from posting while AFB. Pretty sure that's new to 2E, in my defense <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Even in 1e would have made staying conscious pretty damn difficult to most characters. (Ninja'd by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1534_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1534\" data-vbnamecard=\"1534\">totalgit</a> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T20:04:13-07:00","id":1121161,"title":"","content":"Can Slashers take Supernatural Merits or even Micro-templates without losing the Slasher traits?<br /> <br /> Also, what happens to a Slasher or anyone with lower-than-average Integrity who becomes a Major Template? Lower starting Integrity-equivalent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T20:55:55-07:00","id":1121172,"title":"","content":"I think Slashers are a Lesser Template. How Lesser Templates interact is more or less up to the ST; I don't think there's a default. If there is, I think it's that minor templates can't overwrite each other or coexist.<br /> <br /> I don't think lower Integrity affects the new templates morality stat; they typically measure completely different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T21:18:44-07:00","id":1121177,"title":"","content":"Can't have more than one template, but really there's no reason you should limit yourself to that if it fits the story. I'm imagining you're not having a slasher player who's going to be a slasher and ghoul or something. In that case I'd recommend you just drop the slasher template and have it be part of their background, most of the splats are going to have options to be a more murderous sort. I did something like that.<br /> <br /> A Slasher with supernatural powers fits way too many stories to be restricted by a rule about supernatural merits, especially for an NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T02:40:51-07:00","id":1121234,"title":"","content":"I think you can be a slasher without being a Slasher.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T04:54:29-07:00","id":1121262,"title":"","content":"It would be nice if they took away the template, even if only for rippers, doing something similar to wolf-blooded with Tells, Talents and Frailties.<br /> <br /> Though I suspect if that were the case people would just start using them as free benefits for their character without bringing in the downside or fluff connection. I suppose Hunter will let us see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T07:43:01-07:00","id":1123018,"title":"","content":"Can Supernaturals do basic exorcisms and abjurations and other mortal magic and such using their Integrity-equivalent","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T09:31:23-07:00","id":1123042,"title":"","content":"Ive always allowed it but I dont thi k theres a definitive answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T11:08:40-07:00","id":1123085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1123018#post1123018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Supernaturals do basic exorcisms and abjurations and other mortal magic and such using their Integrity-equivalent</div> </div> </div> </div>Summoning, Exorcism, Binding and Warding are just rituals using implements relevant to the ephemeral entity. Nothing suggests it has anything to do with Integrity or the soul so it should possible for all supers to do.<br /> Abjuration, on the other hand, is described as using the character's soul and is directly modified by Integrity, so those specific rules only applies to those with an Integrity rating. Whether or not supernaturals can carry out an Abjuration is left unstated since they don't have any rules for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T08:06:21-07:00","id":1123493,"title":"","content":"If I had Professional Training ** (Athlete) and I did a Dodge roll, do I get 9-again on the roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5387-peteman","name":"Peteman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T08:15:03-07:00","id":1123498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peteman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1123493#post1123493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had Professional Training ** (Athlete) and I did a Dodge roll, do I get 9-again on the roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Defense is a derived trait so stuff like dice tricks (9 Again and Rote Action) and Specialties do not carry over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T11:58:18-07:00","id":1128532,"title":"","content":"Does Whirlwind strike get upgraded to lethal damage by Hand As Weapon (the dot afterward)? My initial thought is no because it's not actually an unarmed strike, it's a passive effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T13:02:39-07:00","id":1128557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1128532#post1128532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Whirlwind strike get upgraded to lethal damage by Hand As Weapon (the dot afterward)? My initial thought is no because it's not actually an unarmed strike, it's a passive effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't a &quot;passive effect&quot; apply regardless of which maneuver is used? Or have videogames taught me wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T13:20:44-07:00","id":1128563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1128557#post1128557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't a &quot;passive effect&quot; apply regardless of which maneuver is used? Or have videogames taught me wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean whirlwind strike is passive, not an active 'unarmed strike' that would be upgraded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T10:49:39-07:00","id":1129296,"title":"","content":"Do weapons with the piercing quality permanently and cumulatively reduce armor rating on a hit? If not, what's the point of using, say, a rapier against someone in a kevlar vest if it only subtracts from their ballistic armor rating?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>she/her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","name":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13652_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:38:59-07:00","id":1129326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1129296#post1129296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do weapons with the piercing quality permanently and cumulatively reduce armor rating on a hit? If not, what's the point of using, say, a rapier against someone in a kevlar vest if it only subtracts from their ballistic armor rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Subtract from ballistic armor first, then general armor.<br /> Armor-piercing attacks in close combat subtract from general<br /> armor only.&quot;<br /> CofD, page 95.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T11:45:46-07:00","id":1129328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manic Pixie Dreamcast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1129296#post1129296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do weapons with the piercing quality permanently and cumulatively reduce armor rating on a hit? If not, what's the point of using, say, a rapier against someone in a kevlar vest if it only subtracts from their ballistic armor rating?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the piercing quality allows a weapon to ignores its piercing value in armor, it doesn't reduce the armor's rating.<br /> <br /> Attacking someone in a Kevlar vest with a rapier would ignore ballistic armor entirely because ballistic armor only applies against ranged attacks, and then ignore one point of its general rating due to the Piercing 1 quality.<br /> <br /> Supporting quote: &quot;Some weapons have an armor piercing quality, usually between one and three. When attacking someone wearing armor, subtract the piercing quality from the target\u2019s armor. Subtract from ballistic armor first, then general armor. Armor-piercing attacks in close combat subtract from general armor only.&quot;<br /> - Chronicles of Darkness, pages 94-95","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-15T15:50:02-07:00","id":1129464,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Hurt Locker is missing that last clause about ignoring ballistic armor in close combat and I didn't think to check the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>she/her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13652-manic-pixie-dreamcast","name":"Manic Pixie Dreamcast","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13652_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T04:55:52-07:00","id":1133733,"title":"","content":"Can we get this pinned also ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T07:08:56-07:00","id":1135432,"title":"","content":"Can a fettered person see or hear the ephemeral being fettered to them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T07:14:15-07:00","id":1135434,"title":"","content":"Not by default. I think it can still use manifestations to become visible though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T08:06:43-07:00","id":1135452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1135432#post1135432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a fettered person see or hear the ephemeral being fettered to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if they had a way to see or hear entities in the correct phase of Twilight.<br /> <br /> It's also possible a fettered entity would hide, like inside the fetter, so stealth might be a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-30-2017, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:21:42-07:00","id":1135478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1135452#post1135452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if they had a way to see or hear entities in the correct phase of Twilight.<br /> <br /> It's also possible a fettered entity would hide, like inside the fetter, so stealth might be a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, a fettered ephemeral would have to use other powers to communicate with it's living fetter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T10:10:30-07:00","id":1135490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1135478#post1135478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, a fettered ephemeral would have to use other powers to communicate with it's living fetter?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they sought to communicate, yes, but it's more likely that they would seek to control and influence them. They're fettered, after all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T10:29:23-07:00","id":1135496,"title":"","content":"Yeah, they can send sort of subliminal suggestions to their host to make them do what they want. Usually promoting their purview in some way. That's why the condition is called &quot;urged&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T09:21:26-07:00","id":1147460,"title":"","content":"This one might just be up to taste, but does Aggravated damage also hurt more than Lethal damage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T16:16:53-07:00","id":1147607,"title":"","content":"Mechanically no, wound penalties are the same. In terms of descriptions that really depends on the injuries. There are cases where it might even hurt less. For example, really serious burns may be painless because the nerves have been damaged beyond functioning, so you can't even accurately judge how bad you're injured because you can't feel anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T17:14:42-07:00","id":1147612,"title":"","content":"It does when it's a bane inflicting the damage. Though as HelmsDerp points out there's no mechanical obviousness beyond the difference between 1/14th of the way dead and 1/7th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T18:20:22-07:00","id":1147632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1147460#post1147460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one might just be up to taste, but does Aggravated damage also hurt more than Lethal damage?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Considering different things do agg to different splats then i would say no. The difference is mearly how hard it is to heal. Fire is lethal to humans but agg to vampires, being burnt is equally painful its just effort needed to heal and lethality that is different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T23:14:24-07:00","id":1147686,"title":"","content":"aggravated does cause permanent conditions such as limb loss. Lethal doesnt","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-06T23:29:58-07:00","id":1147689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1147632#post1147632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering different things do agg to different splats then i would say no. The difference is mearly how hard it is to heal. Fire is lethal to humans but agg to vampires, being burnt is equally painful its just effort needed to heal and lethality that is different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we can safely assume fire isn't more painful to vampires than it is to humans. Sunlight is certainly much more painful to them, and the fire vulnerability works on similar principles. Likewise, merely touching silver is painful to werewolves, but not to humans.<br /> <br /> Personally, I treat aggravated damage descriptions on a case-by-case basis, but generally speaking, aggravated damage from mundane sources is usually painless; since most mundane sources that cause aggravated would cause such severe trauma that the nervous system will usually stop acknowledging it to protect itself. Aggravated damage from Banes I treat as not a more physically painful sensation than equivalent damage from a non-Bane source, but as more distressing on a metaphysical level. Effectively your soul (or similar ephemeral aspect of your being) is being damaged as much as your body is, so while the pain isn't exactly worse. It's just that you experience it spiritually as well as physically.<br /> <br /> You know that scene in Princess Bride when Inigo recognizes Westly's physical pain caused by Rugen's machine because as he put it, &quot;my heart made that sound when Rugen killed my father&quot;? That's kind of how I picture aggravated damage from Banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T11:23:36-07:00","id":1149744,"title":"","content":"If my character wore Reinforced Clothing and had Iron Skin and someone came at them with a knife, getting 1 success with their attack (1 Lethal Damage), would my character take the 1 bashing damage as mentioned in the following rule &quot;When applying armor to an attack dealing lethal damage, the character always takes at least one point of bashing damage from the shock of the blow.&quot;, or because I have Iron Skin, the damage is absorbed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5387-peteman","name":"Peteman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T16:44:26-07:00","id":1149792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peteman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1149744#post1149744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my character wore Reinforced Clothing and had Iron Skin and someone came at them with a knife, getting 1 success with their attack (1 Lethal Damage), would my character take the 1 bashing damage as mentioned in the following rule &quot;When applying armor to an attack dealing lethal damage, the character always takes at least one point of bashing damage from the shock of the blow.&quot;, or because I have Iron Skin, the damage is absorbed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say you would still take one bashing. Iron Skin acts as general armor against bashing damage, meaning that it would be added to your other armor as per the armor layering rules (unless you decide that it doesn't, but then it would just act as normal Reinforced Clothing.)) That is to say, your armor would act as 1L+1B/0 armor with the two dot Iron Skin, and you would thus receive a minimum of one damage from Lethal attacks despite the additional protection. Even if you used Iron Skin's willpower ability to change the damage of a Lethal attack to bashing, I believe it is still counted as &quot;an attack dealing lethal damage&quot; for the armor protection rules.<br /> <br /> Of course, you could rule it the other way if you think it would be more fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T16:44:48-07:00","id":1149793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peteman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1149744#post1149744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my character wore Reinforced Clothing and had Iron Skin and someone came at them with a knife, getting 1 success with their attack (1 Lethal Damage), would my character take the 1 bashing damage as mentioned in the following rule &quot;When applying armor to an attack dealing lethal damage, the character always takes at least one point of bashing damage from the shock of the blow.&quot;, or because I have Iron Skin, the damage is absorbed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You take 1 bashing. Iron skin isnt giving you armour vs a lethal attack and only downgrades any lethal you get if you spent a willpower. It doesnt negate or downgrade the 1 bashing from shock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T13:07:31-07:00","id":1149990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1147689#post1147689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think we can safely assume fire isn't more painful to vampires than it is to humans. Sunlight is certainly much more painful to them, and the fire vulnerability works on similar principles. Likewise, merely touching silver is painful to werewolves, but not to humans.<br /> <br /> Personally, I treat aggravated damage descriptions on a case-by-case basis, but generally speaking, aggravated damage from mundane sources is usually painless; since most mundane sources that cause aggravated would cause such severe trauma that the nervous system will usually stop acknowledging it to protect itself. Aggravated damage from Banes I treat as not a more physically painful sensation than equivalent damage from a non-Bane source, but as more distressing on a metaphysical level. Effectively your soul (or similar ephemeral aspect of your being) is being damaged as much as your body is, so while the pain isn't exactly worse. It's just that you experience it spiritually as well as physically.<br /> <br /> You know that scene in Princess Bride when Inigo recognizes Westly's physical pain caused by Rugen's machine because as he put it, &quot;my heart made that sound when Rugen killed my father&quot;? That's kind of how I picture aggravated damage from Banes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, it's like the Heartbreaker from Saga, but way more deadly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T13:14:38-07:00","id":1149991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1149990#post1149990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, it's like the Heartbreaker from Saga, but way more deadly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on the name, that sounds about right. I've only read the first hardcover collection of Saga, and it's been a long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-15T14:39:20-07:00","id":1150014,"title":"","content":"For reference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VEAGAAQJ7DM\" data-code=\"VEAGAAQJ7DM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VEAGAAQJ7DM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> You should see the movie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T14:35:08-07:00","id":1152030,"title":"","content":"Do other Supernatural Templates have equivalent of Changeling's &quot;Court Mantle&quot; Merit that represents their status within their community? <br /> It seems Mantle will play role in Court Contracts' dice pool in 2nd edition of Changeling the Lost, so I would assume theoretical &quot;crossover contracts&quot; would require an equivalent of such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T15:07:02-07:00","id":1152035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152030#post1152030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do other Supernatural Templates have equivalent of Changeling's &amp;quot;Court Mantle&amp;quot; Merit that represents their status within their community? <br /> It seems Mantle will play role in Court Contracts' dice pool in 2nd edition of Changeling the Lost, so I would assume theoretical &amp;quot;crossover contracts&amp;quot; would require an equivalent of such.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the template. Vampire has Covenant Status, (as well as Clan Status and City Status) for example, which is similar in that it represents standing within a social organization in vampiric society but doesn\u2019t have the same direct impact on their supernatural abilities. Conversely, the closest analogue Werewolf has is probably Renown, which directly affects Gift dice pools (among many other aspects of Gifts) but doesn\u2019t really represent social standing in the same way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T15:10:59-07:00","id":1152039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152035#post1152035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on the template. Vampire has Covenant Status, (as well as Clan Status and City Status) for example, which is similar in that it represents standing within a social organization in vampiric society but doesn\u2019t have the same direct impact on their supernatural abilities. Conversely, the closest analogue Werewolf has is probably Renown, which directly affects Gift dice pools (among many other aspects of Gifts) but doesn\u2019t really represent social standing in the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling also had Merit called &quot;Court Good Will [Court]&quot; which represents allies/Contacts in Court Changeling doesn't belong in. Since it would be unlikely for Changelings to be actually able to join Covenant or such, are there other such equivalents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T15:58:20-07:00","id":1152053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152039#post1152039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling also had Merit called &quot;Court Good Will [Court]&quot; which represents allies/Contacts in Court Changeling doesn't belong in. Since it would be unlikely for Changelings to be actually able to join Covenant or such, are there other such equivalents?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I wouldn't put money on crossover Contracts operating like Court Contracts in the first place except in the case of a Court Contract that <i>is</i> a crossover Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T16:57:11-07:00","id":1152061,"title":"","content":"I posted a thread with this question, but I hadn't seen this thread yet. What are the actual rules for Virtue/Vice Willpower refreshes? The text in the CofD rulebook is ambiguous and contradicts the rules in VtR 2nd and MtA 2nd. <br /> <br /> My understanding has always been: Work towards your Virtue at some risk or cost, all willpower refreshes. Indulge your Vice regardless of cost or risk, 1 willpower point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T19:23:59-07:00","id":1152090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the Storyteller judges that your character\u2019s actions dur-<br /> ing a scene reflect his Vice, he regains one spent Willpower<br /> point.<i><b> Note that acting on a Virtue or Vice does not need to<br /> pose difficulty or risk to your character.</b></i><br /> If the Storyteller judges that your character\u2019s actions dur-<br /> ing a scene reflected her Virtue <i><b>while posing her difficulty<br /> or risk</b></i>, she regains all spent Willpower. She may regain<br /> Willpower up to twice per game session in this way. </div> </div> </div>Mask/Dirge for Vampire gives one for actions with little risk and full refreshes for risk, but that's Mask and Dirge, not Virtue/Vice. It does seem to contradict itself here, so I'm not entirely sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T20:38:01-07:00","id":1152102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152039#post1152039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling also had Merit called &amp;quot;Court Good Will [Court]&amp;quot; which represents allies/Contacts in Court Changeling doesn't belong in. Since it would be unlikely for Changelings to be actually able to join Covenant or such, are there other such equivalents?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as of 2nd Edition, vampires can have Status in multiple Covenants, provided their Clan Status total doesn\u2019t exceed 5 between all Clans they hold Staus in. And Secrets of the Covenants has a 2-dot Merit for each Covenant representing being invested in the Covenant to a degree that\u2019s roughly equivalent to 1 Status without being a full member. For Werewolf, there\u2019s no way for a non-Werewolf to gain Renown, but other creatures can join werewolf packs. There\u2019s no Merit for it or anything like that though. The closest thing would be Pack Bond, a 1 or 3 dot Merit that allows a non-werewolf character to take either 1 or up to 5 dots in Totem (a Merit that pack members can take to give the pavk\u2019s Totem spirit more experiences). Mage doesn\u2019t have anything comparable, as their secret societies are very exclusive, the best you\u2019re going to get in that case is Mystery Cult Initiation in a Cult either led or more likely influenced (e.g. by the Mystery Cult Influence Merit) by a Mage. Prometheans don\u2019t really have social groups bigger than Motlies. Demons don\u2019t have anything remotely comparable, their social groups being even more secretive than those of Mages. Couldn\u2019t tell you about Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T02:27:08-07:00","id":1152143,"title":"","content":"I'd content that there are a few ways for others to be involved in Demon affairs, but as Charlaquin noted it's hardly full status membership. Like a Mage, you can become part of their Cults and gain a number of interesting bonuses (notably, Demon cults can take in supernatural beings alongside humans), but you're hardly going to be let in on their secrets, or even really the entire truth on things. Even if Stigmatics are brought up to know what goes on in the Ring, they aren't full members, and Demons rarely, if ever, include them in the full nitty gritty.<br /> <br /> There is Sympathetic Stigmatic and Sympathetic Demon, which are a pair of linked merits that go to a Demon and a Stigmatic respectively that, well, link them together. Notably, these merits require True Friend, which is something pretty taboo among Demons because Stigmatics aren't the best equiped for Demon life. Additionally, while it gives them notable benefits (particularly with a Demon's Ciper, and the Demon turns up at just the right moment to help the Stigmatic out in perilous times), it has the downside of giving enemies leverage and causing any wounds the Demon takes to also be taken by the human partner. There is no guarentee a Demon will actually bring said Stigmatic into the Ring either.<br /> <br /> The third option is...less standard, where a Demon specifically invites a non-Demon as a full member into the Ring. This is seen as a highly dangerous move by other Unchained, given they are a paranoid bunch and is not discussed at all outside of rumors. There is no merit for this, but if other Demons find out it can mean ostrisization, which is not something you want as a Demon in a God-Machine filled world. Outside of possibly being informed on where a Demon's bolthole is, and access to gadgets, there are no explicite benefits to this kind of partnership for non-Demons.<br /> <br /> (If there are inaccuracies, I apologize; terrible habit, writing this stuff past midnight on a whim)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 10-23-2017, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T03:31:57-07:00","id":1152152,"title":"","content":"Thanks for detailed insight on Unchained society but since context of my question were Contracts I can't imagine Demonic Rings/Agencies, Covenants, or Pentacle Orders coming up.<br /> At the moment it seems that theoretical Machine Contracts and/or Exarch Contracts would base their dicepools on rating in appropriate Mystery Cult?<br /> Do Angels roll their Rank instead of Primum for their Embeds or is there something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T03:53:45-07:00","id":1152154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152152#post1152152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for detailed insight on Unchained society but since context of my question were Contracts I can't imagine Demonic Rings/Agencies, Covenants, or Pentacle Orders coming up.<br /> At the moment it seems that theoretical Machine Contracts and/or Exarch Contracts would base their dicepools on rating in appropriate Mystery Cult?<br /> Do Angels roll their Rank instead of Primum for their Embeds or is there something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Contracts (Changeling powers) or Contacts (general Merit representing information sources)?<br /> Angels generally don't have Embeds - their Influences and Numina combined with their Ephemeral nature obviates the need for them... usually. Some Angel do have Embeds listed, but they are treated more like Numina (Power + Finesse). Embeds don't use Primum anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T05:51:14-07:00","id":1152171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152154#post1152154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Contracts (Changeling powers) or Contacts (general Merit representing information sources)?<br /> Angels generally don't have Embeds - their Influences and Numina combined with their Ephemeral nature obviates the need for them... usually. Some Angel do have Embeds listed, but they are treated more like Numina (Power + Finesse). Embeds don't use Primum anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am trying to piece of how &quot;Custom Crossover&quot; Contracts would work, assuming they wouldn't simply replace Court Contracts under those circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T09:09:21-07:00","id":1152212,"title":"","content":"My advice is to look at an innate ability that a particular splat has, and see about making that a feature that a Changeling would want and could therefore get by making a deal for it. However, depending on the entity it may backfire in some way.<br /> <br /> For example, ponder a Crossover Contract where the Changeling has made a deal with the God-Machine. Pay a Glamour to have perfect body control - the Changeling is able to lie perfectly through their facial expression, voice and body language, and they may get a minor bonus to Athletics actions. The loophole to the contract is to be standing within Infrastructure while you use it. However, unless the Changeling got an exceptional success they must make a Clarity roll at the end, given using the contract alerts it to where the Changeling generally is, and the God-Machine is as potent as the Gentry are in some respects. Dramatic Failure is worse; instead of getting perfect body control, the God-Machine is able to control certain actions the Changeling does, such as flipping a light switch or making them say something without meaning tom while they are under the impression they have attained the desired result. Gaining the contract at all could alter the Changeling's mien by putting circuit patterns across their skin, or an angelic brand over one of their eyes.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure why Crossover Contracts would replace Court Contracts, given they're two different systems. A Court Contract is using the powers that the founder of the court bartered with and formed the court from. A Crossover Contract is where a Changeling makes a deal with another entity of great and reality changing power comparable to the Wyrd. Luna was mentioned by Rose and Megan as being a potential source, and I'm pretty sure the God-Machine could be one too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 10-23-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T09:32:01-07:00","id":1152217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152212#post1152212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm not sure why Crossover Contracts would replace Court Contracts, given they're two different systems. A Court Contract is using the powers that the founder of the court bartered with and formed the court from. A Crossover Contract is where a Changeling makes a deal with another entity of great and reality changing power comparable to the Wyrd. Luna was mentioned by Rose and Megan as being a potential source, and I'm pretty sure the God-Machine could be one too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am going to disagree about G-M Contracts with you there since I don't think it's such a good idea to create Powers based on another Template's default ability. Rather I would imagine God-Machine Contracts &quot;Suite&quot; to consist of Embed and Exploits It would be willing to bestow on Its subject, adjusted to fit Contract guidelines and Changeling rules. I would imagine it would take Lost something in the line of starting to build Infrastructure components in the Hedge or maintaining concealment Infrastructure already in place.<br /> <br /> As for why &quot;Crossover Contracts&quot; may have replaced Courts: Maybe some Courts are started by outsiders (Crossover Court). Or trying to bargain with other great forces is likely to turn Freehold against the transgressor (Lost Pariah). There are some other lore reasons for something like this but mechanic is this: The Changeling would simply treat such Crossover Contracts as Court Contracts and use their altered Mantle Merit for dicepools.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Flash of Inspiration! G-M Contracts specifically might derive their power on how deeply has Changeling become ingrained into Its Infrastructure. In game terms Changeling can replace number of their Aspirations with &quot;Directions&quot; that are chosen by Storyteller to represent orders given by G-M. Initiative to do so is this: God Machine Contract dicepools are Finesse Attribute+Skill+Directions. <br /> Or if we come up with something different we can use this for Exarch Contracts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 10-23-2017, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T13:04:55-07:00","id":1152593,"title":"","content":"Abjuration strips an ephemeral entity of Manifestations. Does this include Twilit Form manifestion, meaning the entity gets sent back to its realm of origin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T13:55:03-07:00","id":1152603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152593#post1152593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abjuration strips an ephemeral entity of Manifestations. Does this include Twilit Form manifestion, meaning the entity gets sent back to its realm of origin?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think so. What even is an Angel\u2019s realm of origin?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T13:59:08-07:00","id":1152605,"title":"","content":"Unimportant, would just mean the angel is out of play until the GM summons it again (or at least until the abjuration wears off, maybe they can then reclaim the manifestation somehow). It just seems weird that when you sucessfully abjure a spirit it's completly free to ruin your day with numina or influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T14:38:35-07:00","id":1152615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152603#post1152603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think so. What even is an Angel\u2019s realm of origin?</div> </div> </div> </div>Usually it seems to be the 'real' world. I think they can be made in other places, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152605#post1152605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just seems weird that when you sucessfully abjure a spirit it's completly free to ruin your day with numina or influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be weird. That's not how it works, though.<br /> <br /> 'If the abjuration is successful, all Conditions tagged by the entity in the abjurist\u2019s Willpower in yards are suppressed for one day. On an exceptional success, the abjurist also becomes an extra bane for the entity until its Conditions return.'<br /> <br /> This would keep it from using things like the Open or Resonant Condition to 'ruin your day.'<br /> <br /> You might be thinking of an Exorcism. And the end result would be the same, providing you did it right. For instance you would be wise to get rid of the desecrated cross on the wall that the demon you're exorcising is Resonant to. Or you would meditate to stifle angry thoughts to banish any Resonant Condition the wrath spirit is clinging onto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-24-2017, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T15:28:13-07:00","id":1152621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152615#post1152615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This would keep it from using things like the Open or Resonant Condition to 'ruin your day.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, so they have a harder time ruining my day with influences. I think it doesn't even say that something needs to be resonant for them to use an influence on it when it fall under their purview, though in my mind it certainly makes sense. Regardless a spirit is still free to use its blast numen to kill you for inconviniencing it, is it not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T15:48:43-07:00","id":1152623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152621#post1152621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, so they have a harder time ruining my day with influences. I think it doesn't even say that something needs to be resonant for them to use an influence on it when it fall under their purview, though in my mind it certainly makes sense. Regardless a spirit is still free to use its blast numen to kill you for inconviniencing it, is it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>It needs to be physically there to Blast. To be physically there it needs to either Fetter, Claim, Possess, or Materialize (not including some outside interference or the rule breaking powers of idigam or Rank 6+ entities). All of these require at least the Open Condition to do. Abjuring gets rid of the Open Condition and the Resonant Condition and keeps new ones from being formed.<br /> <br /> But yes. If you try to Abjure a being that's 100 feet away from you when you only have 3 Willpower, you chose the wrong method to deal with the problem. Though you can always approach it and blast away its Conditions as you do so. Abjuring is not a long-range attack, it's a short range ward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-24-2017, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T15:57:57-07:00","id":1152624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152615#post1152615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually it seems to be the 'real' world. I think they can be made in other places, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s my point exactly. It doesn\u2019t make sense that somehow losing Twilight Form would send them \u201cback to\u201d the real world, since the real world is where they already are, and Twilight Form is how they naturally exist within it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T16:04:25-07:00","id":1152627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152624#post1152624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That\u2019s my point exactly. It doesn\u2019t make sense that somehow losing Twilight Form would send them \u201cback to\u201d the real world, since the real world is where they already are, and Twilight Form is how they naturally exist within it.</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't lose Twilight Form, though. They (or technically the surroundings) would lose the Infrastructure Condition and the angel would start bleeding Essence per hour. It would also lose any Open Condition, meaning it couldn't Materialize, keeping it stuck in Twilight Form and unable to interact with anything that wasn't in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Presumably it would retreat to an area with Infrastructure but I think that would depend on the Rank of the angel, some might just sit there until they die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-24-2017, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T16:13:15-07:00","id":1152629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152627#post1152627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They wouldn't lose Twilight Form, though. They (or technically the surroundings) would lose the Infrastructure Condition and the angel would start bleeding Essence per hour. It would also lose any Open Condition, meaning it couldn't Materialize, keeping it stuck in Twilight Form and unable to interact with anything that wasn't in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Presumably it would retreat to an area with Infrastructure but I think that would depend on the Rank of the angel, some might just sit there until they die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but I was following the proposed functionality to its logical conclusion, so as to demonstrate why it wouldn\u2019t make sense for it to work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T16:18:47-07:00","id":1152630,"title":"","content":"Yeah I was looking for other posts on the subject and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/940069-abjuration-exorcism-question\">saw you saying something similar</a>, I see what you mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T16:58:35-07:00","id":1152636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152593#post1152593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abjuration strips an ephemeral entity of Manifestations. Does this include Twilit Form manifestion, meaning the entity gets sent back to its realm of origin?</div> </div> </div> </div>While Twilight Form is listed as a Manifestation, none of the rules actually treats it as such. Save yourself some headache by just thinking about Twilight Form as the default form rather than a Manifestation. That's really what it is anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 10-24-2017, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T17:07:51-07:00","id":1152639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152623#post1152623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It needs to be physically there to Blast. To be physically there it needs to either Fetter, Claim, Possess, or Materialize (not including some outside interference or the rule breaking powers of idigam or Rank 6+ entities). All of these require at least the Open Condition to do. Abjuring gets rid of the Open Condition and the Resonant Condition and keeps new ones from being formed.<br /> <br /> But yes. If you try to Abjure a being that's 100 feet away from you when you only have 3 Willpower, you chose the wrong method to deal with the problem. Though you can always approach it and blast away its Conditions as you do so. Abjuring is not a long-range attack, it's a short range ward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. They can't use Numina when not manifested? Did I somehow miss that? Iirc they only need to use the Reaching manifestation to affect the physical world when in the Shadow, why couldn't they use Numina while in Twilight? In fact alot of them make lots of sense when seen in the context of twilit entities (Sign for example). I guess it's probably a sensible homerule to say Blast or similar Numina only affect other twilit creatures when used in Twilight, but I don't remember it being anywhere in the rules right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T17:17:18-07:00","id":1152645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152639#post1152639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait. They can't use Numina when not manifested? Did I somehow miss that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I said they can't use Numina on you.<br /> <br /> P129, 'Entities in Twilight can only attack or be attacked by other ephemeral beings of the same type, unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane.'<br /> <br /> They would need some way to affect a non-Twilight entity, which would be difficult near the abjured spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T17:24:49-07:00","id":1152647,"title":"","content":"A few corrections: Fettered ephemerals are still in Twilight Form and are not material, and ephemerals using Claim or Possess are explicitly barred from using Numina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T06:51:02-07:00","id":1152789,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the &