<div class=\"message\">Do you think that maybe a Kindred's heart could be removed from their chest?<br /> Kept intact, but separate, from the vampire.<br /> Thus the one keeping it could force them to do as they please or they stake it with a vengeance.<br /> Good plot? Possible Merit? Screams Cheiron Group or Vindictive Magician to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's an Ordo Dracul ability. Accurately enough called, 'Surgical Heart Removal.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T00:08:41-07:00","id":1155316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1155293#post1155293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that maybe a Kindred's heart could be removed from their chest?<br /> Kept intact, but separate, from the vampire.<br /> Thus the one keeping it could force them to do as they please or they stake it with a vengeance.<br /> Good plot? Possible Merit? Screams Cheiron Group or Vindictive Magician to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T05:42:52-08:00","id":1156301,"title":"","content":"Do the &quot;Broken&quot; condition<br /> <br /> &quot;Apply a -2 to all Social rolls and rolls involving Resolve, and a -5 to any use of the Intimidation Skill&quot;<br /> <br /> Applies to resistance rolls?<br /> <br /> By this i mean someone tries to intimidate a &quot;broken&quot; character would the roll be <br /> <br /> &quot;Manipulation + Intimidation - (Victim\u00b4s composure - 2)&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T10:04:21-08:00","id":1156382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1156301#post1156301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Manipulation + Intimidation - (Victim\u00b4s composure - 2)&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s not a roll, so no. But it would apply to contests, eg \u201cManipulation + Intimidation <i>vs</i> (Victim\u2019s Composure - 2)\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T17:33:38-08:00","id":1156524,"title":"","content":"If you were carrying a shield and were using a one-handed gun, do you get the penalties for concealment, or is it assumed you can move the shield as to not get in your way while you're firing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5387-peteman","name":"Peteman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T01:04:17-08:00","id":1156608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peteman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1156524#post1156524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were carrying a shield and were using a one-handed gun, do you get the penalties for concealment, or is it assumed you can move the shield as to not get in your way while you're firing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still get the penalty, its more than just moving the shield out of the way to not get it, its taking into account and all the ducking, raising it, using the shield over the entire time your using it for concealment. You could argue you dont get a penalty for concealment from a wall because you look around it when your firing back, its more an abstraction of the time your waiting/gaining the bonus that you cant concentrate entirely on firing back as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T04:12:57-08:00","id":1156627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1152789#post1152789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the &quot;can only attack other ephemerals&quot; thing refers to physical attacks. Numina like blast work fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1156608#post1156608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still get the penalty, its more than just moving the shield out of the way to not get it, its taking into account and all the ducking, raising it, using the shield over the entire time your using it for concealment. You could argue you dont get a penalty for concealment from a wall because you look around it when your firing back, its more an abstraction of the time your waiting/gaining the bonus that you cant concentrate entirely on firing back as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of things in the system work this way. Remember, taking an action to attack someone isn't just the discrete action of firing a single round or whatever. It's everything that goes into the ~3 seconds spent trying to harm someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T01:04:24-08:00","id":1156921,"title":"","content":"Wait, you\u2019re saying that carrying a shield gives you a concealment penalty on rolls to shoot other people? I don\u2019t think that\u2019s how that works...<br /> <br /> EDIT: Yeah,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Concealed: A character who wields a shield but doesn\u2019t use it to attack can add its Size to his Defense, and uses its Size as a concealment modifier against ranged attacks. </div> </div> </div>Nothing in there about the concealment modifier penalizing her own attacks.<br /> <br /> EDIT2: Ahh, I found it:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A character who is concealed and wants to fire at someone else takes a penalty to his Firearms attack that\u2019s one less than the penalty afforded by the character\u2019s protection </div> </div> </div>So yeah, if you\u2019re concealed by a shield, incoming Firearms attacks take a penalty equal to its size, and outgoing Firearms attacks take a penalty equal to one less than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-08-2017, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T10:58:26-08:00","id":1157057,"title":"","content":"Can it be assumed that the 1e mechanic of &quot;zero dots in an Attribute means you can't even roll tasks with that Attribute&quot; does not apply in 2e? I can''t find an equivalent statement in any subsequent book and common sense combined with lack of appropriate Skills makes the potential absurdity of e.g. animals successfully performing Research tasks fairly unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T03:05:32-08:00","id":1157233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1157057#post1157057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can it be assumed that the 1e mechanic of &quot;zero dots in an Attribute means you can't even roll tasks with that Attribute&quot; does not apply in 2e? I can''t find an equivalent statement in any subsequent book and common sense combined with lack of appropriate Skills makes the potential absurdity of e.g. animals successfully performing Research tasks fairly unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd assume so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T14:01:38-08:00","id":1157631,"title":"","content":"So, I kept digging around for possible solutions to the question I asked two weeks ago (Merits for Crossover Contracts for Changeling; You guys were incredibly helpful btw, forgot to thank you), and I found satisfying solution for G-M Crossover Contracts: Destiny Merit. It's specifically noted in DtD that beings with the Merit always have Infrastructure Condition. Perfect for depicting Changeling getting more and more interviewed into Its Plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T10:36:21-08:00","id":1160906,"title":"","content":"I know these are just examples and i'm free to change them however i want, but i still have questions about what's written in these examples.<br /> Dread Power: Miracle - description says that when your wish is granted, your aspiration becomes impossible to fulfill or replace. So, what does that mean from roleplaying standpoint? And isn't this a pretty small price?<br /> Jersey Devil. His bane is &quot;Pure seawater no human has swum in&quot;. I know he's pretty powerful, but what does that even mean? Where do you even get something like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23530-dante-ru","name":"Dante[RU]","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T16:04:04-08:00","id":1160996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1160906#post1160906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dread Power: Miracle - description says that when your wish is granted, your aspiration becomes impossible to fulfill or replace. So, what does that mean from roleplaying standpoint? And isn't this a pretty small price?</div> </div> </div> </div>Locking out one of your Aspirations forever means that it basically serves no benefit and offers no reward. Meanwhile, you then have a maximum of two Aspirations to work with going forward, which limits the extent to which your personal drive and destiny can insulate you against Social Maneuvering and stagnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T20:42:48-08:00","id":1161066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante[RU]</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1160906#post1160906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jersey Devil. His bane is &quot;Pure seawater no human has swum in&quot;. I know he's pretty powerful, but what does that even mean? Where do you even get something like this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I got this one. You need to sink him in the ocean deeper than is humanly possible to swim or dive to get such water. A fast boat, an anchor and a trip past the continental shelf would likely do the trick, until someone summons him again, or however he recovers from a Bane caused death. Remember the Immortal Dread power comes with a resurrection clause.<br /> <br /> The real question is who lost/is going to lose their soul to learn that and how are the PCs going to discover that Bane? <br /> <br /> The only way to permanently thwart this devil is to vanquish it with its Bane and if possible prevent its resurrection, an impossible feat for celestial alignments and extremely daunting to erase all record of a dire ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-20-2017, 11:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T20:48:45-08:00","id":1161069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1161066#post1161066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got this one. You need to sink him in the ocean deeper than is humanly possible to swim or dive to get such water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they mean that, since water doesn't just stand still, there's no way to tell who's been in it before. Someone may have never been to that <i>place </i>before, but that <i>water </i>could have been at the Jersey shore a week ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T21:09:05-08:00","id":1161078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1161069#post1161069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they mean that, since water doesn't just stand still, there's no way to tell who's been in it before. Someone may have never been to that <i>place </i>before, but that <i>water </i>could have been at the Jersey shore a week ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well for that interpretation you'd need water that was still sea water, ie not manufactured and possibly predates man like prehistoric sea ice. Melt and you have sea water no human has ever swam in. I will note that is a much more harshly restrictive interpretation, but not impossible with ice core studies.<br /> But then again my original interpretation may be valid, as place could be implied by the restriction of the activity needing to have never taken place there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-21-2017, 12:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T11:13:45-08:00","id":1166310,"title":"","content":"What chronicles are you expected to run in this splat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23562-fruity20","name":"fruity20","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-09T11:54:40-08:00","id":1166314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fruity20</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1166310#post1166310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What chronicles are you expected to run in this splat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mysteries, thrillers, horror and (less so but it's still an option) sci-fi. Most thriller, mystery and horror movie protagonists tend to be flatscan humans, thrown into things beyond their depth. There's a lot of books in first edition that offer advice for this, depending on the game you want to play. Ghost Stories for ghost stories. Tales of 13th Precinct can delve from standard police procedural to something like Seven or Deliver Us From Evil. Inferno has all your demonic needs, offering actual demons and cults and possessed. Mysterious places has some offerings for places that seem weird, and obviously inspirational media for that is all over, with shows like Stranger Things, games like Silent Hill and Fatal Frame, movies like Pet Semetary.<br /> <br /> Before Hunter the Vigil came out I ran a mortal hunter game where each of the PCs had some sort of special knack and they got caught up in a turf war between vampires preying on their neighborhood. There was some Buffy-esque stuff going on, too, like a zookeeper using mystical hyenas to avenge his bullied son. And some sci-fi, as a pathogen got loose in a neighboring school that mixed a rage virus with a flesh-morphing thing, turning rooms of students into masses of angry limbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-09-2017, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-10T15:45:04-08:00","id":1166551,"title":"","content":"Does Close Quarters Combat *** (Armored Coffin) affect creatures with natural armour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5387-peteman","name":"Peteman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T08:09:59-08:00","id":1166708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Peteman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1166551#post1166551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Close Quarters Combat *** (Armored Coffin) affect creatures with natural armour?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say no <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">. That holds true for body armor just as much as anything else. </span></span> </div> </div> </div>The maneuver is taking advantage of the fact you can grab bits of your opponents body armour for easier grappling. If maybe a creatures natural armor was plated, or easy to grab then id maybe allow it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T07:57:28-08:00","id":1167000,"title":"","content":"How would dual wielding pistols work? Add damage once then use the rules for firing at multiple targets with additional penalties if not ambidextrous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T10:38:45-08:00","id":1167040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1167000#post1167000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would dual wielding pistols work? Add damage once then use the rules for firing at multiple targets with additional penalties if not ambidextrous?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The character gets to choose which one to shoot each turn??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T10:55:25-08:00","id":1167046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1167040#post1167040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character gets to choose which one to shoot each turn??</div> </div> </div> </div>This. There's no rule for bursts with more than one weapon, and you can only shoot one per turn when shooting single round. If you want to do something with two firearms you'd have to come up with a Fighting Style for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T20:20:09-08:00","id":1167210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1167000#post1167000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would dual wielding pistols work? Add damage once then use the rules for firing at multiple targets with additional penalties if not ambidextrous?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was rules for duel wielding in 1E, &quot;Gunslinger&quot; merit in the core book. It's a three dot merit, needing three dots in Dexterity and Firearms. -2 offhand penalty if you don't have ambidextrous, -1 to the second attack, and lose your defense if you pick two targets instead of shooting one guy twice.<br /> <br /> It was...pretty overpowered, even with 1E rules. The GMC rules mean that weapons are much deadlier than they where before, though the accuracy went down, and this would be devastating if brought directly into 2E. One of the reasons you don't see a lot of &quot;Double Attack&quot; merits anymore-they are super powerful.<br /> <br /> So if you want to duel wield with GMC rules, there is a two-weapon melee merit in Hurt Locker we could base a house rule on. One of the dots adds the weapon's bonus to the roll (instead of damage). This is a bit strange for what we are going for-it would mean that some guy blasting away with two pistols is more accurate than the guy using the weapon normally. The last one is a true &quot;Attack Two different people at once&quot; attack. It requires 1 Willpower to use, has a penalty of -1 (though I would suggest a larger penalty for guns), and uses one roll. If the roll is successful, you decide which weapon's damage bonus hits which target. This could be made into a two-weapon range attack, if you wanted (though I would suggest steeper penalties, maybe even adding in the opponent's defense).<br /> <br /> As you said, another option is basing the rules on autofire. -1 for trying to hit a second target, another penalty for trying to use two guns at once. If you limit your players to 2 targets for 2 pistols, then as above you can just make them decide which target gets which damage bonus.<br /> <br /> Other than that, the default rules in the current addition are what the other guys said: You have a gun in each hand, you get to choose which one to fire. Twice the bullets, but not as cinematic or impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T20:31:05-08:00","id":1167214,"title":"","content":"Considering how combat works, and each roll is not a single punch or gunshot, you can encompass a volley of bullets from two guns in one Firearms roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T04:11:34-08:00","id":1167260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1167214#post1167214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how combat works, and each roll is not a single punch or gunshot, you can encompass a volley of bullets from two guns in one Firearms roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, nevermind that akimbo gunslinging is a completely impractical thing that only works in movies for rule of cool. It goes extremely against gun safety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T05:47:12-08:00","id":1167276,"title":"","content":"Most effective way to use two guns is to fire with one until it's empty, and then swap to the other. And even then you're only doubling the time between reloads at the cost of making them take twice as long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T09:16:52-08:00","id":1167323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1167260#post1167260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, nevermind that akimbo gunslinging is a completely impractical thing that only works in movies for rule of cool. It goes extremely against gun safety.</div> </div> </div> </div>I keep forgetting that the world of darkness is meant to be a 110% realistic simulation game without any common fantasy or fictional concepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1167214#post1167214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how combat works, and each roll is not a single punch or gunshot, you can encompass a volley of bullets from two guns in one Firearms roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making it a single roll with a fancy description and no real effect is another option, but if he is using vanilla GMC rules he still has to do bullet counting, and would still have to decide which gun actually dealt the damage in the case they are different models.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T09:36:04-08:00","id":1167333,"title":"","content":"My take on dual wielding is to either allow Medium Bursts and use the rules for Autofire. Probably without the extra die and a penalty for using two weapons, unless you got Ambi merit, then you get rid of the penalty.<br /> The other take would be to add both guns damage modifiers and go about normal business, maybe with a penalty on the attack pool.<br /> And add another -1 to initiative modifier for dual wielding.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T01:32:42-08:00","id":1168331,"title":"","content":"Can a Killing Blow be performed on a character that has been Restrained in a Grapple?<br /> <br /> Hold removes Defense --&gt; Restrain inflicts the Immobilized Tilt<br /> Immobilized: 'No combat actions. Can't move or apply Defense.'<br /> Killing Blow: '... when opponent is unconscious, <b>completely immobile, or otherwise totally defenseless.</b>'<br /> <br /> So let's say in combat Character 1 Grapples and Restrains Character 2. Character 3 comes over and sticks a knife in Character 2. Killing Blow?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13318-cainite","name":"Cainite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T02:29:55-08:00","id":1168338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1168331#post1168331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Killing Blow be performed on a character that has been Restrained in a Grapple?<br /> <br /> Hold removes Defense --&gt; Restrain inflicts the Immobilized Tilt<br /> Immobilized: 'No combat actions. Can't move or apply Defense.'<br /> Killing Blow: '... when opponent is unconscious, <b>completely immobile, or otherwise totally defenseless.</b>'<br /> <br /> So let's say in combat Character 1 Grapples and Restrains Character 2. Character 3 comes over and sticks a knife in Character 2. Killing Blow?</div> </div> </div> </div>personally i would say no because <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">If<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> grappled, the character can struggle as normal but can only<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\"> select the Break Free move on a success</span></span></span></span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>No killing blows if your target can struggle still. The target not getting any defense is deadly enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T06:36:38-08:00","id":1168357,"title":"","content":"The way I would represent dual wielding is to allow the character to use burst fire rules with smaller guns that normally can't. So you gain the benefit of bonus dice/multiple targets because you're firing more bullets. I wouldn't allow it with larger automatic weapons, at that point you need both hands to use the weapon effectively at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T07:05:07-08:00","id":1168362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1167333#post1167333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on dual wielding is to either allow Medium Bursts and use the rules for Autofire. Probably without the extra die and a penalty for using two weapons, unless you got Ambi merit, then you get rid of the penalty.<br /> The other take would be to add both guns damage modifiers and go about normal business, maybe with a penalty on the attack pool.<br /> And add another -1 to initiative modifier for dual wielding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd do something similar - use the damage rating for both weapons, but apply the non-Ambidextrous penalty to the roll, require drawing each weapon to take the appropriate action (unless using Quick Draw), and apply both initiative penalties for both weapons.<br /> <br /> This would make dual wielding firearms overall a really crappy idea, but if you really want to specialize in it, it can serve some purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T03:34:24-08:00","id":1168751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cainite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1168331#post1168331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Killing Blow be performed on a character that has been Restrained in a Grapple?</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe that is the intent. Werewolves are all about harrying the opponent and taking them to the ground before finishing them off. Fits perfectly.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T03:41:40-08:00","id":1168752,"title":"","content":"Killing Blow is a general rule, though. Far from unique to werewolves. Rather, they have the Efficient Killer Merit in order to use Killing Blow more often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T05:57:04-08:00","id":1168781,"title":"","content":"Without a merit to reflect special training I don't think an opponent restrained in a grapple should qualify. For one thing, you have to worry about the person holding them. That inflicts a penalty if you're using a firearm, and even with a melee weapon it's going to impact your ability to deliver a perfect lethal blow. For another, Killing Blow mentions having time to line up the attack perfectly. A character being restrained and then killed in the same, or even on the subsequent turn, doesn't really fit with the description of the base option and seems more like something you'd get from a merit like Efficient Killer or Killer Instinct.<br /> <br /> I'd allow it if they took three turns to aim though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-19T06:56:36-08:00","id":1168790,"title":"","content":"New maneuver for the Grappling Style Merit found in Chronicles of Darkness (p. 62) and Hurt Locker (p. 49)<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Maiden (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> <i>Additional prerequisite: Joint Lock Maneuver.</i> Once you've successfully applied the Immobilized Tilt on an opponent you can follow up by locking them completely in place, snuffing out any remaining struggles. As an instant action, roll your normal grappling dice pool contested by the opponents Strength + Stamina. If you succeed the opponent becomes so helpless they're open for killing blows (see Chronicles of Darkness, p. 93) from others.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> This Maneuver can not be used against any opponents with non-human body shapes, unless the character has received special training in such unorthodox grappling techniques.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T16:27:36-08:00","id":1174684,"title":"","content":"Are there rules for fighting hordes? If so where are they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5448-kavagja","name":"Kavagja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T16:51:07-08:00","id":1174690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kavagja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1174684#post1174684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there rules for fighting hordes? If so where are they?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you mean like mass battles or swarms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T09:59:47-08:00","id":1174899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1174690#post1174690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Do you mean like mass battles or swarms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Swarms. Please and thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5448-kavagja","name":"Kavagja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T12:18:06-08:00","id":1174941,"title":"","content":"So Mage, vampire and Demon have descriptions of swarms, maybe others but i didnt check them to be honest. Each description is slightly different though. I would check out the demon core book for the Swarm (enviromental) tilt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T12:20:05-08:00","id":1174942,"title":"","content":"Woops, didnt see my own post so posted twice. lalalala.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-10T19:10:52-08:00","id":1175059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kavagja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1174684#post1174684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there rules for fighting hordes? If so where are they?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since you are in CofD section and not a specific game line here is something:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CofD, Pg. 150</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">The Horde</span></b></span><br /> <i>Low, incessant moaning</i><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Background:</b> When there\u2019s no more room in hell, the dead will walk the earth. That\u2019s how the old saying goes, and whether it\u2019s true or not, sometimes the earth splits, coffins crack, and the unquiet dead crawl out of the ground<br /> to prey on the living. Individually, they\u2019re barely any threat: slow and stumbling, with scarcely animal-level intelligence.<br /> The problem is that they\u2019re never encountered individually,and a dozen or more of the things can drag down even the strongest by sheer weight of numbers.<br /> Sometimes there\u2019s a guiding intelligence behind the Horde: a witch might raise up an army of undead servants,<br /> or a demon might lay a curse on a community. More often, though, the dead simply rise and shamble, hungry for flesh, with no discernible motivation. Maybe the town\u2019s cemetery is cursed ground, or maybe a virus escapes from a military transport truck. Sometimes it just happens, and all you can hope to do is hole up and survive.<br /> <b>Description:</b> The classic zombie horde is made up of a mass of shambling, moaning corpses, usually in various stages of decomposition and often bearing obviously-fatal wounds.<br /> They wander aimlessly, shuffling about with no clear purpose until they scent fresh, living meat. Once they become aware of prey, they might burst into frantic activity, like a crocodile, or they might never vary their plodding, inexorable pace; but either way, if you let them get close, if you let your guard down for even a second, you\u2019re dead.<br /> That\u2019s the classic zombie horde, but with just a few small changes to dice pools and Dread Powers, the Horde pulls double duty as modern \u201cfast\u201d zombies, a hive of monstrous insects, or a pack of weird, wormlike hunters from beneath the ground. Maybe your Horde is the result of a virus that drives living people to phenomenal heights of rage, or maybe it\u2019s some swarm of Precambrian horrors unearthed from an underground vault.<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints: </b>The trick to using the Horde is that it\u2019s not really a \u201cmonster\u201d in the same sense that a murderous Horrors and wonders-antagonists ghost or a hungry werewolf is. The Horde isn\u2019t an antagonist, it\u2019s an environmental threat; use it to force characters together that otherwise wouldn\u2019t interact, whether due to circumstances or deliberate avoidance. The constant threats of the Horde breaking through the defenses, preventing characters from going out and gathering supplies, or reaching safety acts as a stressor, highlighting personal motivations and driving conflict. When you\u2019re developing a story involving the Horde, look at your characters\u2019 (both the players and your Storyteller characters) Virtues, Vices, and Aspirations. Look for characters whose Anchors are, if not directly opposed,<br /> at least orthogonal to each other. Find opportunities to put those characters together in scenes with real stakes: gathering supplies, pushing back a zombie siege, or maybe just patching up the wounded. Put their Aspirations in jeopardy, or make them able to be realized only at risk to the rest of the characters. The Horde isn\u2019t the frying pan or the fire; it\u2019s the pressure cooker.<br /> With the popularity of zombie apocalypse fiction in mainstream media, it\u2019s tempting to see end of the world scenarios and zombies as going hand in hand. While you can certainly tell zombie apocalypse stories with the Chronicles of Darkness, you don\u2019t have to immediately reach for the \u201cblow up the world\u201d button to use the Horde. Smaller outbreaks of the undead, either in remote locations or bad neighborhoods suffering from urban decay, can create the same feeling of isolation. The ubiquity of cell phones and internet connections can make it trickier, but anything from bad weather, to power failures, to larger disasters that jam up phone lines and hinder emergency response services can deal with those problems.<br /> <br /> Best At (7 dice): Sniffing out humans, dragging you down by sheer weight of numbers, anything that benefits from a massive wall of flesh.<br /> Worst At (1 Die): Acting alone, being fast or<br /> clever.<br /> Willpower/Scene: 3<br /> Aspiration: To feast on the flesh of the living.<br /> Initiative: 1<br /> Defense: 3<br /> Speed: 5<br /> Health: 7<br /> Weapons/Attacks:<br /> Type Damage Range Dice Pool<br /> Grapple 0B Melee 7 (in group), 1<br /> (alone)<br /> Bite 2L Melee 7 (in group), 1<br /> (alone)<br /> Banes: Attacks to the head<br /> Dread Powers: Hunter\u2019s Senses (human flesh),<br /> Natural Weapons \u2022\u2022, Toxic \u2022, Unbreakable<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>New Environmental Tilt:</b></span><br /> <b>Zombies!</b><br /> The Horde Traits presented here work for when you need to focus in on an action scene involving a few characters and a modest number of zombies, but when you want to highlight the sheer, swarming mass of the walking dead, they\u2019re not practical. This Tilt represents any area that\u2019s packed full of zombies or similar monsters.<br /> <b>Effects: </b>Characters moving through the Horde are slowed by the mindless, grasping hands and sheer press of decomposing bodies. Within the area affected by the Tilt, characters lose their bonus to Speed (so normal humans have a Speed equal to Strength + Dexterity). Characters who move at anything less than full speed (that is, using an Instant action to run) are subject to an attack using the Horde\u2019s best dice pool. An exceptional success on this attack inflicts the Knocked Down Tilt.<br /> In addition, if the zombies are especially ripe, moving through the area might require characters to make a reflexive Stamina + Composure roll every minute or suffer the moderate version of the Sick Tilt.<br /> <b>Causing the Tilt:</b> Any large group of mostlypassive monsters could cause this Tilt. It also works for modeling the effects of being caught up in a large riot or similar crush of humanity.<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt:</b> The whole point of the Tilt is that it represents too many zombies to fight effectively, but characters might be able to draw the Horde off (maybe by firing guns or operating loud, heavy machinery elsewhere), or drive them back if the Horde suffers from a Bane (if your zombies are afraid of fire, for example, Molotov cocktails or simply carrying torches might disperse them).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T22:42:00-08:00","id":1176698,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to analyze the Integrity stat of another character? The fact that a low Integrity can mean extreme trauma or extreme immorality, and the fact that some people can get away with actual murder without Integrity hits, really interests me as a double edged threat detection system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T00:33:30-08:00","id":1176713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1176698#post1176698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to analyze the Integrity stat of another character? The fact that a low Integrity can mean extreme trauma or extreme immorality, and the fact that some people can get away with actual murder without Integrity hits, really interests me as a double edged threat detection system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure most supernaturals have abilities to tell. If they aren't straight 'give me a number' abilities they have sideways methods.<br /> <br /> Flatscan humans can use the Empath Merit from Hurt Locker, which requires a Wits+Empathy roll. It's not a Supernatural Merit, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T00:40:47-08:00","id":1176715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1176713#post1176713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flatscan humans can use the Empath Merit from Hurt Locker, which requires a Wits+Empathy roll. It's not a Supernatural Merit, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow perfect, I overlooked that (was just looking at the way it helps with Breaking Points). Thanks!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T02:43:51-08:00","id":1177808,"title":"","content":"I'm sure this has been covered already, probably somewhere in this thread. I've searched the specific topics (I.E. Changeling the Lost, Hunter the Vigil, all those) and I see a lot of 2E threads, which leads to my question. I know (or at least I think I know) that 2E versions Changeling, Hunter, and Geist are in the works, so I was wondering if there were any release dates posted anywhere, or a general period of time when to expect these. Oh, and is there going to be a 2E Mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23703-sean-snyder","name":"Sean Snyder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T07:11:53-08:00","id":1177838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sean Snyder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1177808#post1177808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure this has been covered already, probably somewhere in this thread. I've searched the specific topics (I.E. Changeling the Lost, Hunter the Vigil, all those) and I see a lot of 2E threads, which leads to my question. I know (or at least I think I know) that 2E versions Changeling, Hunter, and Geist are in the works, so I was wondering if there were any release dates posted anywhere, or a general period of time when to expect these. Oh, and is there going to be a 2E Mummy?</div> </div> </div> </div>No release dates. <br /> Mummy is getting a 2ED.<br /> The text for Changeling 2ED is already fully available to anyone that backed the KS.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T16:04:41-08:00","id":1181261,"title":"","content":"Something that's not entirely clear to me, but can ephemeral beings use their Numina to affect the physical world at all times, or only if they are Manifested?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T19:34:15-08:00","id":1181313,"title":"","content":"Numina need to be used in conjunction with Reaching to bypass the gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T20:11:25-08:00","id":1181320,"title":"","content":"The Gauntlet is the membrane between the material world and the Shadow Realm, though. Ephemeral beings who are in Twilight are in the material world, just out of step with it. Off the top of my head, I would say an unmanifested ephemeral being can affect material things outside Twilight with their Numina, but note that some Numina have requirements that make this difficult. For example, Awe requires the subject to be able to see the entity, and Aggressive Meme requires the entity to be able to communicate with the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T23:23:12-08:00","id":1181339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1181261#post1181261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that's not entirely clear to me, but can ephemeral beings use their Numina to affect the physical world at all times, or only if they are Manifested?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, Twilight Form is a Manifestation, so ephemeral brings in the material world are always Manifested.<br /> <br /> If an ephemeral being is in the material world, it can use its Numena to affect other beings and objects in the material world, provided it meets any criteria for the Numen in question. For example, Awe requires the subject to see the being using it, so the being would need to Manifest with Image or Materialize or something so it could be seen. However, unless otherwise specified, an ephemeral being doesn\u2019t need to be Materialized in order to use its Numina.<br /> <br /> Affecting entities and objects in other worlds with Numina is more complicated. For example, a spirit in the Shadow needs to be Reaching in order to affect the Material with its Numina and vise-versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T03:29:58-08:00","id":1181355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1181339#post1181339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an ephemeral being is in the material world, it can use its Numena to affect other beings and objects in the material world, provided it meets any criteria for the Numen in question. For example, Awe requires the subject to see the being using it, so the being would need to Manifest with Image or Materialize or something so it could be seen. However, unless otherwise specified, an ephemeral being doesn\u2019t need to be Materialized in order to use its Numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>So an unmanifested can use any of its powers on a target in the material world as long as said power does not require the victim to see/smell/hear/touch the user, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T03:57:51-08:00","id":1181358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1181339#post1181339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, Twilight Form is a Manifestation, so ephemeral brings in the material world are always Manifested.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except while Twilight Form is listed as a Manifestation it's actually never treated as one. If it were the word Manifested wouldn't have any meaning because either the ephemeral is in an ephemeral realm, or it's in the material where it's always Manifested.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T07:07:27-08:00","id":1181387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1181358#post1181358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except while Twilight Form is listed as a Manifestation it's actually never treated as one. If it were the word Manifested wouldn't have any meaning because either the ephemeral is in an ephemeral realm, or it's in the material where it's always Manifested.</div> </div> </div> </div>Twilight Form is treated as a Manifestation unless you presuppose a definition for the word Manifestation (such as its 1e definition), rather than defining it based on what Manifestations actually do in 2e. Twilight Form, Gauntlet Breach, Reaching, Fetter, Claim, and Gate are all Manifestations. What these powers have in common is that they are all either means of entering the material or ways of existing within the material. So, in second edition, at least, Manifested does seem to mean \u201cexisting in the material world.\u201d<br /> <br /> Reaching would seem to be an exception to this definition, but again, only if we presuppose its 1e definition. Keeping in mind that in 2e, Reaching is also the thing werewolves do to cross the gauntlet (as opposed to stepping sideways), and there are no actual rules mechanisms by which a spirit can cross the Gauntlet at Locus in 2e, but they are automatically considered Reaching, and the fact that a Reaching spirit in 2e can perceive the other side of the Gauntlet and affect it with its Numena and other Manifestations, it would seem that Reaching in 2e is in fact a means of existing partly on both sides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1181355#post1181355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So an unmanifested can use any of its powers on a target in the material world as long as said power does not require the victim to see/smell/hear/touch the user, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I would argue that an ephemeral entity in the material world is by definition manifested. An <i>unmaterialized</i> entity can use any of its powers that don\u2019t require touch, an invisible entity can use any of its powers that don\u2019t require it to be seen, etc. Basically, assume an entity can use a power to affect the world it currently exists in, unless that power requires the entity to interact with the world in a way that it can\u2019t do in its current Manifestation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T08:16:38-08:00","id":1181400,"title":"","content":"'Entities in Twilight can only attack or be attacked by other ephemeral beings of the same type, unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane.'<br /> <br /> It's pretty clear people read and do what they want from this, but it certainly appears like you can't just use Numina to, say, blast mortals from Twilight. That said there's a couple that require you to be in Twilight (and based on this you can probably figure out that a few Numina can be used from Twilight on the real world, while most can't).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T08:34:28-08:00","id":1181405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1181387#post1181387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Twilight Form is treated as a Manifestation unless you presuppose a definition for the word Manifestation (such as its 1e definition), rather than defining it based on what Manifestations actually do in 2e. Twilight Form, Gauntlet Breach, Reaching, Fetter, Claim, and Gate are all Manifestations. What these powers have in common is that they are all either means of entering the material or ways of existing within the material. So, in second edition, at least, Manifested does seem to mean \u201cexisting in the material world.\u201d<br /> <br /> Reaching would seem to be an exception to this definition, but again, only if we presuppose its 1e definition. Keeping in mind that in 2e, Reaching is also the thing werewolves do to cross the gauntlet (as opposed to stepping sideways), and there are no actual rules mechanisms by which a spirit can cross the Gauntlet at Locus in 2e, but they are automatically considered Reaching, and the fact that a Reaching spirit in 2e can perceive the other side of the Gauntlet and affect it with its Numena and other Manifestations, it would seem that Reaching in 2e is in fact a means of existing partly on both sides.<br /> <br /> Again, I would argue that an ephemeral entity in the material world is by definition manifested. An <i>unmaterialized</i> entity can use any of its powers that don\u2019t require touch, an invisible entity can use any of its powers that don\u2019t require it to be seen, etc. Basically, assume an entity can use a power to affect the world it currently exists in, unless that power requires the entity to interact with the world in a way that it can\u2019t do in its current Manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't know how Manifestations worked in 1e. I'm talking about every time the 2e books uses the word &quot;Manifest&quot; (and inflections) except in the Manifestations list.<br /> <br /> Inside the spoiler is a list of the majority of times the word &quot;Manifest&quot; appears in the Chronicles of Darkness book (when referring to ephemerals) &quot;Manifest&quot; almost always excludes Twilight Form, and sometimes appear to only refer to Materialize (and maybe Claim). This is what I mean when I say that the book never treats Twilight Form as a Manifestation.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> &quot;Almost every ephemeral being has the ability to <i>Manifest</i>, to make its presence known and affect the physical world, in ways ranging from remaining invisible but using powers, to appearing as insubstantial but visible images, to possessing a victim, sending his soul into hibernation and warping his body to suit their own uses.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here Manifest is refered to as an ability, which excludes Twilight Form which is the default form.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Some are more skilled at it than others (those so weak they can\u2019t Manifest at all are essentially impotent and don\u2019t interact with humans), but all require certain appropriate conditions before they can use these powers.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here the book refers to ephemerals that can't Manifest, despite Twilight Form being a universal Manifestation for all ephemerals. The book also says that Manifestations requires Manifestation Conditions, which also excludes Twilight Form as it requires no Manifestation Condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;An ephemeral being wanting to shift into physical form or inhabit an object, animal or person requires the area, item or character it is Manifesting into to have been prepared for its arrival. Ghosts require Anchors \u2014 places, objects and people that are linked to their living days and reinforce their failing identities. Angels can only appear in the world when enough Infrastructure has been laid out by the God-Machine. Spirits need the emotional resonance of the area or victim-host to match their own. The more powerful the Manifestation, the stronger the Condition needed. The most powerful physical forms and tightly-held victims are the result of careful husbandry by the Manifesting being, slowly building up the necessary Condition by leveraging whatever Manifestation they can produce at first. &quot;<br /> <br /> This is a continuation of the above sentence.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The majority of ghosts are poor at influencing the world, trapped in their insubstantial state and unable to even Manifest, [..]&quot;<br /> <br /> Another reference to ephemerals (ghosts) lacking Manifestations despite all ghosts having Twilight Form.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Ghosts are drawn to places and people that they had emotional connections to in life \u2014 these anchor the ghost in the world and allow those with enough power to Manifest, whereupon they carry out whatever mad urges they still feel and attempt, in their broken state, to further the goals they left undone in life. &quot;<br /> <br /> Another exclusion of Twilight Form as a Manifestation similar to above.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The State of Twilight<br /> Unless they Manifest or use a power to appear, ephemeral beings remain in their insubstantial state when in the material world. This state is described as \u201cTwilight.\u201d&quot;<br /> <br /> Here we have the most obvious and explicit exclusion of Twilight Form as a Manifestation yet. The book straight up says that when the ephemerals don't Manifest they instead are in Twilight Form.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Touching the bane while in Twilight causes a point of lethal damage per turn to non-Manifested entities.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;If the bane has been used as a weapon against the entity, the wounds suffered are aggravated for Manifest entities and lethal for entities still in Twilight.&quot;<br /> <br /> Two more exclusions of Twilight Form being a Manifestation as being in Twilight explicitly not being Manifested.<br /> This is also one of the times Manifested might not only exclude Twilight Form, as much as it just refers to Materialized and Claimed, since most Manifestations (Fettered, Possessed) explicitly leaves the entity still in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Physical attacks on a Manifested entity that would normally cause lethal damage only cause bashing damage unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane. Despite appearing to the naked eye and being solid, a Manifested spirit, ghost, or angel doesn\u2019t have any internal organs to injure.&quot;<br /> <br /> Same thing here. I'm pretty sure they mean Materialized and Claimed since that's the only Manifestations were the ephemeral becomes solid.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;All Manifestation Effects require a Power + Finesse roll to use. &quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;It can attempt to Fetter itself to the subject of the Condition, or, if the Condition is on a location, Manifest.&quot;<br /> <br /> From the Open Condition. Here Manifest can only refer to Materialize since both Possess and Fetter requires a subject.<br /> <br /> Except Twilight Form, of course.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 02-01-2018, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T08:46:29-08:00","id":1181411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1181400#post1181400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Entities in Twilight can only attack or be attacked by other ephemeral beings of the same type, unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane.'<br /> <br /> It's pretty clear people read and do what they want from this, but it certainly appears like you can't just use Numina to, say, blast mortals from Twilight. That said there's a couple that require you to be in Twilight (and based on this you can probably figure out that a few Numina can be used from Twilight on the real world, while most can't).</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s debatable whether use of the Blast Numen constitutes an \u201cattack\u201d in the sense that the word is being used here. However, if we make the reasonable assumption that it does, it\u2019s still arguable that Blast requires touch, and therefore requires Materialization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T08:57:35-08:00","id":1181417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1181405#post1181405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually don't know how Manifestations worked in 1e. I'm talking about every time the 2e books uses the word &quot;Manifest&quot; (and inflections) except in the Manifestations list.<br /> <br /> Inside the spoiler is a list of the majority of times the word &quot;Manifest&quot; appears in the Chronicles of Darkness book (when referring to ephemerals) &quot;Manifest&quot; almost always excludes Twilight Form, and sometimes appear to only refer to Materialize (and maybe Claim). This is what I mean when I say that the book never treats Twilight Form as a Manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Though, I would point out that those uses seem inconsistent. Some of them seem to refer to any means of existing within the material world, others seem to refer to any state of existence other than Twilight, some seem to refer only to Materialization and Claiming, etc. This is likely due in part to the use of natural language, in part to the writing process involving multiple drafts in which Manifestation may have had slightly different meanings, and in part due to the author\u2019s preexisting notions of Manifestation carrying over from 1e. I would still argue that, based on what Manifestations actually are and what they do within the rules, the most technically accurate definition of the word, \u201cManifestation\u201d is, \u201cMeans of entering the material world or way of existing within it.\u201d<br /> From that, we can extrapolate that the most technically accurate definition of, \u201cManifested\u201d is, \u201cexisting within the material world.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T10:55:52-08:00","id":1181440,"title":"","content":"This is not a counterargument since it's probably just a mistake. It's just a small curiosity I'd like to add.<br /> Goetia from Mage doesn't naturally have any Manifestations. By RAW that would include Twilight Form, despite there being an Attainment primarily for seeing and interacting with Goetia in Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T12:04:15-08:00","id":1181459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1181440#post1181440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not a counterargument since it's probably just a mistake. It's just a small curiosity I'd like to add.<br /> Goetia from Mage doesn't naturally have any Manifestations. By RAW that would include Twilight Form, despite there being an Attainment primarily for seeing and interacting with Goetia in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Goetia don\u2019t normally exist in the physical world and therefore don\u2019t normally need Manifestations. It takes magic to allow them to do so, and IIRC, there are a handful of spells that grant Manifestations to ephemeral entities. One would have to do this to a Goetia to give it Twilight Form or something to allow it to exist in the material. I\u2019m pretty sure this is actually working as intended, and further supports the notion that Manifestation = means of existing within the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-01-2018, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T12:19:25-08:00","id":1181464,"title":"","content":"Except Summon Goetia doesn't at all mention that it grants the Twilight Form Manifestation. In fact, it only mentions Materialized, which requires Death or Spirit, as they are the principal Arcana for granting Manifestations. The only two Manifestations explicitly possible through Mind is Familiar and Possession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T12:31:32-08:00","id":1181468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1181464#post1181464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except Summon Goetia doesn't at all mention that it grants the Twilight Form Manifestation. In fact, it only mentions Materialized, which requires Death or Spirit, as they are the principal Arcana for granting Manifestations. The only two Manifestations explicitly possible through Mind is Familiar and Possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should clarify - I think the mistake is in the handful of Mind spells that bring Goetia or other entities into Mind-resonant Twilight neglecting to mention that they grant those entities the Twilight Form Manifestation, not in Goetia lacking Twilight Form naturally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-01-2018, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T01:20:07-08:00","id":1182198,"title":"","content":"What happens when you take something (clothes, weapons) from an ephemeral entity? Are they considered a 'part' of the entity that couldn't be removed? Spirits have a Panalopy, which implies they can get special weapons, can those be taken? And if so, what happens to them if you enter the real world with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2018, 04:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T12:38:23-08:00","id":1182351,"title":"","content":"Where is this Panalopy stuff described in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T15:08:42-08:00","id":1182401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1182351#post1182351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this Panalopy stuff described in?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a first edition thing, but the ephemeral entities rules in second edition says that spirits can have weapons and Stalwart allows for them to be armored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-04-2018, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T16:06:03-08:00","id":1182423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1182401#post1182401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's a first edition thing</div> </div> </div> </div>The only instances of the word &quot;panoply&quot; I can find in my 1e PDFs are all in normal sentences talking about the breadth of options a given being has access to within a particular subset of things like relics or senses. <i>Gods in Exalted</i> have Panoply <i>Charms</i>, but to my recollection there has not been a Werewolf: the Forsaken book which covered the equipment of spirits as a special thing.<br /> <br /> There's a bit of chapter fiction in Geist 1e that implies the coat a ghost was wearing when they drowned is part of its Corpus, but otherwise nothing comes to mind as having specifically addressed the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-04T16:07:54-08:00","id":1182424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1182198#post1182198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when you take something (clothes, weapons) from an ephemeral entity? Are they considered a 'part' of the entity that couldn't be removed? Spirits have a Panalopy, which implies they can get special weapons, can those be taken? And if so, what happens to them if you enter the real world with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it\u2019s like cutting off a lock of hair, or nicking off a scale. A part of the spirit that can be removed without much damage. It\u2019ll be still made of ephemera, so it\u2019ll be of limited use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T08:20:51-08:00","id":1185194,"title":"","content":"That does lead to a related question. I once made a ghost whose Blast manifested as a burst from a ghostly M-16. Could someone also in Ghost-Frequency Twilight grab said gun and use that Blast power?<br /> <br /> Also, is there any way ephemerals, especially spirits, can have their Rank permanently degrade, barring Supernal Magic or Werewolf Rites?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T23:04:28-08:00","id":1185501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1185194#post1185194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That does lead to a related question. I once made a ghost whose Blast manifested as a burst from a ghostly M-16. Could someone also in Ghost-Frequency Twilight grab said gun and use that Blast power?<br /> <br /> Also, is there any way ephemerals, especially spirits, can have their Rank permanently degrade, barring Supernal Magic or Werewolf Rites?</div> </div> </div> </div>Either the gun is just a manifestation of the blast numina so only appears as a m-16 when he uses it and you cant steal it from the ghost, or the gun is a seperate item that the ghost makes his blast numina appear from. Even if you steal the gun you wont get access to the blast numina, you'll just have a ghost m-16. The ghost then probably has to think of another way for his blast numina to manifest..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T06:18:47-08:00","id":1186632,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this question has been addressed already:<br /> <br /> &quot;Advanced Merits&quot; (and epic/legendary) -- conceptually these are great, but I'm wondering where the idea originated from for CofD? Did it appear in a released book, or are all such Merits forum/home brew?<br /> <br /> (I also realize that several published Onyx Path authors have contributed material with advanced/legendary Merits--that's not what I'm looking for; I'm searching for a book occurrence.)<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T06:26:01-08:00","id":1186634,"title":"","content":"I do think the originated in a Hunter book, though i might be mistaken.<br /> For 2ed there are some in Beast and one or two in Mage at least. Not sure about any other in 2ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T08:36:47-08:00","id":1186680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1186634#post1186634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think the originated in a Hunter book, though i might be mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was Mortal Remains that made a reference to Dread Powers above five dots, but it didn't really go into depth for how to implement them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T09:28:18-08:00","id":1186697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1186632#post1186632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if this question has been addressed already:<br /> <br /> &quot;Advanced Merits&quot; (and epic/legendary) -- conceptually these are great, but I'm wondering where the idea originated from for CofD? Did it appear in a released book, or are all such Merits forum/home brew?<br /> <br /> (I also realize that several published Onyx Path authors have contributed material with advanced/legendary Merits--that's not what I'm looking for; I'm searching for a book occurrence.)<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As far as I know they started in Beast. It was then positited by the developers that others could theoretically have such merits as well and that led to the community driven effort to create more.<br /> <br /> There may have been something in a 1e book though, I have not read them all so am not sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T10:08:07-08:00","id":1186708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1186697#post1186697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know they started in Beast. It was then positited by the developers that others could theoretically have such merits as well and that led to the community driven effort to create more.<br /> <br /> There may have been something in a 1e book though, I have not read them all so am not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That gives me a line to follow up on. Thanks! I'll be curious to see if the idea gets used in Changeling, which is probably the closest line in certain themes. Obviously the recent Vampire books (even Thousand Years) didn't find it necessary to take that step in Merit &quot;power&quot;.<br /> <br /> Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T19:48:08-08:00","id":1187727,"title":"","content":"Question about the Light Weapons merit from the corebook: the prerequisites say &quot;Wits \u2022\u2022\u2022 or Fighting Finesse, Dexterity \u2022\u2022\u2022, Athletics \u2022\u2022, Weaponry \u2022\u2022.&quot; Am I correct in interpreting it as &quot;Either Wits 3 or Fighting Finesse, and also Dexterity 3 etc&quot;? As opposed to &quot;Either just Wits 3, or all the following&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-19T23:06:13-08:00","id":1187758,"title":"","content":"That's my reading of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-20T00:48:37-08:00","id":1187771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1187727#post1187727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question about the Light Weapons merit from the corebook: the prerequisites say &quot;Wits \u2022\u2022\u2022 or Fighting Finesse, Dexterity \u2022\u2022\u2022, Athletics \u2022\u2022, Weaponry \u2022\u2022.&quot; Am I correct in interpreting it as &quot;Either Wits 3 or Fighting Finesse, and also Dexterity 3 etc&quot;? As opposed to &quot;Either just Wits 3, or all the following&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The former interpretation would be correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T09:22:17-08:00","id":1188537,"title":"","content":"Another Merits question: can you apply the Library Merit to a Skill you don't have dots in? This would be to represent something like &quot;I inherited a bunch of books on topic (x) from my Grandma&quot; as opposed to &quot;I am interested in topic (x) and have collected these books myself.&quot; Or is this more of a judgement call for the ST?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T12:34:16-08:00","id":1188614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1188537#post1188537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another Merits question: can you apply the Library Merit to a Skill you don't have dots in? This would be to represent something like &amp;quot;I inherited a bunch of books on topic (x) from my Grandma&amp;quot; as opposed to &amp;quot;I am interested in topic (x) and have collected these books myself.&amp;quot; Or is this more of a judgement call for the ST?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like an ST call, but I would certainly allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T12:37:00-08:00","id":1188616,"title":"","content":"Seems reasonable. It's a good way to compensate for the unskilled penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T11:25:46-08:00","id":1190727,"title":"","content":"So, that's a thing that has baffled me for a while.<br /> But, some merits like Police Tactics or Close Quarters Combat refer to rolls for immobilizing, or rolls for disarming.<br /> Except, I can't actually find any such rolls in the books, both restraining an opponent and disarming him are grapple manouvers, which are declared after rolling, and in the case of CQC at least, don't really have any exceptional success/dramatic failure effects on their own.<br /> So yeah, how does all that work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11117-inquisitor","name":"Inquisitor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"138"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T11:56:02-08:00","id":1190732,"title":"","content":"While most of Police Tactics stuff refer to extensions of grappling, the Disarm maneuver is on p89 and doesn't require a grapple (though there is a disarm attempt you can manage while grappling).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T14:35:51-08:00","id":1190802,"title":"","content":"<b>What are all the ways (across the whole <i>CofD</i> spectrum) that can give an animal human-like intelligence?</b> I suddenly became enamored with the idea of a talking dog sidekick/Retainer...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T16:11:01-08:00","id":1190833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1190802#post1190802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>What are all the ways (across the whole <i>CofD</i> spectrum) that can give an animal human-like intelligence?</b> I suddenly became enamored with the idea of a talking dog sidekick/Retainer...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure if a vampire would be able to make the dog actually talk, but animal ghouls do get heightened mental stats, which means at the very least the Ghouled animal would at least be able to understand the vampire; throw the Animalism discipline in and the two could feasibly have an actual conversation.<br /> <br /> I'd say with Life Magic a mage would be able to make a talking dog, but paradox is a thing so it doesn't necessarily seem like a long term solution at the very least.<br /> <br /> One of the Wolf Gifts in werewolf allows a werewolf to have conversations with animals, but I don't know of one that would increase the animal's intelligence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T19:51:11-08:00","id":1190889,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there's another Gift that lets it understand any command given by a packmate but that's not quite human 'intelligence.'<br /> <br /> Claiming would do it, though you wouldn't really have a normal dog there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-01T22:19:37-08:00","id":1190907,"title":"","content":"Cryptids in the DtD sense (animals mutated by exposure to the God-Machine) could become intelligent and also gain the ability to communicate. An Angel or Demon could also end up with an animal Cover, but that doesn't sound like what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Hedge Beasts (at least in 1e) are basically animal-form hobgoblins, so a talking dog would be perfectly reasonable. They're not mentioned in the 2e manuscript preview from the KS, but they're not explicitly disallowed, either. Although a 2e Hedge Dog would have the Hedge Denizen condition, meaning it knows three Goblin Contracts and gains Deprived whenever it leaves the Hedge, which again might not be what you're looking for. (In 1e these were handled by the Hedge Beast Companion merit, rather than Retainer.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","user":"Mad_Maudlin","date":". 03-02-2018, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T07:28:53-08:00","id":1191617,"title":"","content":"Is there a difference between 1 success and 4 success when an action is not contested ? (excluding exceptional success )<br /> <br /> For example I ask my players to roll a perception roll Wits + Composure. My players succeed with 1,2 &amp; 3 successes. Do players who got 1 success get less information than players who got 3 success ? I could not find anything about this in the core book. It seems all it matters is if you get 1 success or 5 (when the roll is not a versus roll).<br /> <br /> <br /> Another question. Do players get minuses when trying to achieve something, they do not have a speciality in ? <br /> For example if I have 4 dots in drive skill, with no specialities and I try to fly a helicopter. Will I get any penalties for trying to achieve a task I am not specialised at ? I might be a pro stunt driver, but I am not a pilot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T08:02:25-08:00","id":1191620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1191617#post1191617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a difference between 1 success and 4 success when an action is not contested ? (excluding exceptional success )</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally no, but combat is a huge exception to that rule. Outside of combat (and certain supernatural powers such as most Auspex uses in VtR) the design philosophy is that the number of successes shouldn't matter as long as it's a Success.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another question. Do players get minuses when trying to achieve something, they do not have a speciality in ?<br /> For example if I have 4 dots in drive skill, with no specialities and I try to fly a helicopter. Will I get any penalties for trying to achieve a task I am not specialised at ? I might be a pro stunt driver, but I am not a pilot. </div> </div> </div>I don't think second edition has rules for it, but it makes sense to penalise actions when the character doesn't have a related Specialty <i>but only for highly specialised actions</i>. You definitely need a Helicopter spec to pilot a helicopter, but not for cars which is what the Drive Skill is primarily about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T08:32:13-08:00","id":1191622,"title":"","content":"For perception the one with most successes get the most details from me, usually.<br /> <br /> Yes, if you're trying to fly a helicopter with no experience doing so what so ever, hence no specialty, you'll take the -3 untrained penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T08:45:32-08:00","id":1191624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1191622#post1191622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For perception the one with most successes get the most details from me, usually.<br /> <br /> Yes, if you're trying to fly a helicopter with no experience doing so what so ever, hence no specialty, you'll take the -3 untrained penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> do you know where in the core book does it state the penalty ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T09:56:20-08:00","id":1191648,"title":"","content":"It's the standard penalty for untrained mental skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T10:25:31-08:00","id":1191658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1191648#post1191648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the standard penalty for untrained mental skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is explicitly about Skills without dots, not Skills without a relevant Specialty, and, as you said, for Mental Skills. Physical Skills such as Drive has a -1 penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-04-2018, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T10:26:47-08:00","id":1191659,"title":"","content":"Oh, woe is me, what shall we do if we cannot abstract the system to similar situations!<br /> <br /> You don't think it's a fitting level of penalty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T10:29:27-08:00","id":1191662,"title":"","content":"Definitely. But I don't present my house rule as a rule and point towards a conflicting rule as a source.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T10:47:38-08:00","id":1191676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1191624#post1191624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> do you know where in the core book does it state the penalty ?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">If you want your character to be capable of piloting aircraft as well, you need to take the Skill Specialty in Piloting.<br /> A character without the Piloting Specialty is considered<br /> untrained if he attempts to operate a plane or other aircraft</span></span> </div> </div> </div>Its literally right there in the skill description guys come on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-04-2018, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T11:02:44-08:00","id":1191682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1191676#post1191676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its literally right there in the skill description guys come on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. In my defence something like that should be presented as a general rule instead of being nested inside a specific skill description. Piloting was just an example; not the focus of the question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T11:21:00-08:00","id":1191687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1191676#post1191676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Its literally right there in the skill description guys come on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I used drive as an example, but it truly is in the skill, haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1013-stralos","name":"Stralos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1013_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T15:53:46-08:00","id":1191764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stralos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1191617#post1191617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a difference between 1 success and 4 success when an action is not contested ? (excluding exceptional success )<br /> <br /> For example I ask my players to roll a perception roll Wits + Composure. My players succeed with 1,2 &amp; 3 successes. Do players who got 1 success get less information than players who got 3 success ? I could not find anything about this in the core book. It seems all it matters is if you get 1 success or 5 (when the roll is not a versus roll).</div> </div> </div> </div>Tessie already answered this, but to be more specific: unless the roll says otherwise, explicitly no. The probability math of the Storytelling System isn't equipped to handle granular successes like, say, the World of Darkness or Exalted's systems do; it's not uncommon to roll only a single success on even quite large dice pools. If you roll successes, your success isn't partial.<br /> <br /> This probably doesn't matter that much for your example, where multiple players in the same party are succeeding, but characters will appear to underperform in general if you restrict the results of lower-threshold successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T16:20:32-08:00","id":1191771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1191682#post1191682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm. In my defence something like that should be presented as a general rule instead of being nested inside a specific skill description. Piloting was just an example; not the focus of the question.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeh wierd that it isnt a general rule, i personally would apply it whenever needed. Esp for things like Crafts etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T11:36:37-08:00","id":1192329,"title":"","content":"I'm looking for a way for a character to be able to permanently change their appearance without the character being part of one of the major game lines. What I am not looking for:<br /> <br /> - Something that copies an existing person (ie New Face from Hunter: The Vigil) or alters just the face.<br /> - Something that is derived from one of the major game lines (Ghouls, Offspring, Oathtakers from Changeling etc).<br /> - Something that is possessed or in some other way has to struggle with something from their free will.<br /> - Something that is immortal as part of the package when being able to obtain this ability.<br /> <br /> Things that I am okay with:<br /> <br /> - A &quot;minor&quot; splat like a low magic user, psychic, witch (Witch Finders) and just about anything from the core books.<br /> - Supernatural merits.<br /> - Dread Powers or Numen.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if this allows for the moving of physical attributes or boosts them: I am looking for just the ability to permanently alter your appearance. CofD sources preferred, but if those don't exist all nWoD books are good. So the question is: does what I'm looking for exist somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T12:25:04-08:00","id":1192348,"title":"","content":"There's always plastic surgery.<br /> <br /> You should probably look up Skinchangers, there's a pretty adaptable template you can use from it and they're not a full game or derived from one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T20:07:21-08:00","id":1192939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1192329#post1192329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking for a way for a character to be able to permanently change their appearance without the character being part of one of the major game lines. What I am not looking for:<br /> <br /> - Something that copies an existing person (ie New Face from Hunter: The Vigil) or alters just the face.<br /> - Something that is derived from one of the major game lines (Ghouls, Offspring, Oathtakers from Changeling etc).<br /> - Something that is possessed or in some other way has to struggle with something from their free will.<br /> - Something that is immortal as part of the package when being able to obtain this ability.<br /> <br /> Things that I am okay with:<br /> <br /> - A &amp;quot;minor&amp;quot; splat like a low magic user, psychic, witch (Witch Finders) and just about anything from the core books.<br /> - Supernatural merits.<br /> - Dread Powers or Numen.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if this allows for the moving of physical attributes or boosts them: I am looking for just the ability to permanently alter your appearance. CofD sources preferred, but if those don't exist all nWoD books are good. So the question is: does what I'm looking for exist somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe in the Hurt Locker book one of the biokinesis merits let's a person change their appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T08:55:26-08:00","id":1193152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1192329#post1192329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm looking for a way for a character to be able to permanently change their appearance without the character being part of one of the major game lines. What I am not looking for:<br /> <br /> - Something that copies an existing person (ie New Face from Hunter: The Vigil) or alters just the face.<br /> - Something that is derived from one of the major game lines (Ghouls, Offspring, Oathtakers from Changeling etc).<br /> - Something that is possessed or in some other way has to struggle with something from their free will.<br /> - Something that is immortal as part of the package when being able to obtain this ability.<br /> <br /> Things that I am okay with:<br /> <br /> - A &quot;minor&quot; splat like a low magic user, psychic, witch (Witch Finders) and just about anything from the core books.<br /> - Supernatural merits.<br /> - Dread Powers or Numen.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if this allows for the moving of physical attributes or boosts them: I am looking for just the ability to permanently alter your appearance. CofD sources preferred, but if those don't exist all nWoD books are good. So the question is: does what I'm looking for exist somewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dread Power Skin-Taker does this (p147 of the Chronicles of Darkness corebook): &quot;The creature can steal the face and skin of another. It must kill the victim first, then spend 2 Willpower and merge the features of the corpse with its own. The change is permanent; it cannot return to an earlier face and appearance&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9493-enmai","name":"Enmai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T08:59:01-08:00","id":1193155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1192939#post1192939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe in the Hurt Locker book one of the biokinesis merits let's a person change their appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one grants a small number of bonuses, but it does not let you change your appearance for purely cosmetic purposes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enmai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1193152#post1193152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dread Power Skin-Taker does this (p147 of the Chronicles of Darkness corebook): &quot;The creature can steal the face and skin of another. It must kill the victim first, then spend 2 Willpower and merge the features of the corpse with its own. The change is permanent; it cannot return to an earlier face and appearance&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen that one, but it's not quite what I'm looking for either.<br /> <br /> Okay, let's make this more easy. Same limits as before, except that the derived templates are fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T14:51:01-08:00","id":1193318,"title":"","content":"No, that is Core Book Biokenisis. Hurt locker has the Doppelganger Merit, which explicitly lets you perfectly imitate others. Not exactly what you are looking for due to your first point, but still.<br /> <br /> Might be easier if you want to explain what you are using it for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T02:39:00-08:00","id":1193472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ruger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1193318#post1193318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that is Core Book Biokenisis. Hurt locker has the Doppelganger Merit, which explicitly lets you perfectly imitate others. Not exactly what you are looking for due to your first point, but still.<br /> <br /> Might be easier if you want to explain what you are using it for?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Doppelganger Merit lets you imitate someone, which is not what I'm looking for.<br /> <br /> I'm looking to build a villain capable of shapeshifting without mimicing other people or the change being of a limited duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T10:06:56-08:00","id":1193610,"title":"","content":"If it's not an NPC you can just have a power that does that. You should probably tie it with some restrictions, but the game is meant to have a toolboxy approach, and since you're not offering this power to PCs, you don't have to concern yourself with balance issues. It would just be a weird thing they do, like the billions of others in the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Look at one of the powers that you've liked from the suggestions, or something else you've seen and preferred, even something from another splat, and just disassociate the rule from them entirely. Wolf-Blooded with the Skinner Tell can carve peoples skin off and wear it. Your Clayface has a special connection to mud and can sculpt faces with special clay mixed with drops of their blood that they can then put on to alter their body entirely. Or they got addicted to using some beauty cream in alpha testing that lets them mold their face however they want before the horrible side effects were realized and the manufacture of further stuff was cancelled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-09-2018, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T16:28:31-07:00","id":1195023,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">While reading through the Corebook in preparation of my first campaign, I stumbled upon a few rules I haven't quite understood yet completly. I apologize in advance if my English isn't the best ... lack of practice. Thanks in advance for all your input.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Circumstances and Equipment (Page 69): </b>If I understand this correctly, there can be multiple modifiers which apply to the same roll? Only the magnitude of each modifier is limited (-5 to +5), not the sheer number?\u200b</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Defense (Page 88 and Page 90): </b><i>&quot;Every time a character applies his Defense against an attack, reduce his Defense by 1 against subsequent attacks until the start of the next turn, when the character at the top of the Initiative order acts again.&quot;</i> This important detail is missing from the Combat Summary Chart, and the GM Screen also. Which one is right, the text or the summary/the screen?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Dodge (Page 88): </b>Could someone explain to me (maybe using an example) how Dodge exactly works? Can I dodge multiple times per turn, as the description of Defense under Stage Three: Attack in the Combat Summary Chart could implicate (&quot;<b>each</b> attack&quot;), but which is not explicitly stated in the text? How exactly is the Dodge Pool modified by muliple attacks during the same turn against the &quot;dodger&quot;? Like &quot;normal&quot; Defense (-1 for each successive attack) or not at all? And what does the last paragraph exactly mean? How am I supposed to know in advance how many opponents are going to attack the &quot;dodger&quot; during the turn? </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Range (Page 90 &amp; 91): </b>Which range penalties are correct? The ones in the desciption text (-1 for medium &amp; -2 for long range), or the ones in the Combat Summary Chart (-1 for medium &amp; -2 for long range), which are printed in the GM Screen also?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Autofire into Close Combat(Shooting into Close Combat \u2013 Page 92)</b><b>: </b>Where exactly can I find the rules which apply in this situation? What exactly happens when I autofire into Close Combat?</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Structure (Vehicle Traits \u2013 Page 99): </b>Shouldn't it say &quot;A vehicle suffering half its Structure ...&quot;, not &quot;An object ...&quot;?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12274-ser-duncan-pennytree","name":"Ser Duncan Pennytree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T18:49:11-07:00","id":1195067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ser Duncan Pennytree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195023#post1195023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Circumstances and Equipment (Page 69): </b>If I understand this correctly, there can be multiple modifiers which apply to the same roll? Only the magnitude of each modifier is limited (-5 to +5), not the sheer number?\u200b</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is also my understanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ser Duncan Pennytree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195023#post1195023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Defense (Page 88 and Page 90): </b><i>&quot;Every time a character applies his Defense against an attack, reduce his Defense by 1 against subsequent attacks until the start of the next turn, when the character at the top of the Initiative order acts again.&quot;</i> This important detail is missing from the Combat Summary Chart, and the GM Screen also. Which one is right, the text or the summary/the screen?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The text is correct. The summaries are just that, summaries, not necessarily comprehensive and complete.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ser Duncan Pennytree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195023#post1195023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Dodge (Page 88): </b>Could someone explain to me (maybe using an example) how Dodge exactly works? Can I dodge multiple times per turn, as the description of Defense under Stage Three: Attack in the Combat Summary Chart could implicate (&quot;<b>each</b> attack&quot;), but which is not explicitly stated in the text? How exactly is the Dodge Pool modified by muliple attacks during the same turn against the &quot;dodger&quot;? Like &quot;normal&quot; Defense (-1 for each successive attack) or not at all? And what does the last paragraph exactly mean? How am I supposed to know in advance how many opponents are going to attack the &quot;dodger&quot; during the turn? </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Dodging is an instant action the character takes, which unlike other instant actions, can take effect before the character's Initiative. (So if Alice is faster than Bob's Initiative and attacks Bob, Bob may declare he is dodging this turn.) A single Dodge action applies for the full turn against all dodgable attacks that occur that turn. Multiple attacks in the same turn apply their normal penalty. This penalty is applied to the character's Defense <i>before</i> it is doubled to determine the number of dice rolled to dodge the attack, which is the meaning of the paragraph which confused you. Each attack is rolled in sequence of Initiative, so for example, after Alice attacks Bob and he dodges, if Lisa also attacks Bob that turn, Bob's dice pool to dodge Lisa's attack is (Defense - 1) doubled. If Frank then <i>also</i> attacks Bob the same turn, his dice pool to dodge Frank's attack is (Defense - 2) doubled.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ser Duncan Pennytree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195023#post1195023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Range (Page 90 &amp; 91): </b>Which range penalties are correct? The ones in the desciption text (-1 for medium &amp; -2 for long range), or the ones in the Combat Summary Chart (-1 for medium &amp; -2 for long range), which are printed in the GM Screen also?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the description text values (-1 for medium, -2 for long) are correct, and the -2/-4 values are artifacts from the previous rules edition which were not caught and corrected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ser Duncan Pennytree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195023#post1195023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Autofire into Close Combat(Shooting into Close Combat \u2013 Page 92)</b><b>: </b>Where exactly can I find the rules which apply in this situation? What exactly happens when I autofire into Close Combat?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Second edition core rules don't appear to specify. First edition specified that autofire fired at someone engaged in close combat automatically targeted everyone that person was engaged with (complete with targeting penalties), even short bursts which normally cannot spread to multiple targets. So if your friend Bob was fending Alice and Frank off with a crowbar, and you wanted to burst-fire at Alice or Frank, you would also target Bob. The normal penalty for shooting into close combat is not applied in this situation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ser Duncan Pennytree</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195023#post1195023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Structure (Vehicle Traits \u2013 Page 99): </b>Shouldn't it say &quot;A vehicle suffering half its Structure ...&quot;, not &quot;An object ...&quot;?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>A vehicle is an object, isn't it? (This is likely a result of stuff being moved around in editing. The Durability and Structure rules apply to non-vehicle objects too.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T19:47:02-07:00","id":1195086,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a>: Thank you very very much. :-) Especially the Dodge Rules make much more sense now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12274-ser-duncan-pennytree","name":"Ser Duncan Pennytree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-13T20:13:27-07:00","id":1195094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195067#post1195067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also my understanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meanwhile, I am increasingly convinced that the net modification of a dicepool cannot normally exceed +/-5 from its natural rating outside the context of applied resistances, given that otherwise a character's natural Traits have drastically less importance than their tools in circumstances where the narrative positioning allows a thing to be done at all.<br /> <br /> In normal play, a complete novice with no innate talent for a skilled task should not be able to match a mortal exemplar at that task just from having top-of-the-line equipment and a very good functional primer on the fundamentals and particulars of what they're trying to accomplish.<br /> <br /> The fact that other gamelines allude to a similar hard limit seems to support this interpretation, as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T02:55:05-07:00","id":1195195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195094#post1195094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, I am increasingly convinced that the net modification of a dicepool cannot normally exceed +/-5 from its natural rating outside the context of applied resistances, given that otherwise a character's natural Traits have drastically less importance than their tools in circumstances where the narrative positioning allows a thing to be done at all.<br /> <br /> In normal play, a complete novice with no innate talent for a skilled task should not be able to match a mortal exemplar at that task just from having top-of-the-line equipment and a very good functional primer on the fundamentals and particulars of what they're trying to accomplish.<br /> <br /> The fact that other gamelines allude to a similar hard limit seems to support this interpretation, as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>In english?<br /> <br /> I assume you mean that in cycling for example a Strength 1 + Athletics 1 person with +4 from super wheels, +4 from super aero frame vs a Str 4 + athletics 4 person on a bike with +2 modifiers shouldnt be on equal terms? But isnt that the point of better equipment/bonuses...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 03-14-2018, 06:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T03:40:21-07:00","id":1195205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195195#post1195195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In english?<br /> <br /> I assume you mean that in cycling for example a Strength 1 + Athletics 1 person with +4 from super wheels, +4 from super aero frame vs a Str 4 + athletics 4 person on a bike with +2 modifiers shouldnt be on equal terms? But isnt that the point of better equipment/bonuses...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm pretty sure that equipment/circumstance bonus max out at +5. As Satchel says, it is weird that a world class performer is outclassed by a newb with good equipment.<br /> <br /> As an example: it would be weird for a classic &quot;nerd&quot; that had some high school gymnastics with a dice pool of 2 strength and 1 athletics to get more dice in a bicycle race then a tour d france cyclist on a normal bike.<br /> <br /> Just an over-the-top for arguments sake example:<br /> Nerd with super bike<br /> Strenght 2<br /> Atletics 1<br /> State of the art bike +3<br /> Aerodynamic biker gear +3<br /> New ultra slick nano grip tires +2<br /> Ultra sonic super accelerator 9000 friction less bike chain +2<br /> = 13 dice<br /> <br /> Tour the France racer with a nomal bike<br /> Strenght 4<br /> Atletics 5<br /> Specialty(bike, racing, mountain roads)<br /> =12 dice<br /> <br /> I'm just not buying that a nerd with better equipment outperforms an world elite athlete with normal gear.<br /> That's why the equipment bonus should stop at +/- 5<br /> <br /> Edit: To be fair imho, equipment bonus should reasonably not even get that high for newbs. Someone that can't handle the equipment shouldn't reasonably get the modifier either. As a house rule, one could perhaps set a max rating of +5 but no higher than the normal dice pool. With means even if you have the +5 equipment but 3 dice without it, you wouldn't be able to use it to it's fullest potential, thus you end up with 6 dice to roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 03-14-2018, 06:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T03:43:39-07:00","id":1195207,"title":"","content":"Fortunately none of that is actually relevant. While the rules state you can combine several tools, what you end up with is a set of tools (which is one &quot;equipment&quot;). Just look at existing equipment such as Automotive Tools, Climbing Gear, Disguise, First Aid Kit, Lockpicking Kit, and Survival Gear. They all consist of various amounts of tools, and grants varying bonuses based on how many tools you have in them. If you use several different singular tools you should just combine them into one kit like the ones already in the book.<br /> <br /> Edit: The vehicle rules also has a unified modification trait for driving rolls which is capped at +5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T05:34:42-07:00","id":1195238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195205#post1195205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just an over-the-top for arguments sake example:<br /> Nerd with super bike<br /> Strenght 2<br /> Atletics 1<br /> State of the art bike +3<br /> Aerodynamic biker gear +3<br /> New ultra slick nano grip tires +2<br /> Ultra sonic super accelerator 9000 friction less bike chain +2<br /> = 13 dice<br /> <br /> Tour the France racer with a nomal bike<br /> Strenght 4<br /> Atletics 5<br /> Specialty(bike, racing, mountain roads)<br /> =12 dice</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it feasible that the newb has all that sweet equipment and the guy actually patronized to compete in the sport doesn't has even better equipment? If you factor all that, the elite cyclist would have twice the pool of the beginner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T06:27:09-07:00","id":1195255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195238#post1195238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is it feasible that the newb has all that sweet equipment and the guy actually patronized to compete in the sport doesn't has even better equipment? If you factor all that, the elite cyclist would have twice the pool of the beginner.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sake of argument.<br /> Or newb has five dots of resources and is a hipster wannabe pro cyclist that can't walk out the door without the best equipment. And the elite athlete just picked up a bike in the park because he didn't want to get eaten by the horrid tentacle monster that just suddenly spawned.<br /> <br /> But no, it's just for sake of argument.<br /> But you mean it's not feasible that a situation can happen in where a newb has much better equipment in any given situation than a pro?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T07:27:09-07:00","id":1195289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195255#post1195255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sake of argument.<br /> Or newb has five dots of resources and is a hipster wannabe pro cyclist that can't walk out the door without the best equipment. And the elite athlete just picked up a bike in the park because he didn't want to get eaten by the horrid tentacle monster that just suddenly spawned.<br /> <br /> But no, it's just for sake of argument.<br /> But you mean it's not feasible that a situation can happen in where a newb has much better equipment in any given situation than a pro?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without some specific set-up by the character at hand, hence why the example is basically white-room scenario trash.<br /> <br /> At which point, if the character goes thru all the services required to acquire such services and equipment, at a significant expense for themselves, I'd allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 03-14-2018, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T09:08:29-07:00","id":1195323,"title":"","content":"Okey so it's &quot;white-room trash&quot; that a rich dude has something a more skillful dude can't afford. And equipment wins over skill. Good to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T13:58:36-07:00","id":1195458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195195#post1195195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In english?</div> </div> </div> </div>Point to the words you don't understand or ask for clarification in a better way, because <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1183342-what-am-i-missing-about-the-sanctum-merit?p=1187705#post1187705\">I'm not putting up with this garbage again</a>.<br /> <br /> This is a system where the most competent subordinates you can get without breaking out full character sheets roll ten dice in the thing they're good at and five dice in everything else. This is a system where you only need one success to do most things that aren't long-term projects and the normal dice math gives you three-in-four odds of success on a roll with average talent and profession-standard training with all else being equal.<br /> <br /> This is a system where certain types of success mean a little more for your roll and the mechanics that expand what types of success do that are treated as a meaningful boon despite being mathematically less influential than flatly adding dice. This is a system where, without changing what successes mean and what counts as exceptional, a character with world-class talent and world-class training and the second-highest singular bonus the system normally allows will roll an exceptional success slightly more than half the time on average, while a character with no talent and no training suffers a non-elective dramatic failure on one roll in ten.<br /> <br /> This is a system where there's typically a distinction between a mechanical element <i>helping your character do a thing</i> and a mechanical element <i>doing a thing in place of your character</i>. If you're rolling fourteen dice from a base pool of one, <i>that is above and beyond the scope of &quot;your character has good equipment and does the thing.&quot;</i> That is <i>&quot;your character's good equipment does the thing.&quot; </i>There are limits to how far the fiction can allow a character to stretch the mechanical conceit of bonus dice relative to their ordinary level of ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T14:41:39-07:00","id":1195475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195289#post1195289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At which point, if the character goes thru all the services required to acquire such services and equipment, at a significant expense for themselves, I'd allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally a good attitude to have, but when it comes to equipment vs traits you run into the problem of rewarding the equipment much more than the XP (or starting dots) spent on building a competent character.<br /> Put two player characters into the suggested situation. If you were to reward my co-player with ludicrous amount of equipment modifiers (that, frankly, doesn't even make any sense in this example) then I'd be pissed that I put precious and limited XP into the same thing. Spending 16 more XP into the same dice pool and still come up one die less...<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, a bicycle is just a single tool. You may modify it to grant a larger bonus, but if you count the individual mods as individual tools you're definitely no longer playing the game as intended. You seriously can't be blind to that, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: And I completely agree with Satchel on this simple point: Equipment is supposed to help your character; not do the thing in place of your character. I know I almost repeated it word for word, but it shouldn't need expanding.<br /> <br /> Second edit: I guess what I'm saying is that equipment bonuses shouldn't get to the point where it devalues XP. You know, that resource that is slowly earned by the player that signifies the character's progress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-14-2018, 06:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T16:01:58-07:00","id":1195518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195475#post1195475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, a bicycle is just a single tool. You may modify it to grant a larger bonus, but if you count the individual mods as individual tools you're definitely no longer playing the game as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this. Eventually you're going to cap that bike out at +5, and you're not going to convince me for a second that any non-bike accessories are going to up your game enough to provide even a +1 bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T18:08:20-07:00","id":1195556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195475#post1195475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Generally a good attitude to have, but when it comes to equipment vs traits you run into the problem of rewarding the equipment much more than the XP (or starting dots) spent on building a competent character.<br /> Put two player characters into the suggested situation. If you were to reward my co-player with ludicrous amount of equipment modifiers (that, frankly, doesn't even make any sense in this example) then I'd be pissed that I put precious and limited XP into the same thing. Spending 16 more XP into the same dice pool and still come up one die less...<br /> <br /> <br /> Besides, a bicycle is just a single tool. You may modify it to grant a larger bonus, but if you count the individual mods as individual tools you're definitely no longer playing the game as intended. You seriously can't be blind to that, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: And I completely agree with Satchel on this simple point: Equipment is supposed to help your character; not do the thing in place of your character. I know I almost repeated it word for word, but it shouldn't need expanding.<br /> <br /> Second edit: I guess what I'm saying is that equipment bonuses shouldn't get to the point where it devalues XP. You know, that resource that is slowly earned by the player that signifies the character's progress.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll disregard the misrepresentation the example again, you're now making it a contest between PCs. But I'll concede to the point of the bike capping at +5 is entirely fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195458#post1195458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a system where there's typically a distinction between a mechanical element <i>helping your character do a thing</i> and a mechanical element <i>doing a thing in place of your character</i>. If you're rolling fourteen dice from a base pool of one, <i>that is above and beyond the scope of &quot;your character has good equipment and does the thing.&quot;</i> That is <i>&quot;your character's good equipment does the thing.&quot; </i>There are limits to how far the fiction can allow a character to stretch the mechanical conceit of bonus dice relative to their ordinary level of ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Offtopic: Incidentally, something Changeling encouraged &lt;.&lt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 03-14-2018, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T02:35:11-07:00","id":1195664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195067#post1195067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dodging is an instant action the character takes, which unlike other instant actions, can take effect before the character's Initiative. (So if Alice is faster than Bob's Initiative and attacks Bob, Bob may declare he is dodging this turn.) A single Dodge action applies for the full turn against all dodgable attacks that occur that turn. Multiple attacks in the same turn apply their normal penalty. This penalty is applied to the character's Defense <i>before</i> it is doubled to determine the number of dice rolled to dodge the attack, which is the meaning of the paragraph which confused you. Each attack is rolled in sequence of Initiative, so for example, after Alice attacks Bob and he dodges, if Lisa also attacks Bob that turn, Bob's dice pool to dodge Lisa's attack is (Defense - 1) doubled. If Frank then <i>also</i> attacks Bob the same turn, his dice pool to dodge Frank's attack is (Defense - 2) doubled.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Normally I agree with everything Stupidloserman says - like a guru - but we have always understood/played this differently at our table. If you dodge, you dodge one attack; other attacks in same turn must roll against your (reduced) defense. I would say this view is (weakly) corroborated by the inclusion of one changeling power that offers one reflexive dodge per turn; also, it means we roll less dice. It does also, however, make dodging much less effective against multiple opponents.<br /> <br /> How do other people run it? I do think the text is ambiguous, but am happy to have it elucidated if I am getting it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","user":"hoodedclaw","date":". 03-15-2018, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T03:11:16-07:00","id":1195671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hoodedclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195664#post1195664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. Normally I agree with everything Stupidloserman says - like a guru - but we have always understood/played this differently at our table. If you dodge, you dodge one attack; other attacks in same turn must roll against your (reduced) defense. I would say this view is (weakly) corroborated by the inclusion of one changeling power that offers one reflexive dodge per turn; also, it means we roll less dice. It does also, however, make dodging much less effective against multiple opponents.<br /> <br /> How do other people run it? I do think the text is ambiguous, but am happy to have it elucidated if I am getting it wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first edition rulebook stated explicitly that a Dodge would apply to all incoming attacks, though that edition's Dodge worked differently:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>World of Darkness Rulebook, p. 156</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Dodge applies to incoming attacks for the remainder of the turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second edition rules are less explicit, but their wording still uses plurals that imply more than one attack facing the effects of the Dodge:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook, p. 88</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Dodging, double the character's Defense but do not subtract it from attack rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are various second edition Fighting Merits whose wording also implies being able to Dodge multiple attacks in one turn, such as Armed Defense \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf's mention of &quot;any attacker&quot; you successfully out-Dodge in a turn, and more clearly, Unarmed Defense \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf's specification that it can only redirect one Dodged attack in a turn (which is of course unnecessary if only one attack can be Dodged each turn).<br /> <br /> The utility of the Changeling power in question is to allow you to Dodge one attack during the same turn in which you took a non-Dodge instant action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T03:29:26-07:00","id":1195675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195671#post1195671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The second edition rules are less explicit ...There are various second edition Fighting Merits whose wording also implies being able to Dodge multiple attacks in one turn</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess - I mean, I can see your reading of it - I just have to squint a touch. We have allowed dodging multiple attacks that occur at the same initiative &quot;click&quot; but in later &quot;initiative clicks&quot;, we always thought there were no more instant actions to give up to get a second dodge action.<br /> <br /> We had tried before rolling once for the dodger, and measuring all attacks against her score, to minimise dice rolls. We never tried rolling dodge for each individual attack; just subtracted the mounting malus for all attackers first. But is awkward too.<br /> <br /> Your reading is valid, though, and we might make the switch, as I do find the text unclear; my main hesitation comes from not wanting to add more rolls to a combat round. But I would be interested to see if others take your approach, or ours, or neither - or even if this is such a niche area of combat it has not been relevant for most players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","user":"hoodedclaw","date":". 03-15-2018, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T08:40:00-07:00","id":1195738,"title":"","content":"The rules update in GMC has an example paragraph that didn't get added to second edition proper. I thought it would clarify the intent but it only muddles it further, implying that the character can only choose to dodge one of four attacks and applies normal defense against the other three.<br /> <br /> That said, I mostly agree with Stupid Loserman, particularly in light of the fighting merits involving the dodge mechanic. As with regular defense I think you can choose to dodge some attacks and not others, if you want to save your maximum bonus to avoid the dude with the chainsaw or whatever.<br /> <br /> As for equipment bonuses/penalties, my interpretation is that multiple sources can grant cumulative modifiers higher than +/-5, but what counts as a 'separate source' should default toward grouping similar sources under one heading. Fancy tires, a top of the line chain, and an ultra lightweight frame are all part of a singular &quot;fancy bike&quot; mod.<br /> <br /> For another example, heavy winds, pouring rain, and frequent thunder might all occur independently and apply hearing penalties, but if they're happening together you have a single &quot;In a hurricane, -5 to hearing&quot; modifier rather than three -2 or -3 modifiers. Now if a Changeling comes along and uses a Contract to magically dampen your hearing, that I would allow to stack with the hurricane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T19:30:00-07:00","id":1196322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1195195#post1195195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In english?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Don't be rude. Rule #1. Not the first time the mods have had to address this with you, don't do it again because there won't be a warning next time.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T00:40:34-07:00","id":1196402,"title":"","content":"Something I noticed in the differences between the God-Machine Chronicles and Chronicles of Darkness is how CoD has no Housing equipment. Does Safeplace account for this, or is this more of a sacrifice to the terrible Wordcount gods?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T11:31:22-07:00","id":1196545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1196402#post1196402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I noticed in the differences between the God-Machine Chronicles and Chronicles of Darkness is how CoD has no Housing equipment. Does Safeplace account for this, or is this more of a sacrifice to the terrible Wordcount gods?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly, it was handled narratively rather than mechanically. Everyone was assumed to have a house roughly related to how much money they had. The guy with five resource dots might live in a mansion or penthouse, while the guy with none but a steady decently paying job might have a reasonably sized house that eats up all his disposable income. For actual effect, they usually used merits rather than equipment, so if you wanted a trapped mansion you would have to use the Hunter Safehouse merit then pay through the nose for it. A Vampire would have a Haven, a Mage would have a Sanctum, and as above a hunter would have a Safehouse. Not having a safeplace merit doesn't mean you are homeless, just that your house doesn't actually give you any special benefit.<br /> <br /> I don't think that it was lack of wordcount that did it, I just think they didn't consider making housing Equipment and wanted to keep it as merits instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T13:42:32-07:00","id":1196586,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar18090_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"18090\" data-vbnamecard=\"18090\">Ruger</a> Thanks, that does make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T07:48:50-07:00","id":1197604,"title":"","content":"What can I do with the occult skill other than investigate myths and identify supernaturals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T08:23:30-07:00","id":1197612,"title":"","content":"You can also identify myths and investigate supernaturals, and that's basically it. It's like asking what you can do with Crafts other than building things (and analyse things that have been built). Occult is definitely smaller in scope than Crafts but also much more useful once you get to use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T08:43:32-07:00","id":1197619,"title":"","content":"K, thanks for clearing that up. I Was Just Somehow Convinced You Could use it to hold ceremonies and rites or somesuch (make and use an ouja Bord for example)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T09:03:54-07:00","id":1197629,"title":"","content":"Well, actually you can. I forgot about those. Summoning, exorcism, binding and warding as well as the research rolls required in order to be able to perform all of those rituals is done with Occult. You can read more about them on pages 138-140 in CofD.<br /> I don't know about Ouija boards, though. If they work (and that's up to the ST) I'd guess you'd require a Supernatural Merit, or that the board itself is supernatural thus not requiring a roll from the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-20-2018, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T10:04:02-07:00","id":1197658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1197612#post1197612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can also identify myths and investigate supernaturals, and that's basically it. It's like asking what you can do with Crafts other than building things (and analyse things that have been built). Occult is definitely smaller in scope than Crafts but also much more useful once you get to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its also very useful in a number of supernatural merits, and the summoning thing you mentioned.<br /> <br /> If you want to do an ouja board, you could always just do it as a ghost summoning then ask it to move the piece around. There are a small amount of rules in the Hunter core book for using it (basically any boards work just as well, lets them communicate without any special numina but they have to make a -3 finesse roll. If you use it alone, its a -1 roll but the ghost gets +1 to numina rolls against the guy using it. No special merits or special board, works for non-ghost entities too, but you do actually have to have the ghost around which is where the occult skill comes in).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T13:48:35-07:00","id":1197730,"title":"","content":"Ouija boards could be considered &quot;mystical equipment&quot; which usually uses Occult to build.<br /> <br /> See page 100 of the CofD core. I think a lot of people missed the expanded craft rules or something, since they never come up in discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T15:05:45-07:00","id":1198855,"title":"","content":"How you resolve Persistent Conditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12764-zwinniak","name":"Zwinniak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T15:29:43-07:00","id":1198868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zwinniak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1198855#post1198855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How you resolve Persistent Conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>All of them should have a 'Resolution' description in their Condition block.<br /> Is there a specific one that's troubling you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T15:40:21-07:00","id":1198870,"title":"","content":"I'm troubled by Persistent thing. What does that even mean? How does it differ from normal Conditions?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12764-zwinniak","name":"Zwinniak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12764_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T15:55:36-07:00","id":1198872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zwinniak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1198870#post1198870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm troubled by Persistent thing. What does that even mean? How does it differ from normal Conditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>'Some Conditions are marked as Persistent. These Conditions typically last for a long time, and can only be resolved permanently with a specific and impressive effort.<br /> Once per chapter, a player can gain a Beat when a Persistent Condition impacts his character\u2019s life.'<br /> <br /> If you're familiar with old WoD or first edition, it's like a derangement or flaw. It can be caused by other things during gameplay, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T23:39:48-07:00","id":1198974,"title":"","content":"To put it another way, a typical Condition exists to be resolved and end. If a Condition is Chekhov's gun, then resolution is the gun going off. That's why it's there. It's a temporary turn in the drama.<br /> <br /> A Persistent Condition does not exist to be resolved and end. It <i>can</i> be resolved and end, and each Persistent Condition is usually listed with a hint of how that would be accomplished. But it's harder or stranger to do, because the Persistent Condition exists to <i>stick around</i> and <i>get in the way.</i> It's a recurring dramatic element or an Achilles heel, a major dramatic complication we know a character by. A Persistent Condition, in its role as Chekhov's gun, has a large clip; it can fire many times before it runs dry. Those moments of strife when the Persistent Condition comes into the spotlight, but isn't resolved, are the moments when the player is awarded a beat. Most Persistent Conditions give examples of situations that would qualify for this beat, separate from how to resolve the Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T01:45:23-07:00","id":1205122,"title":"","content":"Just to be sure: the core CofD book has rules for making Horrors. According to the table on page 142 Horrors get a sum of Attribute points, but it does not list whether they start at 1 or 0 with their Attributes. I suspect that they do, because this would mean that a Potency 1 Horror with 15 dots plus the 9 from each starting Attribute has a total of 24 dots, compared to a standard 5/4/3 character who starts with 1 in each Attribute for a total of 21 dots. Is this correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T16:27:33-07:00","id":1205416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1205122#post1205122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to be sure: the core CofD book has rules for making Horrors. According to the table on page 142 Horrors get a sum of Attribute points, but it does not list whether they start at 1 or 0 with their Attributes. I suspect that they do, because this would mean that a Potency 1 Horror with 15 dots plus the 9 from each starting Attribute has a total of 24 dots, compared to a standard 5/4/3 character who starts with 1 in each Attribute for a total of 21 dots. Is this correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. The attribute points are based on starting values of 0. By horrors you mean ephemeral entities, rank 1 instead of potency 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T16:35:38-07:00","id":1205417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1205416#post1205416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct. The attribute points are based on starting values of 0. By horrors you mean ephemeral entities, rank 1 instead of potency 1?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope, he means Horrors and Potency, they are like &quot;what-ever-you-need-monster-of-the-week&quot; rules in CofD Corebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T01:35:12-07:00","id":1205501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1205417#post1205417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nope, he means Horrors and Potency, they are like &quot;what-ever-you-need-monster-of-the-week&quot; rules in CofD Corebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, skimmed that part assuming it was just ephemeral rules. They seem to be similar just wth dread powers and potency instead of rank and influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:47:30-07:00","id":1205937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1205501#post1205501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, skimmed that part assuming it was just ephemeral rules. They seem to be similar just wth dread powers and potency instead of rank and influences.</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re pretty different. Ephemeral Entities have the simplified Power/Manipulation/Resistance spread, Bans and Banes, Essence, Influences, Manifestations with prerequisite Conditions, Numina, and a few other considerations depending on type. Horrors have the traditional 9 Attribute spread, skills, potentially merits, and dread powers. The only real similarity is that they\u2019re both systems for creating general baddies..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T04:55:19-07:00","id":1205989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1205937#post1205937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They\u2019re pretty different. Ephemeral Entities have the simplified Power/<b>Finesse</b>/Resistance spread, Bans and Banes, Essence, Influences, Manifestations with prerequisite Conditions, Numina, and a few other considerations depending on type. Horrors have the traditional 9 Attribute spread, skills, potentially merits, and dread powers. The only real similarity is that they\u2019re both systems for creating general baddies..</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T05:37:08-07:00","id":1205996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1205416#post1205416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct. The attribute points are based on starting values of 0. By horrors you mean ephemeral entities, rank 1 instead of potency 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean the actual Horrors called Horrors. Page 140 of the core CofD book, page 142 for the table and rules for Attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T15:02:48-07:00","id":1206673,"title":"","content":"Just curious, can I combine fighting style effects as long as there aren't multiple instances of defense sacrificing? (IE, Thrust &amp; Feint from Light Weapons seem pretty designed to work together against a tough foe)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T06:51:32-07:00","id":1206866,"title":"","content":"As long as there is no mention of not being able to combine them, and only one of them sacrifices Defence, and both makes sense together, then yes. Just don't forget the last part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:57:44-07:00","id":1206992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1206673#post1206673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious, can I combine fighting style effects as long as there aren't multiple instances of defense sacrificing? (IE, Thrust &amp; Feint from Light Weapons seem pretty designed to work together against a tough foe)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Hurt Locker specifically says this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T07:19:52-07:00","id":1207642,"title":"","content":"Where are the mentions of the God-Machine in the books published before the GMC and DtD? I've heard that it's been mentioned in World of Darkness (the core book) and wondered if there's any other first edition books that mentions it.<br /> <br /> Edit: In the same vein, are there any changes between the GMC part of Chronicles of Darkness (the book) and the first part of The God-Machine Chronicle (the book)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-16-2018, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T07:50:45-07:00","id":1207659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1207642#post1207642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are the mentions of the God-Machine in the books published before the GMC and DtD? I've heard that it's been mentioned in World of Darkness (the core book) and wondered if there's any other first edition books that mentions it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I heard there was something in Promethean... but not sure, since I was only casually acquainted with 1E back when it was still called the nWoD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T08:21:04-07:00","id":1207662,"title":"","content":"I believe the introductory fiction in nWoD core was supposedly the inspiration for/about the God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T08:40:59-07:00","id":1207665,"title":"","content":"There was also a single V:tR bloodline called the Holy Engineers from Danse Macabre that worship the God Machine (the version based on the original fiction).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T13:34:40-07:00","id":1207744,"title":"","content":"The God Machine was always a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T14:11:53-07:00","id":1207753,"title":"","content":"I had forgot about Holy Engineers. They got weird radio messages, if I'm not mistaken?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1207744#post1207744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God Machine was always a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. What I'm looking for are the first edition mentions so that I can read them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T14:18:51-07:00","id":1207756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1207642#post1207642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are the mentions of the God-Machine in the books published before the GMC and DtD? I've heard that it's been mentioned in World of Darkness (the core book) and wondered if there's any other first edition books that mentions it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Voice of the Angel section in the original nWoD rulebook was the introduction of the concept. Various introductory fictions were later compiled into the God-Machine Anthology book, including those from Mysterious Places and Urban Legends (the latter being the first appearance of the Deva Corporation). Tome of the Watchtowers discusses a myth of the Aether that likens it to a &quot;clockwork god-machine.&quot; Saturnine Night's adventure culminates in the discovery of a vast god-machine of gears churning beneath Detroit. The Danse Macabre introduces the Holy Engineers, who worship the Fury Death from the Voice of the Angel prophecy. There are more quick references.<br /> <br /> Note that the GMC and Demon version of the God-Machine was substantially reimagined from its original setup in the Voice of the Angel. Most of the pre-GMC references derive from the Voice of the Angel presentation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1207642#post1207642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: In the same vein, are there any changes between the GMC part of Chronicles of Darkness (the book) and the first part of The God-Machine Chronicle (the book)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost all of the GMC Introduction (presented in the CofD Rulebook as Gears Within Gears) has been redacted for space. Which is a shame, because it's a really good introduction to the God-Machine as envisioned for the GMC and Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T15:25:33-07:00","id":1207775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1207753#post1207753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know. What I'm looking for are the first edition mentions so that I can read them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most save Summoners (IIRC) are in The God Machine Fiction Anthology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T16:09:56-07:00","id":1207789,"title":"","content":"If different types of ephemeral can't even see or interact with each other in Twilight, how does Essence Thief work? Do they both have to be Materialized or something?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, while looking through my pdf copy of the corebook, I saw that it still is referencing derangements in the Rapture Numina. Where can I get a more up-to-date copy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-16-2018, 07:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T16:46:15-07:00","id":1207800,"title":"","content":"I want to say possessing Essence Thief permits the entity to perceive their chosen prey in Twilight as well, but this does not appear to be the case. At the very least, it doesn't look like you &quot;choose&quot; prey, you just get them all.<br /> <br /> The stray reference to derangements was not removed in errata. It's still there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T17:27:20-07:00","id":1207809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1207800#post1207800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The stray reference to derangements was not removed in errata. It's still there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any word on what the power actually does then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T20:30:17-07:00","id":1207856,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Essence Thief and Rapture</b><br /> <br /> After checking over my collection, most of the 2nd Edition books where Rapture appears copy/pasted the same error (honestly surprised no one caught it during multiple errata passes). <br /> The exception is the version in Werewolf:the Forsaken pg. 192, which explicitly references using a Condition. Since it keeps the Numina language brief, it does not offer a suggested condition beyond &quot;binds her closer to the spirit's wishes&quot;, but I would suggested <i>Deprived</i>, <i>Leveraged</i>, <i>Obsession</i>, or <i>Swooned</i> as good choices.<br /> <br /> As for Essence Thief, the Ghost Eater Numina (W:tF pg. 192) is effectively a more narrow version of the same ability, and explicitly grants the Entity the ability to interact with ghosts. I would consider the ability to interact with other ephemeral types to be a safe assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T13:28:28-07:00","id":1208142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1207775#post1207775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most save Summoners (IIRC) are in The God Machine Fiction Anthology.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Holy Engineers is the only non-fiction reference to the GM before GMC/DtD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T18:29:49-07:00","id":1208269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1208142#post1208142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the Holy Engineers is the only non-fiction reference to the GM before GMC/DtD?</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't verified it but so it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T18:43:56-07:00","id":1208272,"title":"","content":"I think people've mentioned something in the Promethean adventure path. I doubt it says flat out 'God Machine,' though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T20:15:33-07:00","id":1208297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1208272#post1208272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people've mentioned something in the Promethean adventure path. I doubt it says flat out 'God Machine,' though.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's extremely direct. The Hand of the Principle's character sheet quotation is the God-Machine's tagline, the words &quot;God Machine&quot; are used throughout the climactic scene and in preliminary research the characters might make (Voice of the Angel is referenced by name), and one of the sample God-Machine cults in the GMC book alludes to the events of These Mortal Engines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T20:22:11-07:00","id":1208302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1208272#post1208272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people've mentioned something in the Promethean adventure path. I doubt it says flat out 'God Machine,' though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The second subheading of Act Three of the final adventure in the adventure path is Revelation of the God Machine. &quot;God Machine&quot; continues to be capitalized in the text even outside titles and headers.<br /> <br /> As for Tessie's question, that depends on how you define &quot;non-fiction.&quot; Of course, any passage that isn't specifically detailing action resolution or encounter mechanics could be regarded as game &quot;fiction,&quot; in which sense most of the Holy Engineers writeup is too.<br /> <br /> If you meant references outside specific pages of cordoned-off short stories, there are more of those. Tome of the Watchtowers presents it outside the &quot;chapter fiction,&quot; but still as a sort of mythic anecdote. Imperial Mysteries mentions off-hand a few perspectives or speculations made by the imperial ententes about God Machines at work. Some don't namedrop a God Machine directly, but take off from the mythology of the Voice of the Angel in other ways.<br /> <br /> Most references aren't seeded previews of what the God-Machine would become as portrayed in Demon. The Voice of the Angel was the direct inspiration for most of them, and paints a rather different picture of its mythology. If the Voice of the Angel is taken at face value and not as deliberate propaganda, the God Machine is of a fairly different nature from the entity witnessed in Demon.<br /> <br /> A couple early references are, however, previews along the lines of what became Demon. Mister White from the Hunter corebook almost certainly is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 04-17-2018, 11:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T20:46:35-07:00","id":1208309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1208302#post1208302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second subheading of Act Three of the final adventure in the adventure path is Revelation of the God Machine. &quot;God Machine&quot; continues to be capitalized in the text even outside titles and headers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am surprised.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mister White from the Hunter corebook almost certainly is. </div> </div> </div>Totally, always thought that. One of the Slashers, the Trucker one, gave me a God Machine vibe though he was more tangentially connected.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine Anthology is pretty open about its creative origins, 'We had no idea. It wasn't intended to be the basis for anything in the World of Darkness going forward, it was just an evocative piece of fiction to help set the mood.' That kept getting mentioned in fiction or game material (it mentions Saturnine Night and the Holy Engineers), but that it was never defined or explained. Then they made some decisions about what it is and what it does when 1.5 came out.<br /> <br /> I'd guess Matt McFarland championed the idea, he's involved in all the books and obviously was the developer of Demon the Descent. Though it looks like Chuck Wendig was a writer on the same books, except the first edition core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-17-2018, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T22:15:58-07:00","id":1208323,"title":"","content":"Thanks. Now I have a bit more to go through once I get back home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T11:50:07-07:00","id":1210105,"title":"","content":"Is there rules precedent for upgrading arm Wrack gained in the same scene to a persistent condition with later rolls? I.E., dislocating or compound fracturing someone's arm and then ripping skin, tendons and muscles so its pulled off entirely?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-22-2018, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T12:03:59-07:00","id":1210107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1210105#post1210105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there rules precedent for upgrading arm Wrack gained in the same scene to a persistent condition with later rolls? I.E., dislocating or compound fracturing someone's arm and then ripping skin, tendons and muscles so its pulled off entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Superviolence! Specified target, at the arm. Need to do more Aggravated damage than the target's Stamina. This would represent ruining the arm or ripping it off. You can either do it by rolling them over to Aggravated damage or some sort of enhancement that allows that with one's bare hands.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/TL1TqTa.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T17:50:28-07:00","id":1210197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1210105#post1210105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there rules precedent for upgrading arm Wrack gained in the same scene to a persistent condition with later rolls? I.E., dislocating or compound fracturing someone's arm and then ripping skin, tendons and muscles so its pulled off entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hurt Locker has a rule about &quot;Repeated Trauma&quot; leading to persistent conditions, though it isn't super crunchy (just says if a character suffers repeated lethal damage and everyone feels like it go ahead). It specifically has &quot;Arm Disability&quot; as the long-term version of Arm Wrack, including severed arms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T18:49:05-07:00","id":1211644,"title":"","content":"So since in the new changeling there is a merit that says you get Exceptional Success on three to inflict damage with elemental damage instead of Five, But is there any advantage to having and exceptional success on attacks rolls ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T18:51:55-07:00","id":1211645,"title":"","content":"Not normally.<br /> <br /> It's <i>supposed </i>to give you a Condition, like Inspired, but something relevant to the situation. And various abilities might give you a perk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T19:58:55-07:00","id":1211661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1211644#post1211644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So since in the new changeling there is a merit that says you get Exceptional Success on three to inflict damage with elemental damage instead of Five, But is there any advantage to having and exceptional success on attacks rolls ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Inflicting a Tilt without the usual requirements sounds like a common house rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T20:10:52-07:00","id":1211667,"title":"","content":"As is granting a Willpower point. It's actually the Exceptional effect for Down and Dirty, but we've expanded that to regular combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T20:31:23-07:00","id":1211675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1211644#post1211644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So since in the new changeling there is a merit that says you get Exceptional Success on three to inflict damage with elemental damage instead of Five, But is there any advantage to having and exceptional success on attacks rolls ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only way in which attack rolls are treated any differently from other rolls is that getting more than one success has a different outcome even if it's not an exceptional success. You still get a beneficial Condition from rolling five or more successes on an attack roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T05:22:24-07:00","id":1211750,"title":"","content":"I heard people talking about Image/Blast spamming in the D:tD forum and I was confused. I thought that only Materialize and Reaching allowed ephemerals to use their Numina (minus Telekinesis and Left-handed Spanner) outside of Twilight. Looked through my Corebook PDF and didn't see any answers either way. Could anyone tell me what page in which book says Image allows you to use Blast on Material stuff? Is it something only Angels can do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T07:47:23-07:00","id":1211799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1211750#post1211750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I heard people talking about Image/Blast spamming in the D:tD forum and I was confused. I thought that only Materialize and Reaching allowed ephemerals to use their Numina (minus Telekinesis and Left-handed Spanner) outside of Twilight. Looked through my Corebook PDF and didn't see any answers either way. Could anyone tell me what page in which book says Image allows you to use Blast on Material stuff? Is it something only Angels can do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ephemerals can use Numina on targets in the material realm freely when they themselves are in the material realm as well. An angel in Twilight is by definition, barring unusual circumstances, in the material realm. Thus the Blast spamming.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Reaching is for letting spirits use certain compatible Numina across the Gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:56:11-07:00","id":1211892,"title":"","content":"What page is this said on?<br /> <br /> Also, i know what Reaching is used for. I just assumed it went straight from the Hisil to the material frequency of the Flesh. Otherwise, what would be the point","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T13:51:00-07:00","id":1211962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1211799#post1211799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemerals can use Numina on targets in the material realm freely when they themselves are in the material realm as well. An angel in Twilight is by definition, barring unusual circumstances, in the material realm. Thus the Blast spamming.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<b>Entities in Twilight can only attack</b> or be attacked by <b>other ephemeral beings of the same type,</b> unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane&quot; feels salient to the discussion, given that the effects of the Image Manifestation are &quot;the entity's Twilight form becomes visible to material entities.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T14:22:59-07:00","id":1211982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1211962#post1211962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<b>Entities in Twilight can only attack</b> or be attacked by <b>other ephemeral beings of the same type,</b> unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane&quot; feels salient to the discussion, given that the effects of the Image Manifestation are &quot;the entity's Twilight form becomes visible to material entities.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops. <br /> <br /> But does that include Numina as well, or only physical attacks made by ephemerals? The two seem to be distinct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:39:09-07:00","id":1212042,"title":"","content":"It's about physical attacks. Numina and Influences shouldn't have any trouble affecting material things while the entity is in Twilight, just like a mage's spells or a vampire's non-physical Disciplines can affect beings in Twilight without additional rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:47:12-07:00","id":1212049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1211982#post1211982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But does that include Numina as well, or only physical attacks made by ephemerals? The two seem to be distinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blast is explicitly compared to a weapon and other Numina make a point of specifying that the entity needs to be in a state to meaningfully perform the action they rely upon, to say nothing of how &quot;you take damage out of nowhere&quot; isn't really supported by the fiction or the literature that inspired it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T16:51:36-07:00","id":1212054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1212042#post1212042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's about physical attacks. Numina and Influences shouldn't have any trouble affecting material things while the entity is in Twilight, just like a mage's spells or a vampire's non-physical Disciplines can affect beings in Twilight without additional rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interpretation that has come up a few times in the forum but doesn't seem reflected by the books, which call out specific spells or abilities for effecting entities in Twilight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:02:44-07:00","id":1212063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1212049#post1212049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blast is explicitly compared to a weapon and other Numina make a point of specifying that the entity needs to be in a state to meaningfully perform the action they rely upon, to say nothing of how &amp;quot;you take damage out of nowhere&amp;quot; isn't really supported by the fiction or the literature that inspired it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn\u2019t convinced until you said how \u201ctake damage out of nowhere\u201d isn\u2019t probably the intention. <br /> <br /> But in this case, what\u2019s your call on the Image+Blast combo that came up in the Demon threads as one of the means to make angels immediately threatening? Or any other ephemerals doing that, for that matter? Just curious here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T17:32:15-07:00","id":1212079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1212063#post1212063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in this case, what\u2019s your call on the Image+Blast combo that came up in the Demon threads as one of the means to make angels immediately threatening? Or any other ephemerals doing that, for that matter? Just curious here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angels have ephemeral resilience and omnipresent divine backing stopping them from being more than a half-step away from the characters where the story demands it, the Demiurge's own obscurity and lack of honorary Rank mechanics safeguarding their individual weaknesses from exploitation, and the ability to be nigh-on undetectable until it's too late unless the characters are forewarned about an angel due to the God-Machine's capacity to just <i>give them a bleed-free cover identity</i> if they happen to need one. Existing visibly in Twilight doesn't seem like it would actually make the ephemeral attacks of a loyalist (or any other Twilight-dwelling entity) solid to material beings and I don't think they really need such an exploit.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine is the very system a demon inhabits, and even a lesser angel is a tendril of the larger-scale threat of Its will \u2014 it's never just the one loyalist you have to worry about. Further, an angel built to be an immediate threat is an immediate threat in its specific designed context, and the context angels the Machine makes to safeguard things are designed to be <i>flexible </i>\u2014 a versatile and customized spread of Numina is one of the strongest tools in the God-Machine's purpose-built arsenal.<br /> <br /> However, Demon is, again, primarily an espionage game; the major threat of its antagonists lies in escalation over time more than big scary monsters you fight four-on-one. Bigger angels are more likely to be dangerous due to what they're present to account for than out of any intended menace to the Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T21:37:57-07:00","id":1212142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1212063#post1212063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn\u2019t convinced until you said how \u201ctake damage out of nowhere\u201d isn\u2019t probably the intention.<br /> <br /> But in this case, what\u2019s your call on the Image+Blast combo that came up in the Demon threads as one of the means to make angels immediately threatening? Or any other ephemerals doing that, for that matter? Just curious here.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Out of nowhere&quot; is a bit of a misrepresentation, since we're literally talking about the use of the <i>Image</i> Manifestation. Pretty clear where the damage is coming from. But nevertheless, Page 122 of the Chronicles of Darkness rulebook states that &quot;Almost every ephemeral being has the ability to <i>Manifest</i>... ranging from remaining invisible but using powers, to appearing as insubstantial but visible images...&quot;.<br /> <br /> Telekinesis stands out as a Numen which an entity can use without being Materialized, that allows for the same kind of effect (damaging a target), and is most definitely supported by the fiction and literature. See basically every representation of a poltergeist ever. The concept works readily enough regardless. I can see the argument for Blast being treated as a regular attack but the language of the Numen write-up could as easily use combat rules as a reference rather than a literal representation (i.e. &quot;Blast wounds as a lethal weapon&quot;, the quotation marks around the word &quot;weapon&quot; when describing its strength, to me could just be a way of stating that the effect of the Numen should reference the combat rules as easily as it being meant to work as if the character were making a physical attack). It's ambiguous enough that I think it mostly comes down to GM jurisprudence, but letting immaterial entities do things while staying immaterial serves the generally useful story purpose of encouraging players to interact with them through the Bane/Ban systems rather than through the standard combat rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T21:55:18-07:00","id":1212147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1212142#post1212142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Telekinesis stands out as a Numen which an entity can use without being Materialized, that allows for the same kind of effect (damaging a target), and is most definitely supported by the fiction and literature. See basically every representation of a poltergeist ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Telekinesis costs Essence and relies on there being objects to manipulate; I'd allow that for the same reason I'd allow an entity to use its Influences, but Blast is literally just a <i>costless ranged attack</i> originating from the entity itself and there's precious little to support &quot;this thing can strike you but you can't strike it&quot; as an intended effect of the Manifestation Effect whose most obvious application is providing a framework for &quot;as overtly supernatural as a mortals-story seance gets without something going completely wrong&quot; \u2014 this should not be a normal outcome for a Manifestation effect that takes <i>less</i> investment than attaining a physical presence in the material world out of the hazy sensory fog of Twilight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T19:54:53-07:00","id":1213639,"title":"","content":"What does spending a <i>dot</i> of willpower <i>feel</i> like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T20:49:28-07:00","id":1213656,"title":"","content":"An ephemeral being using Blast is literally chucking part of their corpus at targets in high velocity. Ephemeral beings in twilight are intangible. Ergo if they blast something material the blast would just pierce the material thing and carry on without harming the target. Even in the event of being simply visible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T21:09:19-07:00","id":1213661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1213656#post1213656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An ephemeral being using Blast is literally chucking part of their corpus at targets in high velocity. Ephemeral beings in twilight are intangible. Ergo if they blast something material the blast would just pierce the material thing and carry on without harming the target. Even in the event of being simply visible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like that rationale","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T06:44:00-07:00","id":1213772,"title":"","content":"It's flavourful, but not based in any text I know of. Instead, the only example of what a Blast looks like mentions an empty, chilling cold in the bones of the victim. Does Twilight have a separate temperature from the same physical space? Also, the example makes it clear that Blast doesn't have to be a beam or anything that originates from the ephemeral. Rather, it simply just deals damage at a range, and I think that is because it won't force the entity to physically interact with the victim. That's what the regular Power+Finesse attack is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T07:03:28-07:00","id":1213779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1213772#post1213772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's flavourful, but not based in any text I know of. Instead, the only example of what a Blast looks like mentions an empty, chilling cold in the bones of the victim. Does Twilight have a separate temperature from the same physical space? Also, the example makes it clear that Blast doesn't have to be a beam or anything that originates from the ephemeral. Rather, it simply just deals damage at a range, and I think that is because it won't force the entity to physically interact with the victim. That's what the regular Power+Finesse attack is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>An ephemeral being could be made entirely of the concept of cold, or sound. Go back to 1e if you want to see the examples of glass elementals throwing shards of themselves, or quill-like thing being propelled at rapid speed from the back of relevant spirits.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T07:33:42-07:00","id":1213785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1213779#post1213779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An ephemeral being could be made entirely of the concept of cold, or sound. Go back to 1e if you want to see the examples of glass elementals throwing shards of themselves, or quill-like thing being propelled at rapid speed from the back of relevant spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The example was of a ghost, not a spirit of cold. Not that it matters since 2e spirits still have physical-like forms even if they represent non-physical concepts. The Sparkblood Seneschal represents electricity and electrical communication, but still consists of a mass of wires and metals. And why would I look at first edition examples when they don't inform the rules of the current edition? That's just asking to end up with a bunch of misconceptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T08:57:11-07:00","id":1213812,"title":"","content":"Because if it's not addressed directly in second edition, the conception of the first one applies. As directly stated by a number of developers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T09:34:20-07:00","id":1213817,"title":"","content":"Numina <i>are</i> addressed directly. It's the intended mechanics of <i>those very rules</i> we're discussing, and bringing up examples of how first edition's rules worked does nothing to clarify the current rules.<br /> Seriously, patching this edition's updated rules with rules that they're supposed to have replaced can't possibly have been what those developers had intended. Instead, look at the various 1e source books that hasn't been updated. They can still be used in conjunction with the released 2e books, and I'm pretty sure that's what most of these unspecified developers meant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T12:19:00-07:00","id":1213857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1211962#post1211962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<b>Entities in Twilight can only attack</b> or be attacked by <b>other ephemeral beings of the same type,</b> unless the attack utilizes the entity\u2019s bane&quot; feels salient to the discussion, given that the effects of the Image Manifestation are &quot;the entity's Twilight form becomes visible to material entities.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems to me that it\u2019s clear from context that this paragraph refers to the preceding paragraph, \u201cEphemeral beings roll Power + Finesse to attack. Their attacks inflict bashing damage unless the nature of the entity a spirit with metal fists, for example) indicates that it should inflict lethal wounds instead. Some entities use weapons, in which case roll Power + Finesse, then apply weapon damage on a successful attack.\u201d<br /> <br /> That describes what an \u201cattack\u201d from an ephemeral entity is, which the following paragraph then explains can only be done to other beings of the same type. Blast, on the other hand, is never described as an attack.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe entity may <b>wound opponents at a distance</b>. Range is equal to 10 yards per dot of Power, and the entity does not suffer range penalties. <b>If the activation roll succeeds, the Blast wounds as a lethal weapon</b>. The entity may increase the lethality of its Blast by paying Essence \u2014 every 2 Essence spent increases the \u201cweapon\u201d by one lethal damage. The maximum weapon bonus is equal to the entity\u2019s Rank.\u201d<br /> <br /> Blast does not allow the entity to make an attack at any point. It, like other Numena, requires an activation roll, and if that activation roll is successful, it wounds a target at a distance of up to 10*Power yards as a \u201cweapon\u201d, which is written in quotation marks, presumably to distinguish it from an actual weapon attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T12:39:46-07:00","id":1213861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1213639#post1213639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does spending a <i>dot</i> of willpower <i>feel</i> like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Likely a great push that leaves you feeling a bit lessened, as if you've lost some ability to push that far again or are otherwise hollowed out by it, even if only a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T16:39:26-07:00","id":1213957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1213857#post1213857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that it\u2019s clear from context that this paragraph refers to the preceding paragraph, \u201cEphemeral beings roll Power + Finesse to attack. Their attacks inflict bashing damage unless the nature of the entity a spirit with metal fists, for example) indicates that it should inflict lethal wounds instead. Some entities use weapons, in which case roll Power + Finesse, then apply weapon damage on a successful attack.\u201d<br /> <br /> That describes what an \u201cattack\u201d from an ephemeral entity is, which the following paragraph then explains can only be done to other beings of the same type. Blast, on the other hand, is never described as an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an instant action with no cost that rolls Power + Finesse to deal damage based on the rolled successes plus a modifier. The only way in which this is distinguished from a ranged attack sans-quotation-marks with an ephemeral weapon is the lack of capacity for depriving the entity of their ability to use it \u2014 would you let a ghost that got ahold of a Twilight gun hit someone just because it had made itself visible through basic proximity to its Anchor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T22:54:06-07:00","id":1214049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1213957#post1213957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an instant action with no cost that rolls Power + Finesse to deal damage based on the rolled successes plus a modifier. The only way in which this is distinguished from a ranged attack sans-quotation-marks with an ephemeral weapon is the lack of capacity for depriving the entity of their ability to use it \u2014</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so. It\u2019s also different in that it\u2019s defined as a Numen activation roll. Which tells me that this particular type of Power + Finesse roll is affected by things that refer to Numen activation rolls, not to attacks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1213957#post1213957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would you let a ghost that got ahold of a Twilight gun hit someone just because it had made itself visible through basic proximity to its Anchor?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, as that is still an attack as defined in the combat section - \u201cEphemeral beings roll Power + Finesse to attack. Their attacks inflict bashing damage unless the nature of the entity a spirit with metal fists, for example) indicates that it should inflict lethal wounds instead. <b>Some entities use weapons, in which case roll Power + Finesse, then apply weapon damage on a successful attack.</b>\u201d<br /> <br /> Also, I\u2019m not sure where the Image part of this equation is coming from. There is nothing about Blast that suggests the entity needs to be visible to use it. I can understand where the argument that the entity has to be materialized or on the same frequency of Twilight as it\u2019s target, even as I disagree with that interpretation of the text, but I can\u2019t see why anyone who agrees Blast can affect material objects from Twilight would think Image would be required in order for it to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T23:09:17-07:00","id":1214052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214049#post1214049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, as that is still an attack as defined in the combat section - \u201cEphemeral beings roll Power + Finesse to attack. Their attacks inflict bashing damage unless the nature of the entity a spirit with metal fists, for example) indicates that it should inflict lethal wounds instead. <b>Some entities use weapons, in which case roll Power + Finesse, then apply weapon damage on a successful attack.</b>\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I will be frank: the Blast Numen is an attack in every way that matters and insisting that it doesn't count as one just because &quot;the entity can deal lethal damage to a target at a distance as though it had a ranged weapon&quot; is not outright called an &quot;attack&quot; (when Numina include things like &quot;this ephemeral entity is armored and uses a different Attribute to calculate its Defense&quot; and &quot;this ephemeral entity is easy to overlook&quot; as similar innate costless abilities) reads as an obvious bad-faith interpretation.<br /> <br /> If Blast is supposed to be able to affect material targets from Twilight, there is little point in Numina like Telekinesis or Firestarter (which have the R tag and can therefore be reasonable assumed to work from Twilight if they can textually work from the Shadow) being printed in 2e in general, since a simple &quot;depending on the nature of the entity, this may have additional effects on the target or the surroundings&quot; rider like we've seen printed in the writeups of specific entities would cover much of their practical function.<br /> <br /> Blast is already a very useful ability that is expressly described in terms of its utility within the game's systems for combat; it does not need the ability to break the standard limitations of &quot;physically hit something from Twilight to the point of Health damage&quot; to earn its keep.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can\u2019t see why <b>anyone who agrees Blast can affect material objects from Twilight</b> would think Image would be required in order for it to do so. </div> </div> </div>That's where the problem is coming from:<br /> <br /> 1. I do not agree with this supposition, because, again, &quot;an encounter with a spiritual entity does not have to have any telegraphing of its presence whatsoever for it to immediately grievously harm you&quot; is neither a common media touchstone for Chronicles nor in line with 2e's higher incidence of explicit and implicit establishment of the supernatural typically having reasonably visible connective tissue between phenomena (e.g. the whole reason we have Manifestation Conditions as a system of built-upon narrative cues instead of continuing to run Materialize et al as Numina with no use prerequisites).<br /> 2. This discussion <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1211750#post1211750\">is literally happening because of</a> the forwarded supposition that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1207664-angels-and-the-combat-issue?p=1208334#post1208334\">an angel using Image is sufficiently Manifested to attack with the Blast Numen</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 05-02-2018, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T23:25:37-07:00","id":1214054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214052#post1214052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. This discussion <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1211750#post1211750\">is literally happening because of</a> the forwarded supposition that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1207664-angels-and-the-combat-issue?p=1208334#post1208334\">an angel using Image is sufficiently Manifested to attack with the Blast Numen</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, my point was less that they <i>needed</i> Image to attack with Blast, and more that you could replicate a fight between a Materialised Angel and a Demon by using Image instead and by doing so effectively just render the Angel immortal, if you were struggling with the dilemma of &quot;I want my Angel vs Demon fights to be visually dramatic and narratively engaging and not be a cakewalk for the Demon&quot;. The Image suggestion is more to capture the same awe and presence as Materialise otherwise would.<br /> <br /> Of course, I do believe in the basic supposition that Blast can affect material objects from Twilight. I had a long post written with much the same points as Charlaquin, but the internet ate it and I couldn't be bothered after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T01:19:12-07:00","id":1214079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214052#post1214052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will be frank: the Blast Numen is an attack in every way that matters and insisting that it doesn't count as one just because &amp;quot;the entity can deal lethal damage to a target at a distance as though it had a ranged weapon&amp;quot; is not outright called an &amp;quot;attack&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me stop you right there. I am not insisting that it doesn\u2019t count as an attack just because it\u2019s not outright called one, and reducing my argument down to that likewise comes across as bad faith. It is not only not referred to as an attack, but the roll is also referred to explicitly as an activation roll, which is not normally an attack. It is described as functioning <i>like</i> a weapon, but not as actually being a weapon, and the word weapon is put in quotation marks every time it is used. This isn\u2019t just a case of the text failing to call Blast an attack explicitly, this is a case of the text going out of its way to avoid directly correlating Blast with an attack at every opportunity. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214052#post1214052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(when Numina include things like &amp;quot;this ephemeral entity is armored and uses a different Attribute to calculate its Defense&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;this ephemeral entity is easy to overlook&amp;quot; as similar innate costless abilities)</div> </div> </div> </div>None of which, you may notice, involve an activation roll. If the intent was for Blast to be a similarly passive, costless Numen, it could just say \u201cthe entity can make attacks at a distance of up to 10 yards per dot of power. These attacks ignore the target\u2019s defense, do lethal damage, and the entity can spend 2 essence to increase the damage of a successful attack by 1\u201d or something similar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214052#post1214052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">reads as an obvious bad-faith interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know what to tell you. It was genuinely the interpretation I came to from reading the book. I was quite surprised when I first realized others didn\u2019t interpret it that way, as it was the interpretation I intuitively came to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214052#post1214052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Blast is supposed to be able to affect material targets from Twilight, there is little point in Numina like Telekinesis or Firestarter (which have the R tag and can therefore be reasonable assumed to work from Twilight if they can textually work from the Shadow) being printed in 2e in general, since a simple &amp;quot;depending on the nature of the entity, this may have additional effects on the target or the surroundings&amp;quot; rider like we've seen printed in the writeups of specific entities would cover much of their practical function.</div> </div> </div> </div>The R tag is a pretty obvious use for those Numena under my reading of Blast, since Blast lacks it. As well, Blast doesn\u2019t provide an entity that can influence Fire a source of it, or allow any entities to move objects. In fact, dealing damage to material creatures really seems like a very narrow application of both Telekinesis and Firestarter, and would certainly not be the primary reason I would give either to anything but a spirit.<br /> <br /> In fact, turn this comparison around. If Blast <i>can\u2019t</i> be used to affect material beings while the user is in Twilight, how is it not inferior to both of these Numina?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214052#post1214052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blast is already a very useful ability that is expressly described in terms of its utility within the game's systems for combat; it does not need the ability to break the standard limitations of &amp;quot;physically hit something from Twilight to the point of Health damage&amp;quot; to earn its keep.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t agree. What else is its niche? Under your interpretation, what does Blast offer that an ephemeral gun doesn\u2019t? As a storyteller, why would I want use up one of an entity\u2019s limited Numina on Blast rather than giving it a ranged weapon?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214052#post1214052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's where the problem is coming from:<br /> <br /> 1. I do not agree with this supposition, because, again, &amp;quot;an encounter with a spiritual entity does not have to have any telegraphing of its presence whatsoever for it to immediately grievously harm you&amp;quot; is neither a common media touchstone for Chronicles nor in line with 2e's higher incidence of explicit and implicit establishment of the supernatural typically having reasonably visible connective tissue between phenomena (e.g. the whole reason we have Manifestation Conditions as a system of built-upon narrative cues instead of continuing to run Materialize et al as Numina with no use prerequisites).</div> </div> </div> </div>I know you don\u2019t agree with that supposition, I was merely expressing that I find the contingency of using Image first to be inconsistent with that supposition. And while you may be content to interpret the rules through the lens of what exists in CofD inspirational media, I prefer to interpret them based on the words that are written in the books. To each their own though, feel free to run your games the way you like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214052#post1214052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. This discussion <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1211750#post1211750&amp;quot;]is</a> literally happening because of[/URL] the forwarded supposition that <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1207664-angels-and-the-combat-issue?p=1208334#post1208334&amp;quot;]an</a> angel using Image is sufficiently Manifested to attack with the Blast Numen[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but I haven\u2019t been participating in that conversation, yet you asked if I would allow a ghost to shoot a material person with an ephwmeral gun just because it had made itself visible. I merely intended to express that visibility has no bearing on <i>my</i> interpretation of whether or not the entity can attack the material person or use Numina against them (no to the first, yes to the second).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T04:31:52-07:00","id":1214104,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar269_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"269\" data-vbnamecard=\"269\">Charlaquin</a> : So your whole point is that Blast isn't an attack, just a numen activation. That's fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T07:16:44-07:00","id":1214146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214079#post1214079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me stop you right there. I am not insisting that it doesn\u2019t count as an attack just because it\u2019s not outright called one, and reducing my argument down to that likewise comes across as bad faith. It is not only not referred to as an attack, but the roll is also referred to explicitly as an activation roll, which is not normally an attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your argument comes down to &quot;material written back when 'The God-Machine Chronicle' was a rules update that was as close to a Second Edition as we were going to get clearly intends every nuance of the words used to convey it, despite multiple parts of the original text being holdovers from earlier drafts that weren't cleared (e.g. the Fate rules in the pre-ChroD printing, ghosts having the literal Influence: Anchor instead of an Influence relating to their Anchors, etc) and the Numina section in particular containing a reference to a game concept that no longer exists under the word it uses.&quot;<br /> <br /> It does this for the sake of &quot;an ephemeral entity can harm a subject with a power represented by the innate ability to wound subjects within a certain range, dealing lethal damage based on the rolled successes as though it were an attack with a weapon, even if that subject is in a state where it appears pale and semi-transparent and the sounds that they make are distorted and the world otherwise operates at a remove from the entity in question,&quot; a reading that seems to serve no purpose other than to take away any need for an entity to make its presence known in order to directly wound a physical being in contravention of the entire process represented by the Manifestation system introduced in this edition of the game.<br /> <br /> What is the actual concrete benefit of this reading to players of the Revised Storytelling System, given this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is described as functioning <i>like</i> a weapon, but not as actually being a weapon, and the word weapon is put in quotation marks every time it is used. This isn\u2019t just a case of the text failing to call Blast an attack explicitly, this is a case of the text going out of its way to avoid directly correlating Blast with an attack at every opportunity. </div> </div> </div>This is untrue. The word &quot;weapon&quot; is used three times, only once in quotation marks \u2014 and here I must remind you that this is a Numen that represents the ability of an ephemeral entity to wound at a distance in ways that do not necessarily bear any resemblance to the usual things the ChroD system provides additional damaging successes to rolls for \u2014 once with the words &quot;wounds as a&quot; in front of it \u2014 for which see the first point \u2014 and once with no qualifying grammar whatsoever. Leaning hard into semantics is the only way in which this is not clearly intended as &quot;this is mechanically a weapon, even if in the fiction it is not represented as a weapon.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of which, you may notice, involve an activation roll. If the intent was for Blast to be a similarly passive, costless Numen, it could just say \u201cthe entity can make attacks at a distance of up to 10 yards per dot of power. These attacks ignore the target\u2019s defense, do lethal damage, and the entity can spend 2 essence to increase the damage of a successful attack by 1\u201d or something similar. </div> </div> </div>This in turn brings up another point: If Blast is not supposed to be an attack, then one of the entire points of ephemeral beings applying their Defense against every attack (including ranged attacks which normally ignore that Advantage) \u2014 that they have an overwhelming advantage against characters who do not possess their bane \u2014 is obviated by a basic Numen for a class of entity that by default typically <i>represents being armored through a Defense value derived from a single Attribute</i>. I'm reasonably certain the ability to send a stream of fire at another spirit is not supposed to bypass the other spirit having four-inch-thick steel plates for skin.<br /> <br /> Also, if it's not a ranged attack, then the cover mechanics need not apply either, since the entity doesn't suffer range penalties and the description doesn't say anything about it needing to be able to perceive the target. (I hope it should be clear why the default generic &quot;wound at a distance&quot; power should not have this as a universal quality.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The R tag is a pretty obvious use for those Numena under my reading of Blast, since Blast lacks it. </div> </div> </div>The rationale for it not being able to be used from across the Gauntlet is roughly identical to the rationale for it not being usable from Twilight: the interface between the physical world and an unManifested state is not without interference, as 2e's material on Twilight consistently describes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As well, Blast doesn\u2019t provide an entity that can influence Fire a source of it, or allow any entities to move objects. In fact, dealing damage to material creatures really seems like a very narrow application of both Telekinesis and Firestarter, and would certainly not be the primary reason I would give either to anything but a spirit. </div> </div> </div>That was, in point of fact, the reason I said &quot;you could just say that a fiery Blast can set things on fire or a forceful blast can move things around.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, turn this comparison around. If Blast <i>can\u2019t</i> be used to affect material beings while the user is in Twilight, how is it not inferior to both of these Numina? </div> </div> </div>Because it <i>costs nothing to use unless the entity is actively aiming to deal more damage in a single strike, which there is no need to do if the entity can hit its target turn after turn from an invisible state with no up-front investment of Essence</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t agree. What else is its niche? Under your interpretation, what does Blast offer that an ephemeral gun doesn\u2019t? As a storyteller, why would I want use up one of an entity\u2019s limited Numina on Blast rather than giving it a ranged weapon? </div> </div> </div>Because ephemeral objects are uncommon and relatively mundane, because an ephemeral gun does not have an intrinsic thematic tie to the entity that uses it, and because there is nothing to suggest that a gun has infinite ammo just because it exists in Twilight.<br /> <br /> Also because your goal as a Storyteller is expressly not defined by the system as &quot;optimize the antagonists into hard gates on protagonist progress based on their ability to hit ghosts.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know you don\u2019t agree with that supposition, I was merely expressing that I find the contingency of using Image first to be inconsistent with that supposition. And while you may be content to interpret the rules through the lens of what exists in CofD inspirational media, I prefer to interpret them based on the words that are written in the books. </div> </div> </div><i>The fiction and use-advice of the setting is, in fact, the words that are written in the books, and generally has a better track record for not containing unintended side-effects of literalistic reads on the mechanics</i>.<br /> <br /> Nobody writing on the books has seen fit to include anything to the effect of &quot;a mortal stepping into the yard of a haunted house may suffer grievous injury as the wrathful shade freezes the blood in their bones,&quot; but there's plenty of examples on the books of &quot;this power only works if the narrative has proceeded in a way that allows it to work&quot; \u2014 Aggressive Meme requires the entity to be in any position to talk to somebody to use it, Awe works specifically on characters who are looking at the entity, Left-Handed Spanner needs the entity to &quot;touch&quot; its target to work, and so on.<br /> <br /> I am &quot;content&quot; to interpret the rules through <i>the fact that this is a Storytelling game where supernatural powers mean things to the story they are being used in the telling of.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, but I haven\u2019t been participating in that conversation, </div> </div> </div>I got a Notification on the forum's systems because you replied to a post I made addressing <i>that conversation</i>. It is reasonable to assume that your intention was to participate in a discussion you opted to give a lengthy reply in response to. Even if that was not your intention, you expressed confusion at where a part of the discussion was coming from and my response was to point to the source of a discussion point <i>being addressed to that conversation</i>. If you don't want to participate in that discussion then that's fine, but this is a very straightforward chain of events.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T10:55:30-07:00","id":1214220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214104#post1214104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> : So your whole point is that Blast isn't an attack, just a numen activation. That's fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is my point. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T16:19:45-07:00","id":1214352,"title":"","content":"Are people really arguing this? Entities in twilight can blast other entities in twilight, entities who have manifested via materialize can blast other entities who have manifested and everybody else along with it. Image just lets people see its twilight form and therefore it must use materialize if it wants to blast material things...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T16:32:28-07:00","id":1214354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214352#post1214352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are people really arguing this? Entities in twilight can blast other entities in twilight, entities who have manifested via materialize can blast other entities who have manifested and everybody else along with it. Image just lets people see its twilight form and therefore it must use materialize if it wants to blast material things...</div> </div> </div> </div>From what I take, argument seems to be at its heart whether Blast should be a Numen because the book says that it is, or a ranged attack because the story says that it is. By the former, no reason to treat it separately from all the other Numina which can affect non-Twilight things while being Twilight. By the latter, it should be treated separately because direct interaction being hampered is what the whole concept of Twilight is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T20:51:39-07:00","id":1214897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1214352#post1214352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are people really arguing this? Entities in twilight can blast other entities in twilight, entities who have manifested via materialize can blast other entities who have manifested and everybody else along with it. Image just lets people see its twilight form and therefore it must use materialize if it wants to blast material things...</div> </div> </div> </div>21CHermit has it in a nutshell. Honestly, I genuinely hadn't conceived of any other way to treat Blast than as a Numen until this thread, and even though I can now see the argument for treating it as a weapon I still consider that a generous reading of the source material.<br /> <br /> I think the two sides of the argument have been argued about as thoroughly as they can be though. It'll most likely come down to personal preference as to which interpretation gets used in which games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T14:10:49-07:00","id":1218058,"title":"","content":"Per Raw, can animals generate ghosts in 2e? The requirement for a virtue and flaw seem to indicate otherwise, but I'm not clear if animals even have those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T14:30:43-07:00","id":1218061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1218058#post1218058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per Raw, can animals generate ghosts in 2e? The requirement for a virtue and flaw seem to indicate otherwise, but I'm not clear if animals even have those.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never seen ghosts of animals published or otherwise. Generally the ephemeral entity which correspond to them are spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T15:32:22-07:00","id":1218079,"title":"","content":"There's ghost dogs in the Ghost Stories book, so yes. There's also a ghost town.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T15:44:02-07:00","id":1218082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <