hat has (+1 Magnitude) in it's description will require a 3 Dot Scar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2651-thlaylie","name":"Thlaylie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T22:35:42-07:00","id":1456582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thlaylie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1456578#post1456578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Deviant: The Renegades </span>when a Diversion in a Variation says (+1 Magnitude) does that mean that the Scar it's entangled with has to be 1 Magnitude higher as well? IE: A 2 Dot Variation with a Diversion that has (+1 Magnitude) in it's description will require a 3 Dot Scar?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because the Magnitude of the Variation has increased by 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-10T23:04:44-07:00","id":1456583,"title":"","content":"Cool Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2651-thlaylie","name":"Thlaylie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2651_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T06:04:51-07:00","id":1456752,"title":"","content":"Hi there, maybe you can help me. What is the highest Speed available for a Deviant Character and how is it calculated? Merits of all 2nd Edition books are counting when they are allowed for an deviant chara , Cross splats not (so no Ghoul Deviant).<br /> Hope you can help me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-13T11:53:43-07:00","id":1456771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lykas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1456752#post1456752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there, maybe you can help me. What is the highest Speed available for a Deviant Character and how is it calculated? Merits of all 2nd Edition books are counting when they are allowed for an deviant chara , Cross splats not (so no Ghoul Deviant).<br /> Hope you can help me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Speed is Strength + Dexterity + 5. If you start with five dots in each attribute, then Superhuman Strength/Dexterity 5, you'll have a Speed of 25. Fleet of Foot 3 will bring that up to 28, and Gigantic 5, 31. Enhanced Speed 5 (with a Scar Power of 5) will get you a Speed of 31 x 25 = 775. Throw on Aquatic or Flight for even faster specific movement.<br /> <br /> Most other movement-related Merits like Greyhound or Parkour give you more options besides flat Speed increases, and considering the fastest possible Speed a Baseline can run on their own is 18, you've probably left the Chase system long in the dust by then. (This is also of course ignoring whatever all those high-Magnitude Scars are going to do to you.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'd almost forgotten about Animal Transformation, but at that point, the Storyteller's the limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1423,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","user":"espritdecalmar","date":". 08-13-2021, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T11:48:40-07:00","id":1456819,"title":"","content":"I've been out of the forums and the games for more than four years. Is there some list on current books, splats and stuff?<br /> <br /> Was there some big overhaul on the rules since God Machine/2nd ed/CoD?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T20:39:39-07:00","id":1456855,"title":"","content":"Second Edition corebooks have been released for every gameline except Hunter, Mummy, and Deviant. Those three corebooks have also already been written and in the case of Mummy and Deviant laid out and illustrated, but are not finalized for sale to non-backers yet.<br /> <br /> Second Edition Night Horrors supplements exist for Beast, Demon, Promethean, Werewolf, Vampire, and Mage. Notably, Promethean's <i>The Tormented</i> reintroduces the Zeky, Werewolf's <i>Shunned by the Moon</i> is the primary source for full rules on the Pure and the Bale Hounds, Vampire's <i>Spilled Blood</i> contains the Second Edition treatment of Belial's Brood, and Mage's <i>Nameless &amp; Accursed</i> reintroduces the rules for the Rapt (formerly called the Mad), the various forms of Abyssal mages, and the overhauled Second Edition treatment of the Order of Tremere.<br /> <br /> Aside from the Night Horrors books, Vampire has four Second Edition supplements, including a book with a 2e treatment of dhampir. Werewolf has The Pack, Mage has Signs of Sorcery, Changeling has Oak, Ash &amp; Thorn, Geist has Memento Mori, Beast has Building a Legend and a Player's Guide. Of these, the Vampire supplements, The Pack, Signs of Sorcery, and the Beast Player's Guide are traditional length books, whereas OAT, Memento Mori, and Building a Legend are roughly half-length shorter supplements (~50-60 pages or so).<br /> <br /> There are three Dark Eras books (simply titled Dark Eras, Dark Eras Companion, and Dark Eras 2), and the Contagion Chronicle book has been released, with a shorter supplement companion currently released to backers only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-15T01:42:40-07:00","id":1456863,"title":"","content":"I was reading the Authority Vector (contagion chronicle book)<br /> and i was wondering, what counts as a surveillance and communication system for the Surveillance power?<br /> In particular, how would this power works in a low tech setting (medieval or iron age) ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T06:58:54-07:00","id":1459424,"title":"","content":"Is the hitchiking system in midnight roads or social maneuvering better?<br /> <br /> Crowbars and Lockpicks both have the same listed equipment bonus<br /> <br /> but I can imagine no circumstances where Crowbars would be preferred to lockpicks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-18-2021, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T11:54:38-07:00","id":1461251,"title":"","content":"Do I use combat time in turns when attempting a dramatic action such as picking a lock?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T13:51:59-07:00","id":1461263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1461251#post1461251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do I use combat time in turns when attempting a dramatic action such as picking a lock?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the situation. Mostly no, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-24T15:54:14-07:00","id":1461277,"title":"","content":"in vampire if attempting to pick a lock in daylight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T18:26:38-07:00","id":1461637,"title":"","content":"It would depend on the blood potency of the vampire exposed to daylight. At low BP damage intervals are measured in minutes. For more powerful vampires... why would they be trying to pick a lock while exposed to daylight? Subtlety has gone out the window when they're actively burning to death and in frenzy its much faster to just smash the door in.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you can't do it, I'm just hard pressed to think of an instance where time is so crucial you're measuring it in seconds and the characters are opting for quiet, sneaky, and slow over fast but loud, in or out of vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T13:09:15-07:00","id":1461754,"title":"","content":"I was thinking a Revenant being put through a test of his worth by the Circle of the Crone. Also Are the Non supernatural Merits in the chronicles of darkness book probaly kosher in any game?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-27-2021, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T14:37:46-07:00","id":1461764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1461754#post1461754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u2026\u2026 Also Are the Non supernatural Merits in the chronicles of darkness book probaly kosher in any game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel they ought to be, assuming at least one person at the table has the core book so that everyone knows how the Merits actually work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T15:14:06-07:00","id":1461767,"title":"","content":"I would probably not use ones that refer to human-specific things like Vice, Virtue, and Integrity, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T19:32:28-07:00","id":1461790,"title":"","content":"So no problem with Investigative Prodigy in m y Hunter the Vigil game? Other then it might destroy the everman vibe im going for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T13:01:16-07:00","id":1461854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1461790#post1461790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So no problem with Investigative Prodigy in m y Hunter the Vigil game? Other then it might destroy the everman vibe im going for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, if you're STing and a given Merit will hurt your game you shouldn't allow it, period. There is no sense in asking this on the forum.<br /> <br /> By my book every merit is fair play as long as it doesn't hurt the game and the mechanics can be applied, no matter the book. But if they'll hurt play the book doesn't matter, either, just say no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T18:35:43-07:00","id":1462372,"title":"","content":"oh Investigative Aide got me thinking what kind of ability is usable in what kind of investigation<br /> <br /> <br /> obviously medicines best for an autopsy<br /> <br /> Ideas and thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T11:43:22-07:00","id":1462683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1449071#post1449071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Per the book: &quot;For many actions, you don\u2019t need to roll dice. If your character isn\u2019t in a stressful situation \u2014 nobody\u2019s actively trying to tear his throat open, or demolish the building as he works \u2014 you don\u2019t need to roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't need a skill to garden because there is never any situation where you are pruning tomatoes while someone is trying to tear your throat open.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mirrors provides a number of rolls in post-apocalyptic situations. I believe farming and foraging both fell within the Survival category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T20:35:57-07:00","id":1463279,"title":"","content":"It's been a while and I'm rusty. I couldn't find the following rules:<br /> <br /> Is there a tie-breaker for initiative? The combat I just ran had multiple people on both PC and NPC sides with an Initiative of 10. I thought I remembered a tie-breaker, but I might be remembering 1e.<br /> <br /> Is there a way to purposefully put yourself between an ally and an enemy to protect them or take a hit? It hasn't come up, but sacrifice and protecting others is a recurring theme in my current party of Prometheans, so I want to be prepared for if/when they want to put themselves at risk to save others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T20:04:19-07:00","id":1463368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1463279#post1463279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's been a while and I'm rusty. I couldn't find the following rules:<br /> <br /> Is there a tie-breaker for initiative? The combat I just ran had multiple people on both PC and NPC sides with an Initiative of 10. I thought I remembered a tie-breaker, but I might be remembering 1e.<br /> <br /> Is there a way to purposefully put yourself between an ally and an enemy to protect them or take a hit? It hasn't come up, but sacrifice and protecting others is a recurring theme in my current party of Prometheans, so I want to be prepared for if/when they want to put themselves at risk to save others.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First edition has rules to break an initiative tie (highest bonus first, roll off if same bonus), second doesn't clarify. Not much has changed though so the old rule should work.<br /> <br /> There are rules for human shields on page 92. The only factor you'd need to account for is how far you allow a character to move to intercept a hit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-12T23:21:52-07:00","id":1463652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1463279#post1463279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a tie-breaker for initiative? The combat I just ran had multiple people on both PC and NPC sides with an Initiative of 10. I thought I remembered a tie-breaker, but I might be remembering 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always just had the characters in question take their turns 'simultaneously' as far as the narrative is concerned, when this happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-16T15:17:17-07:00","id":1464223,"title":"","content":"For the first level of the Unarmed Defense Style (When facing an unarmed opponent and not Dodging, increase your character\u2019s Defense by half of his Brawl (round down).), do you count creatures attacking with claws and talons and teeth and the like as &quot;unarmed&quot;? Or do you only get the bonus against punches and fists.<br /> <br /> It honestly seems pretty powerful for the first dot of a fighting style, spending one point to add 2 to defense in a lot of situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-17T12:14:06-07:00","id":1464273,"title":"","content":"What is maximum lifting capacity per strength, if any? Do you just eyeball it, or what? Is it based on size with a penalty equal to the difference between strength and object size? When a power such as a Telekinesis Numina gives an approximate strength what is the limit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26294-chris_john","name":"Chris_John","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T00:24:36-07:00","id":1464319,"title":"","content":"An improvised weapon has a Strength requirement equal to its Size. That's generally what I use. Could probably tweak it from there if you absolutely had to, but generally that's sufficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T16:33:50-07:00","id":1464431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris_John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1464273#post1464273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is maximum lifting capacity per strength, if any? Do you just eyeball it, or what? Is it based on size with a penalty equal to the difference between strength and object size? When a power such as a Telekinesis Numina gives an approximate strength what is the limit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this got ported into Second Edition, but this is the chart from 1E:<br /> <br /> 1 Lift a chair 40 lbs.<br /> 2 Lift a large dog 100 lbs.<br /> 3 Lift a public mailbox 250 lbs.<br /> 4 Lift a wooden crate 400 lbs.<br /> 5 Lift a coffin 650 lbs.<br /> 6 Lift a refrigerator 800 lbs.<br /> 7 Overturn a small car 900 lbs.<br /> 8 Lift a motorcycle 1000 lbs.<br /> 9 Overturn a mid-sized car 1200 lbs.<br /> 10 Lift a large tree trunk 1500 lbs.<br /> 11 Overturn a full-sized car 2000 lbs.<br /> 12 Lift a wrecking ball 3000 lbs.<br /> 13 Overturn a station wagon 4000 lbs.<br /> 14 Overturn a van 5000 lbs.<br /> 15 Overturn a truck 6000 lbs.<br /> <br /> It's a little <i>too </i>precise, but if you need a guideline, it's not bad. These are examples of what you can lift without a roll, basically. Originally you had to make a Strength + Stamina roll with your successes added to your effective Strength to see if you could lift the object, but that strikes me as a bit finicky, especially in a system that avoids counting successes on instant actions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T12:30:14-07:00","id":1464528,"title":"","content":"Deviant Question: what\u2019s the RAW and/or RAI for when a character ends up with more than one instance of the same non-repeatable, Tiered Variation? For example, a character consumes Sacred Flesh for a Variation he has natively. My gut instinct is that the character can only benefit from one at a time, but that they can choose which one that is (subject to any activation restrictions imposed by Scars, etc.). <br /> <br /> But what say ye?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T15:54:37-07:00","id":1465339,"title":"","content":"Willpower states it can only a single willpower can be spent on an action. Does that mean you cannot activate merits or other effects that require willpower as well or simply you cant stack +3s or +2s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T00:39:32-07:00","id":1465364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1465339#post1465339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower states it can only a single willpower can be spent on an action. Does that mean you cannot activate merits or other effects that require willpower as well or simply you cant stack +3s or +2s.</div> </div> </div> </div>The literal reading would mean that if you have to spend WP to activate a power you couldn't also spend WP to boost that power's dice pool. But I think it's much more preferable (and quite possibly intentional) to simply not allow stacking bonuses gained from WP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T03:29:08-07:00","id":1465374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1465339#post1465339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Willpower states it can only a single willpower can be spent on an action. Does that mean you cannot activate merits or other effects that require willpower as well or simply you cant stack +3s or +2s.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires Coil of Zirnitra allows you to use willpower for a power activation and another one for increasing dice pool, so i think that your first reading is correct","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T07:28:58-07:00","id":1465397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1465374#post1465374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires Coil of Zirnitra allows you to use willpower for a power activation and another one for increasing dice pool, so i think that your first reading is correct</div> </div> </div> </div>Coil of Zirnitra also explicitly says that the normal limit is once per turn which is outright false since by that time that was an outdated rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T08:22:49-07:00","id":1465773,"title":"","content":"Can someone describe crafting a weapon with a dice bonus and damage to me like im 5? I looked over mage once and saw them distinguish between equipment bonuses and tools and whatnot. They even have merits Signs of Sorcery that mentions increasing armor rating of an object and equipment bonus without specifying a tool. My confusion here is, if weapons are equipment, as changeling explains it and its mentioned various places, what is stopping a guy from saying they want to craft a knife with a +5 equipment bonus in session 1 of a mortal game? If equipment bonuses are equipment bonuses and most weapons basically have 0 equipment bonus, the crafting rules as written kinda sounds like nothing stops this other than logic. Which is odd, cus it seems only magic and such should be able to create item bonuses that high on say weapons. Additionally, it seems that a weapons &quot;weapon bonus&quot; is applied as a penalty to crafting according to the core book when they detail making a chain weapon, so do weapons just never get a raw dice bonus? The inconsistency of all this wording is dizzying. Either its all worded badly, or im missing something very important here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-29-2021, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T08:32:12-07:00","id":1465776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1465773#post1465773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone describe crafting a weapon with a dice bonus and damage to me like im 5? I looked over mage once and saw them distinguish between equipment bonuses and tools and whatnot. They even have merits Signs of Sorcery that mentions increasing armor rating of an object and equipment bonus without specifying a tool. My confusion here is, if weapons are equipment, as changeling explains it and its mentioned various places, what is stopping a guy from saying they want to craft a knife with a +5 equipment bonus in session 1 of a mortal game? If equipment bonuses are equipment bonuses and most weapons basically have 0 equipment bonus, the crafting rules as written kinda sounds like nothing stops this other than logic. Which is odd, cus it seems only magic and such should be able to create item bonuses that high on say weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weapons have a different type of equipment modifier from other equipment. A set of lockpicks gives you +2 dice to rolls that can use them. Weapons instead add their modifier to damage (if you hit). A machete gives +2 successes to a successful attack roll, which means +2 damage from being hit by the machete.<br /> <br /> Crafting equipment is limited by what's reasonable for that type of equipment. You can only do what's logical. For example: You can't craft a set of lockpicks that gives you +5 to rolls because that powerful lockpicking tools is ridiculous. You also can't craft a +5 knife because it's practically impossible to make a knife that deadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T08:44:35-07:00","id":1465778,"title":"","content":"So while I know this isnt a mage topic, it did make me think of a few of examples of how this interacts with things. How would Enriched Item (Mage: Signs of Sorcery), Enhanced Item (Mage Core), and Blessing of Perfection (Changeling Core) interact with say a machete? I didnt want to post the actual text of the merits/contracts but I could if that is allowed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Based off the above logic, it would seem to me that Enhanced Item wouldnt actually improve damage rating cus it specifies +1 to the item's bonus &quot;as a tool&quot; which tools seem fairly well defined and which have a cap of +5? So in the instance of Enhanced Lockpicks you would only be able to dedicate 3 dots to it to cap it at 5, maybe. Enriched Item would actually increase the damage of the Machete to 3 or 4 based on merit dots I think. And finally, Blessing of Perfection seems like it would it would outright bump up the damage to to 5 with a Wyrd of 3 or more... unless there is no cap for damage which would make it 12 with Wyrd 10. Strait bonus die seem to cap at +5 mod but unless im missing something, it doesnt cap damage. I can assume it caps at 5 and basically makes a Machete hit like a Chainsaw but yea, its not explicit. Is anything above incorrect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9236,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","user":"Yig1015w","date":". 10-29-2021, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T15:58:35-07:00","id":1465841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1465778#post1465778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while I know this isnt a mage topic, it did make me think of a few of examples of how this interacts with things. How would Enriched Item (Mage: Signs of Sorcery), Enhanced Item (Mage Core), and Blessing of Perfection (Changeling Core) interact with say a machete? I didnt want to post the actual text of the merits/contracts but I could if that is allowed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Based off the above logic, it would seem to me that Enhanced Item wouldnt actually improve damage rating cus it specifies +1 to the item's bonus &quot;as a tool&quot; which tools seem fairly well defined and which have a cap of +5? So in the instance of Enhanced Lockpicks you would only be able to dedicate 3 dots to it to cap it at 5, maybe. Enriched Item would actually increase the damage of the Machete to 3 or 4 based on merit dots I think. And finally, Blessing of Perfection seems like it would it would outright bump up the damage to to 5 with a Wyrd of 3 or more... unless there is no cap for damage which would make it 12 with Wyrd 10. Strait bonus die seem to cap at +5 mod but unless im missing something, it doesnt cap damage. I can assume it caps at 5 and basically makes a Machete hit like a Chainsaw but yea, its not explicit. Is anything above incorrect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno about being correct or not, but I\u2019d rule that anything that affects Equipment bonuses ought to affect Damage modifiers. And Armor ratings, too. They\u2019re all Equipment. <br /> <br /> Also, my gut feeling is to let overtly magical tinkering raise bonuses/modifiers above the usual cap of 5\u2026 the keyword being \u2018overtly\u2019. Supernal enhancements would make the tool stand out vividly, auspiciously, and ominously. Fae enhancements would make the tool look strangely alluring and hauntingly beautiful. If balance is an issue where player characters could potentially set up a factory line, add in appropriately dramatic requirements for the finishing touch; find a mountaintop Hallow with a Resonance of \u2018sunlight\u2019 and \u2018conquest\u2019 to melt bars of gold into a golden blade of victory; delve into the Hedge to find the bonemeal of an executed Arcadian thief who may or may not be a hibernating Title of a Gentry to craft a skeleton key that unlocks any locks. Things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T18:13:40-07:00","id":1465858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1465778#post1465778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, Blessing of Perfection seems like it would it would outright bump up the damage to to 5 with a Wyrd of 3 or more... unless there is no cap for damage which would make it 12 with Wyrd 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blessing of Perfection replaces the tool's normal bonus rather than adding it and it lasts for one action and its nature as a Common Contract indicates to me that applying its effects to a weapon offers a dice bonus in the same way that improvised weapons suffer a dice penalty for their use rather than doing less damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-29T19:54:27-07:00","id":1465863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1465858#post1465858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blessing of Perfection replaces the tool's normal bonus rather than adding it and it lasts for one action and its nature as a Common Contract indicates to me that applying its effects to a weapon offers a dice bonus in the same way that improvised weapons suffer a dice penalty for their use rather than doing less damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does make things more complicated though. Because they are all basically increases to to the equipment modifier. Now if it is purely a die increase then thay has the normal limits of +5 from all modifiers so it keeps it under control, if you do consider it to increase damage there is no explicit statement saying a max for damage other than coincidentally chainsaw is the strongest and its also 5. So given how we are getting multiple views here, this just tells me i was right to be confused. Lol I appreciate the responses but would be interested in hearing more input from anyone else who has tinkered with those merits/contracts i mentioned above or any other methods of increasing a item bonus for armor and weapons specifically. Cus i recall seeing some things that have added direct damage rather than phrasing it as equipment bonus. I just cant remember what they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T01:22:36-07:00","id":1465876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1465778#post1465778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while I know this isnt a mage topic, it did make me think of a few of examples of how this interacts with things. How would Enriched Item (Mage: Signs of Sorcery), Enhanced Item (Mage Core), and Blessing of Perfection (Changeling Core) interact with say a machete? I didnt want to post the actual text of the merits/contracts but I could if that is allowed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Based off the above logic, it would seem to me that Enhanced Item wouldnt actually improve damage rating cus it specifies +1 to the item's bonus &quot;as a tool&quot; which tools seem fairly well defined and which have a cap of +5? So in the instance of Enhanced Lockpicks you would only be able to dedicate 3 dots to it to cap it at 5, maybe. Enriched Item would actually increase the damage of the Machete to 3 or 4 based on merit dots I think. And finally, Blessing of Perfection seems like it would it would outright bump up the damage to to 5 with a Wyrd of 3 or more... unless there is no cap for damage which would make it 12 with Wyrd 10. Strait bonus die seem to cap at +5 mod but unless im missing something, it doesnt cap damage. I can assume it caps at 5 and basically makes a Machete hit like a Chainsaw but yea, its not explicit. Is anything above incorrect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Enhanced Items are items enhanced by spells. Spells treat weapon modifiers and regular equipment bonuses as the same so any increase to the equipment modifier would increase damage.<br /> <br /> Enriched Items does specify it as a dice bonus, but since it can grant armour ratings to armours it's perfectly balanced to increase the damage of a weapon instead.<br /> <br /> Changeling is pretty good at separating equipment bonuses from weapon damage modifiers (due to rewrite of the core rules, which is why it's called equipment bonus instead of equipment modifier). As such, Blessing of Perfection would not replace the damage of a weapon, but it would replace the equipment bonus that weapon has if it can also be used as a tool. For example, a Wyrd 3 changeling would have +3 on relevant Craft or Survival rolls with their hunting knife but still only do +1 damage with no bonus dice if used as a weapon. (As mentioned, Blessing of Perfection replaces the bonus, not increases.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T07:56:17-08:00","id":1467164,"title":"","content":"Deviant Question (crossover-ish implications)<br /> <br /> Scars that change a character on a fundamental level, such as giving cybernetics or changing them at the atomic level. Does Inhuman Digestion revert them back to 'normal' for a short period? What about Immunity with Area?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What should happen when something like Oxblood Mold (NH - EA p.131) comes into contact with a Deviant?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4011-weaverchilde","name":"Weaverchilde","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T08:13:10-08:00","id":1467563,"title":"","content":"Does general armor rating reduce aggravated damage? It says it reduces total damage by one point starting with the most severe but then the final part says when applying armor to an attack dealing lethal damage they always take atleast one point of bashing. Had a situation where someone did 1 aggravated damage to a target with 3 general armor and it felt odd that it only did bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T09:40:01-08:00","id":1467566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1467563#post1467563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does general armor rating reduce aggravated damage? It says it reduces total damage by one point starting with the most severe but then the final part says when applying armor to an attack dealing lethal damage they always take atleast one point of bashing. Had a situation where someone did 1 aggravated damage to a target with 3 general armor and it felt odd that it only did bashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books are ambiguous. In a lot of cases, whatever deals aggravated damage is specified to ignore mundane armour. I'd just assume that's the case for all sources of aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T10:29:58-08:00","id":1467569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1467566#post1467566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The books are ambiguous. In a lot of cases, whatever deals aggravated damage is specified to ignore mundane armour. I'd just assume that's the case for all sources of aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>After I posted this question, I read the info in hurt locker to compare to most books. It doesnt have the whole lethal damage clause to the 1 bashing damage, it just says a successful attack always inflicts atleast 1 bashing to a armored target, which kind of implies bashing does as well. It makes me wonder if that was an intentional change in Hurt Locker than even bashing do a single point of damage on a hit.<br /> <br /> The ability in question was Talon and Wing (Royal) for changelings attacking a Huntsman wearing Iron Chainmail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9236-yig1015w","name":"Yig1015w","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T15:20:32-08:00","id":1467604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weaverchilde</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1467164#post1467164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deviant Question (crossover-ish implications)<br /> <br /> Scars that change a character on a fundamental level, such as giving cybernetics or changing them at the atomic level. Does Inhuman Digestion revert them back to 'normal' for a short period? What about Immunity with Area?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What should happen when something like Oxblood Mold (NH - EA p.131) comes into contact with a Deviant?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Effects that shut down Variations and Scars should be judged on a case-by-case basis for what makes narrative sense, usually favoring a lack of radical change. Think of Scars and Variations not as causing but <i>reflecting</i> fundamental changes. You are not a cyborg because you have Computer-Aided Processing and a Frozen Heart. You have Computer-Aided Processing and a Frozen Heart as an outgrowing result of being a cyborg*. Remove these things with something like Inhuman Digestion, even permanently, and you are still Remade. Your cybernetic transformation simply is no longer enhancing your mental processing or dulling your emotional affect. Suppressed Variations and Scars aren't undoing your transformation, but impairing or glitching out the results thereof.<br /> <br /> Note also the specific effects of a written power. Immunity cannot suppress the effects of Scars, and an Area Immunity doesn't distinguish between wanted and unwanted effects, so it doesn't make sense to key Immunity 3's effect to the powers of deviants and apply Area to it, because your own Immunity will attempt to shut down your own Variations (arguably including Immunity itself). Area Immunity can still suppress Variations at lower levels. For example, an Area Immunity to Fire will clash against most uses of Pyrokinesis. Oxblood Mold, meanwhile, just inflicts dice penalties on the use of supernatural powers. It leeches supernatural fuel energies too, but most deviants don't have supernatural fuel energies to leech.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*If you want to take this a step further, to be perfectly accurate, you have Computer-Aided Processing and a Frozen Heart as a result of <i>suffering Divergence.</i> Your Divergence in turn was caused by your implantation with cybernetics. Variations and Scars are results of your soul cracking, and unmediated metaphysical transformation is how you crack a soul. If you killed a deviant with Computer-Aided Processing without damaging the implants, and then extracted them, they probably wouldn't be able to reproduce the effects of Computer-Aided Processing, unless you installed them in somebody and cracked <i>their</i> soul open.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T20:30:19-08:00","id":1467634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1467604#post1467604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it doesn't make sense to key Immunity 3's effect to the powers of deviants and apply Area to it, because your own Immunity will attempt to shut down your own Variations (arguably including Immunity itself).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a Clash of Wills. You roll Acclimation plus the Variation's Magnitude of 4, not adding the bonus for duration because Area makes Immunity stop being Perpetual, against effects attempting to target you or anything inside the area. Even if it Clashed with your own powers, Perpetual Variations all intrinsically have at least two more dice to roll against it.<br /> <br /> The note about neutralizing beneficial effects is very probably owed to the fact that Healer exists, as do a number of Scars for which being in an area immune to electricity/fire/radiation/drugs/etc would meaningfully impact attempts to use an entangled Variation or avoid negative effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T21:26:45-08:00","id":1467638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1467566#post1467566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The books are ambiguous. In a lot of cases, whatever deals aggravated damage is specified to ignore mundane armour. I'd just assume that's the case for all sources of aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. In general, a thing that causes Aggravated does so because it is specially harmful to the person, but the rule on minimum damage for an armored target seems to imply that the attack couldn't really bypass the armor and you're just taking the leftover impact, which is Bashing.<br /> <br /> Unless it makes sense for the attack in question to touch you through the armor, it didn't connected as much as it simply transferred impact. The claw of the supernatural being didn't touch you, the silver of the weapon didn't got to the werewolf's skin and so forth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T02:20:52-08:00","id":1467666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1467638#post1467638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. In general, a thing that causes Aggravated does so because it is specially harmful to the person, but the rule on minimum damage for an armored target seems to imply that the attack couldn't really bypass the armor and you're just taking the leftover impact, which is Bashing.<br /> <br /> Unless it makes sense for the attack in question to touch you through the armor, it didn't connected as much as it simply transferred impact. The claw of the supernatural being didn't touch you, the silver of the weapon didn't got to the werewolf's skin and so forth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant sources of damage that are aggravated on their own; not upgraded to aggravated based on who they hit. I agree that silver/silvered weapons interact normally with mundane armour because they're lethal damage weapons. Any damage that comes through (besides the guaranteed bashing from the force) is then upgraded to aggravated if the person taking the damage is a werewolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T11:20:53-08:00","id":1467698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1467666#post1467666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant sources of damage that are aggravated on their own; not upgraded to aggravated based on who they hit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought about that too before posting, but I actually came to a simple conclusion:<br /> <br /> What kind of damage source causes Aggravated, and yet are affected by armor?<br /> <br /> No matter why the source causes Agg, if it is affected by Armor at all, then <u>the minimum damage rule</u> still indicates what you get after the Armor <b>completely</b> bracing the original source.<br /> <br /> The point being, <b>if</b> the Armor applies, and then <b>if</b> the Armor shrugs off <b>all </b>the damage, <b>then</b> the single damage that comes isn't actually due to the source, but to whatever force is still delivered through <b>the armor itself</b>. And I don't see many armors causing Aggravated to the wearer.<br /> <br /> Any source I can think of that would make sense to always cause Agg would either ignore armor completely or enough to never be completely braced by it, so damage cross over through math instead of rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T20:05:24-08:00","id":1468554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yig1015w</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1467569#post1467569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ability in question was Talon and Wing (Royal) for changelings attacking a Huntsman wearing Iron Chainmail.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this particular case I would rule that the changeling's attack does nothing at all, considering the relation between iron and the fae. Or maybe only bashing if you're feeling generous.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T14:32:43-08:00","id":1468635,"title":"","content":"I'm trying to make an hitman character based on the hitman videogame series and I got curious as to how implement a garrote or similar strangulation weapons, I know there is the choke merit for unarmed combat but was wondering how could I actually implement this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T07:46:38-08:00","id":1468685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468635#post1468635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to make an hitman character based on the hitman videogame series and I got curious as to how implement a garrote or similar strangulation weapons, I know there is the choke merit for unarmed combat but was wondering how could I actually implement this.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was how first edition did it. From Armory, p35.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Attacking with a strangle wire \ufb01rst requires the wielder to succeed on a grappling roll. The following round, the attacker can apply the wire to the subject\u2019s neck with a successful Strength + Weaponry roll (\u20133 for a targeted attack, but the victim\u2019s Defense is not subtracted from the attacker\u2019s roll). However, if the attacker makes a successful surprise attack from behind, and the opponent fails her Wits + Composure roll to notice the ambush, the attacker can grapple directly with the Strength + Weaponry roll. The opponent\u2019s Defense is not applied.<br /> The victim may attempt to break the hold every subsequent turn (per the grappling rules, pp. 157\u2013159, the World of Darkness Rulebook). Every turn after the \ufb01rst, the victim takes a cumulative \u20131 penalty to the escape roll, as the blood \ufb02owing to her brain diminishes (maximum \u20135 penalty). Once the victim takes damage equal to her Stamina, she passes out. She can \ufb01ght unconsciousness by succeeding on a re\ufb02exive Stamina roll. A single success allows her to stay conscious until the following turn, when she must succeed again on another Stamina roll. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T08:47:06-08:00","id":1468690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468685#post1468685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was how first edition did it. From Armory, p35.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, what I don't understand is what kind of damage the victim take and what rolls are necessary to use the wire, my guess would be that since you are already applying the wire, you would only need to succede in a grapple roll to apply damage, is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-23T15:46:25-08:00","id":1468708,"title":"","content":"For simplicity's sake you can probably just use the normal grappling rules and treat applying the wire as a Hold move that applies a penalty to the victim's subsequent rolls (I would suggest -2 or -3).<br /> Dealing damage is just the Damage move on a successful grapple check. Lethal if the wire is intended to cut, bashing if it's just restricting bloodflow in order to render the victim unconscious. <br /> <br /> Finally, a successful surprise attack applies the wire directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T06:01:52-08:00","id":1468749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468708#post1468708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lethal if the wire is intended to cut, bashing if it's just restricting bloodflow in order to render the victim unconscious.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is bullshit, despite common in RPGs for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> Garrotes aren't beheading devices and cutting lines only make it less effective. It is a strangulation device and should follow the same rules as a bare hands choke hold, but with equipment bonus to keep the hold.<br /> <br /> A few rare variations have nots that can crush the larynx with the proper maneuver, but that's not the one we see in media and it doesn't work like a normal garrote.<br /> <br /> Cutting with a garrote-like instrument would require far more pressure force than cutting with a blade, with the same edge. Too much to be necessary to track the cutting damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T07:55:47-08:00","id":1468758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468749#post1468749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is bullshit, despite common in RPGs for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> Garrotes aren't beheading devices and cutting lines only make it less effective. It is a strangulation device and should follow the same rules as a bare hands choke hold, but with equipment bonus to keep the hold.<br /> <br /> A few rare variations have nots that can crush the larynx with the proper maneuver, but that's not the one we see in media and it doesn't work like a normal garrote.<br /> <br /> Cutting with a garrote-like instrument would require far more pressure force than cutting with a blade, with the same edge. Too much to be necessary to track the cutting damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not that I have ever strangled someone but I knew a fisherman who lost a finger with a fishing line and piano wire is notoriously sharp so they can definitely cut into human skin, I would say that bashing damage should be applied when using non sharp implements like a scarf or electrical cord.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T08:02:46-08:00","id":1468759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468708#post1468708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For simplicity's sake you can probably just use the normal grappling rules and treat applying the wire as a Hold move that applies a penalty to the victim's subsequent rolls (I would suggest -2 or -3).<br /> Dealing damage is just the Damage move on a successful grapple check. Lethal if the wire is intended to cut, bashing if it's just restricting bloodflow in order to render the victim unconscious.<br /> <br /> Finally, a successful surprise attack applies the wire directly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thats more or less how I immagined it, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T08:53:42-08:00","id":1468762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468758#post1468758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I have ever strangled someone but I knew a fisherman who lost a finger with a fishing line and piano wire is notoriously sharp so they can definitely cut into human skin, I would say that bashing damage should be applied when using non sharp implements like a scarf or electrical cord.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question isn't if it cuts, but how this cut relates to damage. I doubt this fisherman lost the finger by the line being pulled with normal human strength.<br /> <br /> A garrote kills by strangling. A garrote with a sharp cord will still kill by strangling. If the garrote causes Lethal it isn't strangling, because it isn't using the same rules. On the other side, is the cutting actually putting you nearer to death? If every scratch you get that draws any amount of blood was a full lethal damage, life would be far shorter.<br /> <br /> You can use fishing line or piano wire to cut things. And you can use them to make weapons that would certainly cause Lethal. But making a garrote with those lines cause lethal is nonsense, is to ignore how it really works to fixate on the semantics of the definition of damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T10:56:02-08:00","id":1468768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468762#post1468762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question isn't if it cuts, but how this cut relates to damage. I doubt this fisherman lost the finger by the line being pulled with normal human strength.<br /> <br /> A garrote kills by strangling. A garrote with a sharp cord will still kill by strangling. If the garrote causes Lethal it isn't strangling, because it isn't using the same rules. On the other side, is the cutting actually putting you nearer to death? If every scratch you get that draws any amount of blood was a full lethal damage, life would be far shorter.<br /> <br /> You can use fishing line or piano wire to cut things. And you can use them to make weapons that would certainly cause Lethal. But making a garrote with those lines cause lethal is nonsense, is to ignore how it really works to fixate on the semantics of the definition of damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A garrote kills also by crushing the windpipe and can, with enough force, cause decapitation, if you can get leverage over a victim while using a sharp enough implement like a piano wire, you can definitely cut veins and blood vessels, sounds lethal enough to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T11:23:57-08:00","id":1468770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468768#post1468768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A garrote kills also by crushing the windpipe and can, with enough force, cause decapitation, if you can get leverage over a victim while using a sharp enough implement like a piano wire, you can definitely cut veins and blood vessels, sounds lethal enough to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is not the same as defining the entire weapon as causing Lethal.<br /> <br /> Crushing the windpipe is possible with specific maneuvers or by accident/enough force, and isn't more likely because of a sharp wire. Indeed, crushing the windpipe can be done with bare hands, if enough force is applied with the right movement.<br /> <br /> If you can get leverage over a victim enough to cause decapitation with a sharp wire, you're beyond using the <b>weapon status</b> of the wire. In game terms you're causing damage through other means than applying the rules for a simple attack with the weapon.<br /> <br /> We are not talking the many fancy ways one character can kill another with a wire, we're talking the weapon statistics of a garrote being used as a garrote. And on top of that, damage is an approximation of how close you are to dead. Since the garrote is already compressing one's throat and windpipe, enough force will make it lethal <b><i>regardless of sharpness</i></b>, because you're crushing someone's throat with all the vital nerves and vessels therein.<br /> <br /> Upgrading the damage from Bashing to Lethal is a big deal. I'm not looking at the rules for strangling right now, you may want to make the garrote Lethal from start because it's certainly more efficient than strangling with bare hands. But you'll have two variations of the same weapon with strikingly different damage outputs. Is the difference between the two that big because one cuts? When cutting have nothing to do with the way they work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T13:24:14-08:00","id":1468772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468770#post1468770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is not the same as defining the entire weapon as causing Lethal.<br /> <br /> Crushing the windpipe is possible with specific maneuvers or by accident/enough force, and isn't more likely because of a sharp wire. Indeed, crushing the windpipe can be done with bare hands, if enough force is applied with the right movement.<br /> <br /> If you can get leverage over a victim enough to cause decapitation with a sharp wire, you're beyond using the <b>weapon status</b> of the wire. In game terms you're causing damage through other means than applying the rules for a simple attack with the weapon.<br /> <br /> We are not talking the many fancy ways one character can kill another with a wire, we're talking the weapon statistics of a garrote being used as a garrote. And on top of that, damage is an approximation of how close you are to dead. Since the garrote is already compressing one's throat and windpipe, enough force will make it lethal <b><i>regardless of sharpness</i></b>, because you're crushing someone's throat with all the vital nerves and vessels therein.<br /> <br /> Upgrading the damage from Bashing to Lethal is a big deal. I'm not looking at the rules for strangling right now, you may want to make the garrote Lethal from start because it's certainly more efficient than strangling with bare hands. But you'll have two variations of the same weapon with strikingly different damage outputs. Is the difference between the two that big because one cuts? When cutting have nothing to do with the way they work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I honestly don't understand the problem with one version of a garrote causing lethal and another causing bashing, that would be like the difference between a normal weapon and a silver one, the material dictates the type of damage they do, it could be easily implemented, you try to strangle someone using a scarf or some electrical cordage lying around? bashing, you fashion yourself a garrote from piano wire or other sharp material? lethal, again I really don't see where the problem would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T14:51:50-08:00","id":1468781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468772#post1468772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't understand the problem with one version of a garrote causing lethal and another causing bashing, that would be like the difference between a normal weapon and a silver one, the material dictates the type of damage they do, it could be easily implemented, you try to strangle someone using a scarf or some electrical cordage lying around? bashing, you fashion yourself a garrote from piano wire or other sharp material? lethal, again I really don't see where the problem would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm only saying it doesn't make sense, the game certainly won't break because of it. But it still don't make sense.<br /> <br /> Also your comparisons are completely out there. Silver changes type of damage because of a supernatural allergy. And strangling with a random piece of cloth or cord <b><u>isn't</u></b> using a garrote. A garrote is a weapon, designed as such. A scarf is a garrote just as much as a metal candlestick is a knife.<br /> <br /> My problem persists that attributing Lethal damage to some garrotes and not others based on the cord being sharp doesn't make the slightest sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T15:27:34-08:00","id":1468787,"title":"","content":"<b><i>New Merit: Decapitator (\u2022\u2022)</i></b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Strength 4<br /> <b>Effect:</b> When using a sharp or sufficiently thin implement, such as a piano wire, as a tool for strangulation, the character may spend one Willpower point to cause the damage to be lethal instead of bashing.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Despite the name, this Merit rarely causes actual decapitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T15:49:26-08:00","id":1468790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468781#post1468781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm only saying it doesn't make sense, the game certainly won't break because of it. But it still don't make sense.<br /> <br /> Also your comparisons are completely out there. Silver changes type of damage because of a supernatural allergy. And strangling with a random piece of cloth or cord <b><u>isn't</u></b> using a garrote. A garrote is a weapon, designed as such. A scarf is a garrote just as much as a metal candlestick is a knife.<br /> <br /> My problem persists that attributing Lethal damage to some garrotes and not others based on the cord being sharp doesn't make the slightest sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Then I will change it calling it a strangle wire like the armory did, also I really don't understand why a different material wouldn't make sense, a garrote as in a properly made tool for strangulation that uses a type of fiber wouldn't be able to cut like a garrote made from piano wire, I honestly don't understand whats so difficult about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T23:26:58-08:00","id":1468819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468790#post1468790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a garrote as in a properly made tool for strangulation that uses a type of fiber wouldn't be able to cut like a garrote made from piano wire</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of a garrote isn't to cut. Period. Having some cutting capacity doesn't change that, because the garrote doesn't kill through bleeding, it kills through strangulation. I'm equally puzzled at what's so difficult about this.<br /> <br /> I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a>'s Merit above quite good to actually make what you want with a garrote.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, don't feel pressed by my rambling, I don't think your game will be worse with either ruling. I'm just arguing what I think is a more sensible rule for the weapon. But I really think the notion of a cutting wire causing more damage on a weapon/maneuver not based on cutting extremely silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T23:42:50-08:00","id":1468820,"title":"","content":"Basically, if you use a garrote as a garrote, it should be a strangulation-type move in a grapple, causing strangulation. In that case the material doesn't change the damage type because you aren't cutting with it. Using a cord to strangle someone would be the same type of move but with a penalty for being improvised.<br /> <br /> If you do use a garrote as a cutting tool, it would be a different type of damage move with different effects. Thus, it needs to have some way of determining how it deals damage in two different ways. Given that the strength required to cut human skin and other tissues is quite high, the other way of dealing damage should somehow be gated behind high Strength.<br /> One way to do it is to have two different statlines for the same weapon (with the cutting action having a much higher Strength requirement), or (which I personally prefer) have the second move be granted by a Merit (with a high Strength prerequisite) like many other alternate/modified grappling moves.<br /> <br /> Edit: A whole different way of dealing with all of this is to not base strangulation damage on the tool used for it. Instead, have a generic system for strangulation (with appropriate targeting penalty, like -3, to establish the grip), and add equipment modifiers from using tools. That way garrotes wouldn't deal different types of damage regardless of materials used, unless you use them as cutting weapons and not as tools of strangulation, in which case use a damage modifier instead of the rules for strangulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-25-2021, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-25T05:32:01-08:00","id":1468832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468820#post1468820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, if you use a garrote as a garrote, it should be a strangulation-type move in a grapple, causing strangulation. In that case the material doesn't change the damage type because you aren't cutting with it. Using a cord to strangle someone would be the same type of move but with a penalty for being improvised.<br /> <br /> If you do use a garrote as a cutting tool, it would be a different type of damage move with different effects. Thus, it needs to have some way of determining how it deals damage in two different ways. Given that the strength required to cut human skin and other tissues is quite high, the other way of dealing damage should somehow be gated behind high Strength.<br /> One way to do it is to have two different statlines for the same weapon (with the cutting action having a much higher Strength requirement), or (which I personally prefer) have the second move be granted by a Merit (with a high Strength prerequisite) like many other alternate/modified grappling moves.<br /> <br /> Edit: A whole different way of dealing with all of this is to not base strangulation damage on the tool used for it. Instead, have a generic system for strangulation (with appropriate targeting penalty, like -3, to establish the grip), and add equipment modifiers from using tools. That way garrotes wouldn't deal different types of damage regardless of materials used, unless you use them as cutting weapons and not as tools of strangulation, in which case use a damage modifier instead of the rules for strangulation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I will use your second system, strangulation implements will all cause bashing damage plus a weapon modifier based on the tool used, thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T13:02:23-08:00","id":1469010,"title":"","content":"This comes as a surprise for me considering the games I play the most are hunter, Beast, and demon, but I'll be storytelling for the first time and I gotta question. When is the best time to have social maneuvering done rather than just some regular rolls?<br /> <br /> I'm just having trouble what should constitute that mechanic in a way that seems natural and not forced. I understand the mechanic itself, just not when I should and shouldn't use it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T13:10:57-08:00","id":1469012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469010#post1469010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This comes as a surprise for me considering the games I play the most are hunter, Beast, and demon, but I'll be storytelling for the first time and I gotta question. When is the best time to have social maneuvering done rather than just some regular rolls?<br /> <br /> I'm just having trouble what should constitute that mechanic in a way that seems natural and not forced. I understand the mechanic itself, just not when I should and shouldn't use it</div> </div> </div> </div>When the outcome is something that would logically take more than a single roll and the process of persuasion could conceivably be managed by non-Social rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T16:03:39-08:00","id":1469034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469010#post1469010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This comes as a surprise for me considering the games I play the most are hunter, Beast, and demon, but I'll be storytelling for the first time and I gotta question. When is the best time to have social maneuvering done rather than just some regular rolls?<br /> <br /> I'm just having trouble what should constitute that mechanic in a way that seems natural and not forced. I understand the mechanic itself, just not when I should and shouldn't use it</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have been playing for a while and I could count the times I've seen social combat on the fingers of one hand, a shame really because its a very interesting system, anyway, think about social combat as dramatic moments from a movie like talking down someone suicidal, being interrogated by the police, be the one doing the interrogation, negotiating terms etc. in other words, use it when a whole scene is going to evolve around a social interaction with a non cooperative party, there is no need to run an extended social combat for fast talking a guard but you might need it to convince the head of security that you are supposed to be in the building etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T16:11:46-08:00","id":1469036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469034#post1469034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have been playing for a while and I could count the times I've seen social combat on the fingers of one hand, a shame really because its a very interesting system, anyway, think about social combat as dramatic moments from a movie like talking down someone suicidal, being interrogated by the police, be the one doing the interrogation, negotiating terms etc. in other words, use it when a whole scene is going to evolve around a social interaction with a non cooperative party, there is no need to run an extended social combat for fast talking a guard but you might need it to convince the head of security that you are supposed to be in the building etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Social combat is a completely different system from Social Maneuvering and typically takes place over multiple scenes unless you're working with a perfect impression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T16:56:38-08:00","id":1469044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469036#post1469036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Social combat is a completely different system from Social Maneuvering and typically takes place over multiple scenes unless you're working with a perfect impression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry meant maneuvering, don't know how that came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T00:00:09-08:00","id":1469072,"title":"","content":"Thank yall! So to be clear, social maneuvering is best used when the goal is something that the character likely wouldn't be too willing to do for your character, and when the player could do more than simply talk to the character to convince him to help?<br /> <br /> Like, I should make sure both the context and the objective fit what's needed involving doors. As long as my players want something done that makes me think &quot;good luck convincing the NPC&quot; I should use social maneuvering","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-28T16:32:25-08:00","id":1469132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469072#post1469072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as my players want something done that makes me think &quot;good luck convincing the NPC&quot; I should use social maneuvering</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be the best rule of thumb I've ever heard for it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T12:41:55-08:00","id":1469189,"title":"","content":"How many Experiences does it take to gain a dot of Integrity? The Chronicles core says 2, but other books I\u2019ve checked (Deviant and Mage) say 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T13:20:58-08:00","id":1469190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469189#post1469189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Experiences does it take to gain a dot of Integrity? The Chronicles core says 2, but other books I\u2019ve checked (Deviant and Mage) say 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>2 Experiences per dot. The Chronicles of Darkness core book is <i>the</i> core book for characters who use Integrity so ignore all other books if they happen to differ.<br /> <br /> Whoever wrote that part in Mage based it on outdated information. It was copy-pasted to Deviant without anyone catching the error.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T13:21:52-08:00","id":1469191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469189#post1469189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Experiences does it take to gain a dot of Integrity? The Chronicles core says 2, but other books I\u2019ve checked (Deviant and Mage) say 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Deviants and Mages don't have Integrity, so maybe that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T13:24:00-08:00","id":1469192,"title":"","content":"Edit: Removed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T14:18:29-08:00","id":1469201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469189#post1469189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many Experiences does it take to gain a dot of Integrity? The Chronicles core says 2, but other books I\u2019ve checked (Deviant and Mage) say 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter also says 2, and Mage is the only splat that pays for its Integrity equivalent exclusively with a special Experience type in which the cost is not 3 per dot; notably, it's also the only one of those running on the &quot;start high and lose it&quot; model, compared to Pilgrimage, Memory, and Cover, which all start (or can start, in Cover's case) at a low rating and have building them up as a major gameplay element.<br /> <br /> Everyone else either gets their ratings for free (Harmony, Clarity, Satiety) or is paying for it as a Supernatural Tolerance Trait (Synergy, Stability/Acclimation).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T14:42:40-08:00","id":1469203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469201#post1469201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter also says 2, and Mage is the only splat that pays for its Integrity equivalent exclusively with a special Experience type in which the cost is not 3 per dot; notably, it's also the only one of those running on the &quot;start high and lose it&quot; model, compared to Pilgrimage, Memory, and Cover, which all start (or can start, in Cover's case) at a low rating and have building them up as a major gameplay element.<br /> <br /> Everyone else either gets their ratings for free (Harmony, Clarity, Satiety) or is paying for it as a Supernatural Tolerance Trait (Synergy, Stability/Acclimation).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't fully parse what you're saying but I don't think it's relevant to the fact that the XP cost for Integrity in the Supporting Cast appendix in MtA is just taken from the GMC book instead of the CofD book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T14:55:32-08:00","id":1469204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469203#post1469203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't fully parse what you're saying but I don't think it's relevant to the fact that the XP cost for Integrity in the Supporting Cast appendix in MtA is just taken from the GMC book instead of the CofD book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Integrity costs 2. Hunter Integrity also costs 2. Humanity costs 2. Wisdom costs 2 and is the only one of these that is paid for exclusively with non-standard Experiences (Arcane Experiences).<br /> <br /> Cover costs 3 Cover Experiences. Pilgrimage costs 3 Vitriol Experiences. Memory costs 3 Reminisce Experiences. Wisdom costs 2 Arcane Experiences and is the only one of this batch that concerns a character that becomes unplayable when the Trait bottoms out.<br /> <br /> Harmony goes up based on failed Resolve + Composure rolls to hold onto your spiritual half. Clarity goes up with Icons or Wits or Composure or when you heal it by spending time with Touchstones. Satiety goes up when you feed. None of these interact with the Experience economy except Clarity indirectly.<br /> <br /> Synergy doubles as a Supernatural Potency Trait and thus costs 5 Experiences (Synergy Experiences or regular) when you're not getting the freebies from Burden and Remembrance. Stability gets added to when you buy Acclimation, which is part of a deviant's Supernatural Potency Trait and priced accordingly. Neither of them are being paid for purely as an Integrity stat, and thus they're as much outliers to the pricing scheme of the other Traits as the free ones.<br /> <br /> Unless you're trying to pick a fight, my observation has nothing to do with how relevant you think it is to the misprint in the sidebar, which is founded on outdated information <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9444-experience-costs\">old enough to have come up back when the Demon was in the errata-gathering phase</a>. I am presenting precedent for why some Integrity stats cost differently than others. You are not obligated to respond to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T15:07:38-08:00","id":1469207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469204#post1469204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are not obligated to respond to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not obliged, no, but when you respond directly to a question with a semi-related tangent that doesn't actually answer the question, I do want to clear that up to prevent further confusion. It's easy to read a reply talking about XP costs to a post talking about XP costs as a reply to the question in that original post about XP costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T15:50:37-08:00","id":1469210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469207#post1469207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not obliged, no, but when you respond directly to a question with a semi-related tangent that doesn't actually answer the question, I do want to clear that up to prevent further confusion. It's easy to read a reply talking about XP costs to a post talking about XP costs as a reply to the question in that original post about XP costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The gameline that uses Integrity also says Integrity costs 2 Experiences&quot; was the first thing I said in that reply and the person I was replying to is not the person who gets a notification when you reply to my post.<br /> <br /> I am not interested in having an argument with you about how relevant you think my posts are or how badly you can't parse what I'm saying. If Scriptorian doesn't understand what I'm saying then they can tell me so themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T07:04:56-08:00","id":1469250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469210#post1469210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The gameline that uses Integrity also says Integrity costs 2 Experiences&quot; was the first thing I said in that reply and the person I was replying to is not the person who gets a notification when you reply to my post.<br /> <br /> I am not interested in having an argument with you about how relevant you think my posts are or how badly you can't parse what I'm saying. If Scriptorian doesn't understand what I'm saying then they can tell me so themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Please leave the thread.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T12:13:20-08:00","id":1469265,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responses.<br /> <br /> A question concerning the Power Failure Scar in Deviant: for Magnitudes 2 and up, say I make the penalized Scar Finesse roll to activate the Variation in the presence of the weakness, do I still have to then make the Scar Resistance roll to have it not immediately weaken/deactivate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T12:47:27-08:00","id":1469267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469265#post1469265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question concerning the Power Failure Scar in Deviant: for Magnitudes 2 and up, say I make the penalized Scar Finesse roll to activate the Variation in the presence of the weakness, do I still have to then make the Scar Resistance roll to have it not immediately weaken/deactivate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the penalty to the activation roll is enough. Rolling the same dice pool (though once penalised) twice in a roll is just bad design and I don't think it's how it's intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T21:35:06-08:00","id":1469287,"title":"","content":"I'm going to second Tessie on this one. The phrasing &quot;when the character encounters his weakness while an entangled Variation is active&quot; suggests to me the Scar Resistance roll is there specifically to represent when a fire or whatever suppresses your power breaks out mid-scene, whereas the Scar Finesse penalty simplifies the process when the fire is present from the get-go. I could see the writing process going &quot;what does fire do to your power?&quot; &quot;penalizes it&quot; &quot;what if you use your power and then somebody starts a fire?&quot; &quot;uhh&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T03:13:18-08:00","id":1469299,"title":"","content":"Building on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a>'s take, I'd say you probably don't have to make it immediately, as it would mean two rolls in one action, but if you'll probably have to in subsequent rounds.<br /> <br /> I may be wrong as I didn't actually read Deviant yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T07:46:37-08:00","id":1469314,"title":"","content":"My current reading is that a successful Scar Finesse roll activates it for the scene (without the need for further scar Resistance rolls). It seems like if you were meant to roll Resistance to keep it active, that would be the only penalty. However I think that, at Magnitude 3 and higher, a failed Finesse roll should be subject to the same reactivation restrictions as a failed Resistance roll. Otherwise, with a weakness like \u201cday time\u201d where most often the condition is already in place, the higher magnitudes would be seldomly applicable, since you could just keep rerolling to activate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T07:49:37-08:00","id":1469578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1468749#post1468749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is bullshit, despite common in RPGs for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> Garrotes aren't beheading devices and cutting lines only make it less effective. It is a strangulation device and should follow the same rules as a bare hands choke hold, but with equipment bonus to keep the hold.<br /> <br /> A few rare variations have nots that can crush the larynx with the proper maneuver, but that's not the one we see in media and it doesn't work like a normal garrote.<br /> <br /> Cutting with a garrote-like instrument would require far more pressure force than cutting with a blade, with the same edge. Too much to be necessary to track the cutting damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Cut&quot; was an unfortunate and inaccurate substitute for &quot;kill&quot;. As second edition has well noted blunt force trauma kills just as surely as edged weapons, and weapons default to lethal damage with a few specified exceptions.<br /> <br /> What I meant to distinguish was whether it was an implement designed to quickly kill a victim, or an implement designed to render the victim unconscious but able to recover. I am aware that the distinction between the latter and the former can come down to nothing more than the amount of pressure applied or the length of time held. However, what matters to this abstracted and simplified game system is whether the intent of a successful action is to leave the victim rolling (and ultimately failing) to stay conscious, or dead. To that end it does matter to distinguish a weapon that can deal bashing more efficiently than bare hands from one that deals lethal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-04T09:39:37-08:00","id":1469580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1469578#post1469578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To that end it does matter to distinguish a weapon that can deal bashing more efficiently than bare hands from one that deals lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the garrote kills through strangulation, there's not much to differentiate damage type. Little differences in efficacy may exist, but they would apply more as distinct damage rating or equipment bonus to a maneuver than as differing damage types.<br /> <br /> Different styles of garrote try to achieve more ease on applying or holding the weapon's grapple, because they're still all killing through the same method. And not the same method as in <i>cutting</i> or <i>stabbing</i>, but the same method as in <i>crushing the frontal lobe</i>.<br /> <br /> It is an extremely specific weapon, and that's why it doesn't make sense for changing damage type based on either material or construction. Probably a very effective Bashing weapon, since it usually renders the target unconscious before dying, and its actual advantages are to silence the target, immobilize and keep them under relative control. It's not to kill fast, but to kill silently and minimize struggle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T12:50:32-08:00","id":1471449,"title":"","content":"Influence question: the duration of an Influence effect is dependent on the successes gained on the activation roll. However that activation roll is contested if it affects the thoughts or emotions of a sentient being (normally rolls with results dependent on the margin of success are resisted, not contested). So, if an entity wins the contest, is the duration of the effect based on its original total successes, or on the \u201cnet\u201d successes it had over the target?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T14:12:47-08:00","id":1471454,"title":"","content":"Unless the rules for a particular contest say that the opponent's successes subtract from yours, the default is that you use the original number of rolled successes to measure effect. The comparison of the two rolls only matters to determine which side wins.<br /> <br /> Some contests do make that specification. Dodge rolls, for example, subtract successes from the attacker's total even if the attacker's total is larger than the defender's. But that is not the default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T14:40:15-08:00","id":1471455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1471454#post1471454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the rules for a particular contest say that the opponent's successes subtract from yours, the default is that you use the original number of rolled successes to measure effect. The comparison of the two rolls only matters to determine which side wins.<br /> <br /> Some contests do make that specification. Dodge rolls, for example, subtract successes from the attacker's total even if the attacker's total is larger than the defender's. But that is not the default.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was changed / clarified in <b>Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle</b>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p. 7</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How are successes counted in contested actions?</b><br /> The loser\u2019s successes are subtracted from the winner\u2019s.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T15:10:34-08:00","id":1471458,"title":"","content":"Hello, I'm a little confused by the firefight merit, the first dot says that you add your firearms dots to initiative and mention some kind of sinergy with quick draw that would let you draw and shoot with increased initiative in the first turn, what does this mean mechanically?<br /> <br /> The second dot says that you can use suppressive fire even witha a semiautomatic weapon and that you can apply your defense to ranged attacks, again how would this work? you can apply your defense after using suppressive fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T16:27:38-08:00","id":1471462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1471458#post1471458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I'm a little confused by the firefight merit, the first dot says that you add your firearms dots to initiative and mention some kind of sinergy with quick draw that would let you draw and shoot with increased initiative in the first turn, what does this mean mechanically?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Merit applies its Initiative bonus when the character is holding a gun ready to fire. Drawing a weapon is normally an instant action; if it isn't drawn at the start of a fight, you lose a turn just to have it ready, so the Initiative bonus won't apply then. The Quick Draw Merit makes drawing a gun a reflexive action, which allows it to be fired on the same turn (or drawn before it actually gets to your turn). The Firefight Merit allows you to gain the bonus upon reflexively drawing your gun, and then immediately firing it; being reflexive, you could give yourself the bonus after the fight has started to change your position in the action queue before anybody has gotten a chance to act, possibly putting your action first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second dot says that you can use suppressive fire even witha a semiautomatic weapon and that you can apply your defense to ranged attacks, again how would this work? you can apply your defense after using suppressive fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that you only get the Defence against Firearms attacks if you've used a Cover Fire action, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-29T16:46:52-08:00","id":1471465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1471462#post1471462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Merit applies its Initiative bonus when the character is holding a gun ready to fire. Drawing a weapon is normally an instant action; if it isn't drawn at the start of a fight, you lose a turn just to have it ready, so the Initiative bonus won't apply then. The Quick Draw Merit makes drawing a gun a reflexive action, which allows it to be fired on the same turn (or drawn before it actually gets to your turn). The Firefight Merit allows you to gain the bonus upon reflexively drawing your gun, and then immediately firing it; being reflexive, you could give yourself the bonus after the fight has started to change your position in the action queue before anybody has gotten a chance to act, possibly putting your action first.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would say that you only get the Defence against Firearms attacks if you've used a Cover Fire action, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you, so after you used covering fire and some opponents decide shooting back instead of running for cover, you would apply your full defense against them for that turn right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-30T11:19:08-08:00","id":1471496,"title":"","content":"Is &quot;Defense&quot; a valid Athletics specialty?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-30T11:39:46-08:00","id":1471498,"title":"","content":"I would allow 'Dodging' as one. Ultimately, whether something is a valid specialization is up to the ST.<br /> <br /> That said, Defense is not a dice pool. Specializations apply to dice pools. It wouldn't do anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T00:02:04-08:00","id":1472495,"title":"","content":"In the Grapple rules of the core book, the Damage move states: <br /> <i>Damage the opponent by dealing bashing damage equal to the character\u2019s rolled successes. If the character performing the move previously succeeded at a Control Weapon action, add the weapon modifier to his successes.</i><br /> <br /> What is the type of damage inflicted overall? Is the base damage always bashing?<br /> Assuming the character is holding a 1L weapon and rolls 3 successes, the damage inflicted to its opponent is:<br /> a) 4B ?<br /> b) 3B + 1L ?<br /> c) 4L ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T21:59:44-08:00","id":1472549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1472495#post1472495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Grapple rules of the core book, the Damage move states:<br /> <i>Damage the opponent by dealing bashing damage equal to the character\u2019s rolled successes. If the character performing the move previously succeeded at a Control Weapon action, add the weapon modifier to his successes.</i><br /> <br /> What is the type of damage inflicted overall? Is the base damage always bashing?<br /> Assuming the character is holding a 1L weapon and rolls 3 successes, the damage inflicted to its opponent is:<br /> a) 4B ?<br /> b) 3B + 1L ?<br /> c) 4L ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The default unarmed damage is always Bashing unless a Merit ir something says otherwise. With a weapon it is entirely upgraded to the damage type of the weapon, so it would be C).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T04:35:53-08:00","id":1473563,"title":"","content":"Do the benefits of the Professional Training apply to supernatural powers using the Asset Skills?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T04:44:51-08:00","id":1473565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1473563#post1473563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the benefits of the Professional Training apply to supernatural powers using the Asset Skills?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's nothing denying the application, IIRC. Some guy already good at mundanely reading people's emotions (Empathy) also being good at supernaturally reading them (Aura Reading; Wits + Empathy) doesn't look that out of place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T16:13:16-08:00","id":1473605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleksay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1473563#post1473563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the benefits of the Professional Training apply to supernatural powers using the Asset Skills?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as those are supernatural powers accessible for Human characters, since the major splats can't have Professional Training IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T18:23:54-08:00","id":1473618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1473605#post1473605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as those are supernatural powers accessible for Human characters, since the major splats can't have Professional Training IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural characters can have PT (it's even in a couple of the cores; <b>Mage</b>, for example), but they can't use it for Disciplines/Arcana/Gifts/etc. Like, you can have a Discipline Specialty in a Skill, but you can't be professionally trained in it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T04:24:28-08:00","id":1473638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1473605#post1473605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As long as those are supernatural powers accessible for Human characters, since the major splats can't have Professional Training IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Professional training is definitely possible for other splats, especially if you start as a human and later transition to a supernatural template, they can make some character OP (a Rahu with with professional training in Brawl is rolling all attacks with 8 again and as a rote action for example) so I guess its the storyteller call wether to allow it or not in their games but RAW, supernaturals can definitely have professional training.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T04:15:49-08:00","id":1474275,"title":"","content":"I am trying to incorporate elements from the hurt locker in my game but I have trouble understanding how tracking ammo would work, I understand what capacity is and how the new system works but when it comes to the part of acquiring reloads it says that they last for the scene they are acquired or the next, what does this mean? ammo magically disappear after it has been acquired?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T04:52:12-08:00","id":1474277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1474275#post1474275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am trying to incorporate elements from the hurt locker in my game but I have trouble understanding how tracking ammo would work, I understand what capacity is and how the new system works but when it comes to the part of acquiring reloads it says that they last for the scene they are acquired or the next, what does this mean? ammo magically disappear after it has been acquired?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, yes.<br /> The intention is that procuring extra reloads is something you do when you expect combat rather than having to care about longterm stockkeeping (for PCs) &amp; bookkeeping (for players). If there's no combat, then no need to bring extra ammo.<br /> When it works, it provides a bit of a cinematic feel. It's the protagonists having their preparation montage before a fight. Or in a less action hero-type game, it just connects the supply run with the reason for the supply run in a good narrative fashion.<br /> But in a game it can be difficult to know when combat will happen, or even whether it'll be combat at all. If they stock up on ammo but then manage to talk the antagonist down or incapacitate them without using weapons, then that ammo is simply wasted. And if the PCs know they'll be attacked but not when, they either have to go shopping every other scene or be (relatively) unprepared even though they should know better.<br /> <br /> Quick note: It's only the extra ammo that disappears. The weapons themselves automatically refresh the ammo they can hold each scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T04:53:07-08:00","id":1474278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1474275#post1474275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> when it comes to the part of acquiring reloads it says that they last for the scene they are acquired or the next, what does this mean? ammo magically disappear after it has been acquired?</div> </div> </div> </div>I understood it as:<br /> <br /> If the scene in which you\u2019re acquiring extra reloads is the same scene in which you\u2019re using them (ie the gunfight scene), you expect your acquired reloads to be all spent in this scene.<br /> <br /> If the scene in which you\u2019re acquiring extra reloads is the scene that will be immediately followed by the scene in which you\u2019ll actually them, you expect to keep your acquired reloads in that following gunfight scene, because, well of course so because that\u2019s why you were resupplying yourself in the first place. <br /> <br /> So ultimately, extra reloads you get last for one or two scenes. Sorta like the \u201cPower Charge\u201d or \u201cFocus\u201d special moves common in JRPGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T08:48:19-08:00","id":1474287,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the answers everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T11:26:50-08:00","id":1474310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1474275#post1474275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am trying to incorporate elements from the hurt locker in my game but I have trouble understanding how tracking ammo would work, I understand what capacity is and how the new system works but when it comes to the part of acquiring reloads it says that they last for the scene they are acquired or the next, what does this mean? ammo magically disappear after it has been acquired?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would also point out that the abstraction lies in the counterpoint for the gun also reloading between scenes. In the end it doesn't exactly means that the extra ammo disappears, but just that it is incorporated into usual maintenance supplies, as the rule assumes you're using and buying ammo during scenes, enough to keep your gun and your gun skills in shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T03:07:52-08:00","id":1474360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1474310#post1474310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also point out that the abstraction lies in the counterpoint for the gun also reloading between scenes. In the end it doesn't exactly means that the extra ammo disappears, but just that it is incorporated into usual maintenance supplies, as the rule assumes you're using and buying ammo during scenes, enough to keep your gun and your gun skills in shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>My idea in particular regarded a player whose character is a cop and whose standard loadout includes 4 magazines for his handgun, he has been pretty strict about his ammo count and while he liked the system, he was as perplexed as me concerning how many reloads he could use in a scene, with the system as written, as long as he doesn't use burst fire, he would be fine I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T08:14:30-08:00","id":1474374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1474360#post1474360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My idea in particular regarded a player whose character is a cop and whose standard loadout includes 4 magazines for his handgun, he has been pretty strict about his ammo count and while he liked the system, he was as perplexed as me concerning how many reloads he could use in a scene, with the system as written, as long as he doesn't use burst fire, he would be fine I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>See also the Guns Don't Work That Way sidebar. The Hurt Locker system is written under the assumption that you aren't tracking ammo count and magazines individually, so counts are abstracted and you have &quot;enough&quot; magazines in stock, with extra reloads being &quot;more than enough.&quot; If you and your player are tracking magazines down to the shot already, you can probably omit the Capacity system except as a rough guideline for how much burst fire depletes a magazine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T11:36:02-08:00","id":1474381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1474374#post1474374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See also the Guns Don't Work That Way sidebar. The Hurt Locker system is written under the assumption that you aren't tracking ammo count and magazines individually, so counts are abstracted and you have &quot;enough&quot; magazines in stock, with extra reloads being &quot;more than enough.&quot; If you and your player are tracking magazines down to the shot already, you can probably omit the Capacity system except as a rough guideline for how much burst fire depletes a magazine.</div> </div> </div> </div>We were interested in the burst for every firearm aspect of the system (I always find it stupid that you couldn't attack multiple characters in a single action), with trigger discipline, it should be more feasible I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T13:25:56-08:00","id":1474390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1474381#post1474381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I always find it stupid that you couldn't attack multiple characters in a single action)</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal take is that the rule concerns less with how quickly you can pull the trigger and more with how many times in a round you can aim and take a shot that is meaningful enough for the game.<br /> <br /> Well, that and generally multiple attacks are a bad idea from a design standpoint, so it is a limitation of the format.<br /> <br /> Anyway, outside the aesthetic aspect is there an <b><u>actual reason</u></b> for the player to be so adamant about the four magazines? What exactly does they expect to get from it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T13:58:25-08:00","id":1474393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1474390#post1474390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal take is that the rule concerns less with how quickly you can pull the trigger and more with how many times in a round you can aim and take a shot that is meaningful enough for the game.<br /> <br /> Well, that and generally multiple attacks are a bad idea from a design standpoint, so it is a limitation of the format.<br /> <br /> Anyway, outside the aesthetic aspect is there an <b><u>actual reason</u></b> for the player to be so adamant about the four magazines? What exactly does they expect to get from it?</div> </div> </div> </div>He is kinda of a gun nut and since in the last game, the players dealt with a werewolf, where firepower helped a lot, his reasoning as a player and also in character, is that its better to be prepared against anything that I might throw at them, the other players seem to agree too so I'm thinking to turn this into an hunter game at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T17:54:10-08:00","id":1474404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1474393#post1474393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He is kinda of a gun nut and since in the last game, the players dealt with a werewolf, where firepower helped a lot, his reasoning as a player and also in character, is that its better to be prepared against anything that I might throw at them, the other players seem to agree too so I'm thinking to turn this into an hunter game at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remind him that to stay sharp he needs to practice a lot, and that maintenance and accidents (like wet ammo) have costs. With that you can simply assume that he's procuring extra ammo regularly and roll with it as implied, letting him carry his four magazines.<br /> <br /> This is abstracting the game. The actual number of magazines makes little difference, and in real life you would really be subject to a number of circumstances that would make this number fluctuate. His real concern is to be over-prepared, and the rule covers that. Just assume it being used whenever you think it's adequate instead of making it a too involved process and it will run smooth with the same dramatic effect of his paranoia.<br /> <br /> After all, if you're worried enough to be sure to always be with four magazines, you're probably also always verifying them, reassuring yourself they'll be there and work properly, even using up or throwing away one you think isn't reliable anymore, or just stockpiling at home far more than four. The idea is that the same rule covers all of those, so you both have more freedom describing the form and consequences of this behavior.<br /> <br /> If at some point he tires of the constant application of the procuring rule... well, the character is probably tiring from the effort to always be with four magazines in his person, too. This is a lot, not always easy to carry, and certainly not always well received where you go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T18:52:57-08:00","id":1474407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1474404#post1474404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remind him that to stay sharp he needs to practice a lot, and that maintenance and accidents (like wet ammo) have costs. With that you can simply assume that he's procuring extra ammo regularly and roll with it as implied, letting him carry his four magazines.<br /> <br /> This is abstracting the game. The actual number of magazines makes little difference, and in real life you would really be subject to a number of circumstances that would make this number fluctuate. His real concern is to be over-prepared, and the rule covers that. Just assume it being used whenever you think it's adequate instead of making it a too involved process and it will run smooth with the same dramatic effect of his paranoia.<br /> <br /> After all, if you're worried enough to be sure to always be with four magazines, you're probably also always verifying them, reassuring yourself they'll be there and work properly, even using up or throwing away one you think isn't reliable anymore, or just stockpiling at home far more than four. The idea is that the same rule covers all of those, so you both have more freedom describing the form and consequences of this behavior.<br /> <br /> If at some point he tires of the constant application of the procuring rule... well, the character is probably tiring from the effort to always be with four magazines in his person, too. This is a lot, not always easy to carry, and certainly not always well received where you go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I think I might be overthinking this, probably due to the fact that I never played a game with hurt locker rules myself, my idea is to basically let him have his 4 magazines but keep careful track of his burst attacks (he has maxed dexterity and firearms, with professional training in it, so he kinda turned into an action hero badass at this point), once he is out, thats it, no running around during the scene to look for ammo (unless I think it makes sense), this might actually keep him and his love for burst attacks under control, he almost killed the werewolf antagonist of the first game alone with them and I really wouldn't know what to do if he killed my antagonists ahead of schedule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T00:27:54-08:00","id":1475719,"title":"","content":"Kino Mutai had tag Enraged and Street, but no Grapple.<br /> CAN that and double Joint have this tag too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 03-04-2022, 02:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T14:01:56-08:00","id":1475743,"title":"","content":"This might be a very stupid question, but does anyone have any lists of things like virtue/vice and character goals handy? I like using rollable tables to generate NPCs, but I feel like I'm reinventing the wheel by creating my own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26966-frankgrimes","name":"FrankGrimes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26966_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T15:54:20-08:00","id":1475804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrankGrimes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1475743#post1475743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be a very stupid question, but does anyone have any lists of things like virtue/vice and character goals handy? I like using rollable tables to generate NPCs, but I feel like I'm reinventing the wheel by creating my own.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's first edition, so the Virtues and Vices are specifically the seven deadlies and cardinals, but Damnation City for Vampire: the Requiem has a big section of pretty much exactly this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-23T09:55:48-07:00","id":1477098,"title":"","content":"This might be a strange question but are there any tilts or mechanics regarding low blows? One of my players wanted to kick someone in the nuts and I honestly didn't know how to deal with this so I made them do an aimed shot at -2 and if they inflicted more damage than the target stamina, he would have had to make a resolve+stamina roll or suffer both the beaten down tilt and fall unconscious for a number of turns equal to 10-stamina turns, this was very much improvised on the moment so I was wondering if there an official ruling regarding this kind of situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T05:23:42-07:00","id":1477759,"title":"","content":"Does every human, who does not avert his or her gaze when seeing infrastrcture, or rationalize it somehow, becomes Stigmatic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27350-thalaseus","name":"Thalaseus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T05:48:12-07:00","id":1477760,"title":"","content":"Stigmata is the human equivalent of cryptid mutation. It's not a basilisk effect from glimpsing the God-Machine, but a transformation from exposure to Aetheric backwash. Those who become stigmatic by stumbling upon a project of the God-Machine become so because that project was doing something that was producing sufficiently large amounts of occult radiation.<br /> <br /> You don't become stigmatic because you see infrastructure. You see infrastructure as a result of becoming stigmatic.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T06:10:20-07:00","id":1477761,"title":"","content":"That makes sense and clears things up for me, thanks Stupid Loserman (man, what a nick!). Does that mean that one could be in a room adjacent to G-Ms project, never encounter cogs, or angels, or anything supernatural, then come back home and develop stigmata?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27350-thalaseus","name":"Thalaseus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T09:55:46-07:00","id":1477784,"title":"","content":"Theoretically yes, although for a single day's exposure it was probably a pretty heavy project of the sort that's more likely to produce symptoms and side effects to be noticed. Long periods of repeated exposure could eventually do the job with less essence-heavy infrastructure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T14:01:32-07:00","id":1477800,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to start a campaign with a condition in Chronicles of Darkness? Like a blind character would have the blind condition or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T16:12:12-07:00","id":1477808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1477800#post1477800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to start a campaign with a condition in Chronicles of Darkness? Like a blind character would have the blind condition or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>No explicit rules enabling it, nor forbidding it, iirc. Okay as long as others at the table are okay too, I\u2019d say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-31T19:15:12-07:00","id":1477819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1477800#post1477800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a way to start a campaign with a condition in Chronicles of Darkness? Like a blind character would have the blind condition or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say this is one of the primary purposes of several of the Persistent Conditions, effectively serving in this capacity as a replacement for/reconfiguration of 1e's Flaws.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T19:23:34-07:00","id":1477982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1477819#post1477819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say this is one of the primary purposes of several of the Persistent Conditions, effectively serving in this capacity as a replacement for/reconfiguration of 1e's Flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>^this. A worthwhile notation with that comparison is that unlike how World or Chronicles 1st Edition did it, doing something like that doesn't give you starting points, but instead trades out with how those persistent Conditions are basically equally persistent Beat Generators for the entire game(within the reasonable enactment of the rules to the pleasure of the group, of course).<br /> <br /> But yeah, players can definitely do that sort of thing, within reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T22:16:41-07:00","id":1477990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1477982#post1477982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">unlike how World or Chronicles 1st Edition did it, doing something like that doesn't give you starting points,</div> </div> </div> </div>Just World of Darkness. Chronicles 1e's Flaws system never gave you starting points and worked quite similarly to a Persistent Condition's beat trigger: it just gave you XP when it introduced complications to the game session.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-03T23:58:07-07:00","id":1477992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1477990#post1477990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just World of Darkness. Chronicles 1e's Flaws system never gave you starting points and worked quite similarly to a Persistent Condition's beat trigger: it just gave you XP when it introduced complications to the game session.</div> </div> </div> </div>Been a while, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T19:54:45-07:00","id":1479157,"title":"","content":"Curious some situations with a social interaction itss hard to tell what to roll<br /> <br /> <br /> heres a real life example my niece Who was a year and a half at the time was climbing up the stairs because we'd forgotten to put up the baby gate<br /> <br /> Firmly but not angrily I Called out her first and middle name then reminded her &quot;Mommy said no&quot; <br /> <br /> she just glanced at me then started back down the stairs.<br /> <br /> Or in the movie<br /> <br /> &quot;Something about amelia&quot;<br /> <br /> The officers try to be polite visiting the home to take the girl into custody after she had reported sexual abuse by her father<br /> <br /> But when she was stubborn and tried to stymie them in a stubborn belief her daughter was lieing<br /> <br /> <br /> Shes told &quot;Right now your messing around with a charge of obstructing justice is that what you want?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T20:18:20-07:00","id":1479159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1479157#post1479157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious some situations with a social interaction itss hard to tell what to roll<br /> <br /> <br /> heres a real life example my niece Who was a year and a half at the time was climbing up the stairs because we'd forgotten to put up the baby gate<br /> <br /> Firmly but not angrily I Called out her first and middle name then reminded her &quot;Mommy said no&quot; <br /> <br /> she just glanced at me then started back down the stairs.<br /> <br /> Or in the movie<br /> <br /> &quot;Something about amelia&quot;<br /> <br /> The officers try to be polite visiting the home to take the girl into custody after she had reported sexual abuse by her father<br /> <br /> But when she was stubborn and tried to stymie them in a stubborn belief her daughter was lieing<br /> <br /> <br /> Shes told &quot;Right now your messing around with a charge of obstructing justice is that what you want?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The first might as well be just an Attribute roll; no Skills needed. Maybe Wits + Presence? You are using blunt language while having had little to no time to think up an argument.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t fully understand what you meant in the second example (Who\u2019s stymieing whom?), but seeing the last sentence, I\u2019d go for Manipulation + Intimidation. You\u2019re using authorial threats to have someone act to your intentions.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Of course, keep in mind, depending on the characters and the situation they\u2019re in, they may not need to roll in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T20:38:14-07:00","id":1479160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1479157#post1479157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious some situations with a social interaction itss hard to tell what to roll<br /> <br /> <br /> heres a real life example my niece Who was a year and a half at the time was climbing up the stairs because we'd forgotten to put up the baby gate<br /> <br /> Firmly but not angrily I Called out her first and middle name then reminded her &quot;Mommy said no&quot;<br /> <br /> she just glanced at me then started back down the stairs.<br /> <br /> Or in the movie<br /> <br /> &quot;Something about amelia&quot;<br /> <br /> The officers try to be polite visiting the home to take the girl into custody after she had reported sexual abuse by her father<br /> <br /> But when she was stubborn and tried to stymie them in a stubborn belief her daughter was lieing<br /> <br /> <br /> Shes told &quot;Right now your messing around with a charge of obstructing justice is that what you want?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I go with the Power/Finesse/Resistance trinity when in doubt and it usually works, at least in deciding the Attribute (which I guess to be your doubt).<br /> <br /> For those examples, I think both are <i>Presence</i> rolls, maybe Resisted or Contested with <i>Composure</i>. Both have people trying to be <i>socially forceful</i>, not because they bring in authority, but ultimately because they try to impose a new feature to the interaction that denies agency to the other (or convince them they have no agency).<br /> <br /> Thinking in terms of Strength vs Dexterity in a roll, Strength is used for rolls where you try to forcefully change your environment or forcefully reposition yourself/another actor/an element of the environment, changing the configuration of the context, while Dexterity is used when you try to navigate the environment or direct something already in motion without changing the nature of this motion at once, so you direct the dynamic of the context. Such is Presence vs Manipulation to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T22:13:49-07:00","id":1479162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1479157#post1479157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious some situations with a social interaction itss hard to tell what to roll</div> </div> </div> </div>Also remember that sometimes the answer is &quot;nothing.&quot; If there aren't clear and interesting dramatic consequences that delineate success and failure, don't pick up the dice, just keep going.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T08:02:16-07:00","id":1481757,"title":"","content":"curious ccan an interrogation using empathy be done without the interviewee being in chains???","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T08:32:36-07:00","id":1482158,"title":"","content":"A ghost/spirit can use it's manifestation when fettered to someone or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T09:28:16-07:00","id":1483225,"title":"","content":"I feel I already know the answer here but it's a moment of doubt.<br /> <br /> Are style merits bot as 1xp per dot or is it as seperate merits ie 1 dot merit as prerequisite for the second means you spend 2xp on moving to that second dot from 1 dot, instead of 1xp?<br /> <br /> I think it's just 1xp per dot but I'm having a moment where I'm not certain but I can't seem to find a clear answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T10:26:55-07:00","id":1483228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1483225#post1483225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel I already know the answer here but it's a moment of doubt.<br /> <br /> Are style merits bot as 1xp per dot or is it as seperate merits ie 1 dot merit as prerequisite for the second means you spend 2xp on moving to that second dot from 1 dot, instead of 1xp?<br /> <br /> I think it's just 1xp per dot but I'm having a moment where I'm not certain but I can't seem to find a clear answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>It s 1xp per dot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-06T14:30:38-07:00","id":1483253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1482158#post1482158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A ghost/spirit can use it's manifestation when fettered to someone or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Manifestation, but so long as it stays within five yards of the subject, I'd say yes (and also that for plenty of spirits, Fettering is the first step to later Possession and Claiming).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T16:46:54-07:00","id":1484558,"title":"","content":"The ranged combat rules say Defense doesn't apply to Firearms attack. The &quot;Firearms in Close Quarters&quot; rules say that you apply Size+1 as a bonus to Defense...against a Firearm attack. Which rule controls? When it says &quot;bonus&quot; does that mean full Defense applies against Firearm attacks made in close quarters, or /just/ Size+1 as a kind of standalone Defense value?<br /> <br /> In the core book, I'm talking about the &quot;Firearms in Close Combat&quot; rules on page 90. On Page 88, it states flat out that Defense does not apply to Firearms attacks. I could read the rule as either granting a standalone Defense equal to gun Size + 1, or allowing Defense w/ a bonus of Gun Size + 1 in close quarters. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 06-20-2022, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T17:42:05-07:00","id":1484559,"title":"","content":"It appears that this passage was copy and pasted from the God-Machine Rules Update, which was the first presentation of the second edition rules, framed as a patch meant to apply on top of the first edition rules. Thus the GMRU text would be meant to append on top of the 1e World of Darkness Rulebook passage on firearms in close combat, which asserted that as an exception to the general rules, a firearms attack in close combat did not deny the target their Defense: the GMRU text is thus stating that in 2e rules, not only does a close combat target of a firearms attack get to keep their Defense, but they add (Size of the gun + 1) as a bonus to it if the gun is larger than Size 1.<br /> <br /> Presumably the writers of the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook forgot or missed this context when carrying over text from the GMRU.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-20T17:44:18-07:00","id":1484560,"title":"","content":"That makes sense, thanks!<br /> <br /> I checked Deviant, Hunter, Hurt Locker, and the corebook, but it didn't occur to me to check the old GMRU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T14:14:43-07:00","id":1485547,"title":"","content":"Another question - what's the deal with the Extreme Cold and Heat Environmental Tilts and the Extreme Environments (as a source of harm) rules? Do both basically always apply at the same time, or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T20:09:41-07:00","id":1485585,"title":"","content":"My assumption, at least, was that Extreme Cold and Extreme Heat, being Tilts, are meant to be applied as the rules during action scenes (&quot;combat time&quot;), whereas longer-term scenes not tracking time by initiative turns use the Extreme Environment rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-10T12:08:47-07:00","id":1486171,"title":"","content":"In the Havoc rules in Genius: The Transgression, it says that Havoc is caused when a wonder is &quot;touched, picked up, or interacted with by a mere mortal (an untemplated human)&quot;. So does that mean that creatures with Supernatural Templates <i>don't</i> cause Havoc? Because if so, that radically changes the way Geniuses would interact with other factions. If a Genius can sell even mostly reliable wonders to other factions, there are groups out there with the Resources to pay top dollar for such valuable tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26379-aeshdan","name":"Aeshdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26379_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T10:45:49-07:00","id":1486290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeshdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1486171#post1486171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Havoc rules in Genius: The Transgression, it says that Havoc is caused when a wonder is &quot;touched, picked up, or interacted with by a mere mortal (an untemplated human)&quot;. So does that mean that creatures with Supernatural Templates <i>don't</i> cause Havoc? Because if so, that radically changes the way Geniuses would interact with other factions. If a Genius can sell even mostly reliable wonders to other factions, there are groups out there with the Resources to pay top dollar for such valuable tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the text is being pretty explicit there, even clarifying itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T06:02:22-07:00","id":1486404,"title":"","content":"Does any 2e supplement have rules for firearms in the Elizabethan period? In other words, for matchlocks? (Or flintlocks, etc...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T04:35:15-07:00","id":1487565,"title":"","content":"Can you have more than one Professional Training merit track? <br /> <br /> Say your character has Professional Training (Author) 1. You later take dots in a Mystery Cult that grants a dot of a different Professional Training. Do you now have two PT tracks? Should you just add the new dot to your original PT track? Should you just gain the value of the dots, as MtAw 2e recommends for ineligible MC merits (pg106)?<br /> <br /> Professional Training 3 (Breadth of Knowledge) would be the best place to &quot;merge&quot; multiple tracks, but that's a somewhat narrow window.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 07-23-2022, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T22:38:51-07:00","id":1487846,"title":"","content":"Generally, the books call out when you can take a merit multiple times. I would probably not allow it, personally, but it's probably a situation that requires an ST judgment call. I would probably give the value of the dots or just give them the two dots of Contacts like PT would have, but that's me. Two PT tracks means the potential of six skills getting free and unlimited 9-again, and that doesn't sit right with me with the lack any indication that it can be taken multiple times. Other merits have it spelled out when you can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T03:35:18-07:00","id":1487999,"title":"","content":"You can't take Professional Training multiple times, and MCI should (in my opinion) never grant PT in the first place. A Style-like Merit that grants advantages explicitly worth more than a single Merit dot each should not grant dots in another Style-like Merit that grant advantages that are generally even more powerful.<br /> <br /> If you want to take Professional Training multiple times to reflect a character's development in another field, I instead recommend gradually switching out the advantages granted by PT to reflect the new focus. Change Asset Skill, swap Specialties and Contacts, and move the free Skill dot if you drop that as an Asset Skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T16:19:00-07:00","id":1490452,"title":"","content":"How many secret monster societies do you assume there are in a given city? Do you just expect that there's a vampire domain, and a bunch of werewolf packs, and a freehold, and so on in most cities, or would the presence of so many secret societies overlaid in the same location be something unusual about particular city?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","user":"Niknokk","date":". 08-16-2022, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T19:27:52-07:00","id":1490476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1490452#post1490452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many secret monster societies do you assume there are in a given city? Do you just expect that there's a vampire domain, and a bunch of werewolf packs, and a freehold, and so on in most cities, or would the presence of so many secret societies overlaid in the same location be something unusual about particular city?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would probably be unusual, but then it heavily depends on your game. A chronicle where every major city has all the &quot;main&quot; factions then some and most smaller cities have some, too, is perfectly viable. But the most probable situation is that few cities really have a big variety even if they're really big cities, unless they have something that justifies a huge population of everything.<br /> <br /> The most important thing is to consider the needs of your game, though. Crossover is fun, but putting things in the city just for the sake of having them there or to simulate what you think should be standard will only steal the focus and multiply your work while barely adding to your story. Start with what you <b>need</b>, then add stuff only if that's the point of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T14:58:00-07:00","id":1491440,"title":"","content":"Broadly speaking, going 5+ in an attribute causes you to start acting inhuman. You can play the character however you want, of course, but the implication is that you're transcending what most people would consider &quot;normal&quot;. 5+ Resolve, for example, makes you very difficult to sway from a course of action, whether or not the arguments are good or bad. Most of the mental attributes seem like a good excuse to play the character constantly irritated at how &quot;dumb&quot; everyone around them is.<br /> <br /> What attributes or skills could you increase to counterbalance this? Would Empathy help keep you grounded, or would it just make you a more effective sociopath?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T20:48:12-07:00","id":1491551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1491440#post1491440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Broadly speaking, going 5+ in an attribute causes you to start acting inhuman. You can play the character however you want, of course, but the implication is that you're transcending what most people would consider &quot;normal&quot;. 5+ Resolve, for example, makes you very difficult to sway from a course of action, whether or not the arguments are good or bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't share this assumption, and it's not presented in the books, at least not so explicitly as to be a Simple Question with a Simple Answer. Attributes and Skills do not compel your character; they describe capability, not personality. A high Composure means that you have high social resistance, difficult to sway in directions that you don't intend. It does not mean that you're stone-faced and never crack a smile or are never charmed or irritated by anything; it means you have self-control. You <i>may</i> be a stone-faced person who never cracks a smile, and if you have high Intelligence and Wits you <i>may</i> grow frustrated easily with those around you who can't keep up with your thought process. But those are personality traits, and personality traits that would likely manifest in some manner even if you didn't have these high capabilities.<br /> <br /> Empathy, similarly, isn't a score of how much you care about the people around you. There isn't a numerical score for that. Empathy is your skill at <i>discerning and intuiting what people are feeling.</i> Empathy is the ability to read people.<br /> <br /> Certainly the game mechanics don't reflect these traits being transformative in this way. Having higher Attributes mostly means you have more dice, and CofD dice are subject to diminishing returns: going from 2 dice to 3 dice in a pool makes a massively larger difference than going from 6 dice to 7 dice. The high randomness of target number 8 for a success means those dice are never entirely irrelevant, but they're not going to make you perform actions on a profoundly different level from those around you. Traits exceeding the mortal cap are better thought of as supplementary benefits to monsters who almost certainly have picked up greater powers on their way to Potency 6. More reliable, more consistent capabilities. Less likely to make unforced errors... except those militated not by their capabilities, but by their personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T22:51:38-07:00","id":1491555,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I can assure you that many, maybe most people that get irritated about the inability of others to follow their thought process have far less impressive intellect than they think. They're just obnoxious. An intelligent person who isn't impatient or obnoxious won't be like that just because they're smart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T01:16:12-07:00","id":1491565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1491551#post1491551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Empathy, similarly, isn't a score of how much you care about the people around you. There isn't a numerical score for that. Empathy is your skill at <i>discerning and intuiting what people are feeling.</i> Empathy is the ability to read people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I assumed it wouldn't actually balance out the character if 5+ Attributes causes different bahavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1491551#post1491551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't share this assumption, and it's not presented in the books, at least not so explicitly as to be a Simple Question with a Simple Answer. Attributes and Skills do not compel your character; they describe capability, not personality. A high Composure means that you have high social resistance, difficult to sway in directions that you don't intend. It does not mean that you're stone-faced and never crack a smile or are never charmed or irritated by anything; it means you have self-control. You <i>may</i> be a stone-faced person who never cracks a smile, and if you have high Intelligence and Wits you <i>may</i> grow frustrated easily with those around you who can't keep up with your thought process. But those are personality traits, and personality traits that would likely manifest in some manner even if you didn't have these high capabilities.</div> </div> </div> </div> I may be reading too far into The Broken Diamond, Soul Cage, and other Actual Plays. In those, Mages boosting their attributes with magic usually end up changing their behavior slightly. That makes sense to me, mostly because suddenly being a lot more intelligent or socially aware than you normally are WILL have an impact on how you interact with others. Becoming inhumanly resolved or composed would likely have similar effects - you're becoming detatched from the limitations of your nominal peers. It doesn't necessarily mean the character will instantly become an asshole, but there will be differences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1491555#post1491555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, I can assure you that many, maybe most people that get irritated about the inability of others to follow their thought process have far less impressive intellect than they think. They're just obnoxious. An intelligent person who isn't impatient or obnoxious won't be like that just because they're smart.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly pointing to a stereotype; most people have seen that kind of archetype in books or movies. Yes, the people who act like that in real life are usually self-involved jackaninnies. I'm still of the opinion that passing the 5-dot mark in an Attribute should give you an inhuman vibe, although not necessarily malignant. If Presence 2 is the average human, the sheer force of personallity at Presence 6 should turn heads just by walking into a room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":27258,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","user":"Cauthon","date":". 08-28-2022, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T07:54:28-07:00","id":1491594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1491565#post1491565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense to me, mostly because suddenly being a lot more intelligent or socially aware than you normally are WILL have an impact on how you interact with others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but with too much caveats, that's the problem.<br /> <br /> The way you posited your question indicates an expectation of standards for such changes, that's the problematic part. Such changes do occur, but in a case-by-case basis.<br /> <br /> We have a very complex situation here, fraught with traps. Even within the 5 &quot;normal&quot; levels, the interaction between stats and behavior is a question that already filled many threads in this forum and many others across the internet, with no definitive answer in sight. This is definitely not a Simple Question.<br /> <br /> But beyond that, and to give a Simple Answer that does, in fact, exist: however you see it, in the end such expectations work only as limitations on role play, in a game where putting forth your vision of your character is the very point. CoD walked away from more specific descriptions to what a stat feels like precisely because of that. In fact, despite what you say, the game never said what such numbers mean beyond more dice, so even that's just your interpretation.<br /> <br /> Instead of asking what the effect of being &quot;supernaturally high&quot; at a given attribute would be, much less how to counterbalance when you're already stating that you don't want to do that, just asks what this number means for this particular character in your opinion and roll with it. If you feel <b>this </b>character would become obnoxious and <b>this</b> character would want to improve, just roll with it and think about what increasing other traits would do to <b>this </b>character.<br /> <br /> No hard and fast rules, what works for one doesn't necessarily does for other, exploring the question itself in a game and coming up with custom answers will be far more interesting than defining it beforehand, and if you want to explore the matter deeper, make an actual thread about it, because it won't be solved here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T07:32:20-07:00","id":1493210,"title":"","content":"I am sure this question has been answered before at least once, but I can't find it....<br /> Hypothetical - a Mage uses life magic to change into an owl. Happens to make eye contact w/ a vampire. The vampire attempts to influence the mage with animalism.<br /> How stong is the influence on the mage?<br /> Is it obvious to the vampire that this is not a normal owl?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":532,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","user":"Newes","date":". 09-17-2022, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/532-newes","name":"Newes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T19:56:35-07:00","id":1493227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1493210#post1493210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am sure this question has been answered before at least once, but I can't find it....<br /> Hypothetical - a Mage uses life magic to change into an owl. Happens to make eye contact w/ a vampire. The vampire attempts to influence the mage with animalism.<br /> How stong is the influence on the mage?<br /> Is it obvious to the vampire that this is not a normal owl?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Animalism is not effective on shapechangers in animal form. According to the description of <i>Shapechanging </i>in page 152 of the mage core book, the mage seems to retain all sentient reason. The only caveat is that, without spending a Reach, they have to roll to suppress their strong animal instincts. Which means Animalism would automatically fail, since Dominate would be the correct tool. An inexperienced vampire will likely be left confused, while a more senior one will adjust their strategy to uncover what kind of being they are talking to or even consider a diplomatic approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T23:35:24-07:00","id":1494184,"title":"","content":"can meditation be done as an assisted action? Or do something else for helping someone meditate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-03T21:33:42-07:00","id":1494281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1494184#post1494184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">can meditation be done as an assisted action? Or do something else for helping someone meditate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems plausable. Guided meditation is certainly a thing in real life.<br /> <br /> Long shot, but is there a Japanese translation of the Core book? It'd be something interesting to introduce my students to, but outside my weight-class to try and explain whole-cloth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T06:38:39-07:00","id":1494415,"title":"","content":"For combat, I roll my attribute + skill + bonus from weapon - defense (if applicable) and the successes there are the damage inflicted, there's no damage roll or soak roll, right? Going through the combat chapter over and over I feel like this is right, but then I read vigor and I'm stumped, why is it better to add vigor to your weapon than to your strength? (Or is it that you add it to both your strength and your weapon if you activate it?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 10-05-2022, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T07:13:58-07:00","id":1494418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1494415#post1494415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For combat, I roll my attribute + skill + bonus from weapon - defense (if applicable) and the successes there are the damage inflicted, there's no damage roll or soak roll, right? Going through the combat chapter over and over I feel like this is right, but then I read vigor and I'm stumped, why is it better to add vigor to your weapon than to your strength? (Or is it that you add it to both your strength and your weapon if you activate it?)</div> </div> </div> </div>No separate damage rolls, nor Soak rolls \u2014 you inflict your successes as damage, and that\u2019s it. Weapon Modifiers(Bonuses) add directly to the end damage, not the attacking dice pool.<br /> <br /> As for the vampiric Discipline Vigor, it adding to Strength is a persistent (passive) effect, and yes, spending Vitae allows you to additionally apply a Weapon Modifier on top of what you roll from your already-Vigor-enhanced attacking dice pool. (Been awhile since I dived in Vampire, though\u2026)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-05T16:04:45-07:00","id":1494437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1494415#post1494415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For combat, I roll my attribute + skill + bonus from weapon - defense (if applicable) and the successes there are the damage inflicted, there's no damage roll or soak roll, right? Going through the combat chapter over and over I feel like this is right, but then I read vigor and I'm stumped, why is it better to add vigor to your weapon than to your strength? (Or is it that you add it to both your strength and your weapon if you activate it?)</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two rules editions, and the weapon rating does different things in each, which may be the confusion.<br /> <br /> In 1e CofD, weapon rating is bonus dice. You roll Attribute + Skill + Weapon Bonus - Defense, and deal damage equal to your successes. 1e Vigor adds a bonus to your Strength, which is the Attribute you roll when making melee attacks.<br /> <br /> In 2e CofD, weapon rating is bonus <i>damage.</i> You roll Attribute + Skill - Defense, and deal damage equal to your successes <i>plus your Weapon Rating,</i> provided you didn't fail (so you don't deal weapon rating damage if you rolled zero successes, if you fail the roll you do no damage). 2e Vigor adds a bonus to your Strength for free, and if you spend Vitae it <i>also</i> adds itself to your weapon rating. Effectively, the free Vigor Strength bonus functions as dice, but the at-cost weapon bonus functions as automatic successes, provided you roll at least one normal die success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T14:33:02-07:00","id":1494466,"title":"","content":"After acquiring the 4th dot of Martial Arts (The Hand as Weapon), can a character choose to cause bashing damage or are their fists so hardened that holding back is impossible?<br /> <br /> In addition, if a target cannot apply defense against firearms, can a killing blow be the opening attack of a stealthy ambush ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 10-07-2022, 12:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-06T23:06:09-07:00","id":1494496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1494466#post1494466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After acquiring the 4th dot of Martial Arts (The Hand as Weapon), can a character choose to cause bashing damage or are their fists so hardened that holding back is impossible?<br /> <br /> In addition, if a target cannot apply defense against firearms, can a killing blow be the opening attack of a stealthy ambush ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pulling blows to only deal bashing generally costs a WP, but in this case I think it's reasonable that the character simply doesn't apply the fighting style in the attack.<br /> <br /> Killing Blows requires the victim to be completely unmoving, not just unaware.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-07T03:56:58-07:00","id":1494512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1494496#post1494496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pulling blows to only deal bashing generally costs a WP, but in this case I think it's reasonable that the character simply doesn't apply the fighting style in the attack.<br /> <br /> Killing Blows requires the victim to be completely unmoving, not just unaware.</div> </div> </div> </div>So thankfully no snipers using killing blow to do absurd damage as a first move. Got it, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T11:59:53-07:00","id":1495259,"title":"","content":"Is there some kind of yardstick for what the different levels of Dominance means for a cult? Roughly how big they would be/how powerful etc? Because it's kinda hard to judge in a vacuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-19T12:14:10-07:00","id":1495262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1495259#post1495259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there some kind of yardstick for what the different levels of Dominance means for a cult? Roughly how big they would be/how powerful etc? Because it's kinda hard to judge in a vacuum.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some rough correlation to Krewes and Conspiracies that can be helpful, although notably Conspiracies are intended to represent wider entities than Cults and Krewes, so wibbly yardsticks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-24T21:29:40-07:00","id":1495548,"title":"","content":"One thing Im wonderin